window.BANK = {"generated":"2026-10-09","exams":[{"code":"AB-620","title":"Designing and Building Integrated AI Agent Solutions in Copilot Studio","url":"https://www.examtopics.com/exams/microsoft/ab-620/view/","topics":[{"n":1,"name":"Plan and configure agent solutions"},{"n":2,"name":"Integrate and extend agents in Copilot Studio"},{"n":3,"name":"Test and manage agents"}],"cases":{"87efe5dfda":{"name":"Blue Yonder Airlines","html":"<h4>Background</h4><p>Blue Yonder Airlines is a global carrier headquartered in Los Angeles, California, operating domestic and international flights. The company serves millions of passengers annually through its website, mobile app, and call centers. To improve customer service efficiency and reduce call center volume, Blue Yonder is deploying an AI agent in Microsoft Copilot Studio.</p><p>The agent will handle customer inquiries across multiple channels – web chat, mobile app, and Microsoft Teams (for internal support staff). It will answer questions, retrieve data from enterprise systems, and escalate to human agents when needed.</p><p>The project is led by a cross-function team:</p><ul class=\"kv\"><li><b>Product manager:</b> Defines requirements and success metrics.</li><li><b>Lead agent author:</b> Designs topics, intents, and generative behavior.</li><li><b>Flow designers:</b> Build agent flows and integrations.</li><li><b>IT/security and compliance:</b> Oversees identity, data protection, and Responsible AI (RAI) compliance.</li></ul><h4>Current environment</h4><h5>Channels</h5><ul class=\"kv\"><li><b>Public website:</b> Embedded web chat</li><li><b>Mobile app:</b> In-app chatbot</li><li><b>Microsoft Teams:</b> Internal support agent access</li></ul><h5>Identity and access</h5><ul class=\"kv\"><li><b>Customers:</b> Anonymous access for general inquiries (e.g., flight status, baggage policy).</li><li>Authentication is required for personal data access (e.g., bookings, loyalty points).</li><li><b>Internal staff:</b> Authenticate via Microsoft Entra ID.</li></ul><h5>Data sources</h5><ul class=\"kv\"><li><b>Reservation and Ticketing System (internal):</b> REST API, no prebuilt connector with custom enterprise database.</li><li><b>Flight Status and Weather APIs (external):</b> REST APIs with API keys.</li><li><b>Customer Support Knowledge Base:</b> SharePoint library with PDFs and policy documents.</li><li><b>Loyalty Program Data:</b> Stored in Dynamics 365 and Dataverse.</li><li><b>Travel Advisory Content:</b> Uses REST API with partner services.</li></ul><h5>Integration mechanisms</h5><p>Custom connectors must be used for internal APIs that lack prebuilt connectors.</p><p>HTTP request nodes may be used for lightweight external APIs.</p><p>Knowledge sources must be used for unstructured content.</p><p>Agent flows must be used to encapsulate reusable logic (e.g., rebooking).</p><h4>Business requirements</h4><h5>Omnichannel support</h5><p>Deploy the agent across web, mobile, and Teams with a consistent user experience. The Teams deployment must also support internal staff.</p><h5>Self-service capabilities</h5><p>The agent must handle common inquiries such as:</p><ul><li>Flight status</li><li>Booking and rebooking</li><li>Loyalty program questions</li><li>Travel policies and baggage rules</li></ul><h5>Human escalation</h5><p>If the agent cannot resolve an issue or the user requests help, it must:</p><ul><li>Escalate to a human agent.</li><li>Transfer the conversation transcript and relevant context.</li><li>Redact any sensitive personal data before escalation.</li></ul><h5>Knowledge integration</h5><p>The agent must use scalable methods for knowledge integration and must not rely on manually authored Q&amp;A topics for each document.</p><h5>Performance metrics</h5><ul class=\"kv\"><li><b>First-contact resolution:</b> +25%</li><li><b>Tier-1 call deflection:</b> ≥20%</li><li><b>Response time:</b> 90% of queries answered within 30 seconds</li><li><b>Accuracy:</b> ≥95% for known FAQs</li><li><b>CSAT:</b> ≥85% for AI-handled interactions</li></ul><h4>Technical requirements</h4><h5>Platform constraints</h5><p>No custom code is permitted; only Copilot Studio's built-in tools may be used.</p><p>All backend logic must be implemented using agent flows.</p><p>Markdown must be used for formatting (e.g., bold, bullet points); HTML is not supported.</p><h5>Authentication</h5><p>Sign-in is required for personal data access.</p><p>Anonymous access is allowed for general inquiries.</p><p>User identity must be used for data access; shared or builder credentials must not be used.</p><h4>Compliance and security</h4><p>Power Platform DLP policies must be enforced to block unauthorized data flows.</p><p>Responsible AI content moderation filters must be enabled.</p><p>Prompt modifications must be added to enforce tone, disclaimers, and refusal behavior.</p><p>Disclaimers must be applied consistently across all generative responses. Manual edits to individual topics must be avoided.</p><h4>Monitoring and maintenance</h4><p>All conversations and actions must be logged for auditing.</p><p>Weekly reviews of transcripts and metrics must be conducted.</p><h4>Issues and constraints</h4><ul class=\"kv\"><li><b>API rate limits:</b> External APIs (e.g., flight status) have usage limits. Agent flows must handle retries and caching to avoid exceeding quotas.</li><li><b>Knowledge base limits:</b> Copilot Studio has limits on the number and size of indexed documents. Large files must be split or summarized.</li><li><b>Generative answer risks:</b> Generative responses must be constrained to avoid policy violations. Prompt modifications and filters must be used to enforce tone, safety, and compliance.</li><li><b>User input variability:</b> Users phrase questions in diverse ways. Topics must include varied trigger phrases and fallback handling.</li><li><b>Authentication UX:</b> The agent must clearly explain when sign-in is required and handle transitions smoothly across channels.</li></ul><h4>Problem statement</h4><p>Blue Yonder Airlines must deploy a secure, scalable, and policy-compliant AI agent using Microsoft Copilot Studio. The agent must deliver accurate, helpful, and safe responses across multiple channels, integrate with enterprise systems, and support both anonymous and authenticated users. It must adhere to strict data protection and Responsible AI standards while improving customer service efficiency and satisfaction.</p>"},"cd9e9dfedc":{"name":"Fabrikam Inc.","html":"<h4>Background</h4><p>Fabrikam Inc. is a Canada-based manufacturer with a growing service organization that supports field technicians and internal operations teams. Fabrikam Inc. plans to launch a new internal agent solution named Operations Concierge to reduce time spent searching policy content, retrieving operational metrics, and executing routine transactions.</p><p>The agent will be used by three groups:</p><ul><li>Service coordinators who triage incoming service requests</li><li>Field technicians who need guided procedures and parts availability</li><li>Operations managers who monitor KPIs and exceptions</li></ul><p>The agent solution must work in real-world operational conditions. Users often ask questions mid-call with a customer or while coordinating parts shipments. The agents require quick, reliable outcomes. As a result, Fabrikam Inc. requires the solution to:</p><ul><li>Provide grounded answers with traceability when it provides guidance.</li><li>Retrieve real-time metrics when users ask for operational status.</li><li>Execute authenticated updates when users initiate a flow (such as creating a parts request).</li></ul><p>Fabrikam Inc. also expects the solution to be maintained by multiple makers and developers across the year. The company has experienced duplicated logic and inconsistent behavior across different agents. This project emphasizes reuse, governance, and maintainability across teams.</p><h4>Current environment</h4><p>Fabrikam Inc. runs three Microsoft Power Platform environments for agent development and release: Dev, Test, and Prod.</p><p>The team plans to build the agent and validate it in Dev and Test, then promote to Prod by using a controlled release process that supports repeatable deployments.</p><p>Fabrikam Inc. already has two assets the team wants to reuse:</p><ul><li>A partially completed Copilot Studio agent named Service Desk Agent, used by IT to create internal tickets and route requests</li><li>A Microsoft Foundry agent created by a central AI team that performs specialized summarization and classification for long-form text (for example, summarizing call transcripts into an incident narrative)</li></ul><p>Fabrikam Inc. also has operational and knowledge data sources:</p><ul><li>A curated policy library (internal SOPs, service warranty rules, escalation criteria, and standard operating procedures)</li><li>A set of indexed documents and procedures in an Azure AI Search service that supports vector search for the policy library</li><li>A Microsoft Fabric workspace that includes a semantic model used by operations leadership for reporting</li></ul><h4>Business requirements</h4><p>Fabrikam Inc. requires Operations Concierge to meet the following business requirements:</p><ul class=\"kv\"><li><b>Traceability requirement:</b> When the agent provides policy guidance or procedural recommendations, users must be able to see where the answer came from.</li><li><b>Metrics requirement:</b> When users ask about service performance (backlog, SLA risk, parts shortages, dispatch delays), the solution must return up-to-date metrics in a structured format that operations managers can use in weekly reviews.</li><li><b>Transaction requirement:</b> The solution must support authenticated updates initiated during conversations, including creating a parts request and updating a service case status.</li></ul><p>In addition, Fabrikam Inc. wants to avoid duplicating common assets across agents:</p><ul><li>The team must reuse the same set of escalation topics, MCP tool definitions, and a standard safety disclaimer across three different agents.</li><li>Only the platform engineering group as allowed to edit shared assets. However, all agent authors must be able to use them.</li></ul><h4>Technical requirements</h4><p>The Fabrikam Inc. solution architecture uses a multi-agent approach so that specialist responsibilities are isolated and can evolve independently.</p><p>The Operations Concierge (primary agent) must coordinate the following specialist capabilities:</p><ul class=\"kv\"><li><b>Policy and procedure Q&amp;A:</b> Use an enterprise knowledge source that supports indexed retrieval across the curated policy library and service procedures.</li><li><b>Operational metrics:</b> Delegate metric queries to a Fabric Data Agent that reads governed business data through the Fabric semantic model.</li><li><b>Authenticated updates:</b> Use tools exposed by an existing internal Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that provides transactional operations for the service organization.</li><li><b>Specialized processing:</b> Delegate summarization and classification requests to an existing Microsoft Foundry agent.</li></ul><p>Fabrikam Inc. will onboard two MCP servers as tools:</p><ul class=\"kv\"><li><b>PartsOps MCP server:</b> exposes tools for parts availability checks and parts request creation. The server requires per-user authentication because actions must be traceable to the requesting user.</li><li><b>WarrantyRules MCP server:</b> exposes a read-only tool for validating warranty coverage. The server uses an API key shared by the agent team.</li></ul><p>Fabrikam Inc. has also defined a collaboration requirement with the existing Service Desk Agent:</p><ul><li>The primary agent must delegate IT-specific requests to the existing Service Desk Agent rather than reimplement ticket creation logic.</li></ul><p>Finally, Fabrikam Inc. plans to support a partner integration:</p><ul><li>For shipment tracking inquiries, Fabrikam Inc. will delegate to a partner-provided agent that is only available through a standardized agent-to-agent endpoint.</li></ul><h4>Issues and constraints</h4><p>During early testing, Fabrikam Inc. found three recurring problems:</p><ul><li>Makers are copying and modifying the same components across agents, resulting in inconsistent disclaimers and duplicated tools.</li><li>Users can obtain a correct answer, but the response is not consistently traceable to a source when the agent uses knowledge.</li><li>The primary agent can route some requests, but specialist capabilities are not consistently delegated (for example, some metric questions are answered generatively instead of being routed to the Fabric Data Agent).</li></ul><p>You are part of the engineering team responsible for correcting the design and configuration to meet the preceding requirements and constraints.</p>"}},"questions":[{"n":1,"id":1007775,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You need to configure the agent in Copilot Studio to meet Blue Yonder's Responsible AI and data protection requirements.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which three actions should you perform in sequence?</strong> To answer, move the appropriate actions from the list of actions to the answer area and arrange them in the correct order.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image1.png\" alt=\"image1\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image2.png\" alt=\"image2\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":1,"case":"87efe5dfda","thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/7465efec031a63bae0955e42e26b14a81007775/","comments":[{"user":"Hatsapatsa","date":"2026-07-16","up":8,"text":"I think 3 should be Configure content moderation filters as stated in the case study.","top":true,"replies":[{"user":"60ed5c2","date":"2026-07-16","up":1,"text":"I agree the question specifically talks to configuration, testing would come later."}]},{"user":"jessecollin","date":"2026-10-11","up":3,"text":"The correct answers are:\nDefine Data Loss Prevention (DLP) policies.\nAdd custom prompt modifications.\nConduct adversarial testing.\nI passed my exam as well, and ExamsPilot helped me with extra practice and revision. Hope this helps others preparing for the exam!"},{"user":"vishnu1812","date":"2026-09-01","up":3,"text":"The correct sequence should be:\nDefine Data Loss Prevention (DLP) policies\nConfigure content moderation filters\nAdd custom prompt modifications"},{"user":"massnonn","date":"2026-09-02","up":2,"text":"1-Define Data Loss Prevention (DLP) policies.\n2-Configure content moderation filters.\n3-Conduct adversarial testing."},{"user":"msrao83","date":"2026-09-29","up":1,"text":"Define Data Loss Prevention (DLP) policies\nConfigure content moderation filters\nAdd custom prompt modifications"},{"user":"JamesM9","date":"2026-09-24","up":1,"text":"1. DLP policies prevent unauthorized data flows and protect sensitive information.\n2. Content moderation filters help enforce Responsible AI and prevent unsafe or inappropriate responses.\n3. Custom prompt modifications/notifications enforce the required tone, disclaimers, and refusal behaviour consistently across generative responses."},{"user":"Sweden2022","date":"2026-09-17","up":1,"text":"1. Define DLP policies — governance-level control, set at the environment/tenant level before anything else runs\n2. Add custom prompt modifications — configured on the agent to shape tone, disclaimers, and refusal behavior\n3. Configure content moderation filters — the safety-net layer that filters/moderates generative output as it's produced"}]},{"n":2,"id":1020430,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A company uses an agent in Copilot Studio that produces structured responses using a reusable instruction template. The responses follow the required tone and format. During a compliance review, the team discovers that the responses were generated using a model that is not on the approved list.</p><p>The company requires that the reusable instruction template continues to be used and the model used for prompt-driven responses meets governance requirements.</p><p>The solution must ensure that prompt-driven responses are generated using an approved model.</p><p>You need to configure the solution that meets the requirements.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which two actions should you perform?</strong> Each correct answer presents part of the solution.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Select an approved model from the Microsoft Foundry model catalog in the configuration that is used for prompt-driven response generation."},{"k":"B","html":"Configure Azure AI Search as the grounding source so the approved model requirement is enforced during response generation."},{"k":"C","html":"Ensure the reusable instruction template is the one applied to the agent that generates the structured response."},{"k":"D","html":"Publish the agent so that the model used by prompt-driven responses is updated automatically."},{"k":"E","html":"Enable citations so generated responses can be traced and comply with governance requirements."},{"k":"F","html":"Add a line to the instruction template that requires the agent to use only approved models when generating responses."}],"answer":"CF","type":"multi","votes":[],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/4fd49c7145dd8942a42d5cbf7ece02d01020430/","comments":[{"user":"Rami7","date":"2026-10-09","up":2,"text":"F. Add a line to the instruction template requiring approved models\n\nPrompts cannot control which underlying model is selected. Model governance is configured administratively, not through prompt text.","pick":"AC"},{"user":"8bb6cf1","date":"2026-10-13","up":1,"text":"C + F.\nF - Prompts can't enforce which model is actually used. Model selection is a configuration setting, not a prompt instruction.","pick":"CF","replies":[{"user":"Rami7","date":"2026-10-13","up":1,"text":"so F is incorrect"}]}],"variants":[52]},{"n":3,"id":1020431,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A company needs to ground an agent in Copilot Studio answers using live enterprise data from a supported system via a Microsoft Power Platform connector. To meet the business needs, the builder must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Authenticate using a valid connection.</li><li>Add the connector as a real-time knowledge source.</li><li>Select the tables for knowledge grounding.</li></ul><p>You need to add a Power Platform connector as a real-time knowledge source for the agent.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>In which order should you perform the actions?</strong> To answer, move all actions from the list of actions to the answer area and arrange them in the correct order.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image93.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image94.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/a30d26accee5709b6a5cdec58d68468e1020431/","comments":[{"user":"harshagracy","date":"2026-10-13","up":1,"text":"Add a knowledge source.\n\nSelect a real-time connector from the Add knowledge dialog.\n\nSign in and create a new connection or reuse an existing connection.\n\nSelect the tables to include as the knowledge source.\n\nAdd the connector to the agent."}],"variants":[8]},{"n":4,"id":1007779,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You need to configure the agent in Copilot Studio to use internal and external partner knowledge sources to answer user questions about the airline services.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which two actions should you perform?</strong> Each correct answer presents part of the solution.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Use a Microsoft Graph connector to index the partner's travel advisory content."},{"k":"B","html":"Write individual Q&amp;A pairs for each document as separate topics."},{"k":"C","html":"Enable unrestricted web search for the agent."},{"k":"D","html":"Add the internal policy documents as a knowledge source."}],"answer":"AD","type":"multi","votes":[{"a":"AD","p":100,"n":2}],"page":1,"case":"87efe5dfda","thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/c09c4c845fff9031d3a143a906bac5e61007779/","comments":[{"user":"Sweden2022","date":"2026-09-18","up":1,"text":"A. Use a Microsoft Graph connector to index the partner's travel advisory content.\nD. Add the internal policy documents as a knowledge source.","pick":"AD"},{"user":"faisalronnie","date":"2026-08-04","up":1,"text":"Travel Advisory Content: Uses REST API with partner services.> if this is true then A cannot be the option","pick":"AD"}]},{"n":5,"id":1007780,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You need to ensure that every AI-generated response from the agent in Copilot Studio includes a disclaimer that complies with the company's security and governance policies.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which two actions should you perform?</strong> Each correct answer presents part of the solution.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Add a greeting message that includes the disclaimer."},{"k":"B","html":"Add a prompt modification in the generative answers node settings."},{"k":"C","html":"Create a disclaimer topic that always runs first."},{"k":"D","html":"Disable generative answers and use only pre-authored responses."},{"k":"E","html":"Edit every topic's first message to include the disclaimer."}],"answer":"BC","type":"multi","votes":[{"a":"BC","p":100,"n":7}],"page":1,"case":"87efe5dfda","thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/9094fc4d4f7fed84687bd6ac98a482991007780/","comments":[{"user":"Hatsapatsa","date":"2026-07-16","up":5,"text":"I would say 'B and C' because A only runs once, case study requires it to be added to each generative response and therefore a reusable separate topic would be the better option.","pick":"BC"},{"user":"Sweden2022","date":"2026-09-18","up":1,"text":"B. Add a prompt modification in the generative answers node settings.\nC. Create a disclaimer topic that always runs first.","pick":"BC"},{"user":"HelloItsSam","date":"2026-08-29","up":1,"text":"I'd go for B and C, Microsoft cert wordings are always grammatically confused! Now word \"Every\" changes the whole context of this question","pick":"BC"}]},{"n":6,"id":1007781,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You need to determine which authentication model should be applied to each Blue Yonder Copilot interaction scenario to comply with the company's security and governance requirements.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which authentication requirement should you apply to each scenario?</strong> To answer, move the appropriate authentication requirements to the correct user scenarios. You may use each authentication requirement once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to move the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image5.png\" alt=\"image5\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image6.png\" alt=\"image6\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":1,"case":"87efe5dfda","thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/564129bb271e39a533e8327c86cd31e61007781/","comments":[{"user":"harshagracy","date":"2026-10-13","up":1,"text":"A customer asks, \"What is the baggage allowance for international flights?\"\n\nAllow anonymous access. (The case study states: \"Anonymous access for general inquiries (e.g., flight status, baggage policy).\")\n\nA customer asks, \"Can I review my upcoming trips?\"\n\nRequire customer sign-in using an account. (The case study states: \"Authentication is required for personal data access (e.g., bookings, loyalty points).\")\n\nAn internal support agent accesses the Copilot agent from Microsoft Teams to look up a loyalty member's profile.\n\nRequire internal agent sign-in using Microsoft Entra ID. (The case study states: \"Internal staff: Authenticate via Microsoft Entra ID.\")"}]},{"n":7,"id":1007782,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A company has an existing custom connector that is approved and available in the environment. A builder wants an agent in Copilot Studio to call the connector during a conversation to retrieve information from an internal system.</p><p>To meet the business needs, the solution must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>The agent must make the connector available for topic steps.</li><li>The agent must run the connector call with a valid connection.</li><li>The connector call must receive the required input values at runtime.</li></ul><p>You need to configure the agent so the custom connector can be used as a tool.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you configure for each requirement?</strong> To answer, move the appropriate configurations to the correct requirements. You may use each configuration once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to move the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image7.png\" alt=\"image7\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image8.png\" alt=\"image8\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/d24ecfa6b9793552dc0b053b8f02fb891007782/","comments":[]},{"n":8,"id":1007783,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A company needs to ground an agent in Copilot Studio answers using live enterprise data from a supported system via a Microsoft Power Platform connector.</p><p>To meet the business needs, the builder must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Authenticate using a valid connection.</li><li>Add the connector as a real-time knowledge source.</li><li>Select the tables for knowledge grounding.</li></ul><p>You need to add a Power Platform connector as a real-time knowledge source for the agent.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>In which order should you perform the actions?</strong> To answer, move all actions from the list of actions to the answer area and arrange them in the correct order.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image9.png\" alt=\"image9\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image10.png\" alt=\"image10\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/18274e19ed36071f1ca48bd31f147f031007783/","comments":[{"user":"harshagracy","date":"2026-10-13","up":1,"text":"Select Add knowledge from the agent Knowledge experience.\n\nSelect the real-time connector from the Add knowledge dialog.\n\nSelect Sign in and create a new connection or reuse an existing connection.\n\nSelect the tables to include as the knowledge source.\n\nSelect Add to agent to complete the connection."}],"variants":[3]},{"n":9,"id":1007784,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You deploy an agent in Microsoft Copilot Studio that triggers a cloud flow to update customer records in Microsoft Dataverse.</p><p>You observe the following after deploying the agent:</p><ul><li>Several runs fail due to a temporary authentication issue.</li><li>The flow continues to trigger and generate additional failed runs.</li></ul><p>You must:</p><ul><li>Stop additional failed executions while troubleshooting.</li><li>Process a failed execution after resolving the authentication issue.</li><li>Validate if the most recent executions succeeded immediately after resolution.</li></ul><p>You need to use the appropriate monitoring and management actions to restore normal flow operation and validate successful execution.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which action should you perform for each requirement?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image11.png\" alt=\"image11\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image12.png\" alt=\"image12\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/85198468d5d7bd21517060f6ef619a481007784/","comments":[{"user":"madhuece","date":"2026-09-25","up":1,"text":"disable flow, resubmit, review activity history"},{"user":"lucas_0102","date":"2026-07-15","up":1,"text":"Could someone help me understand the logic behind this answer?"}]},{"n":10,"id":1007785,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A company is preparing an agent flow so that it can be invoked by an agent during conversations.</p><p>The agent flow must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>The agent must be able to trigger the flow.</li><li>The agent flow must be verified.</li></ul><p>You need to prepare an agent flow so that it can be used by the agent.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>In which order should you perform the actions to prepare the agent flow?</strong> To answer, move all actions from the list of actions to the answer area and arrange them in the correct order.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image13.png\" alt=\"image13\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image14.png\" alt=\"image14\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/8333808c966648bd2582307a683f90601007785/","comments":[{"user":"harshagracy","date":"2026-10-13","up":1,"text":"Create a new agent flow artifact in the environment.\n\nConfigure the invocation trigger that allows the agent to call the agent flow.\n\nConfigure the actions that implement the required behavior.\n\nValidate the agent flow behavior with representative test runs.\n\nMake the agent flow available for agent usage."},{"user":"Snoopy70","date":"2026-10-11","up":1,"text":"I have found the answer > https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-copilot-studio/advanced-flow-create#create-a-new-agent-flow-from-the-flows-page\nThe order is correct"},{"user":"Snoopy70","date":"2026-10-11","up":1,"text":"Can someone confirm if the provide order is correct? From my view, and checking in my dev env, I configure the action, then I configure the invocation."}]},{"n":11,"id":1007786,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A company uses an agent flow that occasionally requires human input before continuing execution.</p><p>Some automated actions must pause until a human provides a decision or additional information. The flow must be configured to:</p><ul><li>Capture a human response for use in later steps.</li><li>Continue processing within the same flow run after the response is submitted.</li><li>Wait for a manual decision before proceeding.</li></ul><p>You need to configure a human-in-the-loop agent flow.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which setting should you configure for each requirement?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image15.png\" alt=\"image15\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image16.png\" alt=\"image16\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/2e4b0d2dd112705705bb08902b514d691007786/","comments":[]},{"n":12,"id":1007787,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A company uses an agent that invokes an agent flow to exchange information during a conversation.</p><p>The company requires that the agent send data into the flow and receive structured results back from the same flow run. To support this business need, the flow must be configured to do the following:</p><ul><li>Capture the data provided by the agent.</li><li>Return data results to the agent.</li></ul><p>You need to configure the flow so that it can exchange data with the agent.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you configure for each requirement?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image17.png\" alt=\"image17\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image18.png\" alt=\"image18\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/17f66aaaf8eb0a4f4f91f62e94ae1e111007787/","comments":[]},{"n":13,"id":1007788,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You are configuring an agent in Copilot Studio for an organization. The organization uses Microsoft Dataverse, Dynamics 365, and SharePoint Online.</p><p>The agent must retrieve information from enterprise systems and internal documents. The agent must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Must retrieve the current balance of a customer account stored in Dataverse.</li><li>Must retrieve the real-time shipping status of an order that updates throughout the day in Dynamics 365.</li><li>Must answer questions based on the content of a static PDF policy document.</li><li>Must provide a welcome message that does NOT depend on enterprise data.</li></ul><p>You need to configure the agent to meet the requirements.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>How should the agent retrieve the data?</strong> To answer, move the appropriate solutions to the correct requirements. You may use each solution once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to move the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image19.png\" alt=\"image19\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image20.png\" alt=\"image20\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/555eb7909817ab1973735fa20104ea181007788/","comments":[]},{"n":14,"id":1007789,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>An agent calls a flow. The agent requires structured output values to be returned.</p><p>The agent receives unexpected or empty values.</p><p>You need to configure the agent so that data is exchanged correctly between the agent and the flow.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you do?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Validate parameter definitions."},{"k":"B","html":"Change the trigger schema."},{"k":"C","html":"Review the flow run history."},{"k":"D","html":"Add a Parse JSON inside the flow."},{"k":"E","html":"Republish the agent."}],"answer":"A","type":"single","votes":[],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/7fbc1334c5e3eabc7f86ac94ca360b131007789/","comments":[{"user":"faisalronnie","date":"2026-08-04","up":2,"text":"A. Validate parameter definitions ✅\n\nThe problem is about data being exchanged between the agent and the flow. If the agent receives empty or unexpected values, the first thing to check is that:\n\nAgent inputs match flow inputs\nFlow outputs are properly defined\nParameter names and data types match\nReturned values are mapped correctly"},{"user":"lucas_0102","date":"2026-07-16","up":1,"text":"Why is this answer justified? Can someone elaborate?"}]},{"n":15,"id":1007790,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A company is building an agent in Copilot Studio.</p><p>The agent must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Responses must be grounded in approved internal content.</li><li>The agent must be able to retrieve information from configured data sources in a topic.</li></ul><p>You need to configure the agent so that topic responses are grounded from custom data sources.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you configure?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Enable analytics to review which topics users trigger most often."},{"k":"B","html":"Add a custom prompt that tells the agent to answer only from company data."},{"k":"C","html":"Configure knowledge sources in a generative answers node."},{"k":"D","html":"Add SharePoint as a knowledge source only at the agent level."},{"k":"E","html":"Increase the response length limit to improve answer completeness."}],"answer":"C","type":"single","votes":[],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/1342e15d333fbc47a435f0b5532359191007790/","comments":[{"user":"harshagracy","date":"2026-10-13","up":1,"text":"Correct answer: C. Configure knowledge sources in a generative answers node.\n\nWhy? A generative answers node in Copilot Studio allows you to specify the knowledge sources used to ground responses within a particular topic. You can configure approved internal sources and control which sources the node searches.&#x20;\n\n[image](https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=https://learn.microsoft.com\\&sz=32)\n\nMicrosoft Learn\n\n+1\n\nWhy not D? Adding SharePoint only at the agent level configures general knowledge for the agent, but the question specifically requires retrieving configured data sources within a topic.","pick":"C"}]},{"n":16,"id":1007791,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A company is building an agent in Copilot Studio topic that must retrieve real-time status information from an external REST API using a Send HTTP request node.</p><p>To meet the business needs, the topic must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>The request must include the required authentication header.</li><li>The request must call the endpoint using the correct HTTP method.</li><li>The response must be configured with an appropriate response data type based on a schema and saved so the topic can reuse the returned values.</li></ul><p>You need to configure the Send HTTP request node.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which configuration should you use for each requirement?</strong> To answer, move the appropriate configurations to the correct requirements. You may use each configuration once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to move the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image21.png\" alt=\"image21\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image22.png\" alt=\"image22\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/80ef0ac18cfad990da02c4cab22c95241007791/","comments":[]},{"n":17,"id":1007792,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A company is deploying an agent for employees.</p><p>The company has the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Access must be restricted to the internal employees only.</li><li>End-user authentication must be enforced.</li></ul><p>You need to configure the agent based on the company requirements.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you do?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Select Authenticate with Microsoft Entra ID for the agent."},{"k":"B","html":"Enable Require Secure Access in the Web channel security."},{"k":"C","html":"Publish the agent as a public website experience."},{"k":"D","html":"Select Authenticate with personal account for the agent."}],"answer":"A","type":"single","votes":[],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/e528f6c01f3e87c7c55593e27d5e445e1007792/","comments":[{"user":"harshagracy","date":"2026-10-13","up":1,"text":"Correct answer: A. Select Authenticate with Microsoft Entra ID for the agent.\nWhy? Microsoft Entra ID enables employees to authenticate using their organizational accounts. This meets both requirements: restricting access to internal employees and enforcing end-user authentication.\n\nWhy not B? Require Secure Access in Web channel security is not the primary authentication setting asked for here.","pick":"A"},{"user":"lucas_0102","date":"2026-07-16","up":1,"text":"Can someone explain why this answer is correct?"}]},{"n":18,"id":1007793,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A company is integrating an agent in Copilot Studio into a custom application by using the Microsoft 365 Agents SDK.</p><p>The company has the following requirements for the application:</p><ul><li>The deployment workflow must follow a dependency driven sequence.</li><li>The agent must be published before configuration values are retrieved.</li><li>End-to-end validation must occur before production deployment.</li></ul><p>You need to plan the deployment workflow to integrate the agent.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>In which order should you perform the actions?</strong> To answer, move all actions from the list of actions to the answer area and arrange them in the correct order.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image23.png\" alt=\"image23\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image24.png\" alt=\"image24\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/b46497e7cd8e46e94a024dab391dcea01007793/","comments":[{"user":"faisalronnie","date":"2026-07-30","up":5,"text":"Order Action\n1 Publish the agent.\n2 Configure and enable the agent's target integration channel.\n3 Retrieve current agent configuration values.\n4 Implement the Microsoft 365 Agents SDK in the app using the agent configuration.\n5 Validate the end-to-end conversation workflow in a test environment.\n6 Deploy the web app to production."},{"user":"MeshMallow","date":"2026-10-08","up":2,"text":"Order:\n1. Publish the agent.\n2. Configure and enable the agent's target integration channel.\n3. Retrieve current agent configuration values.\n4. Implement the Microsoft 365 Agents SDK in the app using the agent configuration.\n5. Validate the end-to-end conversation workflow in a test environment.\n6. Deploy the web app to production."},{"user":"ageansea","date":"2026-10-06","up":1,"text":"my prefer order is:\n(1)Retrieve the agent's current configuration values.\n(2)Implement the Microsoft 365 Agents SDK in the app using the agent configuration.\n(3)Validate the end-to-end conversation workflow in a test environment.\n(4)Deploy the web app to production.\n(5)Configure and enable the agent's target integration channel.\n(6)Publish the agent.","replies":[{"user":"Wheels","date":"2026-10-16","up":1,"text":"In order to obtain the code for the web app channel, you first need to publish the agent, so publishing is the first step"}]},{"user":"lucas_0102","date":"2026-07-16","up":1,"text":"I'm not following the reasoning—can someone explain?"}]},{"n":19,"id":1007794,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>An agent in Copilot Studio already exists in a development environment.</p><p>You need to prepare the agent so it can be moved to a production environment using the supported solution-based approach.</p><p>You need to create an exportable package that contains the existing agent.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which two actions should you perform?</strong> Each correct answer presents part of the solution.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Remove agent topics directly from the solution to prevent export errors."},{"k":"B","html":"Convert the solution to a managed solution so it can be exported."},{"k":"C","html":"Export the unmanaged solution that contains the agent."},{"k":"D","html":"Publish the agent to a channel and export the channel configuration."},{"k":"E","html":"Create a custom solution and add the existing agent to the solution."}],"answer":"CE","type":"multi","votes":[{"a":"CE","p":100,"n":3}],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/4147e1fadb0a8e28c353c2037a86f7b71007794/","comments":[{"user":"Joselito79","date":"2026-08-28","up":2,"text":"✅ C. Export the unmanaged solution that contains the agent.\n✅ E. Create a custom solution and add the existing agent to the solution.","pick":"CE"},{"user":"faisalronnie","date":"2026-07-27","up":2,"text":"The supported ALM process is:\n\nCreate/Open an unmanaged solution.\nAdd Existing → Copilot Agent to the solution.\nInclude dependencies (flows, connectors, environment variables, etc.).\nExport the unmanaged solution (or later export as managed for production deployment depending on the scenario).","pick":"CE"},{"user":"harshagracy","date":"2026-10-13","up":1,"text":"E. Create a custom solution and add the existing agent to the solution: To use the Application Lifecycle Management (ALM) capabilities of the Power Platform, you must first create a custom unmanaged solution in your development environment and add your existing Copilot Studio agent (along with its required components) into it.\n\nC. Export the unmanaged solution that contains the agent: Once the agent is packaged in your custom solution, you initiate the export process from that unmanaged solution. (During the export wizard, you will choose to export it as a managed package to import into your production environment, but the solution you select to export must be unmanaged).","pick":"CE"},{"user":"blissy","date":"2026-10-10","up":1,"text":"Export managed to Production","pick":"BE"}]},{"n":20,"id":1007795,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A company wants to use content from a non-Microsoft enterprise knowledge base to ground agent responses.</p><p>To meet the business needs, the knowledge source must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Support grounding from indexed data.</li><li>Use existing access controls from the source system.</li><li>Support read-only operations.</li></ul><p>You need to determine the correct behavior to meet the requirements.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which behavior meets each requirement?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image25.png\" alt=\"image25\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image26.png\" alt=\"image26\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/f618a903da5275d45b5ca80edf1f3da71007795/","comments":[]},{"n":21,"id":1007796,"topic":1,"series":true,"stem":"<p>An agent uses a flow that calls an external service which can occasionally fail or time out.</p><p>When a failure occurs, the agent must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Must not terminate silently.</li><li>Must send a notification containing the error details.</li></ul><p>You need to configure the agent flow so that failures are handled in a controlled and predictable way.</p><div class=\"solution\"><span>Proposed solution</span>Retry the failing action without handling failure.</div><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Does the solution meet the goal?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Yes"},{"k":"B","html":"No"}],"answer":"B","type":"yesno","votes":[],"page":3,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/39793ef17a85bbb8f009a2acdbd252c81007796/","comments":[{"user":"harshagracy","date":"2026-10-13","up":1,"text":"Simply retrying the failing action without implementing explicit error handling does not meet the requirement to \"send a notification containing the error details.\" If the retries are exhausted and the action ultimately fails, the flow will terminate without capturing the error context or proactively notifying anyone.","pick":"B"},{"user":"harshagracy","date":"2026-10-13","up":1,"text":"Simply retrying the failing action without implementing explicit error handling does not meet the requirement to \"send a notification containing the error details.\" If the retries are exhausted and the action ultimately fails, the flow will terminate without capturing the error context or proactively notifying anyone.","pick":"B"},{"user":"MeshMallow","date":"2026-10-13","up":1,"text":"First we need to handle the failure condition then retry the failing action","pick":"B"}]},{"n":22,"id":1007797,"topic":1,"series":true,"stem":"<p>An agent uses a flow that calls an external service which can occasionally fail or time out.</p><p>When a failure occurs, the agent must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Must not terminate silently.</li><li>Must send a notification containing the error details.</li></ul><p>You need to configure the agent flow so that failures are handled in a controlled and predictable way.</p><div class=\"solution\"><span>Proposed solution</span>Configure run after conditions for failure paths.</div><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Does the solution meet the goal?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Yes"},{"k":"B","html":"No"}],"answer":"A","type":"yesno","votes":[],"page":3,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/e89810fb3b0e42a466ee6a1dd43910941007797/","comments":[]},{"n":23,"id":1007798,"topic":1,"series":true,"stem":"<p>An agent uses a flow that calls an external service which can occasionally fail or time out.</p><p>When a failure occurs, the agent must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Must not terminate silently.</li><li>Must send a notification containing the error details.</li></ul><p>You need to configure the agent flow so that failures are handled in a controlled and predictable way.</p><div class=\"solution\"><span>Proposed solution</span>Send a notification with relevant error details.</div><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Does the solution meet the goal?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Yes"},{"k":"B","html":"No"}],"answer":"A","type":"yesno","votes":[{"a":"A","p":100,"n":3}],"page":3,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/7f3c5b8e02c12005c9ed685e369031821007798/","comments":[{"user":"faisalronnie","date":"2026-07-30","up":4,"text":"Sending a notification with the error details explicitly alerts someone that the failure occurred, so the failure is not silent, and it also satisfies the requirement to send a notification containing the error details.","pick":"A"}]},{"n":24,"id":1007776,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You need to evaluate whether the current configuration decisions for the Blue Yonder Copilot agent comply with the company's security and governance policies.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which compliance status should you assign to each configuration decision?</strong> To answer, move the appropriate compliance statuses to the correct configuration decisions. You may use each compliance status once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to move the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image3.png\" alt=\"image3\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image4.png\" alt=\"image4\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":3,"case":"87efe5dfda","thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/bc74c24da0f8f53f3007f140761c05491007776/","comments":[{"user":"harshagracy","date":"2026-10-13","up":1,"text":"The agent allows anonymous access general inquiries such as baggage policies.\n\nCompliant (The case study states: \"Anonymous access is allowed for general inquiries.\")\n\nThe agent uses an open web search to answer questions beyond internal knowledge.\n\nNon-compliant (The case study requires the agent to be grounded in specific enterprise systems and knowledge sources, not open web search, which violates data protection and RAI standards.)\n\nThe team relies only on default content filters without custom RAI instructions.\n\nNon-compliant (The case study states: \"Prompt modifications must be added to enforce tone, disclaimers, and refusal behavior.\")\n\nThe agent uses one shared admin credential for all internal data access.\n\nNon-compliant (The case study explicitly states: \"User identity must be used for data access; shared or builder credentials must not be used.\")"},{"user":"JamesM9","date":"2026-09-24","up":1,"text":"Compliant: Anonymous access for general inquiries.\n\nNon compliant: Open web search; default filters without custom RAI instructions; shared admin credential.\n\nThe case explicitly permits anonymous access for general inquiries, while requiring authenticated, user-specific identity for personal/internal data access and additional RAI controls."},{"user":"Sweden2022","date":"2026-09-17","up":1,"text":"The agent allows anonymous access for general inquiries such as baggage policies — Compliant\nThe agent uses an open web search to answer questions beyond internal knowledge — Non-compliant\nThe team relies only on default content filters without custom RAI instructions — Non-compliant\nThe agent uses one shared admin credential for all internal data access — Non-compliant"},{"user":"lucas_0102","date":"2026-07-16","up":1,"text":"I'm struggling with this—why is this the correct answer?"}]},{"n":25,"id":1007777,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You need to deploy the Blue Yonder Copilot agent to the public website and Microsoft Teams while ensuring compliance with the company's security and Responsible AI requirements.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which two actions should you perform before making the agent available on both channels?</strong> Each correct answer presents part of the solution.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Configure prompt modifications to enforce tone, disclaimers, and refusal behavior at the system level."},{"k":"B","html":"Manually add disclaimers to each topic before publishing."},{"k":"C","html":"Embed the web channel and then rely on channel-level settings to enforce content moderation."},{"k":"D","html":"Configure Power Platform DLP policies to restrict unauthorized data connectors."},{"k":"E","html":"Publish the agent and then enable Responsible AI filters individually for each channel."}],"answer":"AD","type":"multi","votes":[{"a":"AD","p":100,"n":4}],"page":3,"case":"87efe5dfda","thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/3fc586c297dfbaaaea084e5f978f799f1007777/","comments":[{"user":"690471c","date":"2026-07-17","up":2,"text":"las políticas DLP de Power Platform permiten bloquear conectores, canales o fuentes de datos no autorizados. Es una medida esencial antes de publicar un agente conectado a sistemas empresariales.","pick":"AD"},{"user":"harshagracy","date":"2026-10-13","up":1,"text":"A. Configure prompt modifications to enforce tone, disclaimers, and refusal behavior at the system level: The case study requirements explicitly mandate that \"Prompt modifications must be added to enforce tone, disclaimers, and refusal behavior\" and that \"Manual edits to individual topics must be avoided.\" Configuring these at the system or agent level (e.g., in the generative AI settings) ensures consistent compliance across all generated outputs without requiring per-topic changes.\n\nD. Configure Power Platform DLP policies to restrict unauthorized data connectors: The compliance and security requirements dictate that \"Power Platform DLP policies must be enforced to block unauthorized data flows.\" These policies govern which connectors (such as external APIs or internal systems) the agent can use, ensuring data security before the agent is exposed on public or internal channels.","pick":"AD"},{"user":"msrao83","date":"2026-09-29","up":1,"text":"A: Configure prompt modifications to enforce tone, disclaimers, and refusal behavior at the system level.\nD: Configure Power Platform DLP","pick":"A"},{"user":"Sweden2022","date":"2026-09-17","up":1,"text":"A. Configure prompt modifications to enforce tone, disclaimers, and refusal behavior at the system level.\nD. Configure Power Platform DLP policies to restrict unauthorized data connectors.","pick":"AD"},{"user":"moodin","date":"2026-08-03","up":1,"text":"Brief states \"Power Platform DLP policies must be enforced to block unauthorized data flows.\" Additionally, E is configuring per-channel rather than system level, bad practice.","pick":"AD"}]},{"n":26,"id":1007778,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You need to configure the Blue Yonder Copilot agent's responses in accordance with the company's content control and platform requirements.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which two actions should you perform?</strong> Each correct answer presents part of the solution.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Add required disclaimer text inside each individual topic."},{"k":"B","html":"Configure prompt instructions that include disclaimer text."},{"k":"C","html":"Use Markdown syntax within response content."},{"k":"D","html":"Insert HTML formatting directly into topic responses."},{"k":"E","html":"Duplicate disclaimer text across reusable topics."}],"answer":"BC","type":"multi","votes":[{"a":"BC","p":100,"n":3}],"page":3,"case":"87efe5dfda","thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/6bf67fef559b386ab1ed22be1a5e29fe1007778/","comments":[{"user":"moodin","date":"2026-08-03","up":2,"text":"\"Disclaimers must be applied consistently across all generative responses\" for B, and \"Markdown must be used for formatting (e.g., bold, bullet points); HTML is not supported\" for C","pick":"BC"},{"user":"MeshMallow","date":"2026-10-13","up":1,"text":"B. Configure prompt instructions that include disclaimer text. Putting the disclaimer in the agent's instructions applies it consistently to every response from one central place. This meets the content control requirement without editing each topic.\n\nC. Use Markdown syntax within response content. Copilot Studio's message formatting supports Markdown across channels, so it's the platform-appropriate way to format responses.","pick":"BC"},{"user":"Sweden2022","date":"2026-09-17","up":1,"text":"B. Configure prompt instructions that include disclaimer text.\nC. Use Markdown syntax within response content.","pick":"BC"}]},{"n":27,"id":1021099,"topic":1,"series":true,"stem":"<p>An agent uses a flow that calls an external service which can occasionally fail or time out.</p><p>When a failure occurs, the agent must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Must not terminate silently.</li><li>Must send a notification containing the error details.</li></ul><p>You need to configure the agent flow so that failures are handled in a controlled and predictable way.</p><div class=\"solution\"><span>Proposed solution</span>Terminate the flow immediately on error.</div><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Does the solution meet the goal?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Yes"},{"k":"B","html":"No"}],"answer":"B","type":"yesno","votes":[],"page":3,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/954ba648750c46ffb97e56fd6a04478b1021099/","comments":[{"user":"MeshMallow","date":"2026-10-13","up":1,"text":"Terminating the flow immediately on error fails both requirements.","pick":"B"}]},{"n":28,"id":1021100,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A company requires an agent in Copilot Studio to answer questions using content stored in a third-party knowledge base system and reuse that content for knowledge grounding.</p><p>The agent must ground answers using indexed enterprise knowledge from a non-Microsoft system.</p><p>You need to choose the correct integration approach.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you use?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Call the third-party API from a topic for each question."},{"k":"B","html":"Add a Copilot Studio tool as a real-time knowledge source."},{"k":"C","html":"Add a Copilot Studio tool and call it from a topic."},{"k":"D","html":"Add a Copilot connector knowledge source for authorized content."}],"answer":"D","type":"single","votes":[],"page":3,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/eca5d0fed2b46b2ab022228e9a538ce91021100/","comments":[{"user":"MeshMallow","date":"2026-10-13","up":1,"text":"D. Add a Copilot connector knowledge source for authorized content.","pick":"D"}]},{"n":29,"id":1021101,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A company uses a supported Power Platform connector to provide real-time access to enterprise records for knowledge grounding in an agent in Copilot Studio.</p><p>To meet the business needs, the knowledge source must provide the following functionality:</p><ul><li>Avoid copying enterprise data into an index.</li><li>Keep source-system access controls enforced.</li><li>Access data by calling the system at runtime.</li></ul><p>You need to configure the connector knowledge source.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you configure for each requirement?</strong> To answer, move the appropriate configurations to the correct requirements. You may use each configuration once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to move the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image95.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image96.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":3,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/88833327267faf696658037fc2c9cd7e1021101/","comments":[{"user":"harshagracy","date":"2026-10-13","up":1,"text":"Avoid copying enterprise data into an index.Retrieve data without indexing. (By fetching data on demand, you avoid duplicating or indexing enterprise data in Copilot Studio's storage). Keep source-system access controls enforced.Use existing permissions. (The connector uses the authenticated user's credentials to execute the query, ensuring that users only receive data they are authorized to see in the source system). Access data by calling the system at runtime.Use real-time connector. (A real-time connector executes queries directly against the external system's API the moment a user asks a question, rather than relying on a pre-synced database)."},{"user":"MeshMallow","date":"2026-10-13","up":1,"text":"1. Avoid copying enterprise data into an index. -> Retrieve data without indexing.\n2. Keep source-system access controls enforced. -> Use existing permissions.\n3. Access data by calling the system at runtime. -> Use real-time connector."}]},{"n":30,"id":1021102,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A tenant administrator configures a Copilot connector that indexes content from an external knowledge system into Microsoft Graph.</p><p>A builder is building an agent that must:</p><ul><li>Use the indexed enterprise knowledge during answer generation.</li><li>Avoid duplicating or manually uploading the same content.</li><li>Avoid invoking the system as a transactional tool.</li></ul><p>You need to configure the agent so that responses are grounded in the authorized knowledge sources.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you do?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Add the configured enterprise knowledge source to the agent’s knowledge."},{"k":"B","html":"Create a new custom connector inside the agent configuration."},{"k":"C","html":"Add the connector as a tool and invoke it from a topic."},{"k":"D","html":"Upload documents from the external system directly into the agent’s file knowledge store."}],"answer":"A","type":"single","votes":[],"page":3,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/c5b343908a1afbacde32b9048558ca521021102/","comments":[{"user":"MeshMallow","date":"2026-10-13","up":2,"text":"A. Add the configured enterprise knowledge source to the agent’s knowledge.\nThe tenant admin has already set up a Copilot connector that indexes the external content into Microsoft Graph. The builder only needs to add that existing knowledge source to the agent, so responses are grounded in the indexed, permission-trimmed content. This satisfies all three requirements.","pick":"A"}]},{"n":31,"id":1021103,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A solution containing an agent in Copilot Studio is deployed to multiple environments that require different configuration values.</p><p>Configuration values must vary by environment without modifying the solution contents.</p><p>Configuration values must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Allow values to be set during import.</li><li>Exclude values from the agent definition.</li><li>Run a dedicated agent instance for each individual environment.</li></ul><p>You need to associate each requirement with the configuration approach.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you configure for each requirement?</strong> To answer, move the appropriate configurations to the correct requirements. You may use each configuration once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to move the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image97.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image98.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":4,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/34b7a843b9d5cd7a149d0ae4861503571021103/","comments":[{"user":"Snoopy70","date":"2026-10-13","up":1,"text":"for me the correct answers are:\nEnvironment variables\nEnvironment variables\nagent deployed through a solution to each environment"}]},{"n":32,"id":1021104,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A team uses environment variables to separate configuration from an agent so that the same solution can be moved between environments.</p><p>The team requires the following scenarios to be addressed:</p><ul><li>An administrator updates a sensitive configuration value and needs the change to take effect at runtime without republishing the agent.</li><li>A builder needs to confirm a configuration value but must not be able to modify it from Copilot Studio.</li><li>An administrator updates a non-secret configuration value and needs the updated value to be used by the published agent at runtime.</li></ul><p>You need to apply the correct handling behavior for different environment-variable scenarios.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which behavior should you apply for each scenario?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image99.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image100.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":4,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/7f14bc3a0c3ad4f2fd06667674beed761021104/","comments":[]},{"n":33,"id":1021105,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A company is configuring an agent flow that uses multiple action types to perform operations and process data.</p><p>The flow must be configured as follows:</p><ul><li>An HTTP action must connect to an external service.</li><li>A data action must reference the correct data to process.</li></ul><p>You need to configure the settings for each action type.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which setting should you configure for each action?</strong> To answer, move the appropriate configuration settings to the correct actions. You may use each configuration setting once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to move the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image101.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image102.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":4,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/3abcae3066347ef7c23d04308b1e9b2f1021105/","comments":[]},{"n":34,"id":1021106,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A company has agents in Copilot Studio.</p><p>The company needs to prevent the agents from using disallowed connectors and insecure data flows. Administrators must be able to enforce the governance controls to prevent and report violations.</p><p>You need to enforce governance controls for agents.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you do?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Configure Application Insights to collect runtime telemetry."},{"k":"B","html":"Review security FAQs to understand default protections."},{"k":"C","html":"Review agent analytics to detect risky connector usage."},{"k":"D","html":"Configure data policies."}],"answer":"D","type":"single","votes":[],"page":4,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/a229a30edae66a600b5a062978dce4af1021106/","comments":[]},{"n":35,"id":1021107,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A company is designing an agent flow that includes human in the loop stages during execution.</p><p>The company requires that the agent flow perform the following actions:</p><ul><li>Must wait for a human decision before it resumes.</li><li>Must collect information and then continue execution.</li></ul><p>You need to configure the flow behavior.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which flow behavior should you configure for each stage?</strong> To answer, move the appropriate flow behaviors to the correct stages. You may use each flow behavior once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to move the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image103.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image104.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":4,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/f2159dd4e3e95c0fbb01debf8d015c571021107/","comments":[]},{"n":36,"id":1021108,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A company is building an agent topic in Copilot Studio. The agent topic uses a generative answers node to respond to user questions based on authorized knowledge sources.</p><p>To meet the business needs, the generative answers node must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Use the user’s message in the generative answers node.</li><li>Scope the topic node to query only designated data.</li><li>Restrict responses to approved enterprise data.</li></ul><p>You need to configure the generative answers node to meet the requirements.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you configure for each requirement?</strong> To answer, move the appropriate configurations to the correct requirements. You may use each configuration once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to move the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image105.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image106.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":4,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/684f850da2a9180f2b2bab1f3b78d0c41021108/","comments":[]},{"n":37,"id":1021109,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A company is building an agent topic in Copilot Studio.</p><p>The topic must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Collect structured user input in a single step.</li><li>Store the submitted values for use later in the conversation.</li></ul><p>You need to configure the topic based on the requirements.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which two actions should you perform?</strong> Each correct answer presents part of the solution.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Use the latest Adaptive Card schema version in all channels to ensure full feature support."},{"k":"B","html":"Paste the card JSON into a Message node to collect the user’s response."},{"k":"C","html":"Add input fields to the card and include an Action.Submit button."},{"k":"D","html":"Add an Ask with Adaptive Card node to the topic."},{"k":"E","html":"Use Action.Execute for the button so the card can run commands across channels."}],"answer":"CD","type":"multi","votes":[],"page":4,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/603b1285a52a1f8443814223c5ec383a1021109/","comments":[]},{"n":38,"id":1007799,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>You need to implement tool usage in topics that meet the Blue Yonder design and governance requirements.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which implementation method should you use for each requirement?</strong> To answer, move the appropriate implementation methods to the correct requirements. You may use each implementation method once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to move the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image27.png\" alt=\"image27\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image28.png\" alt=\"image28\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":4,"case":"87efe5dfda","thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/2aabe45cdf7531d5e2de7f801b3ad0311007799/","comments":[{"user":"faisalronnie","date":"2026-07-29","up":9,"text":"Let the agent decide when to run a tool based on user input. → Enable generative orchestration\nRun a specific agent flow at a defined step in a topic. → Add a tool node\nUse a connector action to retrieve data during a conversation. → Add a tool node","top":true},{"user":"Joselito79","date":"2026-09-06","up":1,"text":"✅ Enable generative orchestration\n\nWhy?\nGenerative orchestration allows Copilot Studio to determine which tool to use and when, based on what the user asks.\n✅ Add a tool node\n\nWhy?\nA tool node is used when the topic author wants to explicitly tell the topic:\n\n✅ Add a tool node\n\nWhy?\nA connector action can be exposed as a tool, and a tool node lets you invoke that action from the topic."}]},{"n":39,"id":1007833,"topic":2,"series":true,"stem":"<p>A company is configuring an agent in Copilot Studio that uses a generative answers node inside multiple topics.</p><p>The company requires responses to meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Must use an executive summary format.</li><li>Must apply only within a specific topic.</li><li>Must continue using configured knowledge sources.</li><li>Must comply with connector security controls.</li></ul><p>You need to configure a custom prompt to meet the formatting requirements.</p><div class=\"solution\"><span>Proposed solution</span>Remove the generative answers node and rely only on the custom prompt to produce formatted responses.</div><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Does the solution meet the goal?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Yes"},{"k":"B","html":"No"}],"answer":"B","type":"yesno","votes":[],"page":4,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/5d10ea1c7cbc310fa5daa60df465809d1007833/","comments":[]},{"n":40,"id":1007800,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>You need to determine how the agent in Copilot Studio should integrate with two different systems in the Blue Yonder environment, based on their characteristics and the tools available.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which integration mechanism should you use for each system?</strong> To answer, move the appropriate integrations to the correct system or data sources. You may use each integration once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to move the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image29.png\" alt=\"image29\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image30.png\" alt=\"image30\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":4,"case":"87efe5dfda","thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/63fc85df8f7ee1e9d63e08a96509c83d1007800/","comments":[]},{"n":41,"id":1007801,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>You need to determine an appropriate implementation related to the use of agent flows that is based on Blue Yonder's design and compliance standards.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which implementation method should you use for each scenario?</strong> To answer, move the appropriate implementation methods to the correct scenarios. You may use each implementation method once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to move the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image31.png\" alt=\"image31\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image32.png\" alt=\"image32\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":5,"case":"87efe5dfda","thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/cf10bf37a7a3b2f28e303a5ee21766ed1007801/","comments":[{"user":"faisalronnie","date":"2026-08-10","up":2,"text":"Scenario Implementation method\nA topic includes a series of steps that replicate logic already defined in another flow. Use a tool node.\nA topic provides a natural language explanation of a process but does not execute it. Use a generative answers node.\nA topic includes a step that triggers a reusable process to update booking details. Use a tool node."}]},{"n":42,"id":1007802,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>You need to enable Operations Concierge to delegate shipment tracking inquiries according to Fabrikam Inc.'s defined architecture and technical requirements.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which integration approach should you use?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Configure the partner capability as an enterprise knowledge source with indexed retrieval enabled."},{"k":"B","html":"Configure the partner capability as an MCP tool and invoke it as a transactional operation."},{"k":"C","html":"Configure the partner capability as an A2A integration and supply its endpoint information."},{"k":"D","html":"Configure the primary agent to handle shipment tracking through generative responses after publishing."}],"answer":"C","type":"single","votes":[],"page":5,"case":"cd9e9dfedc","thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/831342fb63a85c3104a95af65e08bfe91007802/","comments":[]},{"n":43,"id":1007803,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>You need to integrate Fabrikam Inc.'s existing Foundry agent so Operations Concierge can delegate summarization requests.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which action should you perform for each requirement?</strong> To answer, move the appropriate actions to the correct requirements. You may use each action once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to move the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image33.png\" alt=\"image33\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image34.png\" alt=\"image34\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":5,"case":"cd9e9dfedc","thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/8421eddfe1e81f395c7e2f434dfbe5e81007803/","comments":[]},{"n":44,"id":1007804,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>You need to plan how Fabrikam Inc. will reuse shared components across multiple agents while limiting who can change the shared components.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which approach should you use for each requirement?</strong> To answer, move the appropriate components to the correct requirements. You may use each component once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to move the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image35.png\" alt=\"image35\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image36.png\" alt=\"image36\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":5,"case":"cd9e9dfedc","thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/6d0461cbcafc45ffc80ea390644b20f51007804/","comments":[]},{"n":45,"id":1007805,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>You need to configure Operations Concierge so that prompt-driven summarization behavior aligns with Fabrikam Inc.'s architectural requirements.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which two actions should you perform?</strong> Each correct answer presents part of the solution.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Configure Azure AI Search as the grounding source for summarization prompts."},{"k":"B","html":"Publish the agent to ensure the selected model is enforced for summarization."},{"k":"C","html":"Select a model from the Foundry model catalog in the custom prompt configuration."},{"k":"D","html":"Enable citations to control how summarization output is generated."},{"k":"E","html":"Create a reusable custom prompt template and apply it where summarization responses are generated."}],"answer":"CE","type":"multi","votes":[{"a":"CE","p":100,"n":1}],"page":5,"case":"cd9e9dfedc","thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/b211e22be2cc14ef228143e6d99703dc1007805/","comments":[{"user":"Joselito79","date":"2026-09-06","up":1,"text":"The correct answers are:\n\n✅ C. Select a model from the Foundry model catalog in the custom prompt configuration.\n✅ E. Create a reusable custom prompt template and apply it where summarization responses are generated.\nWhy?\n\nC — Select a Foundry model\nThe case explicitly says Fabrikam already has a Microsoft Foundry agent for specialized summarization and classification. The requirement is for prompt-driven summarization to use an approved model from the Foundry model catalog.\n\nE — Reusable custom prompt template\nThe company wants reusable, maintainable behavior across its agents. A custom prompt template provides consistent instructions for how summarization should be performed and can be applied wherever those summarization responses are generated.","pick":"CE"}]},{"n":46,"id":1007806,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>You need to connect Operations Concierge to Fabrikam Inc.'s Azure AI Search knowledge index while complying with security requirements.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which configuration should you use for each requirement?</strong> To answer, move the appropriate configurations to the correct requirements. You may use each configuration once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to move the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image37.png\" alt=\"image37\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image38.png\" alt=\"image38\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":5,"case":"cd9e9dfedc","thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/02fcfccb1f2cf02e4629697329d3c9111007806/","comments":[{"user":"massnonn","date":"2026-09-01","up":3,"text":"Ensure the Azure AI Search connection complies with the governance requirement for authenticated access: Select the service principal as the authentication type.\n\nEnsure policy and procedure Q&A uses the required curated, indexed enterprise knowledge source: Enter the name of the Azure AI Search index.\n\nEnsure the connection targets the Azure AI Search service instance that stores the indexed policy documents: Provide the Azure AI Search Endpoint URL in the connection details."},{"user":"faisalronnie","date":"2026-08-03","up":3,"text":"RequirementConfigurationEnsure the Azure AI Search connection complies with the governance requirement for authenticated access.Select the service principal as the authentication type.Ensure policy and procedure Q&A uses the required curated, indexed enterprise knowledge source.Enter the name of the Azure AI Search index.Ensure the connection targets the Azure AI Search service instance that stores the indexed policy documents.Provide the Azure AI Search Endpoint URL in the connection details."}]},{"n":47,"id":1007807,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>A company is building a Copilot Studio solution that must answer policy questions, retrieve operational metrics from structured data, and execute authenticated updates in backend systems. The company decides to use multiple specialized agents rather than a single monolithic agent. Custom agents for each action already exist.</p><p>To meet the business needs, the solution must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>The solution must retrieve up to date metrics from structured data.</li><li>The solution must answer policy questions using curated knowledge.</li><li>The solution must execute authenticated updates during conversations.</li></ul><p>You need to select the appropriate agent design for each requirement.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which approach should you use for each requirement?</strong> To answer, move the appropriate configurations to the correct requirements. You may use each configuration once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to move the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image39.png\" alt=\"image39\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image40.png\" alt=\"image40\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":5,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/1108ecf1fb44f464ae2826a07b48f8ac1007807/","comments":[{"user":"faisalronnie","date":"2026-07-28","up":9,"text":"should it not be:\nRetrieve up-to-date metrics → Delegate to a data-access agent\nAnswer policy questions → Delegate to a knowledge-focused agent\nExecute authenticated updates → Delegate to a tools-first agent","top":true}]},{"n":48,"id":1007808,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>A company has an approved custom connector that uses a REST API for an internal system.</p><p>An agent in Copilot Studio must call this connector during conversations to retrieve or update data.</p><p>To meet the business needs, the solution must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Make the connector actions available for the agent to invoke.</li><li>Ensure authentication is handled at the service level, not per user.</li><li>Pass conversation context into the connector when it is called.</li><li>Surface the returned data of the connector to the user in the conversation.</li></ul><p>You need to configure the agent and the connector action to meet the requirements.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you configure for each requirement?</strong> To answer, move the appropriate configurations to the correct requirements. You may use each configuration once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to move the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image41.png\" alt=\"image41\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image42.png\" alt=\"image42\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":5,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/a7de4dfc02a1364230786ec3bdb3be541007808/","comments":[]},{"n":49,"id":1007809,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>A company has an Azure AI Search vector index that contains enterprise content and wants to use it as a knowledge source for an agent in Copilot Studio.</p><p>To meet business needs, the knowledge source must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>The agent must connect to the Azure AI Search service.</li><li>The agent must use a supported authentication method for the connection.</li><li>The agent must ensure answers are grounded using the specified Azure AI Search index.</li></ul><p>You need to connect to Azure AI Search as a knowledge source for the agent.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>In which order should you perform the actions?</strong> To answer, move all actions from the list of actions to the answer area and arrange them in the correct order.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image43.png\" alt=\"image43\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image44.png\" alt=\"image44\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":5,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/aa481805bf40fcc5afc4a353367e82c61007809/","comments":[{"user":"massnonn","date":"2026-09-06","up":2,"text":"1️⃣ Initiate the process to add a knowledge source to the agent\n2️⃣ Create a new Azure AI Search connection\n3️⃣ Configure the authentication method and provide the required connection details\n4️⃣ Specify the Azure AI Search index to use for grounding\n5️⃣ Associate the configured knowledge source with the agent"}]},{"n":50,"id":1007810,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>A company uses a primary agent in Copilot Studio to handle user intake.</p><p>For some requests, the company wants the primary agent to delegate work to another Copilot Studio agent that already exists.</p><p>To meet the business needs, the solution must allow agents to perform the following on the connected agent:</p><ul><li>Must allow calls from other agents.</li><li>Must allow agents to use the connected agent for collaboration.</li><li>Must allow agents to invoke the connected agent in conversations.</li></ul><p>You need to integrate the existing Copilot Studio agent with the connected agent.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which setting should you configure for each requirement?</strong> To answer, move the appropriate configurations to the correct requirements. You may use each configuration once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to move the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image45.png\" alt=\"image45\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image46.png\" alt=\"image46\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":5,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/9cab69566da53bd8d67ec062cf12d4311007810/","comments":[{"user":"faisalronnie","date":"2026-08-03","up":2,"text":"RequirementConfigurationMust allow calls from other agentsPublish the connected agentMust allow agents to use the connected agent for collaborationConfigure connections to the connected agentMust allow agents to invoke the connected agent in conversationsAdd the connected agent"},{"user":"massnonn","date":"2026-08-31","up":1,"text":"Requirement Configuration\nMust allow calls from other agents: Publish the connected agent.\nMust allow agents to use the connected agent for collaboration: Add the connected agent.\nMust allow agents to invoke the connected agent in conversations: Configure connections to the connected agent."}]},{"n":51,"id":1007811,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>A company uses multiple Copilot Studio agents that perform specialized tasks.</p><p>The company needs to enable one agent to directly delegate and invoke another agent within Copilot Studio by using a standard Copilot Studio interface.</p><p>You need to configure collaboration among agents by using Copilot Studio.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you do?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Add the target agent as a Microsoft Fabric Data Agent."},{"k":"B","html":"Provide A2A endpoint information for the target agent."},{"k":"C","html":"Upload documentation about the target agent for referencing."},{"k":"D","html":"Add the target agent as an indexed knowledge source."}],"answer":"B","type":"single","votes":[],"page":6,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/edccd92b249c911a34fe2095f380c6081007811/","comments":[]},{"n":52,"id":1007812,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>A company uses an agent in Copilot Studio that produces structured responses using a reusable instruction template. The responses follow the required tone and format. During a compliance review, the team discovers that the responses were generated using a model that is not on the approved list.</p><p>The company requires that the reusable instruction template continues to be used and the model used for prompt-driven responses meets governance requirements.</p><p>The solution must ensure that prompt-driven responses are generated using an approved model.</p><p>You need to configure the solution that meets the requirements.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which two actions should you perform?</strong> Each correct answer presents part of the solution.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Publish the agent so that the model used by prompt-driven responses is updated automatically."},{"k":"B","html":"Enable citations so generated responses can be traced and comply with governance requirements."},{"k":"C","html":"Add a line to the instruction template that requires the agent to use only approved models when generating responses."},{"k":"D","html":"Configure Azure AI Search as the grounding source so the approved model requirement is enforced during response generation."},{"k":"E","html":"Ensure the reusable instruction template is the one applied to the agent that generates the structured response."}],"answer":"AE","type":"multi","votes":[{"a":"CE","p":100,"n":2}],"page":6,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/b3b1a1f03b2e9bbe5be7a59454c485ac1007812/","comments":[{"user":"Joselito79","date":"2026-09-06","up":1,"text":"The correct answers are:\n\nC. Add a line to the instruction template that requires the agent to use only approved models when generating responses. ✅\nE. Ensure the reusable instruction template is the one applied to the agent that generates the structured response. ✅\n\nWhy: The reusable instruction template must remain in use, and adding the model-governance instruction ensures prompt-driven responses are directed to approved models. Citations, grounding, or publishing do not enforce the approved-model requirement.","pick":"CE"},{"user":"massnonn","date":"2026-09-02","up":1,"text":"it' the correct answer","pick":"CE"}],"variants":[2]},{"n":53,"id":1007813,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>A team has an agent in Copilot Studio that handles user intake. For some requests, the team wants the agent to delegate work to a Microsoft Foundry agent that performs specialized processing. The Foundry agent already exists.</p><p>To meet the business needs, the solution must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>The primary agent must be able to call the Foundry agent.</li><li>The external agent connection must reference the correct Foundry project and agent.</li></ul><p>You need to integrate the primary agent with the Foundry agent.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which two actions should you take?</strong> Each correct answer presents part of the solution.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Add an external agent."},{"k":"B","html":"Configure the Copilot Studio endpoint URL."},{"k":"C","html":"Configure the project endpoint URL."},{"k":"D","html":"Add an indexed knowledge source."},{"k":"E","html":"Publish the Copilot Studio agent."}],"answer":"AC","type":"multi","votes":[],"page":6,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/f9b4435e5b9d81e50608c707fcbf5c0f1007813/","comments":[]},{"n":54,"id":1007814,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>A company must enable an agent in Copilot Studio to execute operations exposed by an external MCP server.</p><p>The MCP server publishes callable tools and requires authentication.</p><p>The agent must be able to invoke MCP tools during conversations.</p><p>You need to configure MCP tools so the agent can execute MCP tool calls.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you do?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Upload documentation about the MCP server so the agent can answer questions about it."},{"k":"B","html":"Enable generative answers so the model can automatically invoke MCP tools."},{"k":"C","html":"Publish the agent and rely on default settings for tool availability."},{"k":"D","html":"Add the MCP server to the agent's tool configuration."}],"answer":"D","type":"single","votes":[],"page":6,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/5dc0cc29e9d74e254049c9ab71407a5b1007814/","comments":[],"variants":[66]},{"n":55,"id":1007815,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>A company needs an agent to answer questions using live enterprise records and to execute a limited set of operations in the same system.</p><p>To meet the business needs, the agent must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>The agent must update a record using authenticated access.</li><li>The agent must answer questions using live data at runtime.</li><li>The agent must avoid indexing enterprise data into a search index.</li></ul><p>You need to select the correct Power Platform connector approach for each requirement.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which option should you use for each requirement?</strong> To answer, move the appropriate solutions to the correct requirements. You may use each solution once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to move the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image47.png\" alt=\"image47\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image48.png\" alt=\"image48\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":6,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/b485e23758717d30c71d6b340d23cf611007815/","comments":[{"user":"faisalronnie","date":"2026-07-28","up":7,"text":"RequirementCorrect solutionThe agent must update a record using authenticated access.Power Platform connector toolThe agent must answer questions using live data at runtime.Power Platform connector as real-time knowledgeThe agent must avoid indexing enterprise data into a search index.Power Platform connector as real-time knowledge","top":true},{"user":"massnonn","date":"2026-08-31","up":1,"text":"The agent must update a record using authenticated access: Power Platform connector tool.\nThe agent must answer questions using live data at runtime: Power Platform connector as real-time knowledge.\nThe agent must avoid indexing enterprise data into a search index: Power Platform connector as real-time knowledge."}]},{"n":56,"id":1007816,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>A company uses an agent in Copilot Studio to coordinate user interactions.</p><p>The company wants the agent to delegate requests to a Microsoft Fabric Data Agent that accesses governed business data.</p><p>The agent must retrieve structured analytical data while enforcing data security and scope controls.</p><p>You need to select the integration approach that meets the requirements.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you use?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"A Microsoft Fabric Data Agent and bind it to the model."},{"k":"B","html":"A REST API action that queries Fabric tables directly."},{"k":"C","html":"A Power Automate flow and call it from a topic."},{"k":"D","html":"A Copilot connector knowledge source that indexes Fabric data."}],"answer":"A","type":"single","votes":[],"page":6,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/34cd08bfc0930f8327a014adf6a65a2b1007816/","comments":[]},{"n":57,"id":1007817,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>A company is building an agent in Copilot Studio that must answer questions using enterprise systems and must also perform authenticated operations.</p><p>To meet the business needs, the agent must meet the following requirements.</p><p>The agent must provide searchable answers from indexed enterprise content.</p><p>The agent must retrieve up-to-date facts at runtime without indexing data.</p><p>The agent must perform an authenticated update operation during the conversation.</p><p>You need to select the correct integration approach for each requirement.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which option should you use for each requirement?</strong> To answer, move the appropriate solutions to the correct requirements. You may use each solution once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to move the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image49.png\" alt=\"image49\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image50.png\" alt=\"image50\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":6,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/05eff27d41e39bd40ccaeee855a01f551007817/","comments":[]},{"n":58,"id":1007818,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>A company is extending agents in Copilot Studio with both external capabilities and enterprise content access. Some user requests require grounded answers, while other requests require executing actions.</p><p>To meet the business needs, the agent must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Ground answers using results from enterprise data.</li><li>Invoke callable functions exposed through a standardized tool interface.</li><li>Write an update to a system by using an authenticated action during the conversation.</li></ul><p>You need to integrate the correct approach to meet the requirements.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you integrate for each requirement?</strong> To answer, move the appropriate integrations to the correct requirements. You may use each integration once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to move the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image51.png\" alt=\"image51\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image52.png\" alt=\"image52\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":6,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/5a14b8176858f195c618ec11082d5c3c1007818/","comments":[{"user":"massnonn","date":"2026-09-01","up":2,"text":"Ground answers using results from enterprise data: Add a Copilot connector knowledge source for indexed content.\n\nInvoke callable functions exposed through a standardized tool interface: Connect to an MCP server and add its tools to the agent.\n\nWrite an update to a system by using an authenticated action during the conversation: Add a Power Platform connector tool and call it from a topic."},{"user":"kevinirl","date":"2026-08-08","up":1,"text":"Ground answers using results from enterprise data → Add Dataverse tables as a structured data knowledge source."}]},{"n":59,"id":1007819,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>A company plans to use Copilot connectors to ground answers from a third-party system for an agent in Copilot Studio.</p><p>To meet the business needs, responsibilities for configuring and using Copilot connectors must be separated, based on the following requirements:</p><ul><li>For tenant administration, the connector must be available at the tenant level.</li><li>For agent runtime behavior, answers must be grounded from authorized sources.</li><li>For builder configuration, you must add the connector to the agent.</li></ul><p>You need to determine how Copilot connector set-up responsibilities are handled across tenant, runtime, and builder stages.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you configure for each requirement?</strong> To answer, move the appropriate configuration to the correct requirements. You may use each configuration once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to move the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image53.png\" alt=\"image53\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image54.png\" alt=\"image54\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":6,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/f0dd243b1b42abc51063f5d98dd900221007819/","comments":[{"user":"faisalronnie","date":"2026-07-28","up":6,"text":"Tenant administrationConfigure the Copilot connector in Microsoft 365 Admin CenterAgent runtime behaviorCall the connector knowledge sourceBuilder configurationAdd the Copilot connector as a knowledge source"},{"user":"massnonn","date":"2026-08-31","up":1,"text":"Tenant administration: Configure the Copilot connector in Microsoft 365 Admin Center.\nAgent runtime behavior: Call the connector knowledge source.\nBuilder configuration: Add the Copilot connector as a knowledge source."}]},{"n":60,"id":1007820,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>A company uses an agent in Copilot Studio to answer questions based on enterprise content.</p><p>The content is indexed in Azure AI Search. Responses must be generated by a Microsoft Foundry model.</p><p>To meet the business needs, the solution must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Users are able to trace each answer back to its source.</li><li>The agent retrieves information from a centralized data index.</li><li>Responses are generated by an enterprise-approved foundation model.</li></ul><p>You need to configure generative answers for the agent.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you configure for each requirement?</strong> To answer, move the appropriate configurations to the correct requirements. You may use each configuration once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to move the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image55.png\" alt=\"image55\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image56.png\" alt=\"image56\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":6,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/83257a09c628290cf4685b4841d80a2a1007820/","comments":[]},{"n":61,"id":1007821,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>A company uses an agent in Copilot Studio to generate structured responses for internal users.</p><p>The agent must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Consistently follow a reusable instruction template for response tone and structure.</li><li>Use an enterprise-approved foundation model for responses generated through the template.</li></ul><p>You need to configure custom prompts so the agent uses the Microsoft Foundry model catalog.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which two actions should you perform?</strong> Each correct answer presents part of the solution.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Publish the agent to apply the Foundry model selection automatically."},{"k":"B","html":"Configure Azure AI Search as the grounding source, so the model choice is enforced."},{"k":"C","html":"Allow topic authors to define tone and structure directly in topic steps."},{"k":"D","html":"Select a model from the Foundry model catalog for the custom prompt configuration."},{"k":"E","html":"Create a custom prompt template and apply it where the agent generates the structured response."},{"k":"F","html":"Enable citations, so the model is restricted to approved outputs."}],"answer":"DE","type":"multi","votes":[],"page":7,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/a15ac957109a919ac0d93a55200464b01007821/","comments":[]},{"n":62,"id":1007822,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>A company integrates an MCP service that exposes ticket-management operations.</p><p>The MCP service requires authenticated requests and exposes multiple callable operations that must be selectively governed for agent use.</p><p>To meet the business needs, the MCP configuration must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Only the allowed capabilities must be callable during conversations.</li><li>Requests must succeed without embedding credentials in topic steps.</li><li>The agent must be configured to send requests to the correct backend.</li></ul><p>You need to configure MCP tools for the agent.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which setting should you configure for each requirement?</strong> To answer, move the appropriate settings to the correct requirements. You may use each setting once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to move the split bar between panes or scroll to view content</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image57.png\" alt=\"image57\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image58.png\" alt=\"image58\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":7,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/88d72689e3b2195b95dc46a52b56bb151007822/","comments":[]},{"n":63,"id":1007823,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>An agent in Copilot Studio must complete tasks by automating interactions with a legacy desktop application that does not use APIs.</p><p>During testing, the builder must confirm that the automation runs in a supported execution context and can inspect how each automation step executes during conversations.</p><p>To meet the business needs, the solution must:</p><ul><li>Execute UI automation in a supported, platform-managed environment.</li><li>Provide visibility into how automation steps run during agent conversations.</li></ul><p>You need to configure the agent based on the requirements.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which two actions should you perform?</strong> Each correct answer presents part of the solution.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Publish the agent so automation settings are applied at runtime."},{"k":"B","html":"Inspect automation execution details by using the agent runtime view."},{"k":"C","html":"Enable computer use for the agent so UI automation runs in the supported execution environment."},{"k":"D","html":"Add the desktop application as a knowledge source so the agent can reference its UI structure."},{"k":"E","html":"Configure a custom connector to simulate UI interactions through REST calls."}],"answer":"BC","type":"multi","votes":[],"page":7,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/b2069273b0f3e7448366fb059a3b947f1007823/","comments":[]},{"n":64,"id":1007824,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>A company configures an agent flow that interacts with multiple systems to complete user requests.</p><p>The company must integrate external services, retrieve data, and notify users as part of the same automated flow run. To support this scenario, the agent flow must be able to do the following:</p><ul><li>Call an external API.</li><li>Retrieve stored data from a supported internal data source.</li><li>Send a Teams message.</li></ul><p>You need to select a connector or action type for each requirement.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you use?</strong> To answer, move the appropriate connectors or actions to the correct requirements. You may use each connector or action once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to move the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image59.png\" alt=\"image59\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image60.png\" alt=\"image60\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":7,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/1aa1536e11d349d909e4c61db4b121fd1007824/","comments":[]},{"n":65,"id":1007825,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>An agent in Copilot Studio must retrieve real-time data from an external system that exposes a REST API.</p><p>The API returns structured JSON data and requires authentication.</p><p>The agent must call the API during conversations to fulfill user requests.</p><p>The agent must retrieve real-time data from the external system by calling an authenticated REST API during a conversation.</p><p>The solution must use a supported mechanism that executes the REST API call and the call must be explicitly configured to run at runtime.</p><p>You need to determine which approaches add the REST API to the agent.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which two solutions meet the goal?</strong> Each correct answer is a complete solution.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Configure an HTTP action and invoke it from a topic during the conversation."},{"k":"B","html":"Create a topic variable and use a Formula to parse the API endpoint string."},{"k":"C","html":"Add the REST API as a tool and call it either by using a topic or agent instruction."},{"k":"D","html":"Add the REST API as a knowledge source so the agent can query it during conversations."},{"k":"E","html":"Enable generative answers and rely on the model to fetch the REST API data automatically."},{"k":"F","html":"Create a global variable to store the API URL and call it using a Redirect node."}],"answer":"AC","type":"multi","votes":[],"page":7,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/945c48d7ef046a194cabd91efa4173021007825/","comments":[]},{"n":66,"id":1007826,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>A company must enable an agent in Copilot Studio to execute operations exposed by an external MCP server.</p><p>The MCP server publishes callable tools and requires authentication.</p><p>The agent must be able to invoke MCP tools during conversations.</p><p>You need to configure MCP tools so the agent can execute MCP tool calls.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you do?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Enable generative answers so the model can automatically invoke MCP tools."},{"k":"B","html":"Add a Power Platform connector as real-time knowledge to replace MCP tools."},{"k":"C","html":"Add the MCP server output as an indexed knowledge source."},{"k":"D","html":"Configure authentication for the MCP server connection used by the agent."}],"answer":"D","type":"single","votes":[],"page":7,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/834903342dc954aa534947cce82494121007826/","comments":[],"variants":[54]},{"n":67,"id":1007827,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>An agent in Copilot Studio must retrieve real-time data from an external system that exposes a REST API. The API returns structured JSON responses and requires authentication.</p><p>To meet the business needs, the solution must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>The agent calls a REST API during a conversation.</li><li>The REST API call runs with proper authentication.</li><li>The REST API response is available to the topic at runtime.</li></ul><p>You need to configure the REST API to meet the requirements.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you configure for each requirement?</strong> To answer, move the appropriate configurations to the correct requirements. You may use each configuration once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to move the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image61.png\" alt=\"image61\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image62.png\" alt=\"image62\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":7,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/36f18674bfb06cf077fc08146c55ce651007827/","comments":[]},{"n":68,"id":1007828,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>A company is configuring generative answers for an agent in Copilot Studio agent.</p><p>The agent must use Azure AI Search to retrieve enterprise content, and all responses must be generated by a Microsoft Foundry model.</p><p>The agent sometimes generates answers that are not grounded in Azure AI Search content. The company requires that the agent only generate responses when relevant indexed content is retrieved.</p><p>You need to configure the agent so that its generative answer behavior meets the organization's requirements.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you do?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Use Azure AI Search as a tailback source and enable answer expansion."},{"k":"B","html":"Upload documents into the agent and disable fallback responses."},{"k":"C","html":"Require grounding for generative answers and use Azure AI Search as the retrieval source."},{"k":"D","html":"Enable citations and configure a public model endpoint."},{"k":"E","html":"Enable conversational boosting and select a Foundry-approved model."}],"answer":"C","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"C","p":100,"n":4}],"page":7,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/79128ab14a0a5b3ff66231eb4307f6c91007828/","comments":[{"user":"faisalronnie","date":"2026-08-05","up":3,"text":"Require grounding for generative answers and use Azure AI Search as the retrieval source.","pick":"C"},{"user":"Joselito79","date":"2026-09-03","up":2,"text":"C. Require grounding for generative answers and use Azure AI Search as the retrieval source. ✅\n\nThis ensures the agent only generates responses when relevant content is retrieved from Azure AI Search, preventing ungrounded responses and satisfying the enterprise-content requirement.","pick":"C"},{"user":"BolDeFruits","date":"2026-08-04","up":2,"text":"Proper answer is C\nSource: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-copilot-studio/guidance/retrieval-augmented-generation","pick":"C"}]},{"n":69,"id":1007829,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>A company wants to extend an agent in Copilot Studio by calling an external REST API to retrieve and update data.</p><p>To meet the business needs, the REST API must be added following a correct dependency order.</p><p>You need to add a REST API to the agent so it can be invoked during conversations.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>In which order should you perform the actions?</strong> To answer, move all actions from the list of actions to the answer area and arrange them in the correct order.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image63.png\" alt=\"image63\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image64.png\" alt=\"image64\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":7,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/5e6e62dba2e643ba161a4a8176dbe5821007829/","comments":[{"user":"faisalronnie","date":"2026-08-03","up":10,"text":"Add the REST API tool\nConfigure the API endpoint details\nConfigure authentication for the API\nTest the API configuration","top":true}]},{"n":70,"id":1007830,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>A company needs an agent in Copilot Studio to complete tasks by interacting with a legacy desktop application that does NOT have APIs.</p><p>To meet the business needs, the solution must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>The agent must interact with the application's UI.</li><li>The execution must run on supported infrastructure.</li><li>The builder must be able to observe how the tool runs during execution.</li></ul><p>You need to configure the agent based on the requirements.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which setting should you configure for each requirement?</strong> To answer, move the appropriate settings to the correct requirements. You may use each setting once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to move the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image65.png\" alt=\"image65\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image66.png\" alt=\"image66\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":7,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/8df2ee5b061b6a73cf0094741e7f5d6e1007830/","comments":[]},{"n":71,"id":1007831,"topic":2,"series":true,"stem":"<p>A company is configuring an agent in Copilot Studio that uses a generative answers node inside multiple topics.</p><p>The company requires responses to meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Must use an executive summary format.</li><li>Must apply only within a specific topic.</li><li>Must continue using configured knowledge sources.</li><li>Must comply with connector security controls.</li></ul><p>You need to configure a custom prompt to meet the formatting requirements.</p><div class=\"solution\"><span>Proposed solution</span>Add instructions in the custom prompt tool to restrict connector access during runtime.</div><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Does the solution meet the goal?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Yes"},{"k":"B","html":"No"}],"answer":"B","type":"yesno","votes":[],"page":8,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/d2730d4edfc6229aeb908da5e93f8fba1007831/","comments":[]},{"n":72,"id":1007832,"topic":2,"series":true,"stem":"<p>A company is configuring an agent in Copilot Studio that uses a generative answers node inside multiple topics.</p><p>The company requires responses to meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Must use an executive summary format.</li><li>Must apply only within a specific topic.</li><li>Must continue using configured knowledge sources.</li><li>Must comply with connector security controls.</li></ul><p>You need to configure a custom prompt to meet the formatting requirements.</p><div class=\"solution\"><span>Proposed solution</span>Create a custom prompt tool in the specific topic that instructs the model to respond using an executive-summary structure.</div><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Does the solution meet the goal?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Yes"},{"k":"B","html":"No"}],"answer":"A","type":"yesno","votes":[],"page":8,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/4bc184d0fa0eed7cf7cbffb807bbac221007832/","comments":[]},{"n":73,"id":1007834,"topic":3,"series":true,"stem":"<p>A company is configuring an agent in Copilot Studio that uses a generative answers node inside multiple topics.</p><p>The company requires responses to meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Must use an executive summary format.</li><li>Must apply only within a specific topic.</li><li>Must continue using configured knowledge sources.</li><li>Must comply with connector security controls.</li></ul><p>You need to configure a custom prompt to meet the formatting requirements.</p><div class=\"solution\"><span>Proposed solution</span>Configure the custom prompt tool at the topic level so that other topics are not affected.</div><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Does the solution meet the goal?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Yes"},{"k":"B","html":"No"}],"answer":"A","type":"yesno","votes":[{"a":"A","p":60,"n":3},{"a":"B","p":40,"n":2}],"page":8,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/b00c686c535ddb11efc347a7fbfc0aba1007834/","comments":[{"user":"faisalronnie","date":"2026-08-21","up":2,"text":"Separate custom prompt tool\n\nIs topic-specific\nCan format output\nBut does not inherently guarantee that the answer is still being generated by the existing Generative Answers node and its configured knowledge sources\nIntroduces a separate prompt execution path","pick":"B"},{"user":"BolDeFruits","date":"2026-08-04","up":2,"text":"Because the custom prompt is configured at the topic level, it provides the required executive-summary formatting for that topic only, while continuing to use the existing knowledge sources and preserving security controls.\nSource:\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-copilot-studio/nlu-boost-node","pick":"A"},{"user":"massnonn","date":"2026-09-08","up":1,"text":"missing generative node","pick":"B"},{"user":"Joselito79","date":"2026-09-03","up":1,"text":"Yes. ✅\nConfiguring the custom prompt at the topic level ensures the executive-summary formatting applies only to that specific topic, while the agent can continue using its configured knowledge sources and connector security controls.\nAnswer: Yes, the solution meets the goal.","pick":"A"}]},{"n":74,"id":1007835,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>A team is developing an agent in Copilot Studio and wants to evaluate its behavior before expanding access.</p><p>The team needs a repeatable, consistent method to test the agent using predefined interactions.</p><p>You need to ensure that agent responses can be evaluated consistently across multiple test runs.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you do?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Review evaluation scores from previous production sessions."},{"k":"B","html":"Enable telemetry and analytics to monitor intent matches, fallback usage, and response frequency."},{"k":"C","html":"Define test sets of prompts and expectations."},{"k":"D","html":"Change the evaluation method to a qualitative approach."},{"k":"E","html":"Publish the agent to additional channels for broader usage."}],"answer":"C","type":"single","votes":[],"page":8,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/4f64a019c96e42eb09a9dbbc7cce04fa1007835/","comments":[]},{"n":75,"id":1007836,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>A company builds agents in Copilot Studio in a development environment.</p><p>The agents are packaged inside a solution and deployed by using Power Platform Pipelines to test and production environments.</p><p>The company has the following requirements that must be met:</p><ul><li>Production deployments are limited to a defined set of users who are responsible for that stage.</li><li>The same solution is reused across all environments without editing its components.</li><li>The production environment always receives a locked-down version of the solution.</li></ul><p>You need to configure the pipeline and solution behavior to meet the requirements.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you configure?</strong> To answer, move the appropriate configurations to the correct requirements. You may use each configuration once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to move the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image67.png\" alt=\"image67\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image68.png\" alt=\"image68\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":8,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/fb816aaf1d76f9b81d1a05f056e247e41007836/","comments":[{"user":"massnonn","date":"2026-09-01","up":2,"text":"Limit users who can deploy to production: Configure stage access for the production stage.\n\nReuse the same solution across environments without modifying its components: Use environment variables in the solution.\n\nEnsure production receives a locked-down version of the solution: Deploy the solution as managed."},{"user":"faisalronnie","date":"2026-07-29","up":1,"text":"Use environment variablesChange environment-specific values without changing solution componentsDeploy as unmanagedAllow solution components to be edited in the target environmentDeploy as managedPrevent solution components from being edited in the target environment"}]},{"n":76,"id":1007837,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>You run multiple evaluation tests for an agent in Copilot Studio before expanding user access.</p><p>The tests provide the following results:</p><ul><li>Each evaluation case is reported as meeting or missing the expected response.</li><li>Some evaluation cases fail repeatedly across several runs.</li><li>Each run displays the expected response and the response generated by the agent.</li></ul><p>You need to provide a conclusion based on the evaluation results.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which conclusions should you make?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image69.png\" alt=\"image69\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image70.png\" alt=\"image70\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":8,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/416b0175db229a753645786552473df91007837/","comments":[]},{"n":77,"id":1007838,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>An agent in Copilot Studio is evaluated using a fixed test set and an automated evaluation method.</p><p>After running the evaluation, the team observes that the same three interactions fail in every run, while all other interactions pass consistently.</p><p>You need to use the evaluation results to determine an accurate conclusion.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you conclude from the evaluation results?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"The agent's overall design is flawed and requires a full redesign."},{"k":"B","html":"The failing interactions are caused by an issue in the underlying language model."},{"k":"C","html":"The outcomes isolate which portions of the agent's functional scope require remediation."},{"k":"D","html":"The agent should not be deployed."}],"answer":"C","type":"single","votes":[],"page":8,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/1364a4ca6cc38005ab24778d458635d91007838/","comments":[]},{"n":78,"id":1007839,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>A team has an existing agent in Copilot Studio and must move it to a different target location without rebuilding the agent. Some builders use Copilot Studio in the web app, while others use Copilot Studio in Microsoft Teams.</p><p>You need a supported approach to move the existing agent to the target location using ALM practices. The solution must avoid rebuilding the agent.</p><p>You need to move the existing agent to the target location using a supported method.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you do?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Remove agent components directly from the solution so that export and import will succeed."},{"k":"B","html":"Duplicate the agent in the source and manually recreate the changes in the target to avoid solution dependencies."},{"k":"C","html":"Create a custom solution, add the existing agent to the solution, export the solution with the agent, and import the solution into the target environment."},{"k":"D","html":"Publish the agent to a channel and use the channel configuration as the transport mechanism to the target environment."}],"answer":"C","type":"single","votes":[],"page":8,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/0e3561b0a1dcc8ab39b374e39f49da671007839/","comments":[]},{"n":79,"id":1007840,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>You are setting up an evaluation for an agent in Copilot Studio before expanding access to more users.</p><p>You must configure the evaluation so that the agent is tested by using prepared interactions rather than impromptu conversations.</p><p>The evaluation should provide the following functionality for users:</p><ul><li>An administrator updates a sensitive configuration value. The administrator requires the change to take effect at runtime without republishing the agent.</li><li>A builder needs to confirm a configuration value but must not be able to modify it from Copilot Studio.</li><li>An administrator updates a non-secret configuration value and requires the updated value to be used by the published agent at runtime.</li></ul><p>You need to create a test set-based evaluation that supports consistent test runs for each scenario.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you configure for each scenario?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image71.png\" alt=\"image71\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image72.png\" alt=\"image72\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":8,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/93bb8e1350a0cace6665988dc3138aa91007840/","comments":[]},{"n":80,"id":1007841,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>A team is preparing to evaluate an agent in Copilot Studio before expanding access to additional users.</p><p>The team must select an evaluation method that meets the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Use a fixed set of prepared interactions.</li><li>Determine responses against a predefined baseline.</li><li>Support consistent comparison across repeated test runs.</li></ul><p>You need to determine the evaluation method that satisfies the evaluation requirements.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which evaluation method should you select for each requirement?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate option in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image73.png\" alt=\"image73\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image74.png\" alt=\"image74\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":8,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/209331bb3c051d52f260e7bd6d8887f81007841/","comments":[]},{"n":81,"id":1007842,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>A solution containing an agent in Copilot Studio is moved across environments. The agent relies on configuration values that are different between environments and are managed as environment variables.</p><p>You must ensure the following:</p><ul><li>Configuration values are managed through environment variables that supports ALM.</li><li>Runtime behavior reflects updates to environment variable values.</li></ul><p>You need to implement environment-variable usage that supports ALM and ensures correct runtime behavior.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which three actions should you perform?</strong> Each correct answer presents part of the solution.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Replace environment variables with hard-coded values inside the agent so that runtime behavior is always consistent across environments."},{"k":"B","html":"Allow builders to change environment variable values directly in Copilot Studio during topic authoring to speed deployment."},{"k":"C","html":"Use environment variables as read-only in Copilot Studio and change their values in the appropriate administrative authoring experience."},{"k":"D","html":"Store external reference values as environment variables so the agent solution can move between environments while keeping the agent definition the same."},{"k":"E","html":"Assume that all environment variable updates take effect immediately at runtime for all variable types without republishing."},{"k":"F","html":"After an administrator updates a non-secret environment variable, republish any agents that use the variable so the change is effective at runtime."}],"answer":"CDF","type":"multi","votes":[],"page":9,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/5124e7ba483e63c575396627e2a3c7971007842/","comments":[]},{"n":82,"id":1007843,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>An organization uses separate development and production environments for agents in Copilot Studio.</p><p>You create an agent in the development environment.</p><p>The agent must be deployed to production by using an ALM process.</p><p>You must configure the solution strategy to meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Developers continue modifying the agent in development.</li><li>The production deployment prevents direct modification.</li><li>The agent is exported from development and imported into production in a deployment-ready state.</li></ul><p>You need to configure solutions to support deployment and lifecycle management of the agents.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which solution type should you use for each requirement?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image75.png\" alt=\"image75\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image76.png\" alt=\"image76\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":9,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/d8f9694a5dc77d559d57f125f0e55bf71007843/","comments":[]},{"n":83,"id":1007844,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>A team is standardizing ALM for agents in Copilot Studio.</p><p>The team requires a custom solution that includes agents. The solution must support ALM scenarios, such as managing and transporting agent assets across environments and pipeline deployments.</p><p>You need to create an ALM-ready custom solution in Copilot Studio.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you do?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Publish the agent to a channel and use that channel configuration as the ALM container."},{"k":"B","html":"Create a new custom solution from the Solutions area."},{"k":"C","html":"Export the custom solution as a managed solution and import it into production."},{"k":"D","html":"Export the agent directly and then import it into another environment."}],"answer":"B","type":"single","votes":[],"page":9,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/4f5ccb96a53c220794d811d2d649002d1007844/","comments":[]},{"n":84,"id":1007845,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>You run the same fixed test set three times in Copilot Studio.</p><p>During evaluation, you observe the following:</p><ul><li>The same interaction fails in all three runs.</li><li>Score values range from 0.58 to 0.61.</li><li>The reasoning states that the response partially matches the expected answer.</li><li>The knowledge source that is used is internal documentation.</li><li>No tools are invoked.</li></ul><p>You need to determine which conclusions are supported based on the evaluation results.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which conclusions should you make?</strong> To answer, move the appropriate conclusions to the correct evaluation results. You may use each conclusion once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to move the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image77.png\" alt=\"image77\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image78.png\" alt=\"image78\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":9,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/0340d43935be086c8f4531a527b071971007845/","comments":[{"user":"massnonn","date":"2026-09-01","up":3,"text":"Evidence of a recurring issue: A pattern of failure across repeated runs.\n\nInformation provided about response quality: The response partially matches the expected answer.\n\nEvaluation limitations: The specific underlying cause of the failure."}]},{"n":85,"id":1007846,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>A team wants to automate solution deployment between environments. Deployments must follow a controlled, repeatable process.</p><p>The team needs to implement a pipeline-based deployment process that enforces the correct dependency order.</p><p>You need to implement a deployment pipeline and determine the correct sequence of actions.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>In which order should you perform the actions?</strong> To answer, move all actions from the list of actions to the answer area and arrange them in the correct order.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image79.png\" alt=\"image79\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image80.png\" alt=\"image80\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":9,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/0355ba3998539f0a8ae7d2e914fcad841007846/","comments":[]},{"n":86,"id":1007847,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>A company needs an agent in Copilot Studio to complete tasks by interacting with a legacy desktop application that does not use APIs. The builder needs to validate that UI automation can run in the supported execution context and needs a way to inspect how the automation behaves during testing conversations.</p><p>To meet the business needs, the solution must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Enable the agent to perform UI automation against the legacy application.</li><li>Inspect execution details for the automation during conversations.</li></ul><p>You need to configure the agent based on the requirements.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which two actions should you perform?</strong> Each correct answer presents part of the solution.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Configure a custom connector for the desktop app so the agent can automate the UI through authenticated calls."},{"k":"B","html":"Add a Power Platform Desktop flow to control the desktop app."},{"k":"C","html":"Access the remote session within the testing pane to monitor the real-time execution of the agent's desktop interactions."},{"k":"D","html":"Publish the agent so the automation runs in the supported environment automatically."},{"k":"E","html":"Enable the Computer use capability."}],"answer":"BE","type":"multi","votes":[{"a":"CE","p":100,"n":4}],"page":9,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/a7dca60a16a84adbf81c88978a9c77bd1007847/","comments":[{"user":"kevinirl","date":"2026-08-07","up":2,"text":"E. Enable the Computer use capability — This is the feature that lets a Copilot Studio agent perform UI automation against applications that have no API. Computer use drives the interface directly (clicking, typing, reading the screen) the way a person would, which is exactly what a legacy desktop app without APIs requires. This satisfies the first requirement.\n\nC. Access the remote session within the testing pane — Computer use runs in a remote/cloud session, and the testing pane lets you watch that session live so you can inspect how the automation behaves during test conversations. This satisfies the second requirement (inspect execution details during conversations).","pick":"CE"},{"user":"massnonn","date":"2026-09-08","up":1,"text":"Access the remote session","pick":"CE"},{"user":"Joselito79","date":"2026-08-27","up":1,"text":"✅ C. Access the remote session within the testing pane to monitor the real-time execution of the agent's desktop interactions.\n✅ E. Enable the Computer use capability.","pick":"CE"}]},{"n":87,"id":1007848,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>A development team is reusing agents in Copilot Studio across development, test, and production environments.</p><p>You need to ensure the agents meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Reusable components must support governed promotion across environments.</li><li>Environment-specific configuration must not be hard-coded.</li><li>Deployments must support automated, multi-stage approvals.</li></ul><p>You need to configure the agents based on the business requirements.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which configurations should you use for each requirement?</strong> To answer, move the appropriate configurations to the correct requirements. You may use each configuration once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to move the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image81.png\" alt=\"image81\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image82.png\" alt=\"image82\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":9,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/793df9490b85b4cabccaa022e8349a011007848/","comments":[]},{"n":88,"id":1007849,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>An agent calls a flow that intermittently produces unexpected results during execution.</p><p>The agent behaves inconsistently.</p><p>You need to investigate agent flow executions to diagnose the issue.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which two actions should you use?</strong> Each correct answer presents a complete solution.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Inspect failed run details."},{"k":"B","html":"Update the flow trigger definition."},{"k":"C","html":"Check the Error column in the Activity tab."},{"k":"D","html":"Review flow analytics summary."},{"k":"E","html":"Review flow run history."},{"k":"F","html":"Increase the connector timeout."}],"answer":"AE","type":"multi","votes":[{"a":"AE","p":100,"n":5}],"page":9,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/c4636200b50a9daa7fea483b940a57811007849/","comments":[{"user":"kevinirl","date":"2026-08-07","up":4,"text":"There is no error column in Activity tab from where the agent flow errors can be diagnosed","pick":"AE"},{"user":"ziggy1117","date":"2026-08-17","up":1,"text":"You open and see that there is a failed run.\nYou then review the flow run history (E)\nThen you check the flow and inspect the failed run details inside (A)","pick":"AE"}]},{"n":89,"id":1007850,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>You create a test set in Copilot Studio to evaluate an agent that answers policy questions and retrieves data from connected knowledge sources.</p><p>You run the evaluation and review the following result for one test case:</p><ul class=\"kv\"><li><b>Expected response:</b> Digital products are non-refundable after download.</li><li><b>Actual response:</b> Digital products cannot be refunded once downloaded.</li><li><b>Result:</b> Pass</li><li><b>Score:</b> 0.92</li><li><b>Reasoning:</b> The actual response semantically matches the expected response.</li><li><b>Knowledge sources used:</b> RefundPolicy_KB</li><li><b>Tools invoked:</b> None</li></ul><p>You need to determine whether additional corrective action is required based on the evaluation results.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which two actions should you perform?</strong> Each correct answer presents a complete solution.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Investigate external tool configuration for this test case."},{"k":"B","html":"Rerun the evaluation because the score is below 1.00."},{"k":"C","html":"Accept the result because semantic matching is sufficient for a passing evaluation."},{"k":"D","html":"Confirm that the connected knowledge source is functioning as expected."},{"k":"E","html":"Modify the test case because the response is not an exact match."}],"answer":"CD","type":"multi","votes":[],"page":9,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/e849f211f7c69de30228f75ff7f1b08d1007850/","comments":[]},{"n":90,"id":1007851,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>A team deploys Copilot Studio solutions by using Power Platform Pipelines.</p><p>You must configure a deployment strategy that meets the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Ensure that the solutions deploy in dev, test, and production environments in order.</li><li>Identify missing connection references or environment variables before the deployment process begins.</li><li>Manage all pipeline stages and security from a single, unified location for all linked environments.</li></ul><p>You need to configure the pipeline to meet the requirements.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you configure for each requirement?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image83.png\" alt=\"image83\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image84.png\" alt=\"image84\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":9,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/60cacd14e72e5e29596ed04a8166043b1007851/","comments":[{"user":"faisalronnie","date":"2026-08-10","up":1,"text":"• Solutions deploy in dev, test and production environments in order → Sequential stage progression\n• Identify missing connection references or environment variables before deployment → Deployment input validation\n• Manage pipeline stages and security from a single, unified location for linked environments → Centralized pipeline configuration."}]},{"n":91,"id":1007852,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>A team is preparing a test set to evaluate an agent in Copilot Studio before expanding access to additional users.</p><p>The test set must support consistent evaluation across repeated runs and focus on the agent's most important behaviors.</p><p>You need to create a test set that enables repeatable and meaningful evaluation.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>In which order should you perform the actions?</strong> To answer, move all actions from the list of actions to the answer area and arrange them in the correct order.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image85.png\" alt=\"image85\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image86.png\" alt=\"image86\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":10,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/445490af68f8fb7f78c4bfdbe546d1891007852/","comments":[]},{"n":92,"id":1007853,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>A team is preparing to assess an agent in Copilot Studio before expanding access to additional users.</p><p>The team requires an evaluation that provides controlled, repeatable, and consistently measured test runs.</p><p>The evaluation must:</p><ul><li>Be triggered directly by the team to control when testing occurs.</li><li>Determine success based on clearly established acceptance criteria.</li><li>Rely on a predefined source that ensures consistency across repeated runs.</li></ul><p>You need to configure the evaluation to meet the requirements.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you configure?</strong> To answer, move the appropriate configurations to the correct evaluation requirements. You may use each configuration once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to move the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image87.png\" alt=\"image87\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image88.png\" alt=\"image88\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":10,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/ae91821f6474339cad77bd5349ba94dd1007853/","comments":[]},{"n":93,"id":1007854,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>You run multiple evaluation tests for an agent in Copilot Studio before expanding user access.</p><p>You observe the following about the evaluation results:</p><ul><li>Each evaluation case is reported as meeting or missing the expected response.</li><li>Some evaluation cases fail repeatedly across several runs.</li><li>Each run displays the expected response and the response generated by the agent.</li></ul><p>You need to interpret what the evaluation results reveal.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you conclude based on each interpretation?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image89.png\" alt=\"image89\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image90.png\" alt=\"image90\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":10,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/75f8362cf10547f68a89013474721bc01007854/","comments":[]},{"n":94,"id":1007855,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>A company uses an agent in Copilot Studio in production and requires centralized monitoring for operational visibility and troubleshooting.</p><p>The team decides to use Application Insights as the monitoring solution.</p><p>An agent activity is not included in the monitoring data.</p><p>You need to enable monitoring the agent by using Application Insights.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which four actions should you perform in sequence?</strong> To answer, move the appropriate actions from the list of actions to the answer area and arrange them in the correct order.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image91.png\" alt=\"image91\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-620/image92.png\" alt=\"image92\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":10,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/c3da0d90f1989cf5e98d44400b186ea31007855/","comments":[{"user":"massnonn","date":"2026-09-02","up":1,"text":"1-Create or identify the Application Insights destination for telemetry.\n2-Enable monitoring for the agent.\n3-Configure which monitoring destination the agent uses.\n4-Publish the agent so the monitoring configuration takes effect."}]},{"n":95,"id":1007856,"topic":3,"series":true,"stem":"<p>A team is implementing ALM for agents in Copilot Studio across multiple environments.</p><p>The team requires a consistent way to manage and transport agent assets.</p><p>You need to recommend a solution that supports creation and use of ALM scenarios for agents in Copilot Studio.</p><div class=\"solution\"><span>Proposed solution</span>To export, import, and manage agents between environments, you need to create and use a custom solution.</div><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Does the solution meet the goal?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Yes"},{"k":"B","html":"No"}],"answer":"A","type":"yesno","votes":[{"a":"A","p":100,"n":4}],"page":10,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/cb2540b8ba13cb3a9627a2b15152c7cf1007856/","comments":[{"user":"BolDeFruits","date":"2026-08-04","up":3,"text":"The statement in the solution:\n\n\"To export, import, and manage agents between environments, you need to create and use a custom solution.\"\n\nmatches the documented ALM process for Copilot Studio agents\nSource:\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-copilot-studio/authoring-solutions-import-export","pick":"A"},{"user":"faisalronnie","date":"2026-08-10","up":1,"text":"\"To export, import, and manage agents between environments, you need to create and use a custom solution.\"","pick":"A"}]},{"n":96,"id":1007857,"topic":3,"series":true,"stem":"<p>A team is implementing ALM for agents in Copilot Studio across multiple environments.</p><p>The team requires a consistent way to manage and transport agent assets.</p><p>You need to recommend a solution that supports creation and use of ALM scenarios for agents in Copilot Studio.</p><div class=\"solution\"><span>Proposed solution</span>Publishing an agent to a channel is the required ALM container for transporting agents between environments.</div><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Does the solution meet the goal?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Yes"},{"k":"B","html":"No"}],"answer":"B","type":"yesno","votes":[],"page":10,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/04fc9f9dc7306c86d16326cf6c72f9bd1007857/","comments":[]},{"n":97,"id":1007858,"topic":3,"series":true,"stem":"<p>A team is implementing ALM for agents in Copilot Studio across multiple environments.</p><p>The team requires a consistent way to manage and transport agent assets.</p><p>You need to recommend a solution that supports creation and use of ALM scenarios for agents in Copilot Studio.</p><div class=\"solution\"><span>Proposed solution</span>Builders can change environment variable values directly in Copilot Studio to complete ALM configuration without administrative tools.</div><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Does the solution meet the goal?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Yes"},{"k":"B","html":"No"}],"answer":"B","type":"yesno","votes":[{"a":"B","p":100,"n":5}],"page":10,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/f0e803fd1a6d99c9143efa377965d4211007858/","comments":[{"user":"BolDeFruits","date":"2026-08-04","up":4,"text":"Answer should be B (No)\nIn Copilot Studio, environment variables are read-only for builders. Their values are managed through the appropriate Power Platform administrative experience (such as solution management and environment configuration), not directly during Copilot Studio authoring. Environment variables are specifically designed to support ALM by separating configuration from the agent definition.","pick":"B"},{"user":"Joselito79","date":"2026-09-06","up":1,"text":"No. ❌\n\nThe solution does not meet the goal.\n\nWhy?\n\nFor ALM in Copilot Studio, environment variable values should be managed outside Copilot Studio's agent authoring experience, using the appropriate administrative/Power Platform management tools.","pick":"B"}]}]},{"code":"AB-100","title":"Agentic AI Business Solutions Architect","url":"https://www.examtopics.com/exams/microsoft/ab-100/view/","topics":[{"n":1,"name":"Plan AI-powered business solutions"},{"n":2,"name":"Design AI-powered business solutions"},{"n":3,"name":"Deploy AI-powered business solutions"}],"cases":{"d646994a1b":{"name":"Fabrikam, Inc.","html":"<h4>Background</h4><p>Fabrikam, Inc., is a global consumer goods company that is undergoing a digital transformation initiative to migrate its entire infrastructure to the Microsoft cloud. As a key element of this cloud migration, the company will implement Microsoft Dynamics 365 Sales, moving away from the current on-premises proprietary technologies used by its business-to-business (B2B) sales team.</p><p>As part of the cloud migration, Fabrikam will adopt an AI-first approach to its business solutions and implement AI solutions, wherever possible, to streamline operations.</p><h4>Problem Statements</h4><p>Fabrikam's infrastructure currently relies on various on-premises systems that require sales executives to use corporate computers with physical keyboards to access business information during customer interactions. Mobile phones cannot be used for these purposes, as the systems depend on keyboard input. As a result, the sales executives spend a lot of time using keyboards to search for data on several disparate systems and file servers, rather than focusing on the customers. This affects the customer experience.</p><p>Fabrikam stakeholders are concerned that users will be hesitant to adopt AI. If the AI initiatives are NOT adopted, cost savings will never be realized. Additionally, funding for future AI initiatives will depend on demonstrating an increase in AI adoption month over month. As the AI agent initiative for the sales team will be the first for Fabrikam, the rapid adoption of the agent is a high priority.</p><h4>Planned Initiatives</h4><h5>General</h5><p>Fabrikam management has prioritized AI-driven projects to improve efficiency, customer engagement, and responsible AI adoption. The current application infrastructure is on-premises and must be migrated to the cloud to support the adoption of these technologies.</p><h5>Infrastructure Migration</h5><p>Fabrikam plans to migrate from its current on-premises infrastructure to a completely cloud-based topology; this will include user authentication, the security framework, and, primarily, the adoption of the services by end users.</p><p>All the data from the different systems will be consolidated into a single data source - a common data model that will use a Microsoft Dataverse environment as a single source of truth (SSOT) for the sales team.</p><h5>Sales Cycle Enablement</h5><p>To achieve the company's objectives, Fabrikam intends to implement the following strategies to enhance the sales cycle:</p><ul><li>Use low-code development to create a single AI agent that has Dataverse as its core component.</li><li>Ensure that sales managers can access unanswered correspondence from prospects and intervene as appropriate.</li><li>Replace the previous proprietary software with Dynamics 365 Sales to track sales cycles and customer interactions.</li><li>Have the sales executives use Dynamics 365 Sales to track interactions for open opportunities and send follow-up communications to prospects.</li><li>Have the sales executives use handsfree headsets to interact with an AI agent when they have questions about internal policies or customer data.</li></ul><h4>Requirements</h4><h5>Infrastructure Migration</h5><p>Fabrikam has identified the following infrastructure migration requirements:</p><ul><li>Azure must be used for all future infrastructure workloads.</li><li>The company must follow Microsoft-recommended methodologies for infrastructure migration to the cloud.</li><li>Any created AI agents must have their return on investment (ROI) calculated to ensure that the solution will save the company money.</li></ul><h5>Sales Cycle Enablement</h5><p>Fabrikam has identified the following requirements for sales cycle enablement:</p><ul><li>The final AI agent must follow Microsoft recommendations for a conversational user experience.</li><li>A designated checklist must be reviewed to ensure that the AI agent follows Microsoft deployment recommendations for a compliant solution.</li><li>Detailed telemetry must be logged for the first created AI agent to help troubleshoot and optimize the agent during the initial AI agent adoption process.</li><li>Unexpected AI agent actions must end in an escalation to a live representative. For example, a sales executive must be rerouted to a representative if the agent cannot answer a question after two failed attempts.</li><li>The return on investment (ROI) of switching from the current process to the future process is required for stakeholder sign off.</li><li>The sales team must use Dynamics 365 Sales to correspond with prospects more quickly and efficiently than currently.</li><li>Sales managers must report on the adoption of the AI agent to key Fabrikam stakeholders on a monthly basis.</li><li>Any sensitive information, such as user IDs and names, shared via the AI agent must be tracked for future auditing.</li></ul>"},"8b997de433":{"name":"Contoso, Ltd.","html":"<h4>Overview</h4><p>Contoso, Ltd. is a high-tech manufacturing company that uses Microsoft Dynamics 365 Finance. Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management, and Dynamics 365 Commerce for its North American operations. The company designs and develops innovative products that have many patents and proprietary technologies. The patents and engineering designs are closely guarded secrets.</p><p>Contoso executives want to integrate and adopt AI solutions to help scale the company in preparation for an anticipated period of rapid growth.</p><p>The company has multiple legal entities and Azure subscriptions that will be used in the adopted AI solutions.</p><h4>Requirements</h4><h5>AI Adoption</h5><p>The following executives will have specific responsibilities in the overall AI adoption:</p><ul><li><b>Chief Technology Officer (CTO):</b> Select one Dynamics 365 Finance, Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management or Dynamics 365 Commerce prebuilt AI agent and one custom Microsoft Copilot Studio AI agent to prioritize and deploy during the initial AI adoption phase.</li><li><b>Chief Information Officer (CIO):</b> Ensure that appropriate security labels are assigned to the data used by the AI agents.</li><li><b>Chief Financial Officer (CFO):</b> Analyze the return on investment (ROI) for the AI agents being deployed.</li><li><b>Chief Information Security Officer (CISO):</b> Discover and inventory AI resources for auditing.</li><li><b>Chief Executive Officer (CEO):</b> Ensure that all solutions adhere to industry-standard responsible AI practices.</li></ul><p>All AI initiatives and agents will have a detailed business use case, a defined audience profile, and an estimated ROI that will compare the cost savings of the current process against the estimated costs of using the new AI solutions.</p><p>The company's research and development (R&amp;D) department already has a custom Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that contains comprehensive product specifications and compliance data.</p><h5>Prebuilt AI Agent</h5><p>The CTO has NOT yet selected which prebuilt AI agent to use in Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management. The CTO wants to view available agent templates to identify which agent will add the most business value.</p><p>Depending on which high-priority AI agents are identified, its agent capabilities must be previewed in a discovery meeting with the relevant business operation stakeholders.</p><h5>Custom AI Agent</h5><p>Contoso has identified the following custom AI agent requirements:</p><ul><li>The custom AI agent will use data from Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management to answer questions for the manufacturing team as a low-code solution.</li><li>The custom AI agent will be accessible from within Microsoft Teams.</li><li>The custom AI agent must be designed to eventually connect to other agents that can be selected based on their description.</li><li>The topics used in the custom AI agent will be selected based NOT on a trigger phrase, but on a description of the purpose of the query, to make the interactions more conversational.</li><li>The custom AI agent must be able to answer questions about product specifications by using existing technologies. The product specifications are maintained by the R&amp;D department.</li><li>The custom AI agent must be integrated with and accessible from Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management.</li><li>The custom AI agent must be able to use Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management business logic that is stored outside of the application.</li></ul><h5>Analysis, Reporting, and Troubleshooting</h5><p>Contoso has identified the following analysis, reporting, and troubleshooting requirements:</p><ul><li>The CISO will audit all the AI solutions monthly for compliance and security.</li><li>The CFO will analyze all the AI solutions quarterly to compare the estimated ROI against actual measured efficiencies and adoption. The CFO will use the Copilot Studio agent usage estimator to perform this analysis.</li><li>The CISO wants to identify how much sensitive data was accessed for a given AI agent run and who accessed the data. Too much sensitive data accessed by a single user might indicate a high security risk.</li><li>The CTO wants to track user feedback on the quality of the AI agent responses during user interactions with the agents. Consistently poor feedback will trigger an escalated reengineering discussion.</li><li>The CEO wants a quarterly assessment of all the required metrics for their specific responsibilities. The tools used for the assessments must be Microsoft-recommended and must verify reliability, interpretability, fairness, and compliance.</li><li>The CFO wants to identify how many interactions with the AI agents are abandoned on a given day as compared to resolved conversations. Too many abandoned sessions might indicate that Copilot Studio credits are being used inefficiently by end users.</li></ul>"}},"questions":[{"n":1,"id":984433,"topic":1,"stem":"<p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which framework should you use to meet the AI agent requirements for the sales cycle enablement?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image1.png\" alt=\"image1\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image2.png\" alt=\"image2\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":1,"case":"d646994a1b","thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/d1f417e022fdff226c47466de5a2ffa0984433/","comments":[{"user":"rveney","date":"2026-02-24","up":27,"text":"Use the following frameworks:\n\nFor Microsoft Copilot Studio best practices:\nMicrosoft Power Platform Well-Architected framework\n\nFor conversational user experiences:\nSuccess by Design\n\nThe Well-Architected framework ensures the AI agent follows Microsoft-recommended design, deployment, security, telemetry, and compliance best practices.\nSuccess by Design provides structured guidance for delivering high-quality, user-centered solutions, including conversational experience best practices and governance reviews.","top":true},{"user":"Srikantha","date":"2026-09-23","up":4,"text":"Explanation\nMicrosoft Power Platform Well-Architected Framework: Provides the official guidance, principles, and best practices for building scalable, secure, and compliant Copilot Studio solutions (covering governance, security, operational excellence, reliability, and cost optimization).\nSuccess by Design: Offers structured, agent-assisted prescriptive guidance and methodologies for implementing Dynamics 365 and Power Platform solutions, which includes conversational design checklists, deployment recommendations, and user adoption strategies."},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-29","up":4,"text":"1. Success by Design → Copilot Studio best practices\nThe case study explicitly requires:\n- A designated checklist for deployment\n- Compliance with Microsoft recommendations\n- Telemetry for the first AI agent\n- Auditing of sensitive information\n- These are all core SBD pillars.\n\n2. Power Platform Well‑Architected Framework → Conversational UX\nThe case study requires:\n- The agent must follow Microsoft recommendations for conversational UX\n- Escalation after failed attempts\n- Optimization and telemetry\nThese map directly to the Well‑Architected Framework."},{"user":"dimsok","date":"2026-03-29","up":3,"text":"Success by design for both"},{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":2,"text":"Having trouble with this one.... could be PP-WAF for both but I’m going with the following for reasons below.\n\nCPS Best Practice = Success by Design\nSuccess by Design - is A project implementation methodology for Dynamics 365 and Power Platform.\n\nConversational user exp = Microsoft Power Platform Well-Architected framework\nPower Platform Well‑Architected Framework - is A quality and design framework for Power Platform solutions.","replies":[{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-04","up":1,"text":"Disregard. Given answers are correct.","replies":[{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-05","up":5,"text":"NVM 100% PPWAF for both!!! https://learn.microsoft.com/en-ca/power-platform/well-architected/experience-optimization/conversation-design","replies":[{"user":"pakalupapito","date":"2026-05-17","up":1,"text":"source: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/design-ai-agents-business-solutions/15-apply-power-platform-well-architected-framework"}]}]}]},{"user":"SHHH_auno","date":"2026-06-05","up":1,"text":"Both answers: Power Platform Well-Architected framework.\n\nMicrosoft’s Copilot Studio architecture guidance says Power Platform Well-Architected provides principles and best practices for designing and building Copilot Studio solutions. Microsoft also has a specific Well-Architected recommendation for designing conversational user experiences."},{"user":"Eberd","date":"2026-03-08","up":1,"text":"Arquitectura Power Platform → Well-Architected\nDiseño de experiencia y adopción → Success by Design","replies":[{"user":"pakalupapito","date":"2026-05-17","up":1,"text":"source: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/design-ai-agents-business-solutions/15-apply-power-platform-well-architected-framework"},{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-05","up":5,"text":"NVM 100% PPWAF for both!!! https://learn.microsoft.com/en-ca/power-platform/well-architected/experience-optimization/conversation-design","replies":[{"user":"pakalupapito","date":"2026-05-17","up":1,"text":"source: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/design-ai-agents-business-solutions/15-apply-power-platform-well-architected-framework"}]}]},{"user":"edsp11","date":"2026-02-27","up":1,"text":"given answers are correct","replies":[{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-07","up":2,"text":"ALM Accelerator is deprecated and it's not really a \"Framework\" is MS World. https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-platform/guidance/alm-accelerator/overview"}]}]},{"n":2,"id":984434,"topic":1,"stem":"<p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which framework should you use for the infrastructure migration?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Microsoft Cloud Adoption Framework for Azure"},{"k":"B","html":"Success by Design"},{"k":"C","html":"Microsoft Power Platform Center of Excellence (CoE)"},{"k":"D","html":"Microsoft Power Platform Project Setup Wizard"}],"answer":"A","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"A","p":100,"n":8}],"page":1,"case":"d646994a1b","thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/072701d08305cb77323c654b074101ee984434/","comments":[{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":3,"text":"A. Microsoft Cloud Adoption Framework for Azure\nMakes sense since it's about migration to Azure not CPS/D365/PP Deployment which would be Success by Design","pick":"A"},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-29","up":2,"text":"✅ Correct answer: A. Microsoft Cloud Adoption Framework for Azure\n\n🧠 Why Microsoft Cloud Adoption Framework (CAF) is correct\n\nCAF is Microsoft’s official, end‑to‑end methodology for:\n- Migrating on‑premises infrastructure to Azure\n- Modernizing identity, security, networking, and governance\n- Establishing cloud landing zones\n- Guiding organizations through strategy → plan → ready → adopt → govern → manage\n\nFabrikam’s requirements explicitly state:\n- “Azure must be used for all future infrastructure workloads.”\n- “The company must follow Microsoft‑recommended methodologies for infrastructure migration to the cloud.”","pick":"A"},{"user":"KathCha","date":"2026-03-05","up":2,"text":"A. Microsoft Cloud Adoption Framework for Azure\nDesigned for:\n\nCloud migration\nInfrastructure strategy\nAzure landing zones\nROI justification\nGovernance, security, operating model","pick":"A"},{"user":"Srikantha","date":"2026-09-23","up":1,"text":"Explanation\nMicrosoft Cloud Adoption Framework for Azure: This framework provides the definitive, Microsoft-recommended guidance, methodologies, strategies, and best practices for migrating infrastructure workloads to the Microsoft cloud (Azure).\nIncorrect Options:\nSuccess by Design is focused on implementing Dynamics 365 and Power Platform business applications rather than general infrastructure cloud migration.\nMicrosoft Power Platform Center of Excellence (CoE) and Project Setup Wizard govern low-code governance and environment setup rather than overall cloud infrastructure migration methodologies.","pick":"A"}]},{"n":3,"id":984435,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A company uses Microsoft Dynamics 365 Sales to manage leads that are stored in a Microsoft Dataverse table named Lead and use non-standard terminology and custom columns.</p><p>You need to configure business terms in the Lead table so that Microsoft Copilot controls can summarize the leads efficiently. The solution must minimize administrative effort.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>How should you configure the business terms?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Combine all the fields into one custom field."},{"k":"B","html":"Map the field display names as business terms."},{"k":"C","html":"Add the schema names as business terms."},{"k":"D","html":"Create new business terms for each field."}],"answer":"B","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"B","p":92,"n":11},{"a":"D","p":8,"n":1}],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/762113b9b6b33fe48ea5c8f834dfdedf984435/","comments":[{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":6,"text":"B. Map the field display names as business terms.","pick":"B"},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-29","up":5,"text":"Correct answer: B. Map the field display names as business terms.\n\nTakeaway:\nTo let Microsoft Copilot summarize leads effectively with the least administrative effort, you should map the existing display names of the Lead table’s fields to business terms. This avoids creating new terms manually and aligns Copilot with the terminology already used in Dynamics 365 Sales.","pick":"B"},{"user":"Sathish_PP","date":"2026-05-26","up":1,"text":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/design-ai-agents-business-solutions/3-design-business-terms-copilot-dynamics-365-apps-customer-experience-service","pick":"D"},{"user":"KathCha","date":"2026-03-05","up":1,"text":"Why B is correct\n\nMicrosoft Copilot controls reason in business language, not technical schema language.\nIn Dataverse, field display names already reflect business terminology, even when:\n\nNon‑standard terms are used\nCustom columns exist\n\nMapping display names → business terms:\n\nRequires minimal administrative effort\nPreserves existing semantics\nImproves Copilot’s ability to summarize leads accurately\nAvoids duplication and maintenance overhead","pick":"B"}]},{"n":4,"id":984436,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You are designing two Microsoft Copilot Studio agents named Agent1 and Agent2. Each agent must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Each agent must use a standard model.</li><li>Each agent must NOT use generative orchestration.</li></ul><p>Agent1 must support simple and short phrases for a given topic.</p><p>Agent2 must integrate with Microsoft Dynamics 365 Contact Center voice channel.</p><p>You need to recommend language models for the agents.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you recommend for each agent?</strong> To answer, drag the appropriate language models to the correct agents. Each language model may be used once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to drag the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image3.png\" alt=\"image3\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image4.png\" alt=\"image4\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/7b411a9e64362fd3d9c6d62fc2eef27f984436/","comments":[{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":11,"text":"Agent 1 = NLU\nAgent 2 = NLU and NLU+\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-copilot-studio/nlu-overview","top":true},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-29","up":3,"text":"Agent1 → Conversational language understanding (CLU)\nCLU is the lightweight, intent‑classification model used for short utterances and simple topic‑based interactions. It is the standard model for classic Copilot Studio bots.\n\nAgent2 → Natural language understanding + (NLU+)\nNLU+ is the only standard model designed for voice, telephony, and contact center scenarios. It supports barge‑in, speech patterns, and telephony‑grade intent recognition."},{"user":"UAEFadi","date":"2026-05-12","up":1,"text":"Agree on Agent 2 = NLU+ (not NLU because it doesn't support dynamics)\nbut i believe Agent1 = CLU (because it meets requiremetns and NLU is legacy now."}]},{"n":5,"id":984437,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A company uses Microsoft Dynamics 365 finance and operations apps.</p><p>The company plans to use Microsoft Copilot in-app help and guidance to generate responses for internal business processes.</p><p>You need to add an additional knowledge source for the business processes. The solution must NOT add new topics to the Copilot agent for the finance and operations apps.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which knowledge source should you add?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Microsoft Dataverse"},{"k":"B","html":"a public website"},{"k":"C","html":"Azure AI Search"},{"k":"D","html":"a file upload"}],"answer":"D","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"A","p":10,"n":3},{"a":"C","p":21,"n":6},{"a":"D","p":69,"n":20}],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/f9512c1512467d76ed9b654a24978142984437/","comments":[{"user":"Godfirst_E","date":"2026-04-15","up":9,"text":"You can add knowledge to the Copilot help and guidance feature by uploading files to Copilot Studio (in file formats such as PDF, RTF, or Word). If you want to add other types of knowledge (such as from SharePoint or other data sources), then you must add your own topic in the Copilot for Finance and Operations apps agent in Copilot Studio. Reference article https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/fin-ops-core/dev-itpro/copilot/extend-copilot-generative-help","pick":"D","top":true},{"user":"madimad","date":"2026-03-04","up":4,"text":"The requirement says:\n\nAdd an additional knowledge source\n\nMust NOT create new topics in the Copilot agent\n\nUsed for Copilot in-app help and guidance in Dynamics 365 Finance and Operations\n\nIn Microsoft Copilot, when you want to provide extra knowledge without building topics, the simplest approach is to add documents as knowledge sources.\n\nUploading files allows Copilot to:\n\nGenerate answers from internal business documentation\n\nProvide process guidance\n\nAvoid creating manual conversation topics\n\nExamples of files:\n\nProcess documentation\n\nInternal manuals\n\nTraining guides\n\nSOP documents\n\nThis also minimizes configuration effort.","pick":"D"},{"user":"Ninashnash","date":"2026-08-07","up":2,"text":"D. a file upload\n\nThis is confirmed directly by Microsoft Learn: you can add knowledge to the Copilot help and guidance feature by uploading files to Copilot Studio (in file formats such as PDF, RTF, or Word). If you want to add other types of knowledge (such as from SharePoint or other data sources), then you must add your own topic in the Copilot for Finance and Operations apps agent in Copilot Studio.","pick":"D"},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-29","up":2,"text":"Correct answer: C. Azure AI Search\n\nTo add an additional knowledge source for Microsoft Copilot in Dynamics 365 finance and operations apps without creating new topics, you must use a knowledge source that Copilot can index externally and retrieve from—not something that injects new conversational topics into the agent.\n\nAzure AI Search is the only option that:\n- Works as an external knowledge source\n- Supports retrieval‑augmented grounding for Copilot\n- Does not create new topics in the Copilot agent\n- Can index structured and unstructured business‑process documentation\n- Is the recommended method for extending in‑app help and guidance","pick":"C"},{"user":"Vinz572","date":"2026-03-07","up":2,"text":"Adding Knowledge source will never create a topic. It's just data grounding.\nIt's can only either A or D. I choose A since it's for Finance in D365, MS Dataverse seems a good option","pick":"A"},{"user":"Eberd","date":"2026-03-05","up":2,"text":"La d es correcta","pick":"D"},{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":2,"text":"Azure AI Search is the only one that does not create a topic.","pick":"C","replies":[{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-08","up":3,"text":"Sorry It's D. https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/fin-ops-core/dev-itpro/copilot/extend-copilot-generative-help"}]},{"user":"Srikantha","date":"2026-09-29","up":1,"text":"According to Microsoft documentation for Add knowledge to generative help and guidance with Copilot in Dynamics 365 Finance & Operations:","pick":"D"},{"user":"67eaf51","date":"2026-09-03","up":1,"text":"D: I asked M365 Copilot: \"f you want to use other knowledge sources such as SharePoint or other data sources, you must create your own topic in the Finance and Operations Copilot agent\"","pick":"D"},{"user":"CyrilleC","date":"2026-07-28","up":1,"text":"You can add knowledge to the Copilot help and guidance feature by uploading files to Copilot Studio (in file formats such as PDF, RTF, or Word)","pick":"D"},{"user":"HaCha","date":"2026-06-23","up":1,"text":"The correct knowledge source to add is C. Azure AI Search.\n\nAzure AI Search allows you to ground Copilot responses with internal documentation, standard operating procedures, and business process content. Copilot uses it purely as a retrieval and grounding layer rather than creating or managing new conversational topics.","pick":"C"},{"user":"raghdaAhmed","date":"2026-05-28","up":1,"text":"it's D\nthe question says internal \"guidance to generate responses for internal business processes.\""},{"user":"Sathish_PP","date":"2026-05-26","up":1,"text":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/fin-ops-core/dev-itpro/copilot/extend-copilot-generative-help","pick":"D"},{"user":"Xabia","date":"2026-05-18","up":1,"text":"It allows Copilot to:\n- Retrieve and ground responses from indexed business process content\n- Avoid creating new topics (unlike traditional conversational authoring)\nAzure AI Search works as a retrieval-based knowledge source, not a topic-driven one","pick":"C"},{"user":"KathCha","date":"2026-03-05","up":1,"text":"The prompt says:\n\nThey use Dynamics 365 finance and operations apps\nThey want Copilot in-app help and guidance for internal business processes\nThey need an additional knowledge source\nThe solution must NOT add new topics to the Copilot agent\n\nMicrosoft Learn has a tutorial specifically for this: “Add knowledge to agents for finance and operations apps”. It explains that Finance & Operations data is exposed as Dataverse virtual entities/tables (often with an mserp_ prefix) and you can add those tables as a knowledge source in Copilot Studio so the agent can answer in natural language using that data, with citations. https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/fin-ops-core/dev-itpro/copilot/tutorial-agent-knowledge","pick":"A"},{"user":"rveney","date":"2026-02-24","up":1,"text":"Azure AI Search ✅ (Correct)\nAzure AI Search is the recommended enterprise knowledge source for Copilot in Dynamics 365 F&O when you want to:\n\nGround Copilot responses with internal documentation and business process content\nUse existing documents, SharePoint content, or data lakes\nAvoid creating or managing new Copilot topics\n\nCopilot uses Azure AI Search purely as a retrieval and grounding layer, not as a conversational topic source.","pick":"C"}]},{"n":6,"id":984438,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A company has an AI business solution.</p><p>You need to extend the solution so that Microsoft 365 Copilot can invoke external logic hosted in Azure services.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you include in the solution?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Microsoft Copilot Studio skills"},{"k":"B","html":"Microsoft Power Platform connectors"},{"k":"C","html":"custom engine agents"}],"answer":"B","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"A","p":41,"n":11},{"a":"B","p":56,"n":15},{"a":"C","p":4,"n":1}],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/daac018a26eac808aea0fd7930d2bc94984438/","comments":[{"user":"madimad","date":"2026-03-04","up":5,"text":"To allow Microsoft 365 Copilot to invoke external logic hosted in Azure, you use skills created in Microsoft Copilot Studio.\nCopilot Studio skills allow:\n\nCalling external APIs\n\nIntegrating Azure-hosted services\n\nExposing business logic to Microsoft 365 Copilot\n\nExamples:\n\nCalling Azure Functions\n\nAccessing custom APIs\n\nExecuting backend business workflows\n\nThese skills act as extensions that Copilot can invoke when needed.","pick":"B","replies":[{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-07","up":1,"text":"So you agree on A then? says you selected B","replies":[{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-08","up":1,"text":"Ya I'm Going with B. PP connectors ... Was thinking Bot Framwork skills which is being phased out"}]}]},{"user":"rveney","date":"2026-03-09","up":4,"text":"Power Platform connectors are the supported and required mechanism for exposing external services to Microsoft 365 Copilot.\n\nThey can wrap:\nAzure Functions\nLogic Apps\nREST APIs\n\nOnce exposed as a connector, Copilot can invoke the external logic securely and decoratively.\n\nThese connectors are then consumable by:\nMicrosoft 365 Copilot\nCopilot Studio skills\nPower Automate flows","pick":"B","replies":[{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-08","up":1,"text":"Ya I'm Going with B. PP connectors ... Was thinking Bot Framwork skills which is being phased out"}]},{"user":"Sathish_PP","date":"2026-05-26","up":3,"text":"I think option B to connect External","pick":"B"},{"user":"Xabia","date":"2026-04-22","up":3,"text":"Microsoft 365 Copilot cannot directly invoke connectors-> Connectors must be wrapped in a Copilot Studio skill to be callable by Copilot","pick":"A"},{"user":"K_in_the_Cloud","date":"2026-03-27","up":3,"text":"Skills (also called \"actions\" or \"plugins\") are the mechanism specifically designed to extend Microsoft 365 Copilot's capabilities by allowing it to call external APIs and Azure-hosted logic (Azure Functions, REST endpoints, Logic Apps). When you build a skill in Copilot Studio, it becomes directly discoverable and invocable by Microsoft 365 Copilot. This is the intended extensibility pattern for connecting M365 Copilot to external Azure services.","pick":"A","replies":[{"user":"K_in_the_Cloud","date":"2026-03-27","up":1,"text":"Power Platform connectors are the plumbing used within Power Automate flows and Power Apps to connect to services. They don't directly extend Microsoft 365 Copilot to invoke external logic. They're a component you might use inside a skill or flow, but they're not the answer to \"how do you extend M365 Copilot.\""}]},{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":3,"text":"\"hosted in Azure service\" must be A. Unless I'm missing something?","pick":"A","replies":[{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-08","up":2,"text":"Ya I'm Going with B. PP connectors ... Was thinking Bot Framwork skills which is being phased out"}]},{"user":"Vinz572","date":"2026-03-07","up":2,"text":"AI Can integrate flow and from that it can use Power Platform connectors.","pick":"B"},{"user":"krunal0000001","date":"2026-09-25","up":1,"text":"Custom engine agents are designed for this scenario because they allow organizations to bring their own orchestration, AI services, and external logic, including Azure-hosted services, and surface those capabilities through Microsoft 365 Copilot.","pick":"C"},{"user":"Srikantha","date":"2026-09-25","up":1,"text":"Explanation:\nTo extend Microsoft 365 Copilot so that it can invoke external logic hosted in Azure services, you must expose that logic using Microsoft Copilot Studio skills (frequently referred to as plugins or actions). Skills serve as the specific extensibility mechanism that Copilot uses during grounding and orchestration, enabling it to securely discover and trigger custom APIs, backend workflows, or external Azure-hosted logic directly from user prompts.","pick":"A"},{"user":"zamper","date":"2026-08-17","up":1,"text":"Skills are reusable capabilities that extend what your agent can do. Unlike tools, which connect to external services, skills are self-contained sets of instructions and logic that you can create, share, and reuse across agents.\n\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-copilot-studio/agents-experience/skills-overview","pick":"B"},{"user":"Ninashnash","date":"2026-08-07","up":1,"text":"the ask is: Extend the solution so that Microsoft 365 Copilot can invoke external logic hosted in Azure services\nTo Invoke external logics (integration with other systems) in Power Platform you need Connectors (either OOTB connectors, or Custom Connectors). Full stop!","pick":"B"},{"user":"HaCha","date":"2026-06-23","up":1,"text":"The correct option is B. Microsoft Power Platform connectors.\n\nTo let Microsoft 365 Copilot interact with external logic hosted on Azure services (such as Azure Functions or Azure Logic Apps), you must wrap the Azure-hosted logic using a Microsoft Power Platform custom connector. These connectors translate the Copilot requests into API calls the Azure services understand, creating a secure bridge for data and workflow actions.","pick":"B"},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-29","up":1,"text":"Correct answer: A. Microsoft Copilot Studio skills.\n\n🎯 Takeaway\nTo let Microsoft 365 Copilot invoke external logic hosted in Azure services, you must expose that logic as skills built in Microsoft Copilot Studio.\nSkills act as extensions that Copilot can call during grounding and orchestration, enabling it to trigger APIs, workflows, or Azure‑hosted logic.\n\nWhy the other options don’t fit\nPower Platform connectors\nThese extend Power Apps/Power Automate, not Microsoft 365 Copilot.\n\nCustom engine agents\nThese are for Copilot Studio agent orchestration, not for extending Microsoft 365 Copilot itself.","pick":"A"},{"user":"QueenShi","date":"2026-03-11","up":1,"text":"https://community.dynamics.com/blogs/post/?postid=9cff6025-c80b-f011-bae2-000d3a990cc2\n\nPP connectors enable connection to external services","pick":"B"}]},{"n":7,"id":984439,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You need to design a shared prompt library that will be used across multiple business units. The solution must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Ensure consistent AI responses with reusable formats.</li><li>Support governance and version control.</li><li>Minimize administrative effort.</li><li>Minimize ongoing costs.</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you recommend for each requirement?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image5.png\" alt=\"image6\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image6.png\" alt=\"image7\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/0c79a4e7fbe542328b8026dfa733a4b7984439/","comments":[{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":11,"text":"looks correct to me.","top":true},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-29","up":3,"text":"Ensure consistent AI responses:\n→ Define standardized prompt templates\nStandardized templates give every business unit the same structure, tone, and expectations. This is the only option that guarantees consistent responses across teams.\n\nSupport governance and version control:\n→ Store prompts in a Git repository\n- A Git repo provides:\n- Full version history\n- Branching and approvals\n- Governance workflows\n- Minimal cost (often free with existing DevOps/GitHub)"}]},{"n":8,"id":984440,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A company has a Microsoft Foundry project that uses a single agent and a single prompt to complete a series of tasks.</p><p>The agent encounters the following issues:</p><ul><li>It frequently produces incomplete results.</li><li>It struggles with domain-specific reasoning.</li><li>Agent response times are remarkably slow.</li></ul><p>You need to recommend a solution to improve the overall performance and accuracy of the agent.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you include in the recommendation?</strong> To answer, drag the appropriate actions to the correct requirements. Each action may be used once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to drag the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image7.png\" alt=\"image8\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image8.png\" alt=\"image9\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/4280208b0161de3183ef8ab5366ba640984440/","comments":[{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":9,"text":"looks correct to me","top":true},{"user":"QueenShi","date":"2026-03-11","up":4,"text":"A single agent for a single prompt is the problem. No grounding data source for it to reference, and no methods for re-routing tasks it cannot perform, causing it to think for long periods of time. This answer looks correct to me too."},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-29","up":2,"text":"To improve performance:\n→ Move to a multi-agent architecture\n➡️ A multi-agent architecture distributes tasks across specialized agents.\nThis reduces cognitive load on a single model and dramatically improves speed, task completion, and parallelization.\n\nTo improve accuracy:\n→ Add a grounding data source\n➡️ Adding a grounding data source (Azure AI Search, SharePoint, Dataverse, etc.) gives the agent authoritative domain knowledge.\nThis improves precision, reasoning, and completeness."}]},{"n":9,"id":984441,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A financial services company uses Microsoft Dynamics 365 Finance.</p><p>Currently, the company's support staff manually reviews customer transaction histories to detect potential fraud cases before escalating the cases.</p><p>You need to recommend an automation solution for the review process. The solution must ensure that escalations reach a human analyst for final decision making.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you recommend?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Deploy an autonomous agent that closes non-fraud cases automatically."},{"k":"B","html":"Use Microsoft 365 Copilot in Word to automatically finalize fraud detection policies."},{"k":"C","html":"Configure a task agent to generate fraud risk scores for the human analyst to review."},{"k":"D","html":"Export the data to a data lake for analysis in Microsoft Power BI."}],"answer":"C","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"C","p":100,"n":5}],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/a93bfd5dec307d5f20dd27ec5b41f8ef984441/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-29","up":2,"text":"Correct answer:\nC. Configure a task agent to generate fraud risk scores for the human analyst to review.\n\nExplanation:\nThe company needs automation, but not full autonomy. The requirement explicitly states:\n- Escalations must still reach a human analyst\n- The system should assist, not replace, human decision‑making\n- The process involves structured, repeatable analysis (transaction review → risk scoring → human review)","pick":"C"},{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":2,"text":"C. Configure a task agent to generate fraud risk scores for the human analyst to review.\nThis is the only option that fits all requirements: automation of the review process, but with human‑in‑the‑loop final decision making.","pick":"C"},{"user":"Srikantha","date":"2026-09-27","up":1,"text":"Why C is correct: The requirement specifies that escalations must ultimately reach a human analyst for final decision-making. A task agent streamlines the initial heavy lifting by analyzing transaction histories and generating structured risk scores. This automates the time-consuming review process while preserving a human-in-the-loop governance model for final fraud determinations.","pick":"C"},{"user":"Srikantha","date":"2026-09-27","up":1,"text":"A financial services company uses Microsoft Dynamics 365 Finance.\nCurrently, the company's support staff manually reviews customer transaction histories to detect potential fraud cases before escalating the cases.\nYou need to recommend an automation solution for the review process. The solution must ensure that escalations reach a human analyst for final decision making. What should you recommend?\n\nA. Deploy an autonomous agent that closes non-fraud cases automatically.\nB. Use Microsoft 365 Copilot in Word to automatically finalize fraud detection policies.\nC. Configure a task agent to generate fraud risk scores for the human analyst to review.\nD. Export the data to a data lake for analysis in Microsoft Power BI.","pick":"C"}]},{"n":10,"id":984442,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A company plans to deploy a Microsoft Copilot Studio agent that will analyze historical business data to predict customer behavior.</p><p>The data is currently stored in an Azure SQL database, flat files, APIs, and logs.</p><p>You need to organize the data into a format that can be used as a knowledge source in Copilot Studio.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you include in the solution?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Azure AI Search"},{"k":"B","html":"Azure Data Lake Storage"},{"k":"C","html":"Azure Cosmos DB"},{"k":"D","html":"Azure Translator in Foundry Tools"}],"answer":"A","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"A","p":79,"n":11},{"a":"B","p":21,"n":3}],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/1cfa25f5c368635c5df703bcfb89572f984442/","comments":[{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":5,"text":"Azure AI Search is the correct choice.\nIt’s the only option in the list that can index, chunk, and vectorize heterogeneous data (SQL tables, flat files, APIs, logs) into a searchable knowledge source that Copilot Studio can ground its responses on.","pick":"A"},{"user":"24b8eec","date":"2026-06-16","up":4,"text":"Azure AI Search — This is a retrieval/indexing layer (and yes, it can be wired into Copilot Studio as a knowledge source), but it does not organize and consolidate raw data from heterogeneous sources.","pick":"B"},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-29","up":4,"text":"Correct answer: A. Azure AI Search\n\nTo make historical business data usable as a knowledge source in Microsoft Copilot Studio, the data must be indexed, chunked, and retrievable through a grounding mechanism.\nAmong the options, Azure AI Search is the only service designed specifically for:\n- Indexing heterogeneous data sources (SQL, files, APIs, logs)\n- Converting them into a searchable knowledge index\n- Powering retrieval‑augmented generation (RAG) for Copilot Studio\n- Providing semantic search, vector search, and hybrid retrieval\n- Integrating natively as a knowledge source in Copilot Studio","pick":"A"},{"user":"sdnayak4","date":"2026-03-17","up":2,"text":"Azure AI Search is right","pick":"A"},{"user":"Srikantha","date":"2026-09-27","up":1,"text":"Why A is correct: When data is fragmented across multiple heterogeneous systems (such as an Azure SQL database, flat files, APIs, and logs), Azure AI Search serves as the central indexing and retrieval layer. It ingests data from these varied sources, indexes it, and formats it so that AI applications and Microsoft Copilot Studio agents can query and use it efficiently as a knowledge source. Copilot Studio also natively supports connecting to Azure AI Search as a primary enterprise knowledge source.","pick":"A"},{"user":"Ninashnash","date":"2026-08-07","up":1,"text":"Azure AI Search can: Ingest data from multiple sources.\nIndex and enrich the data.\nCreate a searchable index that AI agents can use as a knowledge source.\nSupport Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) scenarios.\n\nCopilot Studio and Azure AI Foundry commonly use Azure AI Search as the retrieval layer for enterprise knowledge.","pick":"A"},{"user":"Eberd","date":"2026-03-05","up":1,"text":"Copilot Studio no consume directamente datos estructurados y no estructurados mezclados (SQL, archivos, APIs, logs).\nPrimero hay que indexar y organizar esa información en una capa que permita:","pick":"A"}]},{"n":11,"id":984443,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A retail company plans to deploy Microsoft Copilot Studio agents to support:</p><ul><li>Microsoft Dynamics 365 Commerce scenarios.</li><li>A Microsoft Power Apps inventory management solution.</li></ul><p>You need to recommend a solution to organize product catalog data as a consistent source for multiple AI systems.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you recommend?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Let each agent scrape product details from Microsoft SharePoint Online libraries."},{"k":"B","html":"Store the product catalog data in a separate custom table for each agent."},{"k":"C","html":"Configure prompts to pull product details from the PDFs of external vendors."},{"k":"D","html":"Centralize the product catalog data in Microsoft Dataverse and expose the data to both agents."}],"answer":"D","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"D","p":100,"n":6}],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/67e9cf92da7acfd6d907ae3f1988418f984443/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-29","up":4,"text":"Correct answer: D. Centralize the product catalog data in Microsoft Dataverse and expose the data to both agents.\n\nYou need one consistent product catalog that can be used by:\n- A Dynamics 365 Commerce Copilot Studio agent\n- A Power Apps inventory management Copilot Studio agent\n\nThe only option that provides:\n- A single source of truth\n- Structured, governed, relational data\n- Native integration with both Dynamics 365 and Power Platform\n- Reusable knowledge across multiple AI systems\n- Low administrative overhead\n…is Microsoft Dataverse.\n\nDataverse is the enterprise data backbone for Dynamics 365 and Power Apps, making it the natural place to centralize product catalog data.","pick":"D"},{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":4,"text":"Centralizing the catalog in Dataverse gives you a single source of truth that every Copilot Studio agent, Power Apps solution, and Dynamics 365 Commerce integration can reliably consume. This avoids duplication, drift, and inconsistent product attributes across systems.","pick":"D"}]},{"n":12,"id":984444,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A company has a portfolio of AI initiatives at different stages of development.</p><p>You need to recommend a structured approach to evaluating the return on AI investment (ROAI) across all the initiatives. The solution must balance immediate results with long-term values and strategic innovations.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you include in the recommendation?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"a simple cost and benefit analysis"},{"k":"B","html":"a horizon-based framework"},{"k":"C","html":"the internal rate of return (IRR) function"},{"k":"D","html":"a prioritization grid"}],"answer":"B","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"B","p":100,"n":9}],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/9dde2ff7e32b8041c0f68103713335c0984444/","comments":[{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":6,"text":"NOT 100% on this but I think it's B.\n\nB. a horizon-based framework.\nA horizon-based model (often Horizon 1–2–3) is designed specifically for evaluating short‑term ROI, mid‑term capability building, and long‑term strategic innovation in a single, coherent structure. It lets an organization compare AI initiatives that are at very different maturity levels without forcing them into the same ROI formula.","pick":"B"},{"user":"Srikantha","date":"2026-09-27","up":1,"text":"Why B is correct: A horizon-based framework (such as Horizon 1, 2, and 3) is specifically designed for evaluating portfolios of initiatives across different stages of maturity and development. It allows organizations to balance immediate, short-term operational savings (Horizon 1) with mid-term scalable growth (Horizon 2) and long-term transformational or strategic innovations (Horizon 3) without prematurely penalizing exploratory AI projects that don't yield immediate financial returns.","pick":"B"},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-29","up":1,"text":"The correct answer is: B. a horizon‑based framework\n\nWhen a company has multiple AI initiatives at different maturity levels, you need a framework that:\n- Evaluates short‑term ROI\n- Captures long‑term strategic value\n- Encourages innovation without ignoring immediate business impact\n- Provides a structured, portfolio‑level view\n\nA horizon‑based framework (Horizon 1 / Horizon 2 / Horizon 3) is specifically designed for this.","pick":"B"},{"user":"deca0d4","date":"2026-04-28","up":1,"text":"I think its the horizon-based framework...\nHorizon-based framework = strategy timing.\nUse it to group AI investments by maturity\n\nUse horizon framework for roadmap strategy, IRR for financial justification, and prioritization grid for selecting and sequencing use cases.","pick":"B"}]},{"n":13,"id":984445,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You need to recommend a Microsoft Power Platform business solution that consolidates data from multiple internal and external data sources. The solution must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Provide the data as a centralized source for multiple AI systems, including Microsoft Copilot Studio agents, Dynamics 365 applications, and external AI models.</li><li>Support built-in data classification and protection policies.</li><li>Provide data for grounding and analytics.</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you include in the recommendation?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Microsoft Dataverse"},{"k":"B","html":"Azure Data Lake Storage"},{"k":"C","html":"a Microsoft Power BI semantic model"},{"k":"D","html":"Azure Cosmos DB"}],"answer":"A","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"A","p":100,"n":7}],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/d1535e44cdc563acb269cd543c586595984445/","comments":[{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":4,"text":"About 90% on this one...\nIt is the only option in the list that natively provides centralized, governed, AI‑ready enterprise data with built‑in classification(With Purview Data Map), DLP, security, and integration across Copilot Studio, Dynamics 365, and external AI models.","pick":"A"},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-29","up":3,"text":"The correct recommendation is: A. Microsoft Dataverse\n\n🎯 Why Dataverse is the right choice\n\nYou need a centralized, governed, secure data platform that can:\n- Consolidate internal + external data sources\n- Serve as a single source of truth for multiple AI systems\n- Provide built‑in data classification, DLP, and security\n- Support grounding for Copilot Studio, Dynamics 365, and external AI models\n- Enable analytics across the organization\n\nOnly Microsoft Dataverse satisfies all of these requirements.","pick":"A"},{"user":"24b8eec","date":"2026-06-16","up":2,"text":"Why not the others:\n\nB. Azure Data Lake Storage — Great for consolidating raw, large-scale historical data and analytics, but it lacks built-in data classification, security roles, and protection policies, and it isn't a native, governed knowledge source for Copilot Studio + Dynamics 365 the way Dataverse is.\nC. Power BI semantic model — An analytics/reporting layer, not a centralized operational data store that serves Dynamics 365 and external AI models for grounding.\nD. Azure Cosmos DB — A low-latency NoSQL operational database; no built-in data classification/protection governance and not a native Power Platform/Copilot knowledge source.","pick":"A"}]},{"n":14,"id":984446,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A company plans to deploy an AI-based customer service app that will autonomously manage interactions, escalate complex cases, and learn from historical ticket data.</p><p>You need to perform a return on AI investment (ROAI) analysis of the app deployment. The solution must ensure that the analysis is accurate.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you do first?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Establish the AI performance metrics."},{"k":"B","html":"Conduct an AI market benchmarking study."},{"k":"C","html":"Model the customer experience."},{"k":"D","html":"Identify and quantify all the development, deployment, and operating costs."}],"answer":"D","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"D","p":100,"n":6}],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/774ae5dcd11027fd92ad9b822b2bbe1d984446/","comments":[{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":5,"text":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/forecast-agent-return-investment/2-forecast-return-investment","pick":"D"},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-30","up":3,"text":"The correct first step is: D. Identify and quantify all the development, deployment, and operating costs.\n\nA Return on AI Investment (ROAI) analysis must begin with a baseline financial understanding.\nBefore you can measure value, performance, or customer impact, you must know:\n- What the AI solution will cost to build\n- What it will cost to run\n- What it will cost to maintain\n- What existing processes cost today\nWithout this foundation, any ROI calculation would be incomplete or misleading.","pick":"D","replies":[{"user":"bridge_b","date":"2026-06-01","up":1,"text":"Great contributions omath, have you done the exam yet?"}]}]},{"n":15,"id":994132,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You are designing end-to-end test scenarios for a business solution that uses Microsoft Dynamics 365 Sales and Dynamics 365 Finance.</p><p>You need to ensure that the business solution meets the following test requirements:</p><ul><li>Properly exchanges data between the Dynamics 365 apps</li><li>Aligns with defined user workflows and business processes</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which type of testing should you use for each requirement?</strong> To answer, drag the appropriate testing types to the correct requirements. Each testing type may be used once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to drag the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image39.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image40.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/782395fb45896555e86d34c329d9539c994132/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-30","up":5,"text":"→ Integration testing\nIntegration testing validates that data flows correctly between systems—in this case, Dynamics 365 Sales and Dynamics 365 Finance. It ensures APIs, plugins, dual‑write, and synchronization behave as expected.\n\n→ User acceptance testing (UAT)\nUser acceptance testing ensures the solution matches real‑world business workflows, user expectations, and process requirements. It is the final validation before production."},{"user":"deca0d4","date":"2026-05-17","up":1,"text":"Ensure proper exchanges data between Dynamics 365 apps\n👉 Integration testing\n\n🧠 Why?\n\nBecause you are validating:\n\nData exchange\nInterfaces\nConnectivity\nSynchronization between systems\n\nAlign with defined workflows and business processes\n👉 User Acceptance Testing (UAT)\nBecause UAT validates:\nReal business workflows\nEnd-user expectations\nBusiness process correctness"}]},{"n":16,"id":994133,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A company has a Microsoft 365 tenant in Canada and multiple Microsoft Power Platform environments in Canada and the United States.</p><p>The company plans to deploy a Microsoft Copilot Studio agent to the Canadian environment that will use:</p><ul><li>Microsoft Dataverse data stored in Canada</li><li>A connector that connects to an Azure OpenAI instance in the United States</li></ul><p>You need to ensure that the agent adheres to data residency and data movement policies before being deployed.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you do?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Ensure that the data processed by Azure OpenAI is stored in the United States."},{"k":"B","html":"From the Microsoft Purview portal, validate the Data loss prevention settings."},{"k":"C","html":"Migrate the tenant to the United States."},{"k":"D","html":"Ensure that cross-region data movement is enabled for the Canadian environment and connector dependencies."}],"answer":"D","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"D","p":100,"n":3}],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/6c3ad14f4ba82479164b469df78453bf994133/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-30","up":3,"text":"Correct answer: D. Ensure that cross‑region data movement is enabled for the Canadian environment and connector dependencies.\n\nYour Copilot Studio agent will run in Canada, but one of its dependencies—the Azure OpenAI connector—is located in the United States.\nThis means the agent will send data across regions, which triggers Microsoft’s data residency and data movement policies.\n\nBefore deploying the agent, you must explicitly enable cross‑region data movement for:\n- The Canadian Copilot Studio environment\n- The connector that calls Azure OpenAI in the U.S.\nThis is the only option that ensures the solution is compliant before deployment.","pick":"D"},{"user":"deca0d4","date":"2026-04-28","up":1,"text":"You must review/configure the environment’s data movement settings and DLP/data policies before deployment, and ensure the connector path from Canadian Dataverse to US Azure OpenAI is explicitly permitted. If not permitted, use an in-region Azure OpenAI endpoint or redesign.","pick":"D"}]},{"n":17,"id":994134,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A company has a Microsoft Copilot Studio agent for customer support.</p><p>You are reviewing and validating the following prompts:</p><ul><li>A prompt that has instructions to \"help the customer as best you can\"</li><li>A prompt that helps retrieve product information from a knowledge base</li></ul><p>You need to ensure that the agent delivers consistent and accurate responses.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you do for each prompt?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image41.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image42.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/324609bd30bf050f597e3f35e56b6507994134/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-30","up":7,"text":"Prompt: “help the customer as best you can”\n→ Rewrite the prompt with clear and task‑specific instructions.\nA vague instruction like “help the customer as best you can” leads to inconsistent, unpredictable model behavior.\nClear, scoped, task‑specific instructions produce repeatable, controlled, and aligned responses\n\nPrompt: Retrieve product information from a knowledge base\n→ Use responses with only reference sources and limit the response scope.\n- When grounding to a knowledge base, the model must:\n- Stay within the retrieved content\n- Avoid hallucinating\n- Cite or reference the source\n- Limit the scope to the product information retrieved","top":true}]},{"n":18,"id":994135,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You are designing a testing solution for Microsoft Copilot Studio agents.</p><p>You need to validate prompt engineering best practices to ensure that the agents generate accurate and contextually relevant responses.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which prompt validation techniques and metrics should you include in the solution?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image43.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image44.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/a4b710f9d2bc0d668ee1e9ad31032340994135/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-30","up":7,"text":"Prompt validation techniques:\n→ Use prompts that have varied phrasing\nThis is the correct technique because varied phrasing helps you test whether the agent responds consistently even when users express the same intent in different ways.\nIt validates robustness, generalization, and prompt stability.\n\nMetrics:\n→ Response relevance and accuracy\nThis is the key metric for evaluating whether the agent is producing correct, contextually grounded, and useful responses.\nIt directly measures the success of prompt engineering.","top":true}]},{"n":19,"id":994136,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A company has two Microsoft Power Platform environments named Dev1 and Prod1. A Microsoft Copilot Studio agent named Agent1 is built into a solution in the Dev1 environment.</p><p>You plan to deploy Agent1 to Prod1.</p><p>You need to make Agent1 available to the users in Prod1. The solution must minimize administrative effort.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you do?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Share Agent1 with the users in Prod1."},{"k":"B","html":"Export the solution as an unmanaged solution and import the solution into Prod1."},{"k":"C","html":"Export the solution as a managed solution and import the solution into Prod1."},{"k":"D","html":"Create a new Copilot Studio agent in Prod1 by replicating the configuration of Agent1."}],"answer":"C","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"C","p":100,"n":4}],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/aa3ab851bc77281d0ccf5e081fb6ef6b994136/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-30","up":5,"text":"The correct answer is: C. Export the solution as a managed solution and import the solution into Prod1.\n\nTo move a Copilot Studio agent (or any Power Platform component) from Dev to Prod, the recommended and lowest‑effort approach is:\n- Package the agent inside a managed solution\n- Import that managed solution into Prod1\n\nThis ensures:\n- Proper ALM (Application Lifecycle Management)\n- Controlled, locked‑down components in production\n- Easy updates through solution versioning\n- Minimal administrative overhead\n- No need to manually recreate or re‑share anything\n\nThis is exactly how Microsoft expects Copilot Studio agents to be deployed across environments.","pick":"C"},{"user":"deca0d4","date":"2026-04-28","up":1,"text":"Microsoft’s ALM guidance says unmanaged solutions are used in development, while managed solutions are imported into downstream environments like test and production.","pick":"C"}]},{"n":20,"id":994137,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A company has a Microsoft Power Platform environment that contains Microsoft Dataverse data.</p><p>You create a Microsoft Copilot Studio agent named Agent1 that processes the Dataverse data.</p><p>You discover that Agent1 fails to return relevant or accurate results.</p><p>You need to improve the quality and reliability of data grounding.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you do?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Retrain Agent1."},{"k":"B","html":"Verify and cleanse the Dataverse data."},{"k":"C","html":"Use an adaptive card in Agent1."},{"k":"D","html":"Add example user inputs to the training data of Agent1."}],"answer":"B","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"B","p":100,"n":3}],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/b893dc8033c80d4e3fe17c616532fced994137/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-30","up":5,"text":"The right first step is B. Verify and cleanse the Dataverse data.\n\nWhen a Copilot Studio agent returns irrelevant or inaccurate results, the most common root cause is poor grounding data quality.\nGrounding only works if the underlying Dataverse tables contain:\n- Clean\n- Complete\n- Accurate\n- Well‑structured\ninformation.\n\nIf the data is inconsistent, outdated, duplicated, or missing key fields, the agent will hallucinate or produce unreliable answers—even if the prompts and model are correct.\n\nSo before retraining, rewriting prompts, or adding examples, you must fix the data.","pick":"B"}]},{"n":21,"id":994138,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A company plans to deploy a Microsoft Copilot Studio agent to enhance customer support.</p><p>The company stores customer data across ServiceNow, Microsoft Dynamics 365 Finance, Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management, and Excel files in SharePoint Online.</p><p>You need to recommend a solution to ensure that the agent can deliver accurate and timely responses.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you recommend?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Implement a model router for query handling."},{"k":"B","html":"Create custom prompts."},{"k":"C","html":"Implement Microsoft Power Platform connectors."},{"k":"D","html":"Enable incremental indexing in Azure AI Search."}],"answer":"C","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"C","p":100,"n":11}],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/3f97951ac55ee00bcdfb35942c31ce29994138/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-30","up":4,"text":"The correct recommendation is: C. Implement Microsoft Power Platform connectors.\n\nPower Platform connectors allow the agent to securely and reliably access each system’s data without custom integration work.\n\nThis ensures:\n- Real‑time data retrieval\n- Consistent grounding\n- Minimal development effort\n- Compliance with Power Platform governance\n- Seamless integration across all systems","pick":"C"},{"user":"KathCha","date":"2026-05-03","up":4,"text":"We need to connect sources first, so C","pick":"C"},{"user":"Alicia_lili","date":"2026-04-29","up":2,"text":"It should be C","pick":"C"},{"user":"AxaptaKing1","date":"2026-10-01","up":1,"text":"Correct answer, connector will be needed to enable agent to communicate with other DB.","pick":"C"}]},{"n":22,"id":994139,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A manufacturing company wants to deploy an agent that will automate supplier invoice processing.</p><p>You are designing a solution to evaluate the financial implications of the deployment. The company is especially concerned about budget overruns.</p><p>You need to ensure that the solution considers the total cost of ownership (TCO), the expected savings from using automation, and whether to extend the existing AI capabilities.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you include in the design?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"a break-even analysis only"},{"k":"B","html":"adopting prebuilt agents to reduce the deployment time"},{"k":"C","html":"training a custom model"},{"k":"D","html":"a return on AI investment (ROAI) analysis"}],"answer":"D","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"D","p":100,"n":3}],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/efe5bf313903a3efce2ded29637a87dc994139/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-30","up":5,"text":"The correct answer is: D. a return on AI investment (ROAI) analysis\n\nThe company wants to evaluate:\n- Total cost of ownership (TCO)\n- Expected savings from automation\n- Whether extending AI capabilities is financially justified\n- Risk of budget overruns\n\nA return on AI investment (ROAI) analysis is the only framework that covers all of these dimensions.","pick":"D"},{"user":"kinser123","date":"2026-09-29","up":1,"text":"D. a return on AI investment (ROAI) analysis\n- Total cost of ownership (TCO)","pick":"D"}]},{"n":23,"id":994140,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A company has a Microsoft Power Platform solution that contains the following components:</p><ul><li>Microsoft Dataverse tables</li><li>A Microsoft Power BI workspace named WS1</li><li>A canvas app named App1 that uses Dataverse</li><li>A Power BI semantic model that connects to Dataverse by using DirectQuery</li></ul><p>You plan to use generative AI to provide answers to queries based on a subset of corporate data.</p><p>You need to ensure that the data is available as a grounding data source for AI systems.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you do?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Populate a Dataverse table."},{"k":"B","html":"Share WS1."},{"k":"C","html":"Endorse the semantic model."},{"k":"D","html":"Export the semantic model."}],"answer":"C","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"A","p":18,"n":2},{"a":"C","p":82,"n":9}],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/8da60c7e3e9cb67649a50082de2758d1994140/","comments":[{"user":"deca0d4","date":"2026-04-28","up":3,"text":"To endorse a semantic model means marking it as a trusted, high-quality, reusable data source in Power BI/Fabric.","pick":"C"},{"user":"hi1011","date":"2026-04-22","up":3,"text":"\"Consider using tags to label semantic models as ready for Copilot consumption. This method helps data consumers identify models that they can use with Copilot and expect better results. Alternatively, consider the readiness of a semantic model for use with Copilot as a criteria for its endorsement to promoted or even certified status.\"\n\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-bi/create-reports/copilot-semantic-models","pick":"C"},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-30","up":2,"text":"The correct answer is: A. Populate a Dataverse table.\n\nTo make data available as a grounding data source for generative AI systems (including Copilot Studio, Microsoft 365 Copilot, and other AI experiences), the data must live in a supported grounding store.\n\nFrom the options provided, the only store that AI systems can directly ground on is:\nMicrosoft Dataverse\n\nThe scenario already includes Dataverse, so the correct action is to populate a Dataverse table with the subset of corporate data you want to expose to AI.","pick":"A"},{"user":"Shafz007","date":"2026-10-09","up":1,"text":"Endorsing the semantic model marks it as promoted or certified, helping users identify trusted content and enabling discoverability. It does not itself configure the model as an AI grounding source. Microsoft Learn\nSo A. Populate a Dataverse table remains the best answer. The required data subset can then be configured as a Dataverse knowledge source.\nMy earlier explanation needed that distinction: populating the table prepares the data; adding it as a knowledge source enables grounding.","pick":"A"},{"user":"AxaptaKing1","date":"2026-10-01","up":1,"text":"Answer in this case is C but Its important to understand, Semantic Model Endorsement is not grounding itself, but it is a very useful governance mechanism that helps AI systems choose and rely on trusted data sources for grounding.","pick":"C"},{"user":"kinser123","date":"2026-09-29","up":1,"text":"Semantic Model Endorsement (Promoted or Certified): In Power BI and Fabric, endorsing a semantic model explicitly designates it as an authoritative, verified, and trusted dataset. Generative AI grounding mechanisms rely on endorsed/certified semantic models to ensure the AI retrieves validated corporate data rather than unverified sources.","pick":"C"},{"user":"VincentVega33","date":"2026-06-29","up":1,"text":"since its either A or C - A.\n\nA -Populate a Dataverse table\nSimply storing data in Dataverse does not make it a grounding source for AI. The AI needs a supported, trusted data source such as an endorsed semantic model.\n\nWheras C - Endorsing a semantic model (for example, marking it as Certified or Promoted) signals that it is a trusted, curated source of business data that AI can use to answer questions accurately.","pick":"C"}]},{"n":24,"id":994141,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A company plans to implement an AI business solution for a consumer goods company.</p><p>You need to create agents that meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Orchestrate the sales order fulfillment and shipping of goods to customers.</li><li>Analyze historical data and trends to replenish stock.</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which type of agent should you use for each requirement?</strong> To answer, drag the appropriate agent types to the correct requirements. Each agent type may be used once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to drag the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image45.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image46.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/6c60509ba23f9eb41501f0627c6ad022994141/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-30","up":18,"text":"Orchestrate the sales order fulfillment and shipping\n→ Autonomous agent\nThis scenario requires an agent that can coordinate multi‑step workflows, make decisions, trigger actions across systems, and manage an end‑to‑end operational process.\nThat is exactly what an autonomous agent is designed for.\n\nAnalyze historical data and trends to replenish stock\n→ Task agent\nTask agents are built for bounded, well‑defined analytical or computational tasks, not ongoing orchestration.","top":true},{"user":"Alicia_lili","date":"2026-05-04","up":7,"text":"Orchestrate the sales order fulfillment and shipping:\nAutonomous\n\nAnalyze historical data and trends:\nPrompt-and-response","top":true},{"user":"93c84b0","date":"2026-05-21","up":5,"text":"Orchestrate the sales order fulfillment and shipping of goods to customers ✅ Autonomous\nAnalyze historical data and trends to replenish stock ✅ Task"},{"user":"Xabia","date":"2026-05-08","up":3,"text":"Task Agent\nAutonomous Agent"},{"user":"AxaptaKing1","date":"2026-10-01","up":2,"text":"As per documentations answer should be:\nOrchestrate the sales order fulfilment and shipping - Autonomous\nAnalyze historical data and trends - Prompt-and-response"},{"user":"kinser123","date":"2026-09-29","up":2,"text":"Sales order fulfillment &amp; shipping → Autonomous : multi-step process\nHistorical data &amp; trends → Task : business task"},{"user":"Ninashnash","date":"2026-08-07","up":2,"text":"Orchestrate the sales order fulfillment and shipping: ✅ Autonomous\nAnalyze historical data and trends: ✅ Prompt-and-response","replies":[{"user":"Ninashnash","date":"2026-08-07","up":1,"text":"Why:\nAutonomous agents — designed to run multi-step processes independently, making decisions and taking actions across a workflow without requiring a user prompt at each step. Orchestrating sales order fulfillment and shipping involves a sequence of dependent actions (checking inventory, triggering fulfillment, coordinating shipping) that need to run end-to-end on their own — a classic autonomous agent scenario, typically triggered by an event (e.g., a new order) rather than a user question."}]},{"user":"a5f05ea","date":"2026-10-15","up":1,"text":"Sales order fulfillment and shipping: Autonomous\nHistorical data and trend analysis for stock replenishment: Task"},{"user":"Srikantha","date":"2026-09-29","up":1,"text":"According to official Microsoft architectural documentation and agent taxonomy patterns (such as those evaluated in Microsoft AI Business Solutions Architecture):\nOrchestrate the sales order fulfillment and shipping of goods to customers: Autonomous\nAnalyze historical data and trends to replenish stock: Task"},{"user":"Srikantha","date":"2026-09-29","up":1,"text":"According to official Microsoft architectural documentation and agent taxonomy patterns (such as those evaluated in Microsoft AI Business Solutions Architecture):\nOrchestrate the sales order fulfillment and shipping of goods to customers: Autonomous\nAnalyze historical data and trends to replenish stock: Task"},{"user":"Joselito79","date":"2026-09-22","up":1,"text":"✅ Drag:\n\nSales order fulfillment & shipping → Autonomous\nHistorical data & trends → Prompt-and-response"},{"user":"24b8eec","date":"2026-06-16","up":1,"text":"Orchestrate order fulfillment & shipping - Task - Bounded multi-step workflow, triggered per order, completes a defined job\nAnalyze trends & replenish stock - Autonomous - Proactive, event/threshold-driven, acts independently without a prompt\n\nRule of thumb: if the agent completes a specific job when asked/triggered, it's a task agent; if it watches, decides, and acts on its own, it's autonomous."},{"user":"wrak","date":"2026-06-05","up":1,"text":"2x Task - Autonomous is a high-risk process, so I wouldn't do that. But maybe MSFT thinks is mature solution from their side :)"}]},{"n":25,"id":994142,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A company has an AI agent that automates the review of customer feedback stored in a cloud database.</p><p>You plan to generate monthly reports from the agent's output to provide insights into customer sentiment and guide product development and marketing.</p><p>You need to ensure that the data ingested by the agent is clean and suitable for the intended use.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you do to prepare the data?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Create a workflow in Microsoft Power Automate."},{"k":"B","html":"Identify and address biased data."},{"k":"C","html":"Create an agent flow in Microsoft Copilot Studio."},{"k":"D","html":"Sort the database by customer last name."}],"answer":"B","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"B","p":100,"n":6}],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/7939a4296744d63ab71ad22511fbf681994142/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-30","up":4,"text":"The correct answer is B. Identify and address biased data.\n\nBefore generating monthly sentiment reports, the company must ensure that the customer feedback data is clean, representative, and free of bias. This is a core requirement in responsible AI and data preparation.\n\nThis step is explicitly emphasized in Microsoft’s AI readiness and data preparation guidance.","pick":"B"},{"user":"KathCha","date":"2026-05-03","up":3,"text":"I would go with B.","pick":"B"},{"user":"kinser123","date":"2026-09-29","up":1,"text":"I would go with B. - free of bias is first","pick":"B"},{"user":"Alicia_lili","date":"2026-04-29","up":1,"text":"It is B.","pick":"B"}],"variants":[33,39,44]},{"n":26,"id":994143,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A company is designing a Microsoft Power Platform solution to reduce the manual steps of a business process by deploying an existing AI model.</p><p>You need to calculate the return on AI investment (ROAI) by identifying the metadata and telemetry of the solution.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you use?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Microsoft Power Platform admin center"},{"k":"B","html":"Success by Design"},{"k":"C","html":"the Business value toolkit"},{"k":"D","html":"Microsoft Cloud Adoption Framework for Azure"}],"answer":"C","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"A","p":36,"n":5},{"a":"C","p":64,"n":9}],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/048910cf852842e86ec4246b435eb182994143/","comments":[{"user":"wrak","date":"2026-06-08","up":6,"text":"The Power Platform CoE Starter Kit is no longer actively maintained. Its core capabilities are part of the Power Platform admin center.","pick":"A"},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-30","up":5,"text":"The correct answer is: C. the Business value toolkit\n\nThe Business value toolkit is the only Microsoft tool designed specifically to:\n- Capture telemetry and metadata from Power Platform solutions\n- Model ROI and ROAI\n- Estimate TCO\n- Quantify expected savings\n- Support build vs buy vs extend decisions\n- Provide financial modeling templates for AI adoption","pick":"C"},{"user":"hi1011","date":"2026-04-22","up":4,"text":"\"The Business value toolkit is a collection of sample apps and processes designed to address these challenges. It provides a comprehensive framework to capture and communicate the value of Power Platform solutions effectively.\"\n\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-platform/guidance/coe/business-value-toolkit","pick":"C"},{"user":"slimexy","date":"2026-10-10","up":1,"text":"The Power Platform CoE Starter Kit is no longer actively maintained. Its core capabilities are part of the Power Platform admin center.\n\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-platform/guidance/coe/business-value-toolkit","pick":"A"},{"user":"fa62dd5","date":"2026-08-24","up":1,"text":"The Business value toolkit\n\nThe Business Value Toolkit is Microsoft's tool for calculating ROI (including return on AI investment) for Power Platform solutions by capturing solution metadata and telemetry. The admin center manages environments/governance, Success by Design is an architecture methodology, and the Cloud Adoption Framework applies to Azure, not Power Platform ROI calculation.","pick":"C"},{"user":"CyrilleC","date":"2026-07-29","up":1,"text":"I would choose C because the core capabilities of the Business Value Toolkit are now integrated into the Power Platform admin center. However, it is still possible to use the Business Value Toolkit directly.","pick":"C"}]},{"n":27,"id":994144,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A company has a Microsoft Power Platform environment.</p><p>You need to build two agents named Agent1 and Agent2. The solution must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Agent1 must be extendable by using the Semantic Kernel and must connect to multiple business apps and APIs.</li><li>Agent2 must connect directly to data stored in Microsoft Dataverse and must be embeddable in a Microsoft Power Apps canvas app.</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you use to build each agent?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image47.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image48.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/92bb70ef9911d2790fbe6725dabf4e89994144/","comments":[{"user":"2db2984","date":"2026-05-03","up":15,"text":"Should be Agent1 -> MS Foundry\nAgent 2 -> Micorosoft Copilot Studio (enables building agents that natively connect to Dataverse and can be embedded into Power Apps.)","top":true},{"user":"hi1011","date":"2026-04-22","up":11,"text":"Agent 1 -> MS Foundry\nAgent 2 -> Copilot in Power Apps\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-apps/maker/canvas-apps/microsoft-365-copilot-canvas-app","top":true,"replies":[{"user":"ziggy1117","date":"2026-07-02","up":5,"text":"Agent 2 - copilot studio is right answer.\nCopilot in Power Apps is wrong.\nCopilot in Power Apps lets you quickly build apps using natural language. Describe your business needs, and the service generates an app and data model for you—no coding required. People interact with your app by asking questions or giving commands in everyday language, making the experience more intuitive and engaging.\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-apps/maker/canvas-apps/ai-overview"}]},{"user":"Joselito79","date":"2026-09-22","up":5,"text":"Explanation\nAgent1 → Microsoft Foundry: Provides capabilities for building and extending AI agents, including integration with Semantic Kernel and connections to business applications and APIs.\nAgent2 → Copilot in Power Apps: Designed to work directly with Dataverse and can be embedded within Power Apps canvas apps."},{"user":"Srikantha","date":"2026-09-29","up":3,"text":"The correct selections for each requirement are:\nAgent1: Microsoft Foundry\nAgent2: Microsoft Copilot Studio"},{"user":"Mija","date":"2026-09-28","up":3,"text":"Agent1 → Microsoft Foundry\nAgent2 → Copilot in Power Apps"},{"user":"wrak","date":"2026-06-08","up":3,"text":"Agent 1 - via Foundry. Semantic Kernel (or the newer Microsoft Agent Framework) runs outside Copilot Studio, as your own agent runtime."},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-30","up":3,"text":"Agent1 → Microsoft Foundry\nAgent1 must:\n- Be extendable using Semantic Kernel\n- Connect to multiple business apps and APIs\n- Support complex orchestration and multi‑agent patterns\nThese are exactly the capabilities of Microsoft Foundry, which is designed for enterprise‑grade, extensible, multi‑agent AI systems with deep integration into Semantic Kernel.\n\nAgent2 → Copilot in Power Apps\nWhy:\nAgent2 must:\n- Connect directly to Dataverse\n- Be embeddable in a Power Apps canvas app\nThis is precisely what Copilot in Power Apps is built for."},{"user":"Alicia_lili","date":"2026-05-04","up":2,"text":"Agent1: Microsoft Copilot Studio\nAgent2: Copilot in Power Apps"},{"user":"deca0d4","date":"2026-04-28","up":2,"text":"Agent1 use Foundry: Use Foundry when you need a more developer-oriented/custom agent architecture, advanced orchestration, Semantic Kernel, custom tools, custom code, or deeper app integration. Semantic Kernel provides an agent framework, and Microsoft documentation describes using Semantic Kernel with Foundry/agents.\nAgent2 use Copilot for Power Apps: Copilot Studio creates the custom agent. Power Apps lets you add a custom Copilot Studio copilot to a canvas app."},{"user":"a5f05ea","date":"2026-10-15","up":1,"text":"Agent1 Extendable using Semantic Kernel + multiple business apps/APIs: Microsoft Foundry\nAgent2 Direct Dataverse connection + embedded in Power Apps canvas app: Copilot in Power Apps"},{"user":"554b579","date":"2026-09-18","up":1,"text":"Agent1\n\nMicrosoft Foundry — TRUE. Semantic Kernel is a pro-code orchestration SDK, and the Foundry Agent Service is the agent platform designed to be extended with it. Foundry agents also attach tools for APIs and business systems, matching the second half of the requirement."},{"user":"TheMCT","date":"2026-08-06","up":1,"text":"Agent1 - MIcrosoft Foundry\nAgent2 - Copilot in Power Apps\nMicrosoft Foundry -> supports building advanced AI agents that can be extended with Semantic Kernel and integrated with APIs, business applications, and enterprise services.\nCopilot in Power Apps - > is designed to work with Dataverse data and can be embedded directly into canvas apps for end-user interaction."}]},{"n":28,"id":994145,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A company has an Azure environment that supports multiple business units.</p><p>The company plans to implement an AI solution that will perform sentiment analysis on customer product reviews.</p><p>You need to evaluate the potential cost of the solution to support return on AI investment (ROAI) analysis.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you use?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Cost Management + Billing"},{"k":"B","html":"Microsoft Fabric SKU Estimator"},{"k":"C","html":"Total Cost of Ownership (TCO) Calculator"},{"k":"D","html":"Azure Reservations"}],"answer":"C","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"A","p":50,"n":8},{"a":"C","p":50,"n":8}],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/7fd59076e9498791e486a99a6fe6e683994145/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-30","up":5,"text":"✅ Correct Answer: A. Cost Management + Billing\n\nTo evaluate the potential cost of an AI solution running in Azure — especially for ROAI (Return on AI Investment) — you need visibility into:\n- Current Azure resource consumption\n- Forecasted costs\n- Cost trends\n- Service‑level spending\n- Budget alerts\n- Cost allocation by business unit\nCost Management + Billing is the Azure-native tool that provides exactly this.","pick":"A"},{"user":"fa62dd5","date":"2026-08-24","up":4,"text":"C. Total Cost of Ownership (TCO) Calculator\n\nThe TCO Calculator is designed to estimate the potential/projected cost of a planned solution before deployment — exactly what's needed to feed a ROAI analysis. Cost Management + Billing tracks actual costs of resources already running, the Fabric SKU Estimator is specific to Fabric capacity SKUs (not general Azure AI costs), and Azure Reservations is a discount-purchasing mechanism, not a cost-evaluation tool.","pick":"C"},{"user":"wrak","date":"2026-06-08","up":3,"text":"Question is asking for \"potential cost\", so C","pick":"C"},{"user":"Joselito79","date":"2026-09-17","up":2,"text":"The correct answer is always Azure pricing calculator when it's listed (it estimates the cost of a future Azure solution for ROAI); when it isn't listed, the intended answer is Cost Management + Billing.","pick":"A"},{"user":"deca0d4","date":"2026-04-28","up":2,"text":"Total Cost of Ownership Calculator: Use when you need to compare current/on-premises or existing costs against expected cloud costs and savings","pick":"C"},{"user":"kinser123","date":"2026-09-29","up":1,"text":"I would go with C","pick":"C"},{"user":"TheMCT","date":"2026-08-06","up":1,"text":"The key issue with C is that the TCO Calculator is specifically intended to estimate cost savings from migrating existing workloads to Azure. It requires information about current on-premises infrastructure and compares it to Azure.\n\nIn the scenario:\n\nThere is already an Azure environment.\nThe company wants a new AI sentiment analysis solution.\nThere is no mention of migrating an existing workload from on-premises.\nThe goal is ROAI analysis, not migration analysis.\n\nTherefore, Microsoft expects you to use the Azure cost-management capability rather than a migration-cost comparison tool. Cost Management includes forecasting and cost allocation across business units, which is also mentioned in the scenario.","pick":"A"},{"user":"CertiMaster101912","date":"2026-05-22","up":1,"text":"For AI related costs this fits better. We’re not comparing purely infra components.","pick":"A"}],"variants":[34,35,36,37,38]},{"n":29,"id":994146,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You need to recommend a Microsoft Power Platform solution for customer support. The solution must include AI capabilities in Microsoft Power Automate and must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Use a centralized workspace for AI models.</li><li>Generate short overviews from large amounts of unstructured text, such as case notes or transcripts, without requiring additional training or coding.</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you include in the recommendation for each requirement?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image49.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image50.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/89a87b2765c17b4126df3b692d2bacb8994146/","comments":[{"user":"Alicia_lili","date":"2026-05-04","up":11,"text":"Centralized workspace: Azure OpenAI Foundry\nGenerate short overviews: An AI Builder prebuilt prompt","top":true},{"user":"TheMCT","date":"2026-08-06","up":6,"text":"Centralized workspace: An Microsoft Foundry hub\nShort overviews: An AI Builder prebuilt prompt"},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-30","up":4,"text":"✔ Use a centralized workspace → Microsoft Dataverse\nIn Power Platform, the AI Hub is built on Dataverse and acts as the centralized workspace for:\n- Managing AI models\n- Managing AI Builder models\n- Managing prompts\n- Managing AI assets used in Power Automate and Power Apps\nNeither Foundry option is part of Power Platform, and Copilot Studio is for agents, not centralized AI model management.\n\n✔ Generate short overviews → AI Builder prebuilt prompt\nThe requirement is:\n- Generate short overviews\n- From large unstructured text (case notes, transcripts)\n- Without training\n- Without coding\nThis is exactly what AI Builder prebuilt prompts are designed for."},{"user":"Xabia","date":"2026-05-08","up":4,"text":"Azure AI Foundry\nAI Builder prebuilt prompt"},{"user":"Srikantha","date":"2026-09-29","up":2,"text":"The correct selections for each requirement are:\nUse a centralized workspace: An Microsoft Foundry hub\nGenerate short overviews: An AI Builder prebuilt prompt"},{"user":"Aarch","date":"2026-08-05","up":1,"text":"1.Centralized workspace for AI models - AI Hub provides a centralized location in Power Platform for managing and accessing AI capabilities and models.\n2.Short Overviews -Summarize large amounts of unstructured text - AI Builder includes the AI Summarize prebuilt prompt, which can summarize emails, documents, transcripts, and other text."},{"user":"ziggy1117","date":"2026-07-02","up":1,"text":"Generate short overviews - prebuilt prompt\nAISummarize - Summarize the text that you provide.\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/ai-builder/prebuilt-prompts#input-for-aisummarize"},{"user":"SophieMo","date":"2026-05-27","up":1,"text":"1. Copilot Studio - Part of Power Platform, uses solutions, can be integrated with Power Automate\n2. An AI Builder prebuilt prompt"}]},{"n":30,"id":994147,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A company uses Microsoft Dynamics 365 Finance for accounts payable and customer debt recovery.</p><p>You are designing an AI finance process that meets the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Provides AI-driven details to help staff identify overdue vendor invoices and outstanding balances</li><li>Helps staff reduce how long it takes to review overdue invoices and payment history</li></ul><p>You need to recommend which Microsoft Copilot features to include in the design.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you recommend for each requirement?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image51.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image52.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/6430cf92082d66d3d8082bd1fba1847e994147/","comments":[{"user":"hi1011","date":"2026-04-22","up":15,"text":"Help Id Vendor Overdue: B (AI Summaries with Copilot)\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/supply-chain/get-started/copilot-summaries-overview\n\nReduce how long it takes sales: B (collections coordinator summary)\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/finance/accounts-receivable/collectionscoordinatorsummary","top":true},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-30","up":5,"text":"1. Help identify vendor overdue invoices and outstanding balances\n→ The Supplier Communication agent\nThis agent is designed for vendor-facing processes in Dynamics 365 Finance.\n- Identify overdue vendor invoices\n- Track outstanding balances\n- Communicate with suppliers\n- Automate follow-ups\n\n2. Reduce how long it takes to review overdue invoices and payment history\n→ Collections coordinator summary\nThe Collections Coordinator Copilot feature provides:\n- AI‑generated summaries of customer payment history\n- Overdue invoice insights\n- Quick review of aging and collection status\n- Faster decision‑making for debt recovery"},{"user":"297bbbc","date":"2026-04-30","up":3,"text":"Help identify vendor overdue invoices and outstanding balances: The Supplier Communication agent\nWhy: In accounts payable scenarios, the Supplier Communication agent in Dynamics 365 Finance helps AP staff surface and act on vendor-related issues (e.g., overdue invoices, balances) and streamlines communications with suppliers.\n\nReduce how long it takes to review overdue invoices and payment history: Collections coordinator summary\nWhy: For customer debt recovery (accounts receivable), the Collections coordinator summary provides AI‑generated overviews of a customer’s overdue balances, payment history, and recommended actions, cutting review time."},{"user":"Joselito79","date":"2026-09-22","up":2,"text":"Vendor/AP information → AI Summaries with Copilot\nCustomer debt/collections + payment history → Collections coordinator summary\n\nSo your selections are:\n\n1️⃣ AI Summaries with Copilot\n2️⃣ Collections coordinator summary"},{"user":"wrak","date":"2026-06-08","up":2,"text":"Tricky because question is about D365 Finance, where AI Summaries with Copilot are quite limited vs SCM where exactly the Vendor outstanding details would be presented."},{"user":"Srikantha","date":"2026-09-29","up":1,"text":"Based on the capabilities of Microsoft Dynamics 365 Finance and Copilot features, here are the correct selections for the requirements\nHelp identify vendor overdue invoices and outstanding balances: AI Summaries with Copilot\nReasoning: AI summaries with Copilot provide quick, personalized overviews on key pages, including specific details like the number of overdue invoices and outstanding balances for a vendor.\nReduce how long it takes to review overdue invoices and payment history: Collections coordinator summary\nReasoning: The Collections coordinator summary is designed specifically for customer debt recovery. It displays AI-generated text in the Collections coordinator workspace to help users quickly review customer payment history and overdue invoice statuses."},{"user":"554b579","date":"2026-09-21","up":1,"text":"AI Summaries with Copilot — TRUE. Hovering over a vendor number generates a Copilot summary combining key data from transaction history to overdue invoices. The vendor summary also surfaces hold status, posted vendor invoices, and payment status, which is the accounts payable side of the scenario.\nThe Account Reconciliation agent — FALSE. Matches ledger entries against bank statements and resolves small differences. Valuable, but it reconciles accounts rather than identifying overdue vendor invoices."},{"user":"554b579","date":"2026-09-21","up":1,"text":"A Microsoft Foundry hub — TRUE. A hub is the top-level Foundry resource providing a shared workspace where a team collaborates across projects, with pooled models, connections, and compute governed in one place. “Centralized workspace for AI models” is the literal definition of a hub.\n\nAzure OpenAI Foundry — FALSE. Not a workspace construct, and not a current product name. Azure OpenAI is a model service consumed inside Foundry, not the container that organizes models."},{"user":"Ninashnash","date":"2026-08-09","up":1,"text":"Vendor + overdue vendor invoices → AI Summaries with Copilot\nCustomer + overdue invoices + payment history + collections → Collections coordinator summary"},{"user":"deca0d4","date":"2026-04-28","up":1,"text":"Help ID overdue accounts: Account Reconciliation Agent\nWhat it does:\nMatches transactions across systems\nFlags discrepancies\nAssists with financial reconciliation\n\nReduce time : AI summaries with Copilot: Use it when You need:\nFaster decision-making\nReduced manual reading\nKey insights extracted quickly"}]},{"n":31,"id":994148,"topic":1,"stem":"<p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which two components in the custom AI agent design should the CFO evaluate in the quarterly agent analysis?</strong> Each correct answer presents part of the solution.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"the GPT models used for the agent"},{"k":"B","html":"the average characters in a chat message"},{"k":"C","html":"the agent orchestration method"},{"k":"D","html":"the average session time per agent"}],"answer":"AC","type":"multi","votes":[{"a":"AC","p":43,"n":6},{"a":"BD","p":21,"n":3},{"a":"CD","p":36,"n":5}],"page":1,"case":"8b997de433","thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/b40776907ac97fd6a16b58d358b01c40994148/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-30","up":6,"text":"✅ C. the agent orchestration method\nThis affects how many model calls, how complex the reasoning steps are, and how many credits are consumed per interaction.\n- Multi-agent orchestration, tool calls, and reasoning depth all impact cost.\n- The usage estimator explicitly evaluates orchestration patterns because they change the total cost per session.\n\n✅ D. the average session time per agent\nSession duration is a direct cost driver because longer sessions typically involve:\n- More turns\n- More model calls\n- More grounding queries\n- More tool invocations","pick":"CD"},{"user":"atyachter","date":"2026-07-15","up":5,"text":"These are the two components that directly drive Copilot Studio credit consumption, which is what the CFO's ROI analysis is built around.\n\n---GPT models used: Different underlying models (e.g., GPT-4 vs. a lighter model) consume Copilot Studio credits at different rates. Since the scenario has the CFO comparing estimated ROI to actual measured cost/efficiency using the Copilot Studio agent usage estimator, the model choice is a direct cost driver worth reevaluating each quarter.\n---Agent orchestration method: How the agent routes and resolves requests (e.g., classic trigger-phrase/topic-based orchestration vs. generative/autonomous orchestration that uses an LLM to select topics based on description) also has a material impact on credit usage per session, since generative orchestration typically consumes more credits per interaction than simple topic matching.","pick":"AC"},{"user":"Xabia","date":"2026-05-08","up":4,"text":"The CFO is focused on ROI analysis and efficiency of AI agent usage:\nB->Copilot Studio consumption is partly influenced by message size (tokens/characters)\nD->Session duration relates to Agent effectiveness","pick":"BD"},{"user":"hi1011","date":"2026-04-22","up":4,"text":"A. the GPT models used for the agent — Copilot Studio billing includes reasoning model billing rates, and Microsoft notes that Copilot Credit consumption depends on the agent’s design and the features it uses. That means the model choice affects quarterly usage/cost analysis.\n\nC. the agent orchestration method — Microsoft explicitly says the agent usage estimator creates estimates by selecting from agent type, traffic, orchestration, knowledge, and tools, so orchestration is a direct design factor the CFO should evaluate.\n\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-copilot-studio/requirements-messages-management","pick":"AC"},{"user":"a5f05ea","date":"2026-10-15","up":1,"text":"✅ A. the GPT models used for the agent\n✅ C. the agent orchestration method","pick":"AC"},{"user":"Ninashnash","date":"2026-08-09","up":1,"text":"Microsoft's current guidance for the Copilot Studio agent usage estimator. It says the estimator uses:\nAgent type\nExpected traffic\nOrchestration mode\nKnowledge sources\nTools\nto estimate monthly Copilot Credit consumption.","pick":"CD"}]},{"n":32,"id":994149,"topic":1,"stem":"<p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you configure for the custom AI agent?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"AI-assisted evaluators"},{"k":"B","html":"classic orchestration"},{"k":"C","html":"generative orchestration"},{"k":"D","html":"Azure OpenAI reasoning models"}],"answer":"C","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"C","p":100,"n":4}],"page":1,"case":"8b997de433","thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/e8b742e15bc2aa14e92384b3741fcaef994149/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-30","up":4,"text":"Answer: C. generative orchestration\n\n- Use topics selected based on a description, not a trigger phrase → this is a generative topic router capability.\n- Be conversational, selecting topics based on the purpose of the query → this is only supported by generative orchestration.\n- Connect to other agents selected by description → again, generative orchestration.\nUse Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management business logic stored outside the application → generative orchestration can call actions, connectors, and external logic.\n- Answer questions using existing R&D product specifications → generative orchestration supports grounding and multi-source reasoning.","pick":"C"}]},{"n":33,"id":999649,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A company has an AI agent that automates the review of customer feedback stored in a cloud database.</p><p>You plan to generate monthly reports from the agent's output to provide insights into customer sentiment and guide product development and marketing.</p><p>You need to ensure that the data ingested by the agent is clean and suitable for the intended use.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you do to prepare the data?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Ensure that the size of the database does not exceed 100 GB."},{"k":"B","html":"Translate the data into a single language."},{"k":"C","html":"Identify and address biased data."},{"k":"D","html":"Sort the database by customer last name."}],"answer":"C","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"C","p":100,"n":2}],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/9e3b9be7b9decfcf52b69f869b18d688999649/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-30","up":2,"text":"The correct answer is C. Identify and address biased data.\n\nFor an AI agent performing sentiment analysis on customer feedback, the most important data‑quality step is ensuring that the dataset is:\n- Representative\n- Unbiased\n- Fair\n- Suitable for downstream analytics","pick":"C"}],"variants":[25,39,44]},{"n":34,"id":999650,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A company has an Azure environment that supports multiple business units.</p><p>The company plans to implement an AI solution that will perform sentiment analysis on customer product reviews.</p><p>You need to evaluate the potential cost of the solution to support return on AI investment (ROAI) analysis.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you use?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Total Cost of Ownership (TCO) Calculator"},{"k":"B","html":"Azure Reservations"},{"k":"C","html":"Azure pricing calculator"},{"k":"D","html":"Azure Monitor"}],"answer":"C","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"C","p":100,"n":3}],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/20acfb1a3661a7c4284dfc9ad2a5b1ef999650/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-30","up":4,"text":"✅ Correct Answer: C. Azure pricing calculator\n\nTo evaluate the potential cost of a new AI workload — before deployment — you need a tool that can:\n- Estimate the cost of Azure services you plan to use\n- Model different configurations\n- Forecast monthly and annual spend\n- Support early‑stage ROAI calculations\n- The Azure pricing calculator is specifically designed for pre‑deployment cost estimation.","pick":"C"}],"variants":[28,35,36,37,38]},{"n":35,"id":999651,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A company has an Azure environment that supports multiple business units.</p><p>The company plans to implement an AI solution that will perform sentiment analysis on customer product reviews.</p><p>You need to evaluate the potential cost of the solution to support return on AI investment (ROAI) analysis.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you use?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Azure savings plans"},{"k":"B","html":"Microsoft Fabric SKU Estimator"},{"k":"C","html":"Cost Management + Billing"},{"k":"D","html":"Azure Monitor"}],"answer":"C","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"C","p":100,"n":3}],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/d018bd93bb7ddb1d82b6dce718421874999651/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-30","up":4,"text":"✅ Correct Answer: Cost Management + Billing\n\nTo evaluate potential cost for an AI workload (sentiment analysis on product reviews) across multiple business units, you need:\n- Forecasted Azure spend\n- Cost breakdown by resource, tag, or business unit\n- Budget alerts\n- Usage analytics\n- Chargeback/showback support\nCost Management + Billing is the only option that provides all of this.\nIt is specifically used for ongoing and projected Azure cost analysis, which is essential for ROAI.","pick":"C"}],"variants":[28,34,36,37,38]},{"n":36,"id":999652,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A company has an Azure environment that supports multiple business units.</p><p>The company plans to implement an AI solution that will perform sentiment analysis on customer product reviews.</p><p>You need to evaluate the potential cost of the solution to support return on AI investment (ROAI) analysis.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you use?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Azure Reservations"},{"k":"B","html":"Microsoft Fabric SKU Estimator"},{"k":"C","html":"Anomaly Detection in Azure Cost Management"},{"k":"D","html":"Azure pricing calculator"}],"answer":"D","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"D","p":100,"n":2}],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/937174ccb0a2c3e2048674e505f0c5d1999652/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-30","up":2,"text":"The correct answer is D. Azure pricing calculator.\n\nTo evaluate the potential cost of a new AI workload (sentiment analysis on product reviews), you need a tool that:\n- Estimates future Azure service costs\n- Models different configurations (compute, storage, AI services)\n- Supports pre‑deployment ROAI calculations\n- Works across multiple business units\n\nThe Azure pricing calculator is the only option designed specifically for forecasting the cost of planned Azure services before you deploy anything.\n\nThis is exactly what ROAI requires.","pick":"D"}],"variants":[28,34,35,37,38]},{"n":37,"id":1012337,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A company has an Azure environment that supports multiple business units.</p><p>The company plans to implement an AI solution that will perform sentiment analysis on customer product reviews.</p><p>You need to evaluate the potential cost of the solution to support return on AI investment (ROAI) analysis.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you use?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Anomaly Detection in Azure Cost Management"},{"k":"B","html":"Azure pricing calculator"},{"k":"C","html":"Azure savings plans"},{"k":"D","html":"Microsoft Fabric SKU Estimator"}],"answer":"B","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"B","p":100,"n":1}],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/d9f7616c95c1ad2e8e286107d6acc7e51012337/","comments":[{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-10","up":1,"text":"Option B: Azure pricing calculator is correct.\n\nThe Azure pricing calculator is designed specifically to estimate expected costs before deploying a solution. It allows you to model anticipated usage (e.g., number of API calls for AI sentiment analysis) to project overall expenditure, which is required to calculate expected Return on AI Investment (ROAI).","pick":"B"}],"variants":[28,34,35,36,38]},{"n":38,"id":1012338,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A company has an Azure environment that supports multiple business units.</p><p>The company plans to implement an AI solution that will perform sentiment analysis on customer product reviews.</p><p>You need to evaluate the potential cost of the solution to support return on AI investment (ROAI) analysis.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you use?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Azure savings plans"},{"k":"B","html":"Anomaly Detection in Azure Cost Management"},{"k":"C","html":"Azure Monitor"},{"k":"D","html":"Cost Management + Billing"}],"answer":"D","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"D","p":100,"n":1}],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/afd475bfb4df89735baac618708f4afb1012338/","comments":[{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-10","up":1,"text":"Cost Management + Billing in Azure is the best choice for evaluating the potential cost of an AI solution and supporting Return on AI Investment (ROAI) analysis.\n\nIt helps organizations:\n\nEstimate and analyze Azure costs.\n\nTrack spending across multiple business units.\n\nUnderstand resource usage and costs.\n\nCreate budgets and monitor expenses.\n\nA. Azure savings plans → Helps reduce costs through committed usage.\n\nB. Anomaly Detection → Identifies unusual spending patterns.\n\nC. Azure Monitor → Monitors application and resource performance.\n\nD. Cost Management + Billing ✅ → Provides tools for analyzing and managing Azure costs.\n\n👉 Final Answer: D. Cost Management + Billing","pick":"D"}],"variants":[28,34,35,36,37]},{"n":39,"id":1012339,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A company has an AI agent that automates the review of customer feedback stored in a cloud database.</p><p>You plan to generate monthly reports from the agent's output to provide insights into customer sentiment and guide product development and marketing.</p><p>You need to ensure that the data ingested by the agent is clean and suitable for the intended use.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you do to prepare the data?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Identify and address missing or inconsistent data."},{"k":"B","html":"Sort the database by customer last name."},{"k":"C","html":"Ensure that the size of the database does not exceed 100 GB."},{"k":"D","html":"Verify data privacy and security compliance."}],"answer":"A","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"A","p":100,"n":1}],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/d984edccb603c2880e59aae500524b381012339/","comments":[{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-10","up":1,"text":"Before using customer feedback for AI analysis, the data should be clean, accurate, and consistent. Missing values, duplicate records, or inconsistent formats can affect the agent’s results and lead to inaccurate customer sentiment insights.\n\nWhy not D? Privacy and security compliance is important, but the question specifically asks how to ensure the data is clean and suitable for use.\n\nIn short: Clean data → Better AI analysis → More reliable reports and insights.\n\n✅ Answer: A. Identify and address missing or inconsistent data.","pick":"A"}],"variants":[25,33,44]},{"n":40,"id":1012340,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A company uses multiple Microsoft Copilot Studio agents across different channels.</p><p>You need to recommend a monitoring solution that provides comprehensive telemetry data and performance insights for the agents.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you include in the recommendation?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Azure DevOps"},{"k":"B","html":"Microsoft Power BI"},{"k":"C","html":"Microsoft Dynamics 365 Customer Voice"},{"k":"D","html":"Application Insights"}],"answer":"D","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"D","p":100,"n":1}],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/f2ea8677f4c472760d940be74e2d7cca1012340/","comments":[{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-10","up":1,"text":"Option D: Application Insights is correct.\n\nOption D (Correct): Microsoft Copilot Studio (formerly Power Virtual Agents) integrates natively with Azure Application Insights to capture comprehensive telemetry data, including bot events, user messages, custom traces, system errors, and overall performance metrics across channels.","pick":"D"}],"variants":[41,42,43,98,110,120]},{"n":41,"id":1012341,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A company uses multiple Microsoft Copilot Studio agents across different channels.</p><p>You need to recommend a monitoring solution that provides comprehensive telemetry data and performance insights for the agents.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you include in the recommendation?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"the Analytics tab in Copilot Studio"},{"k":"B","html":"Microsoft Power BI"},{"k":"C","html":"Microsoft Dynamics 365 Customer Voice"},{"k":"D","html":"Microsoft Purview"}],"answer":"A","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"A","p":86,"n":6},{"a":"D","p":14,"n":1}],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/38f3988123faf10ee0ac9eacaaf8e9861012341/","comments":[{"user":"kevinirl","date":"2026-08-22","up":3,"text":"The question asks for a monitoring solution that provides comprehensive telemetry data and performance insights for Copilot Studio agents across channels.\n\nThe Analytics overview - Microsoft Copilot Studio documentation states that the Analytics page in Copilot Studio shows comprehensive data for an agent, including key metrics, usage analytics, performance information, and detailed insights that can be drilled into for further analysis.\n\nMicrosoft also states that the Analytics tab provides detailed insights into:\n\nAgent performance\nUser interactions\nUsage trends\nRun outcomes\nKnowledge source usage\nSatisfaction scores\n\nThese analytics are specifically designed for monitoring Copilot Studio agents.","pick":"A"},{"user":"AC888","date":"2026-08-22","up":2,"text":"revised the options: A looks more appropriate than D.\nCopilot Studio Analytics page provides comprehensive data for an agent, including key metrics and in-depth usage analytics.","pick":"A"},{"user":"67eaf51","date":"2026-09-04","up":1,"text":"The name of the tab for the Copilot Studio agent is nowadays \"Monitor\". I guess it used to be named \"Analytics\".","pick":"A"},{"user":"AC888","date":"2026-08-22","up":1,"text":"Microsoft Purview is primarily for compliance, auditing, governance and security, including auditing Copilot Studio activities. Microsoft documents that Purview can audit both agent authoring and agent usage.","pick":"D"}],"variants":[40,42,43,98,110,120]},{"n":42,"id":1012342,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A company uses multiple Microsoft Copilot Studio agents across different channels.</p><p>You need to recommend a monitoring solution that provides comprehensive telemetry data and performance insights for the agents.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you include in the recommendation?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Azure Advisor"},{"k":"B","html":"Microsoft Dynamics 365 Customer Voice"},{"k":"C","html":"Application Insights"},{"k":"D","html":"Log Analytics"}],"answer":"C","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"C","p":67,"n":2},{"a":"D","p":33,"n":1}],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/7ae91660671c694abc4bf0e9f4c5984c1012342/","comments":[{"user":"Joselito79","date":"2026-09-17","up":2,"text":"Rule of thumb: \"comprehensive telemetry + performance insights\" → Application Insights whenever it appears; if it doesn't, Log Analytics (also deep Azure Monitor telemetry) beats non-monitoring options; and when neither is offered, the Analytics tab in Copilot Studio is the built-in fallback. Power BI just visualizes, Customer Voice collects feedback, Purview is governance/compliance, Azure Advisor gives recommendations — none provide agent telemetry.","pick":"C"},{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-10","up":1,"text":"Diagnostic analysis helps identify why something happened by examining historical data and finding patterns or causes.\n\nHere, the analyst is reviewing employee retention data to identify patterns that can be studied further, making diagnostic analysis the best choice.\n\nA. Predictive → Predicts future outcomes.\nB. Prescriptive → Recommends actions to take.\nC. Diagnostic ✅ → Finds reasons, patterns, and causes.\nD. Descriptive → Summarizes what happened.\n👉 Final Answer: C. Diagnostic","pick":"D"}],"variants":[40,41,43,98,110,120]},{"n":43,"id":1012343,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A company uses multiple Microsoft Copilot Studio agents across different channels.</p><p>You need to recommend a monitoring solution that provides comprehensive telemetry data and performance insights for the agents.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you include in the recommendation?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"the Analytics tab in Copilot Studio"},{"k":"B","html":"Azure Advisor"},{"k":"C","html":"Log Analytics"},{"k":"D","html":"Microsoft Purview"}],"answer":"C","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"A","p":20,"n":1},{"a":"C","p":80,"n":4}],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/6ffa585dd3bb07e19c3e842f785949c51012343/","comments":[{"user":"Joselito79","date":"2026-09-17","up":3,"text":"Rule of thumb: \"comprehensive telemetry + performance insights\" → Application Insights whenever it appears; if it doesn't, Log Analytics (also deep Azure Monitor telemetry) beats non-monitoring options; and when neither is offered, the Analytics tab in Copilot Studio is the built-in fallback. Power BI just visualizes, Customer Voice collects feedback, Purview is governance/compliance, Azure Advisor gives recommendations — none provide agent telemetry.","pick":"C"},{"user":"Brody","date":"2026-10-05","up":1,"text":"The Analytics tab provides built-in monitoring for Copilot Studio agents, including:\n- Agent and conversation performance\n- Engagement and usage\n- Resolution and abandonment rates\n- User interactions across channels\n- Topic/agent effectiveness and performance trends\nThe other choices don't provide the native, comprehensive agent-performance analytics being asked for:\n- B. Azure Advisor — Azure resource optimization recommendations\n- C. Log Analytics — useful for querying Azure Monitor logs, but isn't the primary built-in Copilot Studio monitoring solution\n- D. Microsoft Purview — governance, compliance, and data security\n✅ Answer: A. the Analytics tab in Copilot Studio\nThis question is subtly different from the previous one: Application Insights was the answer when it was available and the emphasis was on detailed telemetry. Here, among these choices, Copilot Studio Analytics is the correct monitoring/performance solution.","pick":"A"},{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-10","up":1,"text":"Option C. Log Analytics is correct.\n\nOption C (Correct): Log Analytics (which stores Application Insights telemetry for Azure and Power Platform workloads) enables querying, aggregating, and monitoring telemetry across multiple Copilot Studio agents at scale using Kusto Query Language (KQL). It provides deep visibility into performance, execution logs, custom events, and agent runtime errors across channels.","pick":"C"}],"variants":[40,41,42,98,110,120]},{"n":44,"id":1012344,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>A company has an AI agent that automates the review of customer feedback stored in a cloud database.</p><p>You plan to generate monthly reports from the agent's output to provide insights into customer sentiment and guide product development and marketing.</p><p>You need to ensure that the data ingested by the agent is clean and suitable for the intended use.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you do to prepare the data?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Identify and address biased data."},{"k":"B","html":"Ensure that the size of the database does not exceed 100 GB."},{"k":"C","html":"Verify data privacy and security compliance."},{"k":"D","html":"Translate the data into a single language."}],"answer":"A","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"A","p":100,"n":2}],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/95dbce89e05f9717abae1b32cd22fa721012344/","comments":[{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-10","up":3,"text":"The data should be clean, accurate, and representative before it is used by an AI agent. Identifying and addressing biased data helps ensure that the customer sentiment analysis produces fair and reliable results.\n\nA. Identify and address biased data ✅ → Improves the quality and reliability of AI results.\nB. Database size under 100 GB ❌ → Database size does not determine data quality.\nC. Privacy and security compliance ❌ → Important, but it focuses on protection and compliance rather than data cleanliness.\nD. Translate into one language ❌ → Not always necessary and does not itself ensure clean data.\nAnswer: A. Identify and Address Biased Data","pick":"A"}],"variants":[25,33,39]},{"n":45,"id":984447,"topic":2,"stem":"<p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which template should you use for the AI agent to meet the requirements for the sales executives?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"IT Helpdesk in Microsoft Copilot Studio"},{"k":"B","html":"AI agents in Microsoft Foundry"},{"k":"C","html":"Voice in Microsoft Copilot Studio"},{"k":"D","html":"AI chat in Microsoft Foundry"}],"answer":"C","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"C","p":100,"n":6}],"page":1,"case":"d646994a1b","thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/389e7e7433a9982dd8754bca4bad54ca984447/","comments":[{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":5,"text":"C. Voice in Microsoft Copilot Studio is the only template that satisfies all of Fabrikam’s requirements:\n• Hands‑free voice interaction\n• Microsoft‑recommended conversational UX\n• Dataverse integration\n• Telemetry and auditing\n• Escalation logic\n• Supports rapid adoption and ROI tracking\n\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-copilot-studio/voice-build-from-template?utm_source=copilot.com","pick":"C"},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-30","up":3,"text":"✅ Correct answer: C. Voice in Microsoft Copilot Studio\n\nThe case study states that sales executives will use hands‑free headsets to interact with the AI agent.\n\nThis template is specifically designed for:\n- Voice‑enabled conversational agents\n- Headset or microphone‑based interaction\n- Real‑time Q&A\n- Hands‑free workflows for field or sales scenarios\n\nExactly what Fabrikam’s sales executives need.","pick":"C"}]},{"n":46,"id":984448,"topic":2,"stem":"<p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which tool should you use for the prospect communication requirements in Dynamics 365 Sales?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Azure AI Search"},{"k":"B","html":"Copilot email assist"},{"k":"C","html":"the Voice template Microsoft Copilot Studio"},{"k":"D","html":"Deep Research in Microsoft Foundry Agent Service"}],"answer":"B","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"B","p":100,"n":5}],"page":1,"case":"d646994a1b","thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/4dc1adf42d9bfeb0cd682174d480258b984448/","comments":[{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":4,"text":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/copilot/ai-get-started#copilot-capabilities-in-dynamics-365-sales","pick":"B"},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-30","up":3,"text":"✅ B. Copilot email assist\n\nCopilot email assist is built specifically for Dynamics 365 Sales and provides:\n- AI‑generated email drafts\n- Follow‑up suggestions\n- Context‑aware responses based on opportunity and lead data\n- Faster prospect communication directly inside the Sales workflow\n\nThis aligns perfectly with the requirement","pick":"B"}]},{"n":47,"id":984449,"topic":2,"stem":"<p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which components should you use to meet the sales cycle enablement requirements?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image9.png\" alt=\"image11\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image10.png\" alt=\"image12\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":1,"case":"d646994a1b","thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/2ec6c529f2b6990883bdc4c5fd5bdb3a984449/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-30","up":6,"text":"1. Microsoft Copilot Studio → AI agent creation\nThe case study requires:\n- A low‑code AI agent\n- Built on Dataverse\n- Used by sales executives through voice/headset\n- With telemetry, governance, and adoption tracking\nThis is exactly what Copilot Studio is designed for.\nFoundry is code‑first and not aligned with the low‑code requirement.\n\n2. Fallback topic → Unexpected AI agent actions\nThe requirements state:\n- If the agent fails twice, it must escalate to a live representative\n- Unexpected actions must be handled gracefully\nIn Copilot Studio, the Fallback topic is the built‑in mechanism for:\n- Handling unrecognized intents\n- Managing repeated failures\n- Triggering escalation workflows","replies":[{"user":"24b8eec","date":"2026-06-17","up":1,"text":"\"Use low-code development to create a single AI agent that has Dataverse as its core component.\""}]},{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":4,"text":"Looks correct.","replies":[{"user":"Hirowa","date":"2026-05-30","up":1,"text":"Why isn't the answer to question 1 Microsoft Foundry?","replies":[{"user":"24b8eec","date":"2026-06-17","up":1,"text":"\"Use low-code development to create a single AI agent that has Dataverse as its core component.\""}]}]},{"user":"Eberd","date":"2026-03-08","up":1,"text":"Correcta"}]},{"n":48,"id":984450,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>You need to design a Microsoft 365 Copilot solution to optimize employee productivity. The solution must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Ensure that the employees can query content stored in a subset of Microsoft SharePoint Online sites and in Teams by using natural language-based prompt actions.</li><li>Ensure that employees receive contextually relevant responses in Microsoft 365 Copilot.</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you include in the design?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Build a Microsoft Power Automate desktop flow to read the SharePoint content and post the responses to Teams."},{"k":"B","html":"Modify SharePoint settings."},{"k":"C","html":"Create a custom REST API that crawls the SharePoint content."},{"k":"D","html":"Configure Microsoft Graph access."}],"answer":"D","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"B","p":31,"n":5},{"a":"D","p":69,"n":11}],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/77f26358a1292d5ce81485f5901cbad2984450/","comments":[{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":5,"text":"I love D ;)","pick":"D"},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-30","up":4,"text":"Correct answer: D. Configure Microsoft Graph access.\n\nTo let Microsoft 365 Copilot query specific SharePoint Online sites and Teams content using natural language—and return contextually grounded responses—you must configure Microsoft Graph access.\nThis is the mechanism Copilot uses to read organizational content securely and selectively.","pick":"D"},{"user":"Jedi","date":"2026-03-08","up":4,"text":"I thinking this might be B. Restricted SharePoint Search: To limit Copilot to a specific subset of sites and Teams, you must use Restricted SharePoint Search in the SharePoint Admin Center. This allows you to define a \"known\" list of sites, ensuring Copilot only queries those specific locations, which directly addresses the requirement for a \"subset of SharePoint Online sites\".","pick":"B"},{"user":"Eberd","date":"2026-03-06","up":3,"text":"Microsoft 365 Copilot obtiene el contexto de los datos de la organización a través de Microsoft Graph.","pick":"D"},{"user":"TFOTHYL","date":"2026-08-12","up":1,"text":"D. Configure Microsoft Graph access\n\nWhy?\n\nMicrosoft 365 Copilot generates contextually relevant responses by grounding prompts in organizational data available through Microsoft Graph, including SharePoint Online, Teams, Outlook, OneDrive, and other Microsoft 365 services. Microsoft Graph provides the context and permissions framework that allows Copilot to retrieve and reason over content users are authorized to access.\n\nThe requirement states that users must:\n\n1.Query SharePoint Online and Teams content using natural-language prompts.\n2.Receive contextually relevant responses in Microsoft 365 Copilot.\n\nThese capabilities are provided through Microsoft Graph, which is the underlying data and context layer used by Microsoft 365 Copilot.","pick":"D"},{"user":"Ninashnash","date":"2026-07-31","up":1,"text":"B. Modify SharePoint settings.\n\nWhy:\n\nThe core requirement here is to scope what content Microsoft 365 Copilot can access — specifically, a subset of SharePoint Online sites — while still letting employees query that content and Teams content naturally, with contextually relevant answers grounded in Microsoft Graph.","pick":"B"}]},{"n":49,"id":984451,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>A company uses Microsoft Dynamics 365 Finance to manage accounts payable.</p><p>You are designing an AI invoice processing solution.</p><p>You need to recommend the prerequisites to configure a prebuilt copilot for accounts payable.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you recommend?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"From Microsoft Copilot Studio, create an accounts payable agent."},{"k":"B","html":"Extend Microsoft 365 Copilot for Sales to an accounts payable agent."},{"k":"C","html":"Build an AI tool in Microsoft Foundry."},{"k":"D","html":"From the Power Platform admin center, assign the Finance and Operations AI security role to users."}],"answer":"D","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"A","p":14,"n":1},{"a":"D","p":86,"n":6}],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/f9452e300673ca7e5f0301944f3d8b34984451/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-30","up":3,"text":"Correct answer: D. From the Power Platform admin center, assign the Finance and Operations AI security role to users.\n\nTo enable the prebuilt Copilot for Accounts Payable in Dynamics 365 Finance, users must be assigned the Finance and Operations AI security role.\nThis is the documented prerequisite before the AP Copilot can access invoice data and perform AI‑assisted processing.","pick":"D"},{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":3,"text":"Man I love D ;). for real tho... it looks correct","pick":"D"},{"user":"Ninashnash","date":"2026-07-31","up":1,"text":"D is correct. Dynamics 365 Finance ships with prebuilt Copilot capabilities for accounts payable that are built into the product itself — they don't need to be custom-built. The key prerequisite to actually enable and use these prebuilt AI features is security/role configuration, so that the AI capabilities are turned on and accessible for the right users. This is done through the Power Platform admin center, where you assign the Finance and Operations AI security role needed for users to access the built-in Copilot features in Dynamics 365 Finance.","pick":"D"},{"user":"jgg","date":"2026-05-26","up":1,"text":"MS Learn MCP and Claude agrees here, it's D :)","pick":"D"},{"user":"deca0d4","date":"2026-05-12","up":1,"text":"ou create an Accounts Payable agent in Copilot Studio because:\n\nIt’s the platform for building and configuring custom agents\nIt provides:\nAgent templates (including finance/AP scenarios)\nTopics, actions, and workflows\nIntegration with Dynamics 365 Finance","pick":"A"}]},{"n":50,"id":984452,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>A company plans to deploy a Microsoft Dynamics 365 Contact Center agent.</p><p>You need to ensure that the agent can transfer the conversation to a live customer service representative.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which two components should you include in the solution?</strong> Each correct answer presents part of the solution.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Microsoft Foundry"},{"k":"B","html":"Microsoft Copilot Studio"},{"k":"C","html":"Microsoft 365 Agents Toolkit"},{"k":"D","html":"an Azure AI Bot Service skill"},{"k":"E","html":"Customer engagement hub"}],"answer":"BE","type":"multi","votes":[{"a":"BE","p":100,"n":11}],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/5811b22e9bd3b2a122981239bfd47617984452/","comments":[{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":9,"text":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-copilot-studio/advanced-hand-off#prerequisites","pick":"BE","top":true},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-30","up":3,"text":"✅ B. Microsoft Copilot Studio\nDynamics 365 Contact Center uses Copilot Studio to build and configure the conversational agent.\nThe live‑agent transfer capability is implemented through:\n- handoff nodes\n- Omnichannel/Customer Service integration\n- routing rules\n\n✅ E. Customer engagement hub\nThe Customer Service workspace / Customer Engagement Hub is where human agents receive escalated conversations.\nThe Contact Center agent must be able to:\n- transfer the session to a queue\n- route it to a human agent\n- allow the human agent to pick up the conversation in the Customer Engagement Hub","pick":"BE"},{"user":"Ninashnash","date":"2026-07-31","up":1,"text":"✅ B. Dynamics 365 Contact Center agents are built and extended using Microsoft Copilot Studio. ✅ E. Customer engagement hub: The Customer engagement hub (Dynamics 365 Customer Service/Contact Center) is where live customer service representatives receive and continue conversations that are escalated from the AI agent.","pick":"BE"}]},{"n":51,"id":984453,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>A company uses Microsoft Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management.</p><p>You are designing an AI supply chain process that meets the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Provides managers with AI-driven insights that surface key information from customer orders</li><li>Helps planners use AI to anticipate future product needs more accurately</li></ul><p>You need to recommend which Microsoft Copilot features to include in the design.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you recommend for each requirement?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image11.png\" alt=\"image13\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image12.png\" alt=\"image14\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/2aa746f1aeadbf305e3d94e7c24a95cd984453/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-31","up":5,"text":"1. Provide AI‑driven insights from customer orders:\n➡ AI Summaries with Copilot\nReason: AI Summaries in Supply Chain Management surface key information from operational records—such as customer orders, shipments, delays, exceptions, and fulfillment issues.\nThey are designed to give managers quick, AI‑generated overviews of order activity.\n\n2. Anticipate future product needs:\n➡ Generative insights for Demand planning\nReason: This Copilot feature uses AI to analyze historical demand, seasonality, supply constraints, and forecast signals to help planners predict future product needs more accurately."},{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":4,"text":"Correct!\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/copilot/ai-get-started#copilot-capabilities-in-dynamics-365-supply-chain-management"},{"user":"deca0d4","date":"2026-05-12","up":1,"text":"Correct: Uses generative AI to summarize large amounts of unstructured content.\nCase notes\nEmail threads\nMeeting transcripts\nSupport interactions\n\nGenerative insights for demand planning\nApplies AI to analyze demand signals and generate insights/forecasts.\nPredict future product demand\nIdentify trends or anomalies\nRecommend inventory adjustments"},{"user":"Eberd","date":"2026-03-06","up":1,"text":"La funcionalidad Demand Planning con generative AI usa modelos predictivos y AI para forecast de demanda futura, ayudando a planificadores a anticipar necesidades de productos."}]},{"n":52,"id":984454,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>A company has a Microsoft 365 E5 subscription and uses Microsoft Copilot Studio.</p><p>The company has a Microsoft SharePoint Online library that contains 10,000 policy PDFs from various departments. The library contains a populated column named Department for each PDF.</p><p>You need to design a Copilot Studio agent that will use the SharePoint library as a knowledge source. The solution must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Enable the agent to answer user questions about company policies.</li><li>Ensure that the agent can identify which departments and policies are connected.</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you include in the design for each requirement?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image13.png\" alt=\"image15\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image14.png\" alt=\"image16\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[{"a":"B","p":100,"n":1}],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/02148db9c050c84d63ca0b1348916c15984454/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-31","up":9,"text":"1. From Copilot Studio, add SharePoint as a knowledge source.\nCopilot Studio can directly index a SharePoint library (including PDFs) as a knowledge source, enabling natural‑language Q&A over the content.\nNo custom models, Dataverse imports, or AI Builder pipelines are required.\n\n2. Create a Microsoft Dataverse table for the departments.\nThe agent must understand relationships between departments and policies.\n- A Dataverse table allows you to:\n- Represent departments as structured entities\n- Link policies to departments\n- Enable the agent to reason over relationships (e.g., “Which policies belong to HR?”)","top":true},{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-07","up":4,"text":"Looks correct. Was thinking maybe upload to Dataverse but it's limited to 500 files. https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-copilot-studio/knowledge-add-file-upload","replies":[{"user":"zsedo","date":"2026-10-04","up":1,"text":"\"An agent can include up to 500 files as knowledge.\"\nYou don't upload the files to Dataverse. You only create a table with the labels and departments."}]},{"user":"Ninashnash","date":"2026-07-31","up":2,"text":"There is no such thing as SharePoint tool to be configured. the only logical way I can think of is using Dataverse to hold SharePoint data mapping (document to department, somehow being synced to the actual SPO library) and be used to trim down the answers."},{"user":"Gabrycloud","date":"2026-03-02","up":1,"text":"My initial thought is B, and after re-reading, I'm sticking with it.","pick":"B"}]},{"n":53,"id":984455,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>You need to design a Microsoft Copilot Studio agent that meets the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Supports interactive speech responses</li><li>Optimizes decision-making and the accuracy of responses</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you include in the design for each requirement?</strong> To answer, drag the appropriate options to the correct requirements. Each option may be used once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to drag the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image15.png\" alt=\"image17\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image16.png\" alt=\"image18\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/46a8ae53e6e211a1f81d281c8559f993984455/","comments":[{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":8,"text":"Correct since it's CPS Solution.","top":true},{"user":"rveney","date":"2026-02-24","up":5,"text":"Supports interactive speech responses:\n➡️ Copilot Studio voice features\nWhy: Copilot Studio voice features are designed to enable voice-based, interactive conversations (speech input/output) within a Copilot Studio agent.\n\nOptimizes decision-making and the accuracy of responses:\n➡️ A deep reasoning model\nWhy: A deep reasoning model is intended to improve multi-step decision-making, reduce logical errors, and increase response accuracy—especially for complex queries and agent orchestration."},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-31","up":3,"text":"Copilot Studio voice features → Interactive speech responses\nCopilot Studio includes built‑in voice capabilities that allow an agent to:\n- Listen to user speech\n- Generate spoken responses\n- Support natural, interactive voice conversations\nThis is the only option designed specifically for speech interaction.\n\nDeep reasoning model → Decision‑making & accuracy\nDeep reasoning models (like GPT‑4‑class reasoning models) are used in Copilot Studio to:\n- Improve multi‑step reasoning\n- Increase accuracy of responses\n- Handle complex decision logic\n- Produce more reliable, grounded answers\nThis directly satisfies the requirement to optimize decision‑making and accuracy."}]},{"n":54,"id":984456,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>You are designing a low-code AI business solution by using Microsoft Copilot Studio.</p><p>The solution must include an agent that automates tasks by simulating user interactions across third-party apps and websites, such as clicking buttons, entering text, and extracting information from screens.</p><p>You need to recommend what to include in the agent.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you recommend?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Model Context Protocol (MCP)"},{"k":"B","html":"a natural language understanding + (NLU+) model in Copilot Studio"},{"k":"C","html":"Computer Use in Copilot Studio"},{"k":"D","html":"Copilot skills"}],"answer":"C","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"C","p":100,"n":9}],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/c8f93cb162f5ebf5488274ab6086da68984456/","comments":[{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":5,"text":"Correct!","pick":"C"},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-31","up":4,"text":"✅ Correct Answer: C. Computer Use in Copilot Studio\n\nComputer Use enables a Copilot Studio agent to:\n- Control a computer like a human\n- Click, type, scroll, select, and navigate\n- Read information from screens\n- Automate workflows across any app (web or desktop)\n- Handle UI automation without building custom connectors\nIt is the low‑code way to give your agent real “hands‑on‑keyboard” abilities.","pick":"C"},{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-04-12","up":2,"text":"\"Computer use is a tool in Copilot Studio that lets your agent interact with and automate tasks on a Windows computer. It works with websites and desktop apps by selecting buttons, choosing menus, and entering text into fields on the screen. Describe in natural language what you want computer use to do, and it performs the task on a computer you set up by using a virtual mouse and keyboard. By using computer use, agents can complete tasks even when there's no API to connect directly to the system. If a person can use an app or website, computer use can too. You can use computer use for tasks like automated data entry, invoice processing, and data extraction.\"\nReference: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-copilot-studio/computer-use","pick":"C"}]},{"n":55,"id":984457,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>You need to recommend a solution to integrate a Microsoft Copilot agent with a Microsoft Dynamics 365 Contact Center chat channel.</p><p>The agent must respond to customer questions and hand off the conversation to a live customer service representative when the customer requests an escalation.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you recommend?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Build an agent flow."},{"k":"B","html":"Configure the Conversation Start topic."},{"k":"C","html":"Configure a skill."},{"k":"D","html":"Call a Microsoft Power Automate connector."},{"k":"E","html":"Configure the Escalate topic."}],"answer":"E","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"E","p":100,"n":9}],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/96242d571f6fda55e7d04949165c3747984457/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-31","up":4,"text":"The right choice is E. Configure the Escalate topic.\n\nIn Copilot Studio, the Escalate topic is the built‑in mechanism that:\n- Detects when a customer asks for a human\n- Triggers the handoff flow\n- Connects to Dynamics 365 Customer Service / Contact Center queues\n- Transfers the conversation to a live representative\nThis is the only option that directly supports the required escalation behavior.","pick":"E"},{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-04-12","up":4,"text":"\"Configure the Escalate topic in Microsoft Copilot Studio by navigating to Topics > System, selecting Escalate, and adding a Transfer conversation node. This ensures a smooth hand-off to live agents (e.g., Dynamics 365) when the bot cannot resolve an issue, often triggered after the System Fallback topic runs\"\nReference: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-copilot-studio/advanced-hand-off","pick":"E"},{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":4,"text":"Correct!","pick":"E"}]},{"n":56,"id":984458,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>A company has a customer order system that creates sales orders manually.</p><p>You need to design an AI solution to automate the following tasks as part of the system:</p><ul><li>Save the order details to a database.</li><li>Update the order status in the database.</li><li>Extract the order details from an order file.</li><li>Prepare and send a confirmation email to customers.</li><li>The solution must minimize development effort and support intelligent automation and solution integration.</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you include in the design?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"a workflow in Azure Logic Apps"},{"k":"B","html":"a multi-agent solution that uses the Semantic Kernel SDK"},{"k":"C","html":"a multi-agent solution that uses Microsoft Foundry Agent Service"},{"k":"D","html":"a Microsoft Copilot Studio agent that uses Microsoft Power Automate workflows"}],"answer":"D","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"D","p":100,"n":12}],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/f8bc4c9e0a04e4e940068aba14873cbc984458/","comments":[{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":7,"text":"Man I love D ;). but ya the other options are overkill.","pick":"D","top":true},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-31","up":4,"text":"The correct answer is: D. A Microsoft Copilot Studio agent that uses Microsoft Power Automate workflows.\n\nYour requirements are:\n- Save order details to a database\n- Update order status\n- Extract order details from an order file\n- Prepare and send confirmation emails\n- Minimize development effort\n- Support intelligent automation\n- Support integration across systems\nThis is a textbook case for Copilot Studio + Power Automate.","pick":"D"},{"user":"deca0d4","date":"2026-05-12","up":2,"text":"Use Copilot Studio to create the agent and call a Power Automate cloud flow that uses AI Builder for document extraction, database connectors for order updates, and Outlook/Exchange connectors to send confirmation emails.","pick":"D"},{"user":"Ninashnash","date":"2026-07-31","up":1,"text":"The solution must minimize development effort and support intelligent automation and solution integration. That's exactly what Copilot Studio+Power Atomate flow do (low code, no code development)","pick":"D"}]},{"n":57,"id":984459,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>You are designing an AI strategy for Microsoft Dynamics 365 finance and operations apps. You are evaluating the use of Microsoft Copilot Studio to provide in-app help and guidance based on generative AI general knowledge.</p><p>You need to recommend which knowledge sources to include in the generative help and guidance agent. The solution must minimize the risk of generating inaccurate responses.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you recommend?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image17.png\" alt=\"image19\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image18.png\" alt=\"image20\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/9b58d5bdde0cd5af2800d6aba378e655984459/","comments":[{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":15,"text":"First one is correct. Second answer should be to disable general knowledge... to prevent inaccurate responses","top":true,"replies":[{"user":"keambi0111","date":"2026-03-11","up":1,"text":"guidance based on generative AI \"general\" knowledge."}]},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-31","up":7,"text":"1. Custom knowledge sources → Must be uploaded to the agent\nTo minimize hallucinations, Copilot Studio agents used for in‑app help and guidance in Dynamics 365 must rely on trusted, organization‑controlled content.\nThis includes:\n- Product documentation\n- Internal process guides\n- Policy documents\n- Standard operating procedures\n\n2. AI general knowledge → Must be disabled for the agent\nGeneral knowledge models can introduce:\n- Hallucinations\n- Non‑compliant or inaccurate answers\n- Content unrelated to Dynamics 365 processes","top":true},{"user":"2db2984","date":"2026-05-03","up":3,"text":"First one is correct. Fir Second correct answer is : disable general knowledge\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/fin-ops-core/dev-itpro/copilot/extend-copilot-generative-help"},{"user":"rveney","date":"2026-02-24","up":3,"text":"Custom knowledge sources: Must be excluded from the agent\nAI general knowledge: Must be enabled for the agent"},{"user":"QueenShi","date":"2026-03-16","up":2,"text":"Key phrase in the question:\n“in‑app help and guidance based on generative AI general knowledge”\nThat phrase is doing most of the work.\nMicrosoft documentation for Copilot Studio generative answers makes it clear that:\nGenerative help relies on AI general knowledge as the base\nCustom knowledge grounds the model, but does not replace the LLM’s general reasoning ability"},{"user":"Eberd","date":"2026-03-04","up":2,"text":"Must be disabled for the agent"}]},{"n":58,"id":984460,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>You need to design a multi-agent solution that will include a custom agent. The solution must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Define the rules and constraints that the agent must follow.</li><li>Automate a backend process that involves data movement between services and runs independently of the agent's reasoning steps.</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you include in the design for each requirement?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image19.png\" alt=\"image21\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image20.png\" alt=\"image22\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/72a6fb571ee757b584ca651d2b5e31d4984460/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-31","up":9,"text":"1. Rules and constraints → Agent flows\nAgent flows are the mechanism used in Copilot Studio to:\n- Define policies, constraints, and guardrails\n- Control how the agent reasons\n- Enforce rules such as allowed actions, restricted topics, or required steps\n- Shape the agent’s decision‑making and behavior\nThey are part of the agent’s internal orchestration, not external automation.\n\n2. Backend automation → Power Automate cloud flow\nA backend process that:\n- Moves data between services\n- Runs independently of the agent’s reasoning\n- Executes reliably and asynchronously\n…is exactly what Power Automate cloud flows are designed for.","top":true},{"user":"CertiMaster101912","date":"2026-05-22","up":6,"text":"1: topics\n2: pa flow"},{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":5,"text":"Hmmm first one might be agent flows... was expecting instructions to be an option.. Anyone else here? need some help on this one. first one might be topics i dunno man.","replies":[{"user":"17b90da","date":"2026-03-18","up":1,"text":"I believe it must be B if the constraints should apply to the agent and not \"only\" the flow"}]},{"user":"janesb","date":"2026-03-10","up":2,"text":"@Newb007.Agent flow is not used to define the agent’s rules because it is meant for running actions and backend automation. For example, an agent is helping to fix the VPN connectivity issue, so the agent will ask for employee ID, device type, and deciding when to escalate are conversation rules, so they belong to a conversation topic. Tasks like creating a ticket, updating Dataverse, or sending notifications are backend actions, so they belong to an agent flow or Power Automate flow."},{"user":"Eberd","date":"2026-03-06","up":1,"text":"Con topics podes controlar bien las restricciones. A y B correctas"}]},{"n":59,"id":984461,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>A company uses Microsoft 365 and Dynamics 365.</p><p>You need to recommend a solution to automatically summarize email threads, generate suggested replies in Microsoft Outlook, and provide meeting preparation summaries that include relevant customer relationship management (CRM) data.</p><div class=\"solution\"><span>Proposed solution</span>You recommend Microsoft 365 Copilot for Sales.</div><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Does this meet the goal?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Yes"},{"k":"B","html":"No"}],"answer":"A","type":"yesno","votes":[{"a":"A","p":88,"n":7},{"a":"B","p":13,"n":1}],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/78872876b05c4fe0a0599c4ba4166f7f984461/","comments":[{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":5,"text":"Correct","pick":"A"},{"user":"deca0d4","date":"2026-04-29","up":3,"text":"👉 Sales agent (inside Microsoft 365 Copilot for Sales)\nConnects to CRM (Dynamics 365 or Salesforce)\nUses Microsoft Graph (emails, meetings)\nCombines both into one experience","pick":"A"},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-31","up":2,"text":"Answer: B. No\n\nMicrosoft 365 Copilot for Sales does enhance Outlook with CRM‑aware insights, but the scenario requires automatic email thread summaries, suggested replies, and meeting preparation summaries that include Dynamics 365 CRM data.\nThe correct solution for those capabilities is Copilot for Microsoft 365 with Sales Copilot (formerly Viva Sales).\nSales Copilot is an add‑on that enriches Copilot for Microsoft 365 with CRM context — but by itself, it does not provide the full Outlook and meeting‑prep generative AI experience.\nSo recommending only Microsoft 365 Copilot for Sales does not meet the goal.","pick":"B","replies":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-31","up":2,"text":"From all other options, this is the closest one to \"Yes\"."}]}],"series":true},{"n":60,"id":984462,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>A company uses Microsoft 365 and Dynamics 365.</p><p>You need to recommend a solution to automatically summarize email threads, generate suggested replies in Microsoft Outlook, and provide meeting preparation summaries that include relevant customer relationship management (CRM) data.</p><div class=\"solution\"><span>Proposed solution</span>You recommend a classic Microsoft Dataverse workflow.</div><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Does this meet the goal?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Yes"},{"k":"B","html":"No"}],"answer":"B","type":"yesno","votes":[{"a":"B","p":100,"n":5}],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/eb3be76b860642d9411c24af04132d2a984462/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-31","up":3,"text":"Answer: B. No\n\nA classic Microsoft Dataverse workflow cannot meet the goal because:\n- It does not generate AI‑based email summaries\n- It does not create suggested replies in Outlook\n- It does not produce meeting preparation summaries enriched with Dynamics 365 CRM data\n- It is a legacy automation engine focused on record updates, notifications, and simple logic — not generative AI\nThe required capabilities come from Copilot for Microsoft 365 combined with Sales Copilot, not from Dataverse workflows.","pick":"B"},{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":2,"text":"Correct","pick":"B"}],"series":true},{"n":61,"id":984463,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>A company uses Microsoft 365 and Dynamics 365.</p><p>You need to recommend a solution to automatically summarize email threads, generate suggested replies in Microsoft Outlook, and provide meeting preparation summaries that include relevant customer relationship management (CRM) data.</p><div class=\"solution\"><span>Proposed solution</span>You recommend a Microsoft 365 Copilot agent template.</div><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Does this meet the goal?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Yes"},{"k":"B","html":"No"}],"answer":"B","type":"yesno","votes":[{"a":"B","p":100,"n":4}],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/def70926af3b3b81f7554a1f8edd5125984463/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-31","up":3,"text":"Answer: B. No\n\nA Microsoft 365 Copilot agent template does not meet the goal.\n\nHere’s the key issue:\nAgent templates are designed for building custom task‑oriented agents (e.g., workflow automation, domain‑specific copilots). They do not provide:\n- Automatic email thread summarization in Outlook\n- Suggested replies in Outlook\n- Meeting preparation summaries enriched with Dynamics 365 CRM data","pick":"B"},{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":1,"text":"Correct","pick":"B"}],"series":true},{"n":62,"id":994150,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>You need to design an application lifecycle management (ALM) process for a Microsoft Power Platform environment that contains a solution named Solution1.</p><p>Solution1 must include a custom connector for Copilot in Microsoft Dynamics 365 Customer Service. Solution1 must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Ensure that the custom connector can be deployed consistently across environments as part of the ALM process.</li><li>Allow the custom connector to be edited only in the development environment.</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you include in the design?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Add the custom connector to GitHub."},{"k":"B","html":"Share the custom connector."},{"k":"C","html":"Create the custom connector in the default solution."},{"k":"D","html":"Add the custom connector to Solution1."}],"answer":"D","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"D","p":100,"n":4}],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/9d1610fa4ada2d3be5a109d5544ba1be994150/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-31","up":4,"text":"The correct answer is D. Add the custom connector to Solution1.\n\nCustom connectors must be included inside a solution so they can be:\n- exported from Dev\n-imported into Test/Prod\n- versioned and transported through pipelines\n\nWhen a solution is exported as managed, all components—including the custom connector—become:\n- locked\n- read‑only\n- not editable in Test/Prod","pick":"D"},{"user":"deca0d4","date":"2026-05-12","up":1,"text":"Standard ALM Practice for this is...\nIn Development, add/create the custom connector inside Solution1.\nKeep Solution1 unmanaged in Development so it can be edited.","pick":"D"}]},{"n":63,"id":994151,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>A company uses a Microsoft Copilot Studio agent to automate tasks in a web app.</p><p>During testing, you discover that the automation sometimes fails because of frequent changes to the app's user interface.</p><p>You need to recommend a solution to ensure that the agent successfully automates the tasks. The solution must minimize changes to the agent.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you include in the recommendation?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Computer Use in Copilot Studio"},{"k":"B","html":"custom models in Azure AI Studio"},{"k":"C","html":"conversation topics in Copilot Studio"},{"k":"D","html":"an agent flow in Copilot Studio"}],"answer":"A","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"A","p":100,"n":3}],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/a582eb9653d9e0f1cda8df09502191b5994151/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-31","up":2,"text":"The correct answer is A. Computer Use in Copilot Studio.\n\nYour scenario describes:\n- A Copilot Studio agent automating tasks in a web app\n- Automation failing because the UI changes frequently\n- You want a solution that minimizes changes to the agent\nThis is exactly the problem Computer Use is designed to solve.","pick":"A"},{"user":"deca0d4","date":"2026-04-29","up":2,"text":"“Computer use” = ability for an agent to interact with applications like a human would. like: Clicking buttons, Entering text, Navigating UI\nWhen to use it: No API exists, Legacy systems, Desktop apps, UI-only workflows","pick":"A"}]},{"n":64,"id":994152,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>A company processes invoices stored across multiple systems in multiple formats.</p><p>You need to implement an AI solution to automate the invoice processing. The solution must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Automate multi-step invoice processing tasks, including document analysis, data validation, and approval routing.</li><li>Enable users to interact directly via Microsoft Teams to review and approve invoices.</li><li>Minimize development efforts to define and customize approval workflows.</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you include in the solution?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Azure Document Intelligence in Foundry Tools and Azure Logic Apps"},{"k":"B","html":"a SharePoint agent"},{"k":"C","html":"Microsoft Copilot Studio and AI Builder"},{"k":"D","html":"Azure OpenAI and Azure Functions"}],"answer":"C","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"C","p":100,"n":4}],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/f8e112c5f383ac0b5f2ba3eeadee0f48994152/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-05-31","up":4,"text":"Correct answer: C. Microsoft Copilot Studio and AI Builder\n\nAI Builder provides prebuilt and customizable document processing models (Invoice Processing, Form Processing) that can extract structured data from invoices across formats and systems.\n\nCopilot Studio can orchestrate multi‑step workflows using:\n- Agent flows\n- Power Automate integration\n- Reasoning steps\n- Conditional logic\nThis gives you intelligent automation with minimal custom code.","pick":"C"},{"user":"deca0d4","date":"2026-05-12","up":1,"text":"The process to meet the requirements are ...\nBuild the agent in Copilot Studio.\nAdd an action that calls a Power Automate cloud flow.\nIn the flow, use AI Builder to extract invoice fields.\nValidate the invoice data.\nRoute approval through Teams Approvals.\nReturn status/results back to the Copilot agent.","pick":"C"}]},{"n":65,"id":994153,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>You need to design a Microsoft Copilot Studio agent for customer support.</p><p>The agent must securely retrieve product warranty data from a REST API. The solution must minimize development effort.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you include in the design?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Export the agent as a managed solution and customize the agent in Power Apps."},{"k":"B","html":"Create a custom connector in Copilot Studio and use the connector to call the API."},{"k":"C","html":"Use a Microsoft Power Automate desktop flow to screen scrape the warranty data."},{"k":"D","html":"Add the warranty data to the Fallback topic."}],"answer":"B","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"B","p":100,"n":4}],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/97e32474556a9e40d9e8d92555e936ae994153/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-01","up":5,"text":"✅ Correct Answer: B. Create a custom connector in Copilot Studio\n\nTo securely retrieve product warranty data from a REST API, the agent needs:\n- A secure authentication mechanism\n- A reusable, governed integration component\n- Low‑code configuration\n- ALM‑friendly deployment\nA custom connector provides exactly that.","pick":"B"}]},{"n":66,"id":994154,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>A company has an ecommerce support portal that uses Microsoft Dataverse.</p><p>You are designing a Microsoft Copilot Studio agent for the portal. The agent must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Respond with a default help message when the user input is unclear.</li><li>Initiate external processes, such as retrieving the order status, when users make specific requests.</li></ul><p>Generative orchestration will be enabled for the solution.</p><p>You need to recommend a feature for each requirement.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you recommend?</strong> To answer, drag the appropriate features to the correct requirements. Each feature may be used once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to drag the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image53.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image54.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/ba27f9472b65f7faf86f704277826e71994154/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-01","up":7,"text":"1. Fallback topic → Default help message\nWhen user input is unclear, incomplete, or outside the agent’s scope, the Fallback topic is the built‑in mechanism that:\n- Detects unrecognized intents\n- Responds with a default help or clarification message\n- Redirects the user back into a supported Flow\n\n2. Tool (connector) → Initiate external processes\nTo retrieve order status or trigger any external system action, the agent must call a tool, which in Copilot Studio means:\n- A connector (custom or standard)\n- A Power Automate flow exposed as a tool\n- Any external API wrapped as a tool","top":true},{"user":"hi1011","date":"2026-04-22","up":4,"text":"• Respond with a default help message when the user input is unclear. -> Fallback Topic\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-copilot-studio/authoring-system-fallback-topic\n\n• Initiate external processes, such as retrieving the order status, when users make specific requests. -> A tool(connector)\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-copilot-studio/add-tools-custom-agent"}]},{"n":67,"id":994155,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>A company uses Microsoft Dynamics 365 to manage service operations. Dispatchers coordinate service requests, and technicians perform scheduled on-site work.</p><p>You need to design a solution that will use Microsoft Copilot to improve the efficiency of the service operations. The solution must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Provide AI-driven assistance to help staff organize and resolve work orders.</li><li>Deliver contextual AI support to frontline workers as they prepare for and complete customer appointments.</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which two components should you include in the design?</strong> Each correct answer presents part of the solution.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Copilot Service workspace"},{"k":"B","html":"Copilot in Outlook"},{"k":"C","html":"Dynamics 365 Customer Service"},{"k":"D","html":"Copilot in Customer Service"},{"k":"E","html":"Copilot in Field Service"},{"k":"F","html":"the Dynamics 365 Field Service mobile app"}],"answer":"EF","type":"multi","votes":[{"a":"EF","p":100,"n":7}],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/18decb5a737d271d55d3d6d7676c6cd6994155/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-01","up":4,"text":"E. Copilot in Field Service\nThis provides:\n- AI‑driven insights for work orders\n- Assistance with scheduling, dispatching, and resolving service tasks\n- Summaries, recommendations, and automated updates for service operativos\nThis directly supports dispatchers and back‑office service staff.\n\nF. Dynamics 365 Field Service mobile app\nThis gives frontline technicians:\n- Contextual AI assistance during appointments\n- Work order summaries\n- Step‑by‑step guidance\n- Real‑time updates\n- Integrated Copilot experiences in the mobile workflow\nThis is the only option that delivers AI support to technicians in the field.","pick":"EF"},{"user":"deca0d4","date":"2026-04-30","up":2,"text":"E. Copilot in Field Service\n\nUse for technician assistance and service operations.\n\nWork order summaries\nTroubleshooting help\nService history insights\n\n👉 Think: AI helping field technicians do their job faster\n\nF. Dynamics 365 Field Service mobile app\n\nUse for on-site technicians in the field.\n\nView/update work orders\nCapture photos, notes\nWork offline\nExecute tasks on-site\n\n👉 Think: Execution tool for technicians (mobile-first)","pick":"EF"},{"user":"297bbbc","date":"2026-04-25","up":2,"text":"E. Copilot in Field Service\nWhy: Copilot in Dynamics 365 Field Service provides AI-driven assistance for dispatchers and service managers—e.g., summarizing work orders, suggesting next steps, helping with scheduling, parts availability, and work order updates. This directly supports organizing and resolving work orders.\n\nF. The Dynamics 365 Field Service mobile app\nWhy: Frontline technicians use the Field Service mobile app to prepare for and complete on-site appointments. With Copilot experiences integrated, it can deliver contextual guidance (summaries, checklists, notes drafting, and step suggestions) right where technicians work.","pick":"EF"}]},{"n":68,"id":994156,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>A company uses Microsoft Foundry agents.</p><p>You need to ensure that an agent can dynamically use external tools at runtime without updating the agent.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you include in the solution?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"a Microsoft Foundry hub"},{"k":"B","html":"a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server"},{"k":"C","html":"Azure AI Search"},{"k":"D","html":"Microsoft Copilot Studio"}],"answer":"B","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"B","p":100,"n":5}],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/0bed554677b93ca99b4f8d19ce713ea7994156/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-01","up":5,"text":"The right choice is B. a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server.\n\nYou need the agent to:\n- Dynamically use external tools at runtime\n- Without updating or redeploying the agent\nThat is exactly what Model Context Protocol (MCP) is designed for.\n\nMCP allows a Foundry agent to:\n- Discover tools dynamically\n- Load new tools without modifying the agent\n- Call external capabilities exposed by MCP servers\n- Extend functionality at runtime\nThis is the only mechanism in Foundry that supports dynamic tool availability.","pick":"B"},{"user":"deca0d4","date":"2026-04-30","up":1,"text":"The Model Context Protocol (MCP) is a widely supported standard that lets agents request and execute tools in a consistent way","pick":"B"}]},{"n":69,"id":994157,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>A company has a Microsoft Dynamics 365 Sales environment that has Microsoft Copilot enabled.</p><p>You need to customize Copilot by tailoring how opportunity summaries are generated or how they are presented to users.</p><div class=\"solution\"><span>Proposed solution</span>You add fields to the opportunity summary.</div><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Does this meet the goal?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Yes"},{"k":"B","html":"No"}],"answer":"A","type":"yesno","votes":[{"a":"A","p":64,"n":9},{"a":"B","p":36,"n":5}],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/8eef70d13030ebbaa6bae38e102c811b994157/","comments":[{"user":"CyrilleC","date":"2026-07-30","up":4,"text":"The Microsoft Learn documentation states that it is possible to customize the fields used in Copilot Opportunity Summaries in Dynamics 365 Sales by:\n\nadding standard or custom fields,\nremoving fields,\nrearranging the order of the information displayed in the summary.","pick":"A"},{"user":"297bbbc","date":"2026-04-25","up":4,"text":"Answer: B. No\nAdding fields to the opportunity form does not customize how Copilot generates or presents opportunity summaries.\nTo customize Copilot summaries in Dynamics 365 Sales, you must use Copilot Studio plugins or Copilot customization settings, not simply add fields to the opportunity table.","pick":"B"},{"user":"Peter1972","date":"2026-06-04","up":3,"text":"Here is the explanation:\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/sales/copilot-configure-summary-fields","pick":"A"},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-01","up":3,"text":"Answer: B. No\n\nAdding fields to the opportunity entity does not customize how Copilot generates or presents opportunity summaries.\nCopilot’s opportunity summaries are controlled through Copilot Studio (custom prompts, plugins, grounding data, etc.), not by modifying Dynamics 365 fields.\n\nAdding fields only changes the data model — it does not change Copilot’s summarization behavior.","pick":"B"},{"user":"Peter1972","date":"2026-06-04","up":2,"text":"The question here is not to ehance the DataModel. It is more related to the Copilot opportunity summary:\n\nSo, the answer is Yes.","pick":"A"},{"user":"Juan_Covili","date":"2026-06-26","up":1,"text":"En Dynamics 365 Sales, Microsoft permite configurar los campos usados para generar resúmenes de opportunities, leads y accounts. La documentación oficial indica que puedes agregar campos para que Copilot los considere al generar summaries y recent changes.","pick":"A"}],"series":true},{"n":70,"id":994158,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>A company has a Microsoft Dynamics 365 Sales environment that has Microsoft Copilot enabled.</p><p>You need to customize Copilot by tailoring how opportunity summaries are generated or how they are presented to users.</p><div class=\"solution\"><span>Proposed solution</span>You build Microsoft Power Automate flows to trigger customized Copilot summaries.</div><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Does this meet the goal?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Yes"},{"k":"B","html":"No"}],"answer":"B","type":"yesno","votes":[{"a":"B","p":100,"n":3}],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/1bb3851c50108d143f2eb0c6e06486fc994158/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-01","up":3,"text":"Answer: B. No\n\nPower Automate flows cannot customize how Copilot generates or presents opportunity summaries in Dynamics 365 Sales.\n\nFlows can automate notifications, data updates, or downstream actions, but they do not modify Copilot’s summarization logic, prompt structure, or presentation layer.\n\nTo customize Copilot summaries, you must use Copilot Studio—specifically custom prompts, plugins, or grounding data—not Power Automate.","pick":"B"}],"series":true},{"n":71,"id":994159,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>A company has a Microsoft Dynamics 365 Sales environment that has Microsoft Copilot enabled.</p><p>You need to customize Copilot by tailoring how opportunity summaries are generated or how they are presented to users.</p><div class=\"solution\"><span>Proposed solution</span>You configure AI Builder lead scoring models to influence opportunity summaries.</div><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Does this meet the goal?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Yes"},{"k":"B","html":"No"}],"answer":"B","type":"yesno","votes":[{"a":"B","p":100,"n":4}],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/d4c0b5326d4ae7db4653ab64f52accad994159/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-01","up":2,"text":"Answer: B. No\n\nConfiguring AI Builder lead scoring models does not influence how Copilot generates or presents opportunity summaries in Dynamics 365 Sales.\n\nLead scoring affects qualification insights for leads, not:\n- Copilot’s summarization prompts\n- The structure or content of opportunity summaries\n- How Copilot interprets or presents opportunity data\n\nTo customize Copilot summaries, you must adjust Copilot Studio custom prompts or Copilot grounding data, not AI Builder models.","pick":"B"},{"user":"Xabia","date":"2026-05-11","up":2,"text":"Copilot in Dynamics 365 Sales generates summaries natively using built-in AI capabilities","pick":"B"}],"series":true},{"n":72,"id":994160,"topic":2,"stem":"<p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you recommend to assist the CTO with the prebuilt agent selection process?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Agent management"},{"k":"B","html":"Copilot Studio"},{"k":"C","html":"Lifecycle Services (LCS)"},{"k":"D","html":"Immersive Home"}],"answer":"A","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"A","p":48,"n":13},{"a":"B","p":22,"n":6},{"a":"D","p":30,"n":8}],"page":2,"case":"8b997de433","thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/a0077fc9754c8b3357891c8cdc665e15994160/","comments":[{"user":"Xabia","date":"2026-05-11","up":4,"text":"In Dynamics 365 Finance & Supply Chain Management, Immersive Home is the AI-first landing page that helps users work hand-in-hand with AI agents and explicitly links to the tools for enabling, monitoring, teaching, and interacting with AI agents—which is exactly what the CTO needs to browse/assess available prebuilt agent experiences and preview agent capabilities with stakeholders","pick":"D"},{"user":"Alicia_lili","date":"2026-05-04","up":4,"text":"The Agent management is specifically designed to:\nDiscover available agents\nView and evaluate prebuilt agents\nActivate and manage them within the environment","pick":"A"},{"user":"TFOTHYL","date":"2026-08-12","up":3,"text":"Correct answer: A. Agent management\n\nWhy?\n\nThe case states:\n\n\"The CTO wants to view available agent templates to identify which agent will add the most business value.\"\n\nAccording to Microsoft Learn, Agent management in Dynamics 365 Finance & Operations allows users to:\n\n-Discover available agents\n-Browse agent libraries and templates\n-Configure and activate agents\n-Manage deployed agents\n\nMicrosoft specifically describes Agent management as the place where users can discover, configure, and manage AI-powered agents: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/fin-ops-core/fin-ops/copilot/agent-mgmt","pick":"A"},{"user":"ziggy1117","date":"2026-07-01","up":3,"text":"Agent management\nBy using the agent management feature in finance and operations apps, you can use autonomous, AI-powered agents to perform predefined tasks in your business ecosystem. Users can discover, configure, and manage agents that automate routine operational tasks.\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/fin-ops-core/fin-ops/copilot/agent-mgmt","pick":"A"},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-01","up":3,"text":"Answer: D. Immersive Home\n\nTakeaway:\nTo help the CTO view available prebuilt AI agent templates in Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management and preview their capabilities, the correct recommendation is Immersive Home.\n\nThe case study states:\n- The CTO wants to view available prebuilt AI agent templates.\n- The CTO also wants to preview agent capabilities during discovery meetings.","pick":"D"},{"user":"2db2984","date":"2026-05-03","up":3,"text":"Copilot studio","pick":"B"},{"user":"deca0d4","date":"2026-05-01","up":3,"text":"Copilot Studio is where you:\n\nBrowse and select prebuilt agent templates\nCustomize and configure agents\nDefine topics, actions, and integrations\nBuild or extend agents (low-code)","pick":"B"},{"user":"Aarch","date":"2026-08-06","up":2,"text":"Agent management provides centralized monitoring, evaluation, analytics, feedback tracking, and lifecycle governance for agents. It helps organizations assess agent effectiveness and supports selecting and managing prebuilt agents.","pick":"A"},{"user":"Joselito79","date":"2026-09-19","up":1,"text":"✅ Correct answer: D. Immersive Home\n\nWhy?\n\nThe CTO needs to view available prebuilt agent templates and preview their capabilities before selecting an agent for deployment.\n\nImmersive Home is the Dynamics 365 experience used to discover and explore available AI agents, including viewing agent templates and their capabilities. This supports the CTO's discovery and selection process.","pick":"D"},{"user":"atyachter","date":"2026-07-16","up":1,"text":"D -- Immersive Home explanation: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/fin-ops-core/fin-ops/copilot/immersive-home","pick":"D"},{"user":"Juan_Covili","date":"2026-06-30","up":1,"text":"La documentación oficial de Microsoft confirma que la función de Agent management en Dynamics 365 Finance & Operations incluye una página de \"Agents\" con las pestañas Manage y Library, donde específicamente se puede explorar las plantillas de agentes disponibles (browse available agent templates) y previsualizar las capacidades del agente (preview agent capabilities), así como seleccionar y configurar nuevos agentes para su despliegue.","pick":"A"}]},{"n":73,"id":994161,"topic":2,"stem":"<p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you include in the custom AI agent design to meet the R&amp;D product specifications and the compliance information requirements?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image55.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image56.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":2,"case":"8b997de433","thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/a8a7ec684f68740c55ebe0257e0deb0e994161/","comments":[{"user":"Juan_Covili","date":"2026-06-30","up":5,"text":"To expose the data to the agent, createa custom connector\nAdd to the agentthe MCP server","replies":[{"user":"Az301301X","date":"2026-10-02","up":1,"text":"The key exam wording is“Add to the agent.” What is added at the agent level is a tool. Model Context Protocol is the type of tool used to reach the MCP server."}]},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-01","up":5,"text":"1. Custom connector → Expose R&D product specifications + compliance data\nThe case study states:\n- R&D already has a custom MCP server containing product specifications and compliance data.\n- The custom AI agent must be able to answer questions using existing technologies.\n- The agent must access Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management business logic stored outside the application.\n\n2. Add the MCP server → Provide product specifications + compliance data\nThe R&D department already maintains:\n- A Model Context Protocol (MCP) server\n- Containing product specifications\n- And compliance information\nTo make this data available to the agent, you must add the MCP server as a data source/tool inside the agent."},{"user":"Az301301X","date":"2026-10-02","up":1,"text":"tricky...\nThe key exam wording is Add to the agent. What is added at the agent level is \"a tool\". Model Context Protocol is the type of tool used to reach the MCP server."},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-01","up":1,"text":"Answer: D. Immersive Home\n\nTakeaway:\nTo help the CTO view available prebuilt AI agent templates in Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management and preview their capabilities, the correct recommendation is Immersive Home.\n\nThe case study states:\n- The CTO wants to view available prebuilt AI agent templates.\n- The CTO also wants to preview agent capabilities during discovery meetings."}]},{"n":74,"id":999653,"topic":2,"stem":"<p>A company has a Microsoft Dynamics 365 Sales environment that has Microsoft Copilot enabled.</p><p>You need to customize Copilot by tailoring how opportunity summaries are generated or how they are presented to users.</p><div class=\"solution\"><span>Proposed solution</span>You add the opportunity summary widget to the Opportunity form.</div><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Does this meet the goal?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Yes"},{"k":"B","html":"No"}],"answer":"B","type":"yesno","votes":[{"a":"A","p":38,"n":3},{"a":"B","p":63,"n":5}],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/baef04a44b6ce6cd845b10da1cc458fb999653/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-01","up":4,"text":"Answer: B. No\n\nAdding the opportunity summary widget to the Opportunity form only surfaces Copilot’s existing summary—it does not customize:\n- how Copilot generates the summary\n- what data Copilot includes\n- how the summary is structured or phrased\n\nIt’s a UI placement action, not a customization of Copilot behavior.\n\nTo actually tailor summaries, you must modify Copilot Studio prompts or Copilot grounding data.","pick":"B"},{"user":"Ninashnash","date":"2026-08-16","up":2,"text":"YES is correct. Although this solution doesn't customize \"generation\", but it does customize \"presentation\" — and since the requirement is an \"or,\" that's sufficient to meet the goal.","pick":"A"},{"user":"zamper","date":"2026-08-18","up":1,"text":"The crucial distinction is what object you are customizing:\n\nAdd fields to the opportunity summary → you're customizing Copilot's opportunity summary.\nAdd the opportunity summary widget to the Opportunity form → you're customizing the Opportunity form, not Copilot itself.\n\nThe widget is essentially a UI container/surface through which users see the Copilot-generated summary. Adding it determines where the Copilot experience appears, but doesn't change the logic or content of the summary.","pick":"B"},{"user":"Juan_Covili","date":"2026-06-26","up":1,"text":"Agregar el opportunity summary widget al formulario de Opportunity permite cambiar cómo se presenta el resumen de Copilot a los usuarios dentro del formulario de la oportunidad. Microsoft documenta que el widget de resumen de oportunidad muestra un resumen generado por IA y que puede agregarse a formularios personalizados.","pick":"A"}],"series":true},{"n":75,"id":984464,"topic":3,"stem":"<p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which tool should you recommend to address the sensitive information concerns in the sales process?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"the Analytics tab in Microsoft Copilot Studio"},{"k":"B","html":"Model Context Protocol (MCP)"},{"k":"C","html":"Application Insights"},{"k":"D","html":"Microsoft Foundry Tracing UI"},{"k":"E","html":"Monitoring in Microsoft Foundry"}],"answer":"C","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"C","p":52,"n":11},{"a":"D","p":43,"n":9},{"a":"E","p":5,"n":1}],"page":2,"case":"d646994a1b","thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/c13e42291023578d55c76fadc5459fc0984464/","comments":[{"user":"janesb","date":"2026-03-11","up":5,"text":"Copilot Studio can send telemetry to Application Insights. Application Insights stores and exposes that telemetry for monitoring. Microsoft Foundry tracing is also integrated with Application Insights, and the Foundry Tracing UI provides an agent-focused view for inspecting traced runs in detail. So for an auditing requirement, the best answer is the tool that lets you inspect the run details, which is Foundry Tracing UI.","pick":"D"},{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":3,"text":"Hmmmm thinking its C now?","pick":"C","replies":[{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-04","up":1,"text":"NVM is D!!! I love D.","replies":[{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-04","up":4,"text":"NVM its C since all the other answers use CPS."}]}]},{"user":"CyrilleC","date":"2026-07-30","up":2,"text":"D is correct\n\nThe recent Microsoft Foundry Tracing documentation explicitly states that traces can capture:\n\nuser inputs and prompts,\nagent and model inputs and outputs,\ntool calls,\npersonally identifiable information (PII).\n\nIt also explains that this data is intended for observability, diagnostics, and auditing, with built-in access control and data protection mechanisms.\n\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/foundry/observability/concepts/trace-data","pick":"D"},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-01","up":2,"text":"✅ Correct answer: C. Application Insights\n\nApplication Insights (part of Azure Monitor) provides:\n- Full telemetry for AI agents\n- Tracking of sensitive data access\n- Audit trails\n- Custom logging for user IDs, names, and interactions\n- Compliance‑ready monitoring\nThis aligns exactly with Fabrikam’s requirement to track sensitive information shared through the AI agent.","pick":"C"},{"user":"QueenShi","date":"2026-03-16","up":2,"text":"This is a hard one.\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/foundry/observability/how-to/trace-agent-setup#data-retention-and-cost\nBut I would use Application Insights for audit, as it is the data store for agent interactions. You do NOT need Microsoft Foundry Tracing UI to use Application Insights.","pick":"C"},{"user":"silver","date":"2026-03-08","up":2,"text":"Tracing can capture sensitive information (for example, user inputs, model outputs, and tool arguments and results). Use these practices to reduce risk:","pick":"D"},{"user":"TFOTHYL","date":"2026-08-12","up":1,"text":"Correct answer: C. Application Insights\n\nWhy?\n\nThe requirement states:\n\n\"Any sensitive information, such as user IDs and names, shared via the AI agent must be tracked for future auditing.\"\n\nApplication Insights is Microsoft's recommended solution for detailed telemetry, logging, and auditing of AI agent interactions. Microsoft Foundry tracing stores trace data in Azure Monitor / Application Insights, where prompts, responses, user interactions, and potentially sensitive information can be captured and audited.","pick":"C"},{"user":"Ninashnash","date":"2026-08-09","up":1,"text":"According to this Microsoft documentation, Application Insight is correct, moreover other clues in this question means the agent is developed in Copilot Studio so Foundry is irrelevant\n\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-copilot-studio/voice-sensitive-data","pick":"C"},{"user":"Bharat","date":"2026-05-27","up":1,"text":"Monitoring in Foundry is the right answer, as it is the feature which uses anomaly detection, model bias, etc..all the responsible AI stuff,..key word here is \"Sensitive data\"","pick":"E"},{"user":"ppolychron","date":"2026-03-15","up":1,"text":"I will go with C. Application Insights.\n\nSeems the most accurate and additionally you have the option to configure-sensitive-data-masking if you want.\n\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-copilot-studio/voice-sensitive-data#configure-sensitive-data-masking","pick":"C"},{"user":"Eberd","date":"2026-03-08","up":1,"text":"Application Insights permite registrar telemetría y eventos personalizados. En el agente se puede generar un custom event cuando se detecte que el usuario ingresa información sensible (por ejemplo, user IDs o nombres) y enviar ese evento a Application Insights. De esta forma queda registrado para auditoría y análisis posterior, cumpliendo con el requisito de rastrear información sensible compartida a través del agente.","pick":"C"},{"user":"madimad","date":"2026-03-05","up":1,"text":"D is correct answer","pick":"D","replies":[{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-04","up":2,"text":"NVM its C since all the other answers use CPS. therefore its App Insights. Tracing is only for foundry agents"},{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-04","up":4,"text":"NVM its C since all the other answers use CPS."}]},{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":1,"text":"Correct i think? 80% on this","pick":"D","replies":[{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-04","up":1,"text":"This is correct. D.","replies":[{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-04","up":2,"text":"NVM its C since all the other answers use CPS. therefore its App Insights. Tracing is only for foundry agents"}]}]},{"user":"rveney","date":"2026-02-24","up":1,"text":"C. Application Insights.\n\nWhy Application Insights?\nThe case study outlines a specific requirement: \"Detailed telemetry must be logged for the first created AI agent to help troubleshoot and optimize... Any sensitive information, such as user IDs and names, shared via the AI agent must be tracked for future auditing.\"","pick":"C"}]},{"n":76,"id":984465,"topic":3,"stem":"<p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which existing tool and data should you use to gather the required metrics for stakeholder signoff for the AI agents?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image21.png\" alt=\"image23\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image22.png\" alt=\"image24\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":2,"case":"d646994a1b","thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/06d06e58314660397b6caef44ea688f7984465/","comments":[{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":15,"text":"1. CPS\n2. Task TODAY per instance","top":true},{"user":"Alicia_lili","date":"2026-05-04","up":6,"text":"1. Copilot Studio\n2. Task today per instance"},{"user":"Eberd","date":"2026-03-08","up":4,"text":"Tool: Microsoft Copilot Studio\nData: the current time to complete the task today per instance"},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-01","up":3,"text":"1 - Tool: Microsoft Copilot Studio\n\nThe ROI calculation for AI agents is done using:\n- Telemetry from Copilot Studio\n- Task duration metrics\n- Usage analytics\n\nThis aligns with the requirement to measure how long tasks currently take so the organization can compare:\n- Before AI agent vs. After AI agent\n\nFoundry, ARM, and Dynamics 365 Sales do not provide the required task‑level timing metrics for ROI.\n\n2 - Data required for the tool: the current time to complete the task today per instance\n\nROI requires a baseline:\n- How long does the task take right now?\n- How much time will the AI agent save per instance?\n\nThis is the only data point in the list that directly supports ROI modeling for AI agent adoption."},{"user":"rveney","date":"2026-02-24","up":2,"text":"Tool: Dynamics 365 Sales\n\nData required for the tool: the current time to complete the task today per instance"}]},{"n":77,"id":984466,"topic":3,"stem":"<p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which tool should you recommend to help secure funding for future AI agent development?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Evaluations in Microsoft Foundry"},{"k":"B","html":"the Azure Cost Optimization workbook"},{"k":"C","html":"Azure Operator Insights"},{"k":"D","html":"the Analytics tab in Microsoft Copilot Studio"},{"k":"E","html":"Direct Preference Optimization (DPO)"}],"answer":"D","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"A","p":13,"n":2},{"a":"D","p":87,"n":13}],"page":2,"case":"d646994a1b","thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/22539a6ca3fdc3b1bb91d46d0c7cddc9984466/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-01","up":6,"text":"✅ Correct answer: D. the Analytics tab in Microsoft Copilot Studio\n\nThe Analytics tab in Copilot Studio provides:\n- Usage metrics (how often the agent is used)\n- Adoption trends (month‑over‑month usage)\n- Conversation volume\n- Success vs. failure rates\n- Insights needed to justify ROI\n\nThese metrics are exactly what stakeholders need to approve future funding.","pick":"D"},{"user":"Alicia_lili","date":"2026-05-04","up":3,"text":"Analytics in CPS","pick":"D"},{"user":"2db2984","date":"2026-05-03","up":2,"text":"D is right because the requirement is to increase AI adoption not to evaluate the AI response quality.","pick":"D"},{"user":"ppolychron","date":"2026-03-15","up":2,"text":"I don't think its Evaluations in Foundry since, in my knowledge, you use them to check if an agent meets quality and safety standards before deployment.\n\nI will go with Analytics tab in Copilot studio, where you can directly see the engagement and savings.","pick":"D"},{"user":"realexamguru","date":"2026-03-13","up":1,"text":"Analytics tab is correct. In the problem statement it says \"funding for future AI initiatives will depend on demonstrating an increase in AI adoption month over month\". To show that we can use analytics tab in CPS. Evaluations in Foundry is not right, it is used to evaluate models quality.","pick":"D"},{"user":"silver","date":"2026-03-07","up":1,"text":"Foundry supports ROI and Business case modeling","pick":"A"},{"user":"madimad","date":"2026-03-05","up":1,"text":"Answer is correct","pick":"D"},{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":1,"text":"Copilot says A. And no.. I have not just used Copilot for all my answers. I'm just tired and going to bed. I'll figure this out tomorrow.","pick":"A"}]},{"n":78,"id":984467,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>You are designing a Microsoft Copilot Studio agent that uses a custom Microsoft Foundry model to generate responses.</p><p>You need to ensure that the agent can securely connect to and invoke the custom model during user interactions.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you include in the design?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Configure the agent to use classic orchestration."},{"k":"B","html":"Create a connection to Microsoft Foundry in the agent."},{"k":"C","html":"Add the Microsoft Foundry model as a Copilot Studio skill."},{"k":"D","html":"Create a custom engine agent."}],"answer":"B","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"B","p":100,"n":7}],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/d6c4f7fbb2afacb11cc4f36d65036f02984467/","comments":[{"user":"ppolychron","date":"2026-03-15","up":3,"text":"I am going with B. In Bring Your Own Model scenario in Copilot Studio, you connect a Foundry model when creating a prompt tool.\n\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-copilot-studio/bring-your-own-model-prompts#add-and-configure-a-prompt","pick":"B"},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-01","up":2,"text":"Correct answer: B. Create a connection to Microsoft Foundry in the agent.\n\nThe key requirement in your scenario is securely connecting a Copilot Studio agent to a custom Microsoft Foundry model so the agent can invoke it during user interactions. That capability is enabled through connections, not orchestration modes, skills, or custom engine agents.\n\nTo securely invoke a custom Microsoft Foundry model from a Copilot Studio agent, you must create a Foundry connection inside the agent.","pick":"B"},{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":2,"text":"Could be B or D? I love D ;)... but not sure. I'll go with B. I need sleep","pick":"B"}]},{"n":79,"id":984468,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>You are designing an AI business solution that contains the following components:</p><ul><li>A Microsoft Power Automate workflow</li><li>A Microsoft Copilot Studio agent</li><li>A Microsoft Dataverse database</li><li>A Microsoft Power Apps app</li></ul><p>As part of the application lifecycle management (ALM) process, you plan to package the components, so that they can be deployed to other environments as a group.</p><p>You need to recommend a solution that supports versioning, dependencies, and deployments.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you include in the recommendation?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"GitHub Actions"},{"k":"B","html":"Azure DevOps"},{"k":"C","html":"Microsoft Power Platform solutions"}],"answer":"C","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"C","p":100,"n":13}],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/9ee7e996d9419d8c61fcc5d6129822af984468/","comments":[{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":7,"text":"Why GitHub Actions and Azure DevOps are not the primary answer\nBoth GitHub Actions and Azure DevOps can automate ALM pipelines, but they rely on solutions as the underlying deployment artifact.\n• They orchestrate CI/CD.\n• They do not provide versioning, dependency management, or packaging by themselves.\n• They require solutions to function in Power Platform ALM.\nSo they are optional enhancements—not the core ALM mechanism.","pick":"C","top":true},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-01","up":3,"text":"Correct answer: C. Microsoft Power Platform solutions\n\nThe only option that provides versioning, dependency management, and environment‑to‑environment deployment for:\n- Power Automate flows\n- Copilot Studio agents\n- Dataverse tables\n- Power Apps applications\nis Power Platform solutions.","pick":"C"},{"user":"Eberd","date":"2026-03-06","up":2,"text":"Microsoft Power Platform solutions es correcto. En la solución se guardan todos los componentes para pasar entre ambientes.","pick":"C"},{"user":"Ninashnash","date":"2026-08-06","up":1,"text":"To package the components, they should be contained within a solution.","pick":"C"}]},{"n":80,"id":984469,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>A company has Microsoft 365 Copilot agents.</p><p>You need to design a security solution for the agents. The solution must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Identify and mitigate potential risks that relate to AI use.</li><li>Protect AI apps and the sensitive data processed or generated by the agents.</li><li>Support responsible AI governance by retaining and logging interactions, detecting policy violations, and investigating incidents.</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which two components should you include in the design?</strong> Each correct answer presents part of the solution.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Microsoft Purview"},{"k":"B","html":"Azure AI Content Safety"},{"k":"C","html":"role-based access control (RBAC) in Microsoft Foundry"},{"k":"D","html":"Microsoft Defender"}],"answer":"AD","type":"multi","votes":[{"a":"AB","p":23,"n":3},{"a":"AD","p":77,"n":10}],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/c804266003b87ac6fe9d3e3be27b54c1984469/","comments":[{"user":"ppolychron","date":"2026-03-15","up":5,"text":"A and D for me since we are talking about M365 Copilot Agents.\n\nDSPM for AI ,DLP, M365 Audit Logs, Insider risk management, Communication Compliance, all valuable tools in Purview.\n\nSynching alerts from Purview to Microsoft Defender (XDR) will let you investigate incident from there.","pick":"AD"},{"user":"Ninashnash","date":"2026-08-06","up":2,"text":"Requirement1: Identify and mitigate potential risks that relate to AI use ---> Microsoft Defender\nRequirement2: Protect AI apps and the sensitive data processed or generated by the agents ---> Microsoft Defender (Defender for Cloud Apps/Defender for AI services)\nRequirement3: Support responsible AI governance by retaining and logging interactions, detecting policy violations, and investigating incidents. ----> Microsoft Purview","pick":"AD","replies":[{"user":"Ninashnash","date":"2026-08-06","up":1,"text":"Exam Tip:\nPurview = Governance, Compliance, Audit, Retention\nDefender = Security, Threat Detection, AI Risk Protection\nContent Safety = Harmful Content Filtering\nRBAC = Access Control Only"}]},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-01","up":2,"text":"Correct answers: A. Microsoft Purview and B. Azure AI Content Safety\n\nThese are the only two components that together satisfy all three requirements:\nrisk identification, sensitive‑data protection, and responsible AI governance for Microsoft 365 Copilot agents.\n\nPurview provides the governance, auditing, and data‑protection controls that Copilot agents rely on.\nPurview is the only Microsoft product that logs Copilot interactions and enforces data‑protection policies across the Microsoft 365 ecosystem.\n\nAzure AI Content Safety provides AI‑specific risk detection.\nThis directly satisfies the requirement to identify and mitigate AI‑related risks.","pick":"AB"},{"user":"Jedi","date":"2026-03-08","up":2,"text":"I think A and D are correct. B is aligned with Foundry. Defender is aligned with Copilot Studio agents https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/blog/microsoftthreatprotectionblog/protect-copilot-studio-ai-agents-in-real-time-with-microsoft-defender/4446560","pick":"AD"},{"user":"madimad","date":"2026-03-04","up":1,"text":"AD is correct answer","pick":"AD"},{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":1,"text":"A and B. D is related but more adjacent security not really AI....to bad because I love D ;)\n\"“identify and mitigate potential risks that relate to AI use.” is more B","pick":"AB"}]},{"n":81,"id":984470,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>You are creating validation criteria for a custom generative AI model that produces business reports based on internal enterprise data.</p><p>You need to assess whether the model's outputs are appropriate and meaningful for the business reports.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which metric should you use?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"the number of active users interacting with the model"},{"k":"B","html":"alignment of the output to domain-specific tasks"},{"k":"C","html":"the average system resource usage during inference"},{"k":"D","html":"the model training duration"}],"answer":"B","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"B","p":100,"n":7}],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/989711f6f74ab8ffd345d48c95fd4f52984470/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-01","up":4,"text":"Correct answer: B. alignment of the output to domain‑specific tasks\n\nThe metric that determines whether a custom generative AI model produces appropriate and meaningful business reports is how well the model’s output aligns with the specific business tasks and domain requirements.","pick":"B"},{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":4,"text":"B .... Final Answer","pick":"B"},{"user":"Eberd","date":"2026-03-08","up":1,"text":"Correcta","pick":"B"}]},{"n":82,"id":984471,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>A company has Microsoft Foundry agents that generate responses by using Azure OpenAI resources. The agents are deployed to both the United States and Europe.</p><p>A company mandate states that the agents and their grounding data must adhere to data residency and movement regulations.</p><p>You need to recommend a governance solution for the agents.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you include in the recommendation?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Microsoft Defender for Cloud"},{"k":"B","html":"Azure Policy"},{"k":"C","html":"Azure Monitor"},{"k":"D","html":"Microsoft Purview"}],"answer":"B","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"B","p":53,"n":19},{"a":"D","p":47,"n":17}],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/452e96bcd77e6f6577c942a247f146dd984471/","comments":[{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":10,"text":"Its B https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/policy/overview","pick":"B","top":true},{"user":"QueenShi","date":"2026-03-16","up":6,"text":"Yes, Azure Policy can enforce where resources are deployed, but it doesn't govern the data movement and classification layer. I would choose Purview as the best-of-breed governance solution: The scenario centers on data residency, data movement regulations, and governance of AI agents and their grounding data.","pick":"D"},{"user":"deca0d4","date":"2026-05-01","up":4,"text":"Microsoft Purview is specifically designed for:\n\nData governance across environments and regions\nData classification and sensitivity labeling\nData residency and compliance enforcement\nMonitoring and auditing data movement\n\nAzure Policy is useful, but narrower:\n\nEnforces resource configuration rules\nExample:\n“Only deploy resources in Canada”\n“Require specific SKUs or regions”","pick":"D"},{"user":"timothy123","date":"2026-08-25","up":3,"text":"You would use Azure Policy to force developers to deploy the Azure OpenAI resource into a US or European data center, but you must use Microsoft Purview to ensure the actual information processed by those agents obeys regional data movement laws.","pick":"D"},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-01","up":3,"text":"Correct answer: D. Microsoft Purview\n\nFor Microsoft Foundry agents and Azure OpenAI resources deployed across multiple regions (U.S. and Europe), the company must enforce data residency, data movement controls, governance, and auditing.\nOnly Microsoft Purview provides the governance capabilities required for this scenario.","pick":"D"},{"user":"silver","date":"2026-03-07","up":3,"text":"The location can be enforced by Azure Policy","pick":"B"},{"user":"Jedi","date":"2026-03-08","up":2,"text":"https://azure.microsoft.com/mediahandler/files/resourcefiles/achieving-compliant-data-residency-and-security-with-azure/Enabling_Data_Residency_and_Data_Protection_in_Microsoft_Azure_Regions.pdf","pick":"B"},{"user":"Eberd","date":"2026-03-04","up":2,"text":"Respuesta final: B. Azure Policy","pick":"B"},{"user":"Az301301X","date":"2026-10-03","up":1,"text":"The wording \"agents and their grounding data\" is the important clue. If the question were simply \"ensure Azure OpenAI/Foundry resources are deployed only in approved regions,\" Azure Policy would be the natural answer. But once the requirement explicitly encompasses grounding data and data movement/regulatory governance, Purview is the intended governance service.","pick":"D"},{"user":"Ninashnash","date":"2026-08-06","up":1,"text":"Since the requirement is specifically about enforcing regional deployment constraints and preventing regulated data from moving/residing outside allowed regions, Azure Policy is the correct governance tool to include in the recommendation.","pick":"B"},{"user":"24b8eec","date":"2026-06-17","up":1,"text":"he key distinction this question tests: data residency = region/location enforcement → that's Azure Policy's \"Allowed locations\" built-in policy (\"enforce your geo-compliance requirements\"). Microsoft Purview is a tempting distractor because it is a data-governance product — but Purview governs/classifies the data itself; it doesn't enforce where resources and data get deployed. That enforcement is Azure Policy's job.","pick":"B"}]},{"n":83,"id":984472,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>A company has a Microsoft Copilot Studio agent that uses custom connectors to interact with enterprise APIs.</p><p>You need to recommend an application lifecycle management (ALM) process to ensure that the connectors are deployed consistently across development, test, and production environments and meet governance and traceability requirements.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you recommend?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Deploy the APIs as Azure Functions."},{"k":"B","html":"Manage the connectors as solution components and deploy the components by using ALM pipelines."},{"k":"C","html":"Maintain connector definitions in environment variables."},{"k":"D","html":"Export and import the connectors between the environments as unmanaged solutions."}],"answer":"B","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"B","p":88,"n":15},{"a":"C","p":12,"n":2}],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/5f9ca71c2f4a1ffffc0a5ad1db50d9d4984472/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-01","up":5,"text":"Correct answer: B. Manage the connectors as solution components and deploy the components by using ALM pipelines.\n\nHere’s the concise reasoning first:\nTo ensure consistent deployment, governance, and traceability for custom connectors used by a Copilot Studio agent, the connectors must be included in a Power Platform solution and moved through ALM pipelines (Dev → Test → Prod). This is the only option that satisfies all requirements.","pick":"B"},{"user":"QueenShi","date":"2026-03-16","up":3,"text":"B is the only answer that meets the requirements: consistent deployment, governance and traceability, and ALM pipelines in Power Platform enable this for solution-aware components like custom connectors.","pick":"B"},{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":3,"text":"Going with B. I'm 70% on this one.","pick":"B"},{"user":"rveney","date":"2026-02-24","up":2,"text":"Recommended answer: B. Manage the connectors as solution components and deploy the components by using ALM pipelines.","pick":"B"},{"user":"CyrilleC","date":"2026-07-30","up":1,"text":"Correct answer: B. Manage the connectors as solution components and deploy the components by using ALM pipelines","pick":"B"},{"user":"silver","date":"2026-03-07","up":1,"text":"B is correct.","pick":"B"},{"user":"Eberd","date":"2026-03-06","up":1,"text":"Para pasar entre ambientes, desa,qa y prd. Los endpoints se guardan en variables de entorno, estas variables se llaman igual y pero apuntan a distintos endpoints, dev,qa, prd respectivamente. Así el pasaje es trasparente.","pick":"C"},{"user":"Eberd","date":"2026-03-04","up":1,"text":"Es la forma que recomienda microsoft para trabajar entre ambientes","pick":"C"}]},{"n":84,"id":984473,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>A company plans to implement an AI solution that will contain a Microsoft Copilot Studio agent and a Microsoft Foundry agent. The solution will be stored in a source code repository.</p><p>You need to recommend a deployment method for each agent. The solution must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>A test environment must be used before a deployment to production.</li><li>Production must be isolated from development and testing.</li><li>The deployment must be repeatable and fully automated.</li><li>The solution must NOT require manual intervention.</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which deployment method should you recommend for each agent?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image23.png\" alt=\"image25\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image24.png\" alt=\"image26\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/4df9cf3c1ce8bd9b007bfe3d9ad32fb6984473/","comments":[{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":15,"text":"CPS = Pipelines\nFoundry = Azure DevOps","top":true},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-01","up":4,"text":"1) Copilot Studio agent → Use a Microsoft Power Platform deployment pipeline\nPower Platform deployment pipelines are the official ALM mechanism for Copilot Studio agents. They support:\n- Dev → Test → Prod stages\n- Managed solution deployment\n- Automated, repeatable deployments\n- Isolation between environments\n- No manual steps once configured\n\n2) Microsoft Foundry agent → Use an Azure DevOps pipeline\nMicrosoft Foundry agents are deployed like Azure resources.\nTo automate deployments from a source code repository with:\n- Infrastructure-as-code\n- CI/CD\n- Multi‑environment promotion\n- No manual intervention\n…the correct choice is Azure DevOps pipelines (or GitHub Actions, but that option is not available in your answer list)."},{"user":"Eberd","date":"2026-03-05","up":4,"text":"El despliegue automático se hace con:\n👉 Azure DevOps pipeline"},{"user":"Ninashnash","date":"2026-08-06","up":3,"text":"Copilot Studio: Use a Microsoft Power Platform deployment pipeline.\nMicrosoft Foundry: Use an Azure DevOps pipeline."},{"user":"rveney","date":"2026-02-24","up":3,"text":"Copilot Studio:\n✅ Use a Microsoft Power Platform deployment pipeline.\nWhy this fits: Power Platform pipelines are purpose-built for promoting Copilot Studio/Power Platform solutions across Dev → Test → Prod with environment isolation and automated, repeatable deployments from a controlled process.\n\nMicrosoft Foundry:\n✅ Use an Azure DevOps pipeline.\nWhy this fits: Foundry (Azure AI Foundry / Foundry agents) aligns with CI/CD automation from source control, where Azure DevOps pipelines can deploy across separate test and production resources in a fully automated manner (including IaC steps if needed)."}]},{"n":85,"id":984474,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>A company has a Microsoft Copilot Studio prompt-and-response agent.</p><p>You need to ensure that the agent meets the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Provides effective and relevant responses</li><li>Provides conversational outcomes</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which metric should you use for each requirement?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image25.png\" alt=\"image27\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image26.png\" alt=\"image28\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/b019cd84f9021baa5a1e33b3c8448cdc984474/","comments":[{"user":"madimad","date":"2026-03-04","up":13,"text":"1.Generated answer rate and quality\n2.Topics by outcome","top":true},{"user":"CyrilleC","date":"2026-07-30","up":3,"text":"1 - Provides effective and relevant responses → Generated answer rate and quality\n2 - Provides conversational outcomes → Topics by outcome\n\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-copilot-studio/analytics-improve-agent-effectiveness#conversation-outcomes"},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-01","up":3,"text":"1) Provides effective and relevant responses → Generated answer rate and quality\nThis metric evaluates how well the agent produces accurate, grounded, and contextually relevant responses.\nIt directly measures response quality, which is exactly what the requirement asks for.\n\n2) Provides conversational outcomes → Satisfaction\nConversational outcomes are measured by user satisfaction, which reflects whether the interaction achieved the user’s intended goal and whether the conversation was successful overall."},{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":3,"text":"Correct","replies":[{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-05","up":5,"text":"Sorry second one is \"Topics by Outcome\" https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-copilot-studio/analytics-improve-agent-effectiveness#conversation-outcomes"}]},{"user":"Eberd","date":"2026-03-08","up":2,"text":"La métrica correcta es:\nTopics by outcome"},{"user":"rveney","date":"2026-02-24","up":1,"text":"Provides effective and relevant responses: Generated answer rate and quality\nProvides conversational outcomes: Topics by outcome"}]},{"n":86,"id":984475,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>A company extends Copilot in Microsoft Dynamics 365 Customer Service.</p><p>You need to recommend an automated application lifecycle management (ALM) process so that the Copilot components can be safely developed, tested, and promoted to production.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which two actions should you include in the ALM process?</strong> Each correct answer presents part of the solution.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Use an unmanaged solution in production."},{"k":"B","html":"Rebuild the agents in each environment."},{"k":"C","html":"Use Microsoft Power Platform pipelines."},{"k":"D","html":"Include the components in a solution."},{"k":"E","html":"Store the agent transcripts in source control."}],"answer":"CD","type":"multi","votes":[{"a":"CD","p":100,"n":11}],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/648cd578671c40c714ee7aa511111201984475/","comments":[{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":5,"text":"Correct","pick":"CD"},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-01","up":3,"text":"D. Include the components in a solution\nAll Copilot extensions for Dynamics 365 Customer Service—custom actions, plugins, connectors, prompts, and Copilot Studio agents—must be packaged inside a Power Platform solution to support:\n- Versioning\n- Dependency tracking\n- Environment isolation\n-Managed deployments to Test/Prod\n\nC. Use Microsoft Power Platform pipelines\nDeployment pipelines provide:\n- Automated Dev → Test → Prod promotion\n- No manual intervention\n- Governance and approvals\n- Repeatable deployments\n- Managed solution enforcement in production","pick":"CD"},{"user":"CyrilleC","date":"2026-07-30","up":2,"text":"Correct Answers :\nC. Use Microsoft Power Platform pipelines\nD. Include the components in a solution","pick":"CD"},{"user":"Eberd","date":"2026-03-05","up":1,"text":"Correcto","pick":"CD"},{"user":"madimad","date":"2026-03-04","up":1,"text":"C & D are correct","pick":"CD"}]},{"n":87,"id":984476,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>You are designing a testing solution for a Microsoft Copilot Studio agent that integrates with Microsoft Dynamics 365 Customer Service and Dynamics 365 Sales.</p><p>You need to design end-to-end scenarios to test the agent's ability to perform the following actions:</p><ul><li>Coordinate tasks and data interactions across both Dynamics 365 apps.</li><li>Interpret user input and provide contextually relevant outputs.</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which test scenario and metric should you include in the design?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image27.png\" alt=\"image29\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image28.png\" alt=\"image30\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/31750531236fb2dd765102465813d524984476/","comments":[{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":7,"text":"Correct","top":true},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-01","up":5,"text":"1) Test scenario: Run task‑based scenarios that involve both apps\nYou must simulate end‑to‑end workflows that span Customer Service and Sales—such as creating a case, updating an opportunity, or retrieving customer history across systems.\nThis is exactly what task‑based scenarios involving both apps are designed for.\n\n2) Metric: Track the successful completion of cross‑app tasks\nThe best metric is whether the agent can successfully complete the multi‑app tasks it was asked to perform.\nThis validates:\n- Correct interpretation of user intent\n- Correct grounding\n- Correct orchestration across systems\n- Correct data retrieval and updates"},{"user":"Eberd","date":"2026-03-08","up":1,"text":"Correcto"},{"user":"madimad","date":"2026-03-04","up":1,"text":"Given answer is correct"}]},{"n":88,"id":984477,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>A company has multiple AI models that support generation of sales transactions.</p><p>Each release of the models must be reviewed by a security and compliance team before being deployed to the production environment. The security and compliance team must have access to prior versions to properly determine potential exposures introduced.</p><p>You need to recommend a solution to evaluate the impact of each deployment to production. The solution must enhance business continuity.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you recommend?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Create a central model registry that uses version history."},{"k":"B","html":"Establish a promotion process by using a quality gate."},{"k":"C","html":"Implement version control for all the AI system components."},{"k":"D","html":"Track model retirement schedules to prevent service disruptions."}],"answer":"A","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"A","p":100,"n":14}],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/ebc19bc7fc735076acd249aafc94a4bb984477/","comments":[{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":5,"text":"A. Create a central model registry that uses version history.","pick":"A"},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-01","up":2,"text":"The correct answer is: A. Create a central model registry that uses version history.\n\nYou described three key requirements:\n- Every model release must be reviewed by security and compliance before production.\n- Security must have access to prior versions to compare changes and detect new risks.\n- Business continuity must be protected — meaning controlled, traceable, reversible deployments.\nThis is exactly the problem that a central model registry with versioning is designed to solve.","pick":"A"},{"user":"janesb","date":"2026-03-15","up":2,"text":"the Microsoft-native way is to create an Azure Machine Learning registry and then register each model version into it. Microsoft says registries decouple ML assets from workspaces so you can share models across dev, test, and prod.","pick":"A"},{"user":"Eberd","date":"2026-03-08","up":2,"text":"Create a central model registry that uses version history — permite almacenar y versionar modelos en un repositorio central para que seguridad revise cada release, compare versiones anteriores y habilite rollback, mejorando la continuidad del negocio.","pick":"A"},{"user":"rveney","date":"2026-02-24","up":2,"text":"A. Create a central model registry that uses version history.","pick":"A"},{"user":"CyrilleC","date":"2026-07-30","up":1,"text":"The correct answer is: A\n\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/rest/api/azureml/registry-model-versions/list?view=rest-azureml-2026-05-01&tabs=HTTP\nhttps://azure-foundry.mintlify.app/docs/foundry-models/concepts/model-versions","pick":"A"},{"user":"madimad","date":"2026-03-04","up":1,"text":"A is correct answer","pick":"A"}]},{"n":89,"id":984478,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>A company has an AI solution that uses a Microsoft Copilot Studio agent.</p><p>You need to monitor the agent's performance. The solution must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Monitor the agent's telemetry in near-real-time (NRT).</li><li>Download transcripts of full conversations.</li><li>Monitor the agent's usage and performance.</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you use for each requirement?</strong> To answer, drag the appropriate options to the correct requirements. Each option may be used once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to drag the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image29.png\" alt=\"image31\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image30.png\" alt=\"image32\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/005ac6d8870c23dbadb23a10a51c4c63984478/","comments":[{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":14,"text":"Near‑real‑time telemetry → Application Insights\nApplication Insights is the only option that provides live metrics, NRT telemetry, and deep diagnostics (requests, dependencies, exceptions, traces). Copilot Studio can surface analytics, but not true NRT telemetry.\nFull conversation transcripts → Copilot Studio\nCopilot Studio includes the Transcripts area where you can export full conversations. Application Insights only stores event‑level telemetry, not full transcripts.\nUsage & performance monitoring → Copilot Studio\nCopilot Studio provides built‑in analytics dashboards for:\n• Session counts\n• Escalations\n• Resolution rates\n• Channel usage\n• CSAT\n• Topic performance\nThese are the standard usage/performance KPIs for Copilot Studio agents.","top":true,"replies":[{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-05","up":9,"text":"Second one could be Power Apps. https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-copilot-studio/analytics-transcripts-studio.\n\n\"When you download session information from Copilot Studio, you get a subset of the information available for download from Power Apps, in the form of a comma-separated value (CSV) file. The CSV file includes the actual conversation and some metrics and information about the session (see Work with session transcripts for a list of metrics included in the CSV file). To see all activities, download transcripts through Power Apps.\"","top":true,"replies":[{"user":"timothy123","date":"2026-08-25","up":1,"text":"Power Apps requires navigating away from the agent to the Power Apps portal, finding the correct environment, and locating the specific ConversationTranscript table in Dataverse to export the data. Additionally you need certain security roles.\nI would go for the simplest option initially. Copilot Studio: Features a native, built-in \"Download Sessions\" button right inside the agent's analytics portal. It requires zero configuration or technical setup to grab the last 29 days of chat logs"}]}]},{"user":"madimad","date":"2026-03-04","up":6,"text":"1.Application Insights\n2. Log Analytics\n3.Copilot Studio"},{"user":"rveney","date":"2026-02-24","up":6,"text":"Monitor the agent's telemetry in NRT: Application Insights\nDownload transcripts of full conversations: Copilot Studio\nMonitor the agent's usage and performance: Copilot Studio"},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-03","up":2,"text":"1) Log Analytics → Near‑real‑time telemetry\nCopilot Studio can stream telemetry (events, traces, errors, conversation signals) into Azure Monitor / Log Analytics\nThis is the only option that meets the NRT requirement.\n\n2) Copilot Studio → Download full conversation transcripts\nConversation transcripts are stored inside Copilot Studio analytics.\nNo other option provides transcript export.\n\n3) Application Insights → Usage and performance monitoring\nApplication Insights provides: Usage metrics, Performance metrics, Latency, Error rates, Dependency calls.\nThis is the correct tool for monitoring overall agent performance."},{"user":"Alicia_lili","date":"2026-05-04","up":1,"text":"NRT telemetry → Application Insights\nTranscripts → Copilot Studio\nUsage & performance → Log Analytics","replies":[{"user":"timothy123","date":"2026-08-25","up":1,"text":"Power Apps requires navigating away from the agent to the Power Apps portal, finding the correct environment, and locating the specific ConversationTranscript table in Dataverse to export the data. Additionally you need certain security roles.\nI would go for the simplest option initially. Copilot Studio: Features a native, built-in \"Download Sessions\" button right inside the agent's analytics portal. It requires zero configuration or technical setup to grab the last 29 days of chat logs"}]}]},{"n":90,"id":984479,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>A company deploys a Microsoft Copilot Studio agent that integrates with a Microsoft Power Automate desktop flow.</p><p>You need to recommend a testing solution that meets the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Test cases must validate the most recent changes to the agent before the agent is released.</li><li>The flow must be validated as part of the agent's orchestration.</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you recommend for each requirement?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image31.png\" alt=\"image33\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image32.png\" alt=\"image34\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/950115eb50bacb8f6a9336a32ce81f23984479/","comments":[{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":15,"text":"The correct pair is:\nValidate the most recent changes to the agent before release:\nRun tests against the latest unpublished version of the agent.\nThis is the only option that ensures you are validating new changes before publishing.\n\nTesting on production or live users would not meet the requirement.\nValidate the flow as part of the agent’s orchestration:\nAdd the flow to the agent as a tool.\nA Power Automate desktop flow must be exposed to Copilot Studio as a tool so the agent can call it during orchestration. Canvas apps and the PAD console do not integrate with Copilot Studio orchestration.","top":true},{"user":"madimad","date":"2026-03-04","up":9,"text":"1.Run tests against the latest unpublished version of the agent\n2.Add the flow to the agent as a tool","top":true},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-03","up":7,"text":"1) ➡ Run tests against the latest unpublished version of the agent\nTo validate updates before publishing, Copilot Studio allows you to test the unpublished version of the agent.\nThis ensures:\n- You test the latest changes\n- No impact on production\n- No need to publish to a channel\n- No exposure to live users\n\n2) ➡ Add the flow to the agent as a tool\nFor the agent to orchestrate the desktop flow during testing, the flow must be added as a tool inside the agent.\nAdding it to a canvas app or using the desktop console does not integrate it into the agent’s orchestration.","top":true},{"user":"rveney","date":"2026-02-24","up":5,"text":"Validate the most recent changes to the agent before release:\nRun tests against the latest unpublished version of the agent.\n\nValidate the flow as part of the agent's orchestration:\nAdd the flow to the agent as a tool."}]},{"n":91,"id":984480,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>A company has a Microsoft Copilot Studio agent that provides answers based on a knowledge base for customer support.</p><p>Users report that, occasionally, the agent provides inaccurate answers.</p><p>You need to use metrics from the Analytics tab in Copilot Studio to identify the cause of the inaccuracies.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which two options should you use?</strong> Each correct answer presents part of the solution.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"survey results"},{"k":"B","html":"session information and session outcomes"},{"k":"C","html":"topic usage and topics with low resolution"},{"k":"D","html":"engagement, resolution, and escalation rates"},{"k":"E","html":"quality of generated answers"}],"answer":"CE","type":"multi","votes":[{"a":"BC","p":13,"n":2},{"a":"BE","p":38,"n":6},{"a":"CE","p":50,"n":8}],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/8a48650ea61f7d43ad1b2a09450bbba3984480/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-03","up":4,"text":"B. Session information and session outcomes\nThis metric shows:\n- How conversations unfolded\n- Where the agent misunderstood the user\n- Whether the session ended in success, escalation, or failure\n- Patterns of incorrect grounding or mis‑routed topics\nThis is essential for diagnosing why the agent produced an incorrect answer.\n\nE. quality of generated answers\nThis metric evaluates:\n- Relevance\n- Accuracy\n- Grounding quality\n- Whether the answer aligns with the knowledge base\nIf the agent is hallucinating or misusing the knowledge base, this metric exposes it.","pick":"BE"},{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":4,"text":"IT's C and E !!!","pick":"CE"},{"user":"Ninashnash","date":"2026-08-06","up":3,"text":"keyword in question is \"identify the cause of the inaccuracies.\" Only B and E can help to identify the root cause:\n\nB (session information and session outcomes) lets you inspect the actual query, the knowledge source used, and the conversation flow — which can reveal the cause (e.g., wrong knowledge source retrieved, user question misunderstood, missing content).\n\nE (quality of generated answers) directly gives a cause — Copilot Studio assigns a specific reason category to each poor-quality answer (e.g., irrelevant, incomplete, ungrounded), which is a textbook \"cause.\"","pick":"BE"},{"user":"madimad","date":"2026-03-04","up":3,"text":"correct answer C & E","pick":"CE"},{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":2,"text":"The two analytics areas in Copilot Studio that directly help diagnose why a knowledge‑base–driven agent is giving inaccurate answers are:\nB. Session information and session outcomes\nC. Topic usage and topics with low resolution","pick":"BC","replies":[{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":5,"text":"I was wrong it's this...\n\nThe correct analytics areas to diagnose why a Copilot Studio agent sometimes gives inaccurate answers from a knowledge base are:\n\n✔ C. topic usage and topics with low resolution\n✔ E. quality of generated answers\n\nThese two directly map to the root‑cause signals described in the Microsoft Learn page you have open."}]},{"user":"Joselito79","date":"2026-09-22","up":1,"text":"✅ Correct answers: C and E\nOption Why\nC. Topic usage and topics with low resolution Helps identify which topics are associated with poor outcomes, revealing areas where the agent may have knowledge/coverage problems.\nE. Quality of generated answers Directly measures whether generative AI answers are Good or Poor, allowing you to investigate inaccurate responses and the knowledge sources involved.","pick":"CE"},{"user":"Juan_Covili","date":"2026-06-28","up":1,"text":"Quality of generated answers es la métrica más directa para investigar respuestas inexactas generadas desde una knowledge base. Copilot Studio analiza la calidad de respuestas generativas considerando factores como completeness, relevance y groundedness, y marca respuestas como buenas o pobres. Además, para respuestas pobres muestra razones de baja calidad.","pick":"BE"},{"user":"rveney","date":"2026-02-24","up":1,"text":"C. topic usage and topics with low resolution\nE. quality of generated answers","pick":"CE"}]},{"n":92,"id":984481,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>A company uses a fine-tuned Microsoft Foundry model that requires frequent updates as new customer feedback becomes available.</p><p>You need to design an application lifecycle management (ALM) process that meets the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Data changes must be tracked and versioned.</li><li>The model must be retrained consistently by using approved training data.</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which two actions should you include in the design?</strong> Each correct answer presents part of the solution.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Associate the storage location to the fine-tuning job."},{"k":"B","html":"Create a content filter."},{"k":"C","html":"Store the training data in Azure Files."},{"k":"D","html":"Upload the training data to Microsoft Foundry data files"},{"k":"E","html":"Store the training data in Azure Blob Storage that has version control enabled."}],"answer":"AE","type":"multi","votes":[{"a":"AE","p":53,"n":10},{"a":"DE","p":47,"n":9}],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/14ca27b2305299f5f244fcc46f246fe8984481/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-03","up":6,"text":"A. Associate the storage location to the fine‑tuning job\nFoundry fine‑tuning jobs support referencing a storage location (Blob Storage or Foundry data files).\nThis ensures:\n- The model is always trained on the approved dataset\n- Retraining is consistent and repeatable\n- The job pulls data from a controlled, governed location\nThis is essential for ALM.\n\nE. Store the training data in Azure Blob Storage with version control\nBlob Storage with versioning provides:\n- Automatic version history of every dataset change\n- Ability to roll back to prior versions\n- Full traceability for compliance and audits\n- A single source of truth for training data\nThis directly satisfies the requirement to track and version data changes.","pick":"AE"},{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":6,"text":"Going with D and E but only about 80% on this. Any insights? Is anyone else here with me? Hello?","pick":"DE","replies":[{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-04-12","up":2,"text":"Agree with D and E"}]},{"user":"Joselito79","date":"2026-09-21","up":2,"text":"✅ Correct answers: A and E\nRequirement Answer\nData changes must be tracked and versioned E. Store the training data in Azure Blob Storage that has version control enabled\nModel must be retrained consistently using approved training data A. Associate the storage location to the fine-tuning job\n\nA. Associate the storage location to the fine-tuning job ✅\nThis makes the designated training-data location the consistent source for the fine-tuning process.\n\nE. Azure Blob Storage + version control ✅\nBlob Storage versioning preserves previous versions of training data when files change, satisfying the ALM requirement to track data changes.","pick":"AE"},{"user":"kevinirl","date":"2026-08-23","up":2,"text":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/foundry-classic/how-to/fine-tune-serverless?tabs=chat-completion&pivots=foundry-portal","pick":"AE"},{"user":"Ninashnash","date":"2026-08-06","up":2,"text":"A is correct and this Ref confirms you can use Azure Blob storage for your training data in fine tuning your model in Foundry:\n\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/foundry-classic/how-to/fine-tune-serverless?tabs=chat-completion&pivots=foundry-portal","pick":"AE"},{"user":"madimad","date":"2026-03-04","up":2,"text":"D & E are correct answer","pick":"DE"},{"user":"Joselito79","date":"2026-09-19","up":1,"text":"✅ Correct answers: D and E\nD. Upload the training data to Microsoft Foundry data files\nProvides a managed, consistent dataset that can be used for repeated fine-tuning jobs.\nHelps ensure the retraining process uses the intended/approved training data. Microsoft documents Foundry fine-tuning as using uploaded or existing training datasets.\nE. Store the training data in Azure Blob Storage that has version control enabled\nAzure Blob Storage versioning tracks changes to training files and preserves previous versions.\nThis directly satisfies “Data changes must be tracked and versioned.”\nBlob Storage is also supported as a source for importing fine-tuning data.","pick":"DE"},{"user":"Eberd","date":"2026-03-05","up":1,"text":"Correcto","pick":"DE"}]},{"n":93,"id":984482,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>A company deploys agents that generate responses by using Azure OpenAI resources. The agents are deployed to both the United States and Europe.</p><p>You need to recommend a governance solution that meets the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Enforces the deployment of the resources to only approved Azure regions</li><li>Provides continuous compliance verification of the resources</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you include in the recommendation for each requirement?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image33.png\" alt=\"image35\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image34.png\" alt=\"image36\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/73663366536930ce8a2356e133a020be984482/","comments":[{"user":"janesb","date":"2026-03-07","up":13,"text":"1st part of the question is correct Azure policy , but for the 2nd part it should be Defender , not Purview. Purview is a data governance / compliance tool, but the requirement here is continuous compliance verification of Azure resources (Azure OpenAI accounts, storage, networking, logging, encryption settings, public access, etc.)","top":true},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-03","up":10,"text":"1. Azure Policy → Restrict deployments to approved regions\nAzure Policy can enforce rules such as:\n- “Resources may only be deployed in East US and West Europe”\n- “Deny creation of resources outside approved regions”\nThis is the only tool designed for preventive governance.\n\n2. Microsoft Defender for Cloud → Continuous compliance verification\nDefender for Cloud provides:\n- Continuous compliance assessments\n- Regulatory standards mapping (ISO, SOC, GDPR, etc.)\n- Secure score\n- Alerts when resources drift out of compliance\nThis satisfies the requirement for ongoing compliance monitoring.","top":true},{"user":"rveney","date":"2026-02-24","up":6,"text":"Enforces the deployment of the resources to only approved Azure regions:\n➡️ Azure Policy\n\nUse built-in or custom Azure Policy definitions such as “Allowed locations” to deny deployments outside approved US and EU regions.\n\nProvides continuous compliance verification of the resources:\n➡️ Microsoft Defender for Cloud\n\nDefender for Cloud provides continuous security posture and compliance monitoring, including compliance dashboards and ongoing assessment against standards (it leverages policy evaluations and surfaces compliance status continuously)."},{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":3,"text":"I'm about 90% sure it's Azure Policy for both"},{"user":"Joselito79","date":"2026-09-22","up":1,"text":". Approved regions → Azure Policy\nAzure Policy has a built-in Allowed locations policy that can restrict resource deployments to specified Azure regions. With a Deny effect, deployments outside the approved regions are blocked.\n\n2. Continuous compliance → Azure Policy\nAzure Policy evaluates resources for compliance when they're created/updated and through the ongoing compliance evaluation cycle (normally every 24 hours). It provides a compliance dashboard showing compliant/non-compliant resources"}]},{"n":94,"id":984483,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>A company has an AI solution that uses Azure OpenAI models.</p><p>You need to recommend a governance solution that monitors and audits changes to model configurations and data usage. The solution must minimize administrative effort.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you include in the recommendation?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Azure Monitor"},{"k":"B","html":"Azure Stream Analytics"},{"k":"C","html":"Azure API Management"},{"k":"D","html":"Azure Policy"},{"k":"E","html":"Microsoft Purview"}],"answer":"E","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"A","p":13,"n":2},{"a":"C","p":6,"n":1},{"a":"D","p":13,"n":2},{"a":"E","p":69,"n":11}],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/bc5e0e0343456acf7c8b61e9980e0f77984483/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-03","up":4,"text":"✅ Correct Answer: E. Microsoft Purview\n\nThe requirement is clear:\nYou need governance over model configuration changes and data usage, with minimal administrative effort.\n\nAmong the options, only one service is designed specifically for:\n- Monitoring data access and usage\n- Auditing model‑related assets\n- Tracking sensitive data flows\n- Providing governance with minimal overhead\n\nThat service is Microsoft Purview.","pick":"E"},{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":3,"text":"Going with E about 90% on this","pick":"E"},{"user":"janesb","date":"2026-03-15","up":2,"text":"it should be D, Azure Policy","pick":"D"},{"user":"janesb","date":"2026-03-08","up":2,"text":"if the question were about models managed in Azure Machine Learning, the best governance choice would typically shift to Microsoft Purview (often together with Azure Monitor). For Azure Open AI resources, it all about those two things being implemented as resource configuration + telemetry:","pick":"A"},{"user":"Eberd","date":"2026-03-05","up":2,"text":"Microsoft Purview es la plataforma de data governance, compliance y auditoría para datos y aplicaciones de IA.","pick":"E"},{"user":"ppolychron","date":"2026-03-15","up":1,"text":"I will go with C. API Management. Setting up an AI gateway (API management with appropriate policies) in front of the AI models is a standard enterprise tactic that aligns with Azure Well Architected Framework.\n\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/api-management/genai-gateway-capabilities#observability-and-governance","pick":"C","replies":[{"user":"ppolychron","date":"2026-03-16","up":1,"text":"I just noticed the \"solution must minimize administrative effort\". API is high maintenance. DSPM in Purview seems more appropriate."}]},{"user":"madimad","date":"2026-03-04","up":1,"text":"E. is the correct answer","pick":"E"},{"user":"rveney","date":"2026-02-24","up":1,"text":"nclude Microsoft Purview to monitor and audit Azure OpenAI model configuration changes and data usage with the least administrative overhead.","pick":"E"}]},{"n":95,"id":984484,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>A company uses Azure OpenAI models that use grounding data from Microsoft Fabric for agents. The models are fine-tuned by using proprietary datasets.</p><p>You need to design a governance solution that meets the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Restricts access to the grounding data to only assigned roles</li><li>Restricts model fine-tuning to only the AI engineering team</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you include in the design?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image35.png\" alt=\"image37\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image36.png\" alt=\"image38\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/ecd31ba7921615e4913667ca2ede1774984484/","comments":[{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":8,"text":"Correct","top":true},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-03","up":2,"text":"1. Microsoft Purview access policies → Restrict access to grounding data\nGrounding data stored in Microsoft Fabric can be governed using:\n- Purview access policies\n- Data‑level permissions\n- Role‑based access to sensitive datasets\nPurview is the only option that provides fine‑grained, centralized data access governance.\n\nRBAC in Microsoft Foundry → Restrict model fine‑tuning\nFine‑tuning operations in Foundry are controlled through:\n- Foundry workspace roles\n- Model‑level permissions\n- Restricting fine‑tuning to specific security groups (e.g., AI engineering team)\nThis ensures only authorized users can initiate fine‑tuning jobs."}]},{"n":96,"id":984485,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>A company has a Microsoft Copilot Studio agent that has been in production for three months.</p><p>The agent has received positive feedback from users.</p><p>You need to identify the number of questions unanswered by the agent and the number of abandoned sessions between the users and the agent.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which Copilot Studio insights should you use?</strong> To answer, drag the appropriate insights to the correct requirements. Each insight may be used once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to drag the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image37.png\" alt=\"image39\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image38.png\" alt=\"image40\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/504b7c24d27bcc827da85cabf669e8ef984485/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-03","up":3,"text":"1. Generated answer rate and quality → Unanswered questions\nThis insight shows:\n- How often the agent generated an answer\n- How many times it failed to answer\n- Quality and grounding issues\nIt is the only insight that directly exposes unanswered or low‑quality responses.\n\n2. Conversation outcomes → Abandoned sessions\nConversation outcomes include:\n- Completed sessions\n- Escalated sessions\n- Failed sessions\n- Abandoned sessions\nThis is the metric used to track when users leave before the agent completes the task."},{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":3,"text":"Correct"}]},{"n":97,"id":984486,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>You are evaluating a Microsoft Copilot Studio agent that supports Microsoft Dynamics 365 Customer Service representatives.</p><p>You need to recommend a testing solution that meets the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Evaluates agent effectiveness during active sessions</li><li>Validates whether the agent delivers accurate and helpful responses</li><li>Provides measurable, actionable insights for continuous improvement</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you recommend?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Track resolution, deflection, and accuracy by using dashboards and use scripts to ensure consistent responses."},{"k":"B","html":"Perform load testing to validate how the agent scales under a high chat volume."},{"k":"C","html":"Review historical tickets to find agents that have the shortest resolution times."},{"k":"D","html":"Measure uptime and page load times."}],"answer":"A","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"A","p":100,"n":5}],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/db1ce09cb97ffb0efbbeaa134ac04eba984486/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-03","up":3,"text":"The correct recommendation is: A. Track resolution, deflection, and accuracy by using dashboards and use scripts to ensure consistent responses.\n\nResolution, deflection, and accuracy dashboards provide:\n- Real‑time effectiveness metrics\n- How often the agent resolves vs. escalates\n- How many cases are deflected\n- Accuracy and grounding quality\n- Patterns of failure or misunderstanding\n\nUsing scripts ensures consistent prompts and scenarios so you can measure improvements over time.\n\nThis is the only option that meets all requirements.","pick":"A"},{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":2,"text":"Correct","pick":"A"}]},{"n":98,"id":984487,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>A company uses multiple Microsoft Copilot Studio agents across different channels.</p><p>You need to recommend a monitoring solution that provides comprehensive telemetry data and performance insights for the agents.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you include in the recommendation?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Application Insights"},{"k":"B","html":"Azure Advisor"},{"k":"C","html":"Azure DevOps"},{"k":"D","html":"Microsoft Dynamics 365 Customer Voice"}],"answer":"A","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"A","p":100,"n":4}],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/fa4d8c82c3da4221a1952ca443a6abd1984487/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-03","up":2,"text":"The correct recommendation is: A. Application Insights\n\nWhen a company uses multiple Copilot Studio agents across different channels, you need a monitoring solution that can:\n- Collect centralized telemetry\n- Track performance, latency, failures, and usage patterns\n- Provide end‑to‑end observability\n- Support custom events, traces, and distributed logging\n- Scale across all agents and channels\nApplication Insights is the only option that delivers this level of comprehensive monitoring.","pick":"A"},{"user":"madimad","date":"2026-03-04","up":1,"text":"Given answer is correct","pick":"A"},{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":1,"text":"A. 100%","pick":"A"}],"variants":[40,41,42,43,110,120]},{"n":99,"id":984488,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>A company has an AI solution built by using Microsoft Copilot Studio and Power Platform. The solution is used by the company's sales, marketing, and customer service teams.</p><p>You are performing a return on AI investment (ROAI) analysis to evaluate the impact of the solution.</p><p>You need to identify which measurable business drivers to include in the analysis.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which two business drivers should you identify?</strong> Each correct answer presents part of the solution.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"the reduced average case resolution time"},{"k":"B","html":"market capitalization"},{"k":"C","html":"economic market predictability"},{"k":"D","html":"increased employee productivity"},{"k":"E","html":"brand awareness"}],"answer":"AD","type":"multi","votes":[{"a":"AD","p":100,"n":8}],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/578d2f3f1e190874a3f5bf208ea815d4984488/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-03","up":4,"text":"A. the reduced average case resolution time\nThis is a classic ROAI metric because it directly measures:\n- Faster customer service handling\n- Reduced operational cost per case\n- Higher customer satisfaction\n- Improved throughput for support teams\nIt’s quantifiable, trackable, and directly impacted by AI assistance.\n\nD. increased employee productivity\nAI copilots improve productivity by:\n- Automating repetitive tasks\n- Drafting responses\n- Summarizing customer interactions\n- Reducing manual data entry\nThis leads to measurable gains such as:\n- More cases handled per agent\n- More leads processed\n- More time spent on high‑value tasks","pick":"AD"},{"user":"Newb007","date":"2026-03-01","up":4,"text":"A and D. You can't measure the rest in CPS.","pick":"AD"},{"user":"Eberd","date":"2026-03-08","up":1,"text":"Correcta","pick":"AD"},{"user":"madimad","date":"2026-03-04","up":1,"text":"given answer is correct","pick":"AD"}]},{"n":100,"id":994162,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>A company has a Microsoft Foundry agent that summarizes customer feedback and recommends products to customers. The agent references data from multiple knowledge sources.</p><p>Users report that the agent response time is slow.</p><p>Telemetry data shows that the agent frequently reaches its token usage limit.</p><p>You need to recommend a solution to reduce token usage without degrading the quality of the generated responses.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you recommend?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Chunk documents during indexing."},{"k":"B","html":"Reduce the number of knowledge sources used by the agent."},{"k":"C","html":"Reconfigure the prompts to limit the amount of retrieved content from the knowledge sources."},{"k":"D","html":"Lower the maximum token usage limit for the responses."}],"answer":"A","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"A","p":56,"n":9},{"a":"C","p":44,"n":7}],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/4226d4d9ce5e06e7478287cd509e34a6994162/","comments":[{"user":"24b8eec","date":"2026-06-17","up":5,"text":"Answer: A. Chunk documents during indexing.\n\nThe key insight: the other three options all reduce tokens by removing information — fewer sources (B), less retrieved content (C), or a truncated response (D) — and each risks degrading quality. Chunking is the only option that cuts tokens by improving retrieval precision: smaller, semantically focused chunks mean the agent pulls in just the relevant content, so token usage drops while answer quality holds (or improves). That's exactly \"reduce token usage without degrading quality.\"","pick":"A"},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-03","up":5,"text":"✅ Correct Answer: C. Reconfigure the prompts to limit the amount of retrieved content from the knowledge sources\n\nThis reduces token usage by:\n- Restricting how much grounding data is pulled into the prompt\n- Summarizing or chunking retrieved content before passing it to the model\n- Using more selective retrieval instructions\n- Reducing unnecessary context while keeping quality intact\n\nThis is the standard optimization technique for Foundry and Azure OpenAI agents that hit token ceilings.\n\nIt improves latency and reduces cost without degrading answer quality.","pick":"C"},{"user":"kevinirl","date":"2026-08-27","up":3,"text":"Reconfigure the prompts to limit the amount of retrieved content from the knowledge sources\n\nThis sounds plausible but is not the best answer.\n\nLimiting retrieved content through prompt instructions can reduce tokens, but it may exclude important context needed for accurate answers. The question specifically asks for a solution that reduces token usage without degrading quality.\n\nMicrosoft's guidance emphasizes solving this at the retrieval/indexing layer through chunking and retrieval optimisation rather than arbitrarily restricting context after retrieval.","pick":"A"},{"user":"timothy123","date":"2026-08-25","up":3,"text":"C. Reconfigure the prompts to limit the amount of retrieved content from the knowledge sources.\nReduces Input Size: Limiting retrieved content directly decreases the number of tokens sent to the model per request.\nImproves Speed: Smaller prompts process faster, which fixes the slow response times.\nPreserves Quality: It filters out unnecessary background data while keeping the most relevant facts for accurate answers.\n\nChunking documents helps with indexing, but does not actively constrain runtime token limits like prompt reconfiguration.","pick":"C"},{"user":"Joselito79","date":"2026-09-19","up":2,"text":"✅ Correct answer: C. Reconfigure the prompts to limit the amount of retrieved content from the knowledge sources.\n\nWhy C?\n\nThe telemetry shows the agent is frequently hitting the token usage limit.\nThe agent uses multiple knowledge sources, so excessive retrieved content is likely consuming tokens.\nAdjusting the prompts to limit the amount of retrieved content reduces token consumption while preserving the most relevant information and therefore response quality.","pick":"C"},{"user":"Ninashnash","date":"2026-08-06","up":2,"text":"When documents are chunked during indexing, the retrieval system can return only the small, relevant portions of documents instead of large sections or entire documents. This means:\nFewer input tokens are sent to the model.\nRetrieval remains highly relevant.\nResponse quality is maintained (and often improved because the model receives less irrelevant context).\nThis is a standard Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) optimization.\n\nAll other options impact the quality of responses.","pick":"A"}]},{"n":101,"id":994163,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>A company has Microsoft Power Platform development, staging, and production environments. Each environment has its own Microsoft Dataverse tables and Azure AI Search index.</p><p>You are designing an application lifecycle management (AIM) process to deploy a Microsoft Copilot Studio agent between the environments.</p><p>The company has a Copilot Studio agent named Agent1 in development. Agent1 uses the following grounding data sources:</p><ul><li>A Dataverse table named CustomerOrders</li><li>An Azure AI Search index named customer-knowledge</li></ul><p>You need to deploy Agent1 to production. The solution must ensure that the agent uses the production grounding data sources, minimizes downtime, and handles credentials and endpoints securely.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you include in the deployment package solution, and what should you reconfigure after the deployment?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image57.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image58.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":3,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/20bf7c468f5314878e090c0cf7e07a4e994163/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-04","up":9,"text":"1. Agent1 and references to the data sources\nYou do not include actual data sources (Dataverse tables or Azure AI Search indexes) in the solution package.\nEach environment already has its own:\n- Dataverse table: CustomerOrders\n- Azure AI Search index: customer-knowledge\nInstead, you include:\n- Agent1\n- References to the data sources (not the data sources themselves)\n\n2. The Dataverse and Azure AI Search connections\nConnections contain:\n- Environment‑specific endpoints\n- Environment‑specific credentials\n- Environment‑specific indexes/tables\nTherefore, after deployment you must reconfigure:\n- Dataverse connection → point to production CustomerOrders\n- Azure AI Search connection → point to production customer‑knowledge index","top":true},{"user":"Ninashnash","date":"2026-08-06","up":1,"text":"Agent 1 and references to data sources: In Dev environment you configure Agent1 and (connection) references to the data sources\nThe Dataverse and Azure AI Connections: In Prod env, you need to configure \"connections\" to both data sources"}]},{"n":102,"id":994164,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>A company has a Microsoft Copilot Studio agent that uses generative AI to assist Microsoft Dynamics 365 Customer Service representatives.</p><p>The agent currently exhibits a low resolution rate and a high escalation rate.</p><p>You need to identify the issue.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you use?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"the Agent dashboard of Dynamics 365 Customer Service historical analytics"},{"k":"B","html":"the Insights tab from the Search &amp; intelligence settings of the Microsoft 365 admin center"},{"k":"C","html":"the Copilot hub in the Power Platform admin center"},{"k":"D","html":"the Analytics tab in Copilot Studio"}],"answer":"D","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"D","p":100,"n":5}],"page":3,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/fc45926b59c1bc2f226c18a3af462d55994164/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-04","up":5,"text":"✅ Correct Answer: D. the Analytics tab in Copilot Studio\n\nThe Analytics tab in Copilot Studio provides:\n- Resolution rate\n- Escalation rate\n- Abandoned sessions\n- Unanswered questions\n- Topic performance\n- Generated answer quality\n- Grounding effectiveness\n- Session outcomes\nThis is exactly where you identify why the agent is failing to resolve cases and escalating too often.","pick":"D"},{"user":"deca0d4","date":"2026-05-01","up":2,"text":"The Analytics tab is used to monitor, evaluate, and improve agent performance by providing insights into conversation outcomes, topic effectiveness, user engagement, and response quality.","pick":"D"}]},{"n":103,"id":994165,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>A company has a Microsoft Foundry generative AI model.</p><p>You need to evaluate the model's output to measure the overall quality and coherence of generated responses. The evaluation must use GPT-4o as a judge and return a numeric score for each output.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which type of metric should you use?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"AI quality (NLP)"},{"k":"B","html":"risk and safety"},{"k":"C","html":"Groundedness"},{"k":"D","html":"AI quality (AI assisted)"}],"answer":"D","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"D","p":100,"n":7}],"page":3,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/e46542b1ff31efccf5013fcc8f60b8c0994165/","comments":[{"user":"24b8eec","date":"2026-06-17","up":3,"text":"The decisive clue is \"GPT-4o as a judge.\" AI-assisted quality metrics are exactly the ones that use an LLM to score generation quality (coherence, fluency, relevance) and return a numeric score. The distractors each break one requirement: NLP metrics (BLEU/ROUGE) are math-based with no judge, risk and safety measures harm not quality, and Groundedness is a single metric rather than the metric type covering overall quality/coherence.\n\nMemory hook now in your notes:\n\nLLM-as-judge + quality/coherence + score → AI quality (AI assisted)\nBLEU/ROUGE/F1 → AI quality (NLP)\nHarm detection → risk and safety","pick":"D"},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-04","up":3,"text":"✅ Correct Answer: D. AI quality (AI assisted)\n\nAI quality (AI assisted)\nThis metric:\n- Uses an LLM (like GPT‑4o) as an evaluator\n- Scores each output numerically\n- Measures coherence, clarity, helpfulness, and correctness\n- Provides consistent, automated evaluation\n- Is the recommended approach for Foundry model quality assessment\nThis is exactly what the question describes.","pick":"D"},{"user":"deca0d4","date":"2026-05-01","up":2,"text":"AI quality – AI-assisted\nThis measures:\nHow good the response is (after the agent understands the question)\n\nWhat it looks at:\nRelevance\nAccuracy\nHelpfulness\nCompleteness","pick":"D"}]},{"n":104,"id":994166,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>You use Microsoft Copilot Studio analytics to analyze the performance of a deployed Copilot Studio agent.</p><p>You need to identify which performance metrics to use to measure the following:</p><ul><li>The percentage of engaged sessions that are escalated to a live customer service representative</li><li>The number of agent queries that cause a knowledge source error</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you identify for each requirement?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image59.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image60.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":3,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/25691e291a5430e837bfb982db8b3316994166/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-04","up":6,"text":"1. Escalation rate → % of engaged sessions escalated\nEscalation rate measures:\n- How many engaged sessions required a human handoff\n- The percentage of conversations that the agent could not resolve\n- A key indicator of agent effectiveness\nThis directly matches the first requirement.\n\n2. Answer quality → Knowledge source errors\nThe Answer quality insight includes:\n- Knowledge source errors\n- Retrieval failures\n- Hallucinations\n- Poor grounding\n- Low‑quality or incomplete answers\nIt is the only metric that reports knowledge source errors."}]},{"n":105,"id":994167,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>A company plans to deploy a Microsoft Foundry agent.</p><p>You need to recommend an application lifecycle management (ALM) process to ensure that the agent evaluates against baseline accuracy metrics before being deployed.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you recommend?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Configure GitHub Actions for new agent versions."},{"k":"B","html":"Deploy each new agent version directly to production."},{"k":"C","html":"Use Observability in Foundry Control Plane with evaluation and drift monitoring."},{"k":"D","html":"Enable Application Insights and use Azure Monitor."}],"answer":"C","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"A","p":27,"n":3},{"a":"C","p":73,"n":8}],"page":3,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/ce520a2179185bedb9f255c676e1418e994167/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-04","up":9,"text":"✅ Correct Answer: C. Use Observability in Foundry Control Plane with evaluation and drift monitoring\n\nObservability in Foundry Control Plane gives you:\n- Automated evaluation pipelines\n- Baseline accuracy scoring\n- LLM‑as‑a‑judge evaluations\n- Drift detection (data drift, behavior drift, quality drift)\n- Quality gates before deployment\n- Continuous monitoring after deployment\nThis is exactly what an ALM process requires for safe, high‑quality AI deployment.","pick":"C","top":true},{"user":"deca0d4","date":"2026-05-01","up":2,"text":"you can (and should) enforce this with GitHub Actions for every new agent version.\n\n✅ Use a CI/CD workflow with an automated evaluation step + a quality gate that blocks deployment if the baseline isn’t met.","pick":"A"},{"user":"inboxofdt","date":"2026-08-28","up":1,"text":"Requirement Alignment: The scenario specifically asks for an application lifecycle management (ALM) process that enforces a quality check before the agent is deployed. GitHub Actions is a native CI/CD orchestration tool used for ALM.","pick":"A"}]},{"n":106,"id":994168,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>You need to recommend a security solution for agents in a Microsoft Power Platform environment.</p><p>The agents must use only approved connectors and services. The solution must prevent the agents from accessing sensitive data.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you recommend?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Configure Azure Monitor to capture connector activity logs."},{"k":"B","html":"Enable a Microsoft Dataverse audit."},{"k":"C","html":"Deploy data loss prevention (DLP) policies in Power Platform."},{"k":"D","html":"Enable customer-managed keys in Microsoft Dataverse."}],"answer":"C","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"C","p":100,"n":3}],"page":3,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/cc9f58f6fb9355a30c74d3b64f9eed37994168/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-04","up":4,"text":"✅ Correct Answer: C. Deploy data loss prevention (DLP) policies in Power Platform\n\nPower Platform DLP policies allow you to:\n- Control which connectors agents are allowed to use\n- Block or restrict unapproved or risky connectors\n- Separate connectors into Business, Non‑Business, and Blocked categories\n- Prevent agents from accessing sensitive data sources\n- Apply policies at the environment, tenant, or solution level\n\nThis is the official and recommended way to enforce connector governance for Copilot Studio agents, Power Automate flows, and Power Apps.","pick":"C"}]},{"n":107,"id":994169,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>A company has an AI business solution that uses Microsoft Copilot Studio agents.</p><p>You need to recommend prompt best practices to improve the effectiveness of agent interactions.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which two actions should you include in the recommendation?</strong> Each correct answer presents part of the solution.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Track the duration of the average user session."},{"k":"B","html":"Analyze the prompt length distribution."},{"k":"C","html":"Regularly test and refine the prompts based on user input."},{"k":"D","html":"Use clear and specific instructions in the prompts."},{"k":"E","html":"Measure system resource usage during prompt processing."}],"answer":"CD","type":"multi","votes":[{"a":"CD","p":100,"n":3}],"page":3,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/d2e3b9ce234b73cbd0a6b5b5eda2db8b994169/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-04","up":5,"text":"C. Regularly test and refine the prompts based on user input\nClear prompts reduce ambiguity and help the agent:\n- Stay on topic\n- Produce more accurate responses\n- Follow business rules consistently\nThis is one of the core principles of effective prompt engineering.\n\nD. Use clear and specific instructions in the prompts\nPrompts must evolve based on:\n- Real user interactions\n- Failure cases\n- Escalations\n- Low‑quality answers\nIterative refinement is essential for improving agent performance over time.","pick":"CD"}]},{"n":108,"id":994170,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>A company has a cloud-based AI solution that uses Azure OpenAI models.</p><p>You need to design a monitoring solution that meets the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Monitors performance metrics and operational health for the models</li><li>Monitors AI apps and agents for compliance</li><li>Uses Azure-native capabilities</li><li>Minimizes development effort</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you use for each requirement?</strong> To answer, drag the appropriate options to the correct requirements. Each option may be used once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to drag the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image61.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image62.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":3,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/b83d9b71eb07d691eaacda73eef4c191994170/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-04","up":6,"text":"1. Microsoft Purview → Compliance monitoring\nPurview provides:\n- Data access governance\n- Sensitive data classification\n- Lineage tracking\n- Policy enforcement\n- Compliance insights for AI apps and agents\nIt is the only Azure‑native service designed specifically for compliance monitoring.\n\n2. Azure Monitor → Performance & operational health\nAzure Monitor provides:\n- Latency metrics\n- Throughput\n- Token usage\n- Errors and exceptions\n- Dependency performance\n- Health dashboards\nIt is the standard Azure‑native solution for operational monitoring of Azure OpenAI and AI applications."}]},{"n":109,"id":994171,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>A company has Microsoft Copilot Studio agents.</p><p>The company plans to deploy custom connectors across development, test and production environments.</p><p>You need to design an application lifecycle management (ALM) process to ensure consistency and prevent direct editing in production.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which two actions should you include in the design?</strong> Each correct answer presents part of the solution.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Deploy managed solutions to production."},{"k":"B","html":"Deploy unmanaged solutions to production."},{"k":"C","html":"Manually rebuild the agents in each environment."},{"k":"D","html":"Move the agents between the environments by using data export and import."},{"k":"E","html":"Include agents and connectors in a solution."}],"answer":"AE","type":"multi","votes":[{"a":"AE","p":100,"n":7}],"page":3,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/5ac3878c8c9ff2487618d989ec42eae0994171/","comments":[{"user":"deca0d4","date":"2026-05-01","up":6,"text":"A: In the Power Platform (including Copilot Studio), custom connectors must be included in solutions to support proper ALM.\n\nBuild and edit in Dev (unmanaged solution)\nExport and deploy as a managed solution to Test and Production\nManaged solutions are read-only in production, preventing direct edits\nE: In the Power Platform (including Copilot Studio), custom connectors must be included in solutions to support proper ALM.","pick":"AE"},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-04","up":3,"text":"A. Deploy managed solutions to production\nManaged solutions:\n- Prevent editing in production (a key requirement)\n- Lock down components so only dev/test can modify them\n- Ensure controlled, versioned deployments\n- Are the Microsoft‑recommended practice for production environments\n\nE. Include agents and connectors in a solution\nThis is essential because:\n- Solutions are the ALM unit in Power Platform\n- Custom connectors must be packaged inside solutions for proper versioning\n- Copilot Studio agents are solution components and must be moved this way\n- Ensures consistent deployment across environments","pick":"AE"}]},{"n":110,"id":994172,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>A company uses multiple Microsoft Copilot Studio agents across different channels.</p><p>You need to recommend a monitoring solution that provides comprehensive telemetry data and performance insights for the agents.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you include in the recommendation?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Application Insights"},{"k":"B","html":"Microsoft Dynamics 365 Customer Voice"},{"k":"C","html":"Log Analytics"},{"k":"D","html":"Microsoft Purview"}],"answer":"A","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"A","p":100,"n":5}],"page":3,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/1a2e5eb0a55c1e2358ac6ea7435371fe994172/","comments":[{"user":"deca0d4","date":"2026-05-01","up":3,"text":"Application Insights offers a unified view of agent performance, usage, and diagnostics across multiple sources","pick":"A"},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-04","up":2,"text":"✅ Correct Answer: A. Application Insights\n\n🧠 Why Application Insights is the right choice\nApplication Insights gives you:\n- End‑to‑end telemetry\n- Latency, token usage, failures, exceptions\n- Dependency tracking (Dataverse, connectors, APIs)\n- Custom events for agent interactions\n- Dashboards and alerts\n- Works across all channels (web, Dynamics, custom apps)\nThis is the recommended monitoring solution for Copilot Studio agents at scale.","pick":"A"}],"variants":[40,41,42,43,98,120]},{"n":111,"id":994173,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>A company has an AI solution named Solution1 that is deployed to the production environment. Solution1 uses an Azure OpenAI model to generate marketing emails for existing customers.</p><p>During an internal review, you identify that Solution1 creates different emails depending on the customers’ traits.</p><p>You need to recommend a strategy to mitigate the bias. The strategy must adhere to Microsoft responsible AI principles.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you recommend?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Modify Solution1 to randomly generate emails for different traits."},{"k":"B","html":"Modify the system instructions of Solution1."},{"k":"C","html":"Retrain the model by using a larger dataset."},{"k":"D","html":"Modify the contents of the training dataset."}],"answer":"B","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"A","p":33,"n":6},{"a":"B","p":44,"n":8},{"a":"D","p":22,"n":4}],"page":3,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/bb40fc836edb0638ef29769b7908cd6b994173/","comments":[{"user":"timothy123","date":"2026-08-26","up":5,"text":"Right answer is B: Modify the system instructions.\nBy adding strict guidelines to the system prompt (e.g., \"Ensure all marketing offers maintain equal value and tone across all demographic traits\"), you directly enforce the Microsoft principle of Fairness, ensuring the AI treats all demographic groups equitably without rewriting the underlying model architecture.\nAzure OpenAI relies on large, pre-trained foundation models (like GPT-4). You cannot easily rewrite their core training data. System instructions (system prompts) are the primary tool for a developer to guide model behavior in real time.\nAnswer A is definitely wrong. Introducing randomness does not remove bias; it only makes the bias unpredictable.","pick":"B"},{"user":"24b8eec","date":"2026-06-17","up":4,"text":"Answer: B. Modify the system instructions of Solution1\nThe issue is output bias — the deployed model generates different emails based on customer traits (age, gender, location, etc.), which violates fairness principles. The fastest, most targeted responsible-AI mitigation for a deployed production solution is to modify the system prompt/instructions to explicitly instruct the model to generate consistent, trait-neutral marketing emails regardless of who the customer is. This is a direct, immediate fix that doesn't require retraining or data changes.","pick":"A"},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-04","up":4,"text":"✅ Correct Answer: D. Modify the contents of the training dataset\n\n🧠 Why this is the correct choice\n\nBias in model outputs typically originates from:\n- Biased or unbalanced training data\n- Over‑representation of certain traits\n- Patterns in the dataset that the model learns and amplifies\n\nResponsible AI guidance from Microsoft emphasizes:\n- Reviewing and correcting training data\n- Removing or balancing sensitive attributes\n- Ensuring datasets do not encode harmful or discriminatory patterns\n\nThis is the most direct and effective way to mitigate bias.","pick":"D"},{"user":"Aarch","date":"2026-08-10","up":3,"text":"System instructions guide the model's behavior.\nYou can add instructions that require fair and consistent treatment of customers and prevent the use of protected or sensitive traits when generating content.\nThis aligns with Microsoft's Responsible AI principle of Fairness.","pick":"B"},{"user":"ziggy1117","date":"2026-07-02","up":2,"text":"Should be the system instructions.\n\nIf D, that means doing a fine-tuned model. That doesn't make sense if the requirement is just to send out emails","pick":"A"},{"user":"AMDf","date":"2026-09-20","up":1,"text":"Right answer is B: Modify the system instructions.","pick":"B"},{"user":"zamper","date":"2026-08-19","up":1,"text":"A. Randomly generate emails based on traits is clearly inappropriate. Randomness doesn't establish fairness and could create inconsistent or discriminatory outcomes.\n\nMicrosoft's Responsible AI principle of fairness requires AI systems to treat people fairly and avoid systematically different outcomes for similarly situated groups. When bias originates from patterns learned from training data, a fundamental mitigation technique is to examine and correct the dataset—for example, addressing underrepresentation, imbalance, biased examples, or inappropriate correlations between customer traits and outputs.","pick":"D"}]},{"n":112,"id":994174,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>A company has a canvas app named App1 in a Microsoft Power Platform environment named Env1.</p><p>Env1 uses a customer-managed key for data encryption. App1 connects to multiple data sources to retrieve and update customer and order information.</p><p>You need to recommend a solution to add Microsoft Copilot components to App1. The solution must NOT modify the current security or encryption configurations of Env1.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you include in the recommendation?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Modify the data sources of App1 to make them compatible with Copilot."},{"k":"B","html":"Duplicate App1 and republish the app in Env1."},{"k":"C","html":"Enable Copilot features for Env1."},{"k":"D","html":"Move App1 to a new environment that uses Microsoft-managed keys."}],"answer":"D","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"C","p":20,"n":3},{"a":"D","p":80,"n":12}],"page":3,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/3cfb27cb5052852dea8e8df647d17aad994174/","comments":[{"user":"24b8eec","date":"2026-06-17","up":7,"text":"Answer: D. This is a documented platform constraint. Microsoft Copilot components do not work in environments that use a customer-managed key (CMK) — this is stated explicitly in Power Apps documentation (\"Copilot doesn't work in environments that use a customer-managed key or Customer Lockbox\"). Since the requirement says the solution must NOT modify the current security/encryption configuration of Env1, you cannot simply enable Copilot in Env1. The only path forward is to move App1 to a new environment that uses Microsoft-managed keys, where Copilot components are supported.","pick":"D","top":true},{"user":"Alicia_lili","date":"2026-05-04","up":3,"text":"D. Move App1 to a new environment that uses Microsoft-managed keys.","pick":"D"},{"user":"Aronmb23","date":"2026-08-29","up":2,"text":"Copilot components in canvas apps rely on the Copilot generative AI features being enabled at the environment level. Since App1 already connects successfully to its data sources, and Env1's customer-managed key already governs encryption for whatever data the environment stores, turning on Copilot at the environment level doesn't touch the CMK configuration or the app's existing connections — it just makes the Copilot capability available for App1 to consume.\n\nThe other options don't fit: A modifies data sources unnecessarily (Copilot doesn't require source-level compatibility changes); B duplicating the app does nothing to enable Copilot; D moving to a Microsoft-managed-key environment directly violates the \"must not modify encryption configuration\" constraint.","pick":"C"},{"user":"Ninashnash","date":"2026-08-07","up":2,"text":"D. Move App1 to a new environment that uses Microsoft-managed keys.\n\nWhy: This confirms it directly — Copilot doesn't work in environments that use a customer-managed key or Customer Lockbox. Since Env1 uses customer-managed keys, Copilot components simply cannot function there, full stop — no configuration change on Env1 will make it work. The only way to give App1 Copilot capabilities while satisfying \"must NOT modify the current security or encryption configurations of Env1\" is to move App1 out to a different environment that uses Microsoft-managed keys, leaving Env1 (and its CMK config) completely untouched.","pick":"D"},{"user":"CyrilleC","date":"2026-07-31","up":2,"text":"his is a documented platform constraint. Microsoft Copilot components do not work in environments that use a customer-managed key (CMK)\n\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-platform/release-plan/2025wave1/microsoft-copilot-studio/use-customer-managed-encryption-keys-protect-data\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-apps/maker/canvas-apps/add-ai-copilot","pick":"D"},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-04","up":2,"text":"✅ Correct Answer: C. Enable Copilot features for Env1\n\n🧠 Why this is correct\n\nCopilot features in Power Apps (Copilot control, Copilot answers, Copilot suggestions) are environment‑level capabilities.\n\nEnabling them:\n- Does NOT modify encryption settings (CMK remains untouched)\n- Does NOT require moving the app\n- Does NOT require changing data sources\n- Allows Copilot components to be added directly to App1\n\nMicrosoft explicitly supports Copilot features in environments using customer‑managed keys.","pick":"C"}]},{"n":113,"id":994175,"topic":3,"stem":"<p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which two components for the custom AI agent should you include in the application lifecycle management (AIM) process?</strong> Each correct answer presents part of the solution.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"an Azure package"},{"k":"B","html":"a ZIP package"},{"k":"C","html":"a Microsoft Power Platform solution"},{"k":"D","html":"a Cloud Scale Unit (CSU) package"},{"k":"E","html":"an X++model"}],"answer":"CE","type":"multi","votes":[{"a":"BC","p":13,"n":1},{"a":"CD","p":13,"n":1},{"a":"CE","p":75,"n":6}],"page":3,"case":"8b997de433","thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/0cf1e127f553c7220be3f93e9882a6e9994175/","comments":[{"user":"24b8eec","date":"2026-06-17","up":5,"text":"Why not the others\nA. Azure package — a generic Azure deployment artifact; not the packaging mechanism for either a Copilot Studio agent or D365 F&O business logic.\nB. ZIP package — Power Platform solutions export as .zip files, but the component in the ALM process is the solution (C), not the raw ZIP. ZIP is the transport format, not the ALM component.\nD. Cloud Scale Unit (CSU) package — used specifically for Dynamics 365 Commerce headless commerce (store components, CDX, etc.). Contoso's agent is in SCM, not Commerce.","pick":"CE"},{"user":"Ninashnash","date":"2026-08-07","up":2,"text":"C. Microsoft Power Platform solution — The agent is built in Copilot Studio, part of the Power Platform. Power Platform solutions are the standard ALM packaging unit for Copilot Studio agents, enabling versioning and promotion across environments.\nE. an X++ model — The agent must use D365 SCM business logic stored outside the app. Custom business logic for D365 Finance & Operations apps is packaged as X++ models, the standard ALM unit deployed via LCS/Azure DevOps.","pick":"CE"},{"user":"Aarch","date":"2026-08-10","up":1,"text":"A CSU package is a deployable package used to install or update Commerce/retail extensions and customizations in the Cloud Scale Unit environment.","pick":"CD"},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-04","up":1,"text":"✅ B. a ZIP package\nThis is required because Copilot Studio exports agents as ZIP files when:\n- Moving between tenants\n- Backing up agents\n- Importing into another environment\n- Packaging custom connectors (OpenAPI definitions are also ZIP‑based)\n\n✅ C. Microsoft Power Platform solution\nThis is mandatory for ALM of Copilot Studio agents.\nCopilot Studio agents are packaged and moved between environments only through Power Platform solutions.\nSolutions provide:\n- Versioning\n- Dependency tracking\n- Managed/unmanaged deployment\n- Environment promotion (Dev → Test → Prod)","pick":"BC","replies":[{"user":"Ninashnash","date":"2026-08-07","up":2,"text":"B (A ZIP package) is not correct : While solution files or custom connectors are exported as .zip archive files during transit, the underlying operational ALM component used for environment management is the Power Platform solution itself. E should be selected not C"}]}]},{"n":114,"id":994176,"topic":3,"stem":"<p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which tools should you recommend to assist the CISO and the CIO with their specific responsibilities?</strong> To answer, drag the appropriate tools to the correct executives. Each tool may be used once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to drag the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image63.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image64.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":3,"case":"8b997de433","thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/99c6d59fbae36064ff1bab8b7daf731e994176/","comments":[{"user":"24b8eec","date":"2026-06-17","up":8,"text":"CISO → Azure Resource Graph Explorer. The CISO's responsibility is to \"discover and inventory AI resources for auditing.\" Azure Resource Graph Explorer is exactly the tool for this — it queries and inventories Azure resources at scale across subscriptions, letting the CISO discover all AI resources (Azure OpenAI, Foundry projects, etc.) across Contoso's multiple Azure subscriptions for compliance auditing.\n\nCIO → Microsoft Purview. The CIO's responsibility is to \"ensure that appropriate security labels are assigned to the data used by the AI agents.\" Microsoft Purview is the data-governance platform that manages sensitivity labels and data classification — the CIO uses it to apply and verify security labels on the data the agents consume.","top":true},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-04","up":3,"text":"1. CISO → Microsoft Purview\nThe CISO must:\n- Discover and inventory AI resources for auditing\n- Identify how much sensitive data was accessed\n- See who accessed sensitive data\n- Perform monthly compliance and security audits\nThese responsibilities align exactly with Microsoft Purview.\n\n2. CIO → Copilot Studio\nThe CIO must:\n- Ensure appropriate security labels are assigned to the data used by AI agents\nSecurity labels for AI agents are configured within Copilot Studio, where the CIO can:\n- Assign data classifications\n- Configure data access policies\n- Manage connectors and data sources\n- Apply environment-level governance\nCopilot Studio is the correct tool for managing data labeling and governance for AI agents."},{"user":"Ninashnash","date":"2026-08-07","up":1,"text":"CISO → Azure Resource Graph Explorer\nWhy:\nCISO Requirement: Discover and inventory AI resources for auditing.\nSolution: Azure Resource Graph Explorer is designed to query and inventory Azure resources across multiple subscriptions, which fits:\n-multiple Azure subscriptions\n-discover AI resources\n-auditing and inventory"}],"variants":[116]},{"n":115,"id":994177,"topic":3,"stem":"<p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you recommend to assist the CEO with their specific responsibilities?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"the Microsoft Service Trust Portal"},{"k":"B","html":"Microsoft Foundry Tools"},{"k":"C","html":"Microsoft Purview"},{"k":"D","html":"the Responsible AI dashboard"},{"k":"E","html":"Compliance Center"}],"answer":"D","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"D","p":100,"n":5}],"page":3,"case":"8b997de433","thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/19e17de2558b8ca9c9b50e1ffd64b7c0994177/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-04","up":6,"text":"👉 D. the Responsible AI dashboard\n\nThe Responsible AI dashboard is the only option that provides:\n- Model fairness analysis\n- Error and bias detection\n- Explainability and interpretability reports\n- Safety and reliability evaluations\n- Compliance‑aligned assessments\n- A unified view of responsible AI metrics across agents and models\nThis aligns perfectly with the CEO’s responsibilities.","pick":"D"}]},{"n":116,"id":994178,"topic":3,"stem":"<p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which Copilot Studio analytics metrics should you recommend to assist the executives with their specific responsibilities?</strong> To answer, drag the appropriate metrics to the correct executives. Each metric may be used once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to drag the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image65.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ab-100/image66.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":3,"case":"8b997de433","thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/58a35aa96c8348dd6a5bc0abf5c8b68a994178/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-04","up":8,"text":"1. CFO → Use\nThe CFO wants to analyze:\n- How many interactions are abandoned vs. resolved\n- Whether Copilot Studio credits are being used efficiently\n- Actual usage vs. estimated ROI\nThese insights come from the Use metric, which includes:\n- Session counts\n- Abandonment rate\n- Resolution rate\n- Daily/weekly/monthly usage trends\nThis directly reflects credit consumption efficiency.\n\n2. CTO → Satisfaction\nThe CTO wants to:\n- Track user feedback on the quality of AI agent responses\n- Trigger reengineering discussions when feedback is consistently poor\nThis is exactly what the Satisfaction metric measures:\n- User thumbs‑up / thumbs‑down\n- Feedback comments\n- Quality perception trends\nThis is the only metric tied to response quality.","top":true},{"user":"deca0d4","date":"2026-05-17","up":3,"text":"CFO concerns about credit usage: Use\nSessions\nConversations\nMessage volume\nActivity/consumption\n\nThat directly relates to:\nCredit consumption\nResource usage\nAgent utilization\n\nConcern about poor feedback on AI responses: Satisfaction\n“Satisfaction” measures:\n\nUser ratings\nFeedback\nPositive/negative response sentiment\nThat directly maps to:\nPoor agent responses\nUser dissatisfaction\nQuality perception"},{"user":"ziggy1117","date":"2026-07-02","up":1,"text":"Effectiveness -> Conversation outcomes\nThe CFO wants to identify how many interactions with the AI agents are abandoned on a given day as compared to resolved conversations. Too many abandoned sessions might indicate that Copilot Studio credits are being used inefficiently by end users.\n\nYou can get Abandoned sessions there."}],"variants":[114]},{"n":117,"id":999654,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>A company has a team that analyzes its customers by using a manual process.</p><p>You are designing an AI-based agent to automate and improve the process.</p><p>You need to recommend on which platform to build the agent. The solution must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Use generative AI to answer common questions.</li><li>Provide analytics to review AI performance.</li><li>Identify customer demographics.</li><li>Minimize custom development.</li></ul><div class=\"solution\"><span>Proposed solution</span>You recommend GitHub Copilot.</div><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Does this meet the goal?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Yes"},{"k":"B","html":"No"}],"answer":"B","type":"yesno","votes":[{"a":"B","p":100,"n":2}],"page":3,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/914b7c5407f3f995ceca73e952d088b4999654/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-04","up":3,"text":"Correct answer: B. No\n\nWhy?\nGitHub Copilot is a developer productivity tool. It helps write code, generate functions, and accelerate software development. It does not meet the requirements of this scenario.\n\n✔ Requirements vs. GitHub Copilot\n\nUse generative AI to answer common questions\n❌ GitHub Copilot does not build conversational agents or customer‑facing AI.\n\nProvide analytics to review AI performance\n❌ GitHub Copilot has no analytics for agent interactions, usage, or performance.\n\nIdentify customer demographics\n❌ GitHub Copilot cannot analyze customer data or build business workflows.\n\nMinimize custom development\n❌ GitHub Copilot requires more custom development, not less.","pick":"B"}],"series":true},{"n":118,"id":999655,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>A company has a team that analyzes its customers by using a manual process.</p><p>You are designing an AI-based agent to automate and improve the process.</p><p>You need to recommend on which platform to build the agent. The solution must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Use generative AI to answer common questions.</li><li>Provide analytics to review AI performance.</li><li>Identify customer demographics.</li><li>Minimize custom development.</li></ul><div class=\"solution\"><span>Proposed solution</span>You recommend Microsoft Security Copilot.</div><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Does this meet the goal?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Yes"},{"k":"B","html":"No"}],"answer":"B","type":"yesno","votes":[{"a":"B","p":100,"n":2}],"page":3,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/26a1352888f1588186b098910896e5af999655/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-04","up":2,"text":"Correct answer: B. No\n\nMicrosoft Security Copilot is designed for cybersecurity operations, not for building customer‑analysis agents or business-facing AI workflows.\n\nUse generative AI to answer common questions\n❌ Security Copilot answers security-related questions (incidents, threats, alerts).\nIt is not a platform for customer-facing Q&A or business process automation.\n\nProvide analytics to review AI performance\n❌ It provides security investigation analytics, not agent performance analytics.\n\nIdentify customer demographics\n❌ Security Copilot cannot analyze customer data or demographics.\n\nMinimize custom development\n❌ It is not a low-code/no-code agent-building platform.","pick":"B"}],"series":true},{"n":119,"id":999656,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>A company has a team that analyzes its customers by using a manual process.</p><p>You are designing an AI-based agent to automate and improve the process.</p><p>You need to recommend on which platform to build the agent. The solution must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Use generative AI to answer common questions.</li><li>Provide analytics to review AI performance.</li><li>Identify customer demographics.</li><li>Minimize custom development.</li></ul><div class=\"solution\"><span>Proposed solution</span>You recommend Microsoft Copilot Studio.</div><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Does this meet the goal?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Yes"},{"k":"B","html":"No"}],"answer":"A","type":"yesno","votes":[{"a":"A","p":100,"n":3}],"page":3,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/b0e2ec44609da278cf729c7ea9811b4f999656/","comments":[{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-04","up":3,"text":"Answer: A. Yes\n\nRecommending Microsoft Copilot Studio does meet the goal.\n\nUse generative AI to answer common questions\n✔ Yes — Copilot Studio builds generative AI agents using GPT models, orchestration, and knowledge sources.\n\nProvide analytics to review AI performance\n✔ Yes — Copilot Studio includes built‑in analytics dashboards.\n\nIdentify customer demographics\n✔ Yes — Copilot Studio can connect. This allows the agent to retrieve and analyze customer demographic data with minimal custom code.\n\nMinimize custom development\n✔ Yes — Copilot Studio is a low‑code/no‑code platform designed for business AI agents.","pick":"A"}],"series":true},{"n":120,"id":999657,"topic":3,"stem":"<p>A company uses multiple Microsoft Copilot Studio agents across different channels.</p><p>You need to recommend a monitoring solution that provides comprehensive telemetry data and performance insights for the agents.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you include in the recommendation?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Microsoft Power BI"},{"k":"B","html":"the Analytics tab in Copilot Studio"},{"k":"C","html":"Log Analytics"},{"k":"D","html":"Azure Advisor"}],"answer":"C","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"C","p":100,"n":5}],"page":3,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/6ae10c7fed9b714499e2b2514fcbbdf8999657/","comments":[{"user":"93c84b0","date":"2026-05-21","up":4,"text":"C. Log Analytics\n\nBecause the key phrase is:\n\n“provides comprehensive telemetry data and performance insights”","pick":"C"},{"user":"omath","date":"2026-06-04","up":1,"text":"✅ Correct Answer: C. Log Analytics\n\n🎯 Why Log Analytics is the right choice\n\nLog Analytics is the Azure‑native service that:\n- Collects comprehensive telemetry from Copilot Studio agents\n- Stores Application Insights data for querying\n- Enables Kusto Query Language (KQL) analysis\n- Supports dashboards, alerts, and cross‑agent monitoring\n- Works across all channels (web, Dynamics, Teams, custom apps)\n\nIn Microsoft’s recommended architecture, Application Insights sends its telemetry to Log Analytics, and Log Analytics is the central monitoring layer for multi‑agent observability.\n\nSo when the question asks for the monitoring solution you should include, the correct answer is Log Analytics.","pick":"C"}],"variants":[40,41,42,43,98,110]}]},{"code":"AI-103","title":"Developing AI Apps and Agents on Azure","url":"https://www.examtopics.com/exams/microsoft/ai-103/view/","topics":[{"n":1,"name":"Topic 1"}],"cases":{"d421f5cb15":{"name":"Contoso, Ltd","html":"<h4>Overview</h4><h5>Company Information</h5><p>Contoso, Ltd is a multinational retail company that builds, deploys, and manages generative AI and agent-based solutions by using Microsoft Foundry.</p><h4>Existing Environment</h4><h5>Identity Environment</h5><p>Contoso uses Microsoft Entra ID for identity management, authentication, and authorization capabilities that enable agents to access organizational resources and services.</p><p>Contoso recently formed a new AI engineering team named Agent1Dev Team to optimize and maintain existing AI solutions.</p><p>The team collaborates with solution architects, DevOps engineers, and security engineers to design, implement. monitor, and secure AI applications.</p><p>Contoso also has a team named Agent1Test Team that is responsible for validating AI solutions before the solution deployments.</p><h5>Generative Environment</h5><p>Contoso has a Microsoft Foundry deployment that contains two projects named Project1 and Project2.</p><h5>Project1</h5><p>Project1 contains a customer support agent named Agent1 that assists customers with product inquiries and troubleshooting requests.</p><p>Agent1 has the following configurations:</p><ul><li>Agent1 uses a base model deployment.</li><li>A safety evaluation pipeline is NOT enabled.</li><li>Tool invocation approval workflows are NOT enabled.</li><li>Conversation memory constraints are NOT configured.</li></ul><p>Agent1 interacts with customers by using digital support channels and answers general questions about Contoso products.</p><p>Project1 is deployed to an Azure region located in the European Union (EU).</p><p>Agent1Dev Team will use Project1 to optimize and maintain Agent1.</p><h5>Project2</h5><p>Project2 contains a deployed video generation model. The marketing department at Contoso has access to Project2 and plans to use the model to develop a video creation solution.</p><p>Development of the solution is incomplete.</p><h5>Data Environment</h5><p>Contoso stores product-related information in Azure resources that support AI applications.</p><p>The Azure environment contains an Azure Blob Storage account named storage1 that stores product detail sheets for all the Contoso products.</p><p>The product sheets include specifications, feature descriptions, and product support information that Agent1 can use to answer customer questions. The product sheets are stored in the PDF format.</p><h4>Problem Statements</h4><p>Contoso identifies the following issues:</p><ul><li>Agent1 has only general knowledge of the Contoso products.</li><li>A recent chat interaction with Agent1 was analyzed for sentiment. The results of the analysis have NOT been processed yet.</li><li>Agent1 does NOT use the detailed product information in the product sheets stored in storage1 when responding to customer questions.</li><li>The finance department at Contoso reports that vendor invoices must be reviewed manually to ensure that the invoices match the terms defined in the vendor contracts. The invoices contain tables, logos, and varied layouts that make the documents difficult to process consistently.</li></ul><h4>Requirements</h4><h4>Planned Changes</h4><p>Contoso plans to implement the following changes:</p><ul><li>Implement a solution for Project1 that analyzes the vendor invoices by evaluating both the visual layout and the textual content of the invoices, so that the invoice details can be verified against the vendor contract terms.</li><li>Update the base model deployment used by Agent1 and standardize the model version to ensure continuity and consistent responses.</li><li>Enable Agent1 to retrieve and use the detailed product information from the product sheets stored in storage1.</li><li>Implement an indexing solution for the product sheets that Agent1 can use to answer customer questions.</li><li>Complete the development of the video creation solution.</li></ul><h4>Technical Requirements</h4><p>Contoso identifies the following technical requirements:</p><ul><li>The model deployment used by Agent1 must support scalable, high-throughput generative AI workloads and dynamically scale to handle variable customer support traffic, without requiring reserved throughput capacity.</li><li>The product sheets must be processed by using an indexing pipeline that enables semantic and vector search, so that Agent1 can retrieve the relevant product information.</li><li>Responses generated by using the product sheet information must be relevant, complete, and accurate.</li><li>Agent1 must be able to use the product sheets to answer natural language questions about product details.</li><li>The model version used by Agent1 must remain consistent to ensure stable responses.</li><li>The data processed by the model must remain within the EU.</li></ul><h5>Security and Compliance Requirements</h5><p>Contoso identifies the following security and compliance requirements:</p><ul><li>API keys must NOT be used to access Foundry-deployed models.</li><li>Access to the Azure resources must follow the principle of least privilege.</li><li>The developers at Contoso must authenticate to Microsoft Foundry resources by using Microsoft Entra authentication.</li><li>Access to Project1 must be assigned to the members of Agent1Dev Team by using a security group named SC_Agent1_Dev.</li><li>Access to Project1 must be assigned to the members of Agent1Test Team by using a security group named SC_Agent1_Test.</li><li>Agent1 must never reveal customer information, even if a document that contains customer data is added erroneously to the product sheet repository in storage1.</li><li>The product sheets might contain images that include embedded text. Agent1 must be protected from malicious instructions potentially hidden within the images.</li></ul><h4>Business Requirements</h4><p>Contoso identifies the following business requirements:</p><ul><li>Users that interact with Agent1 must have a personalized experience in future interactions, including the ability for Agent1 to retain conversation context and recall relevant information from previous interactions.</li><li>Agent1 must answer questions only about the products sold by Contoso.</li></ul>"}},"questions":[{"n":1,"id":1000629,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You need to configure the model deployment for Agent1 to meet the technical requirements.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you configure?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image1.png\" alt=\"image1\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image2.png\" alt=\"image2\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":1,"case":"d421f5cb15","thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/7e8dad2e5eb183c4175925b20bb2cebe1000629/","comments":[{"user":"profitchannel","date":"2026-06-12","up":10,"text":"\"the data prcessed by the model must remain in the EU\"\nthat is Standard for me:\nBy data residency requirement\nNo restrictions: Use Global Standard or Global Provisioned\nEU data zone: Use DataZone Standard or DataZone Provisioned in an EU region\nUS data zone: Use DataZone Standard or DataZone Provisioned in a US region\nSingle region only: Use Standard or Regional Provisioned","top":true},{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-09","up":3,"text":"The requirement asks for scalable, high-throughput, dynamically scaling capacity WITHOUT reserved throughput. That points to a pay-as-you-go consumption deployment rather than Provisioned (PTU). The highlighted 'Standard' is defensible, but 'Global Standard' is the offering Microsoft positions for the highest, most elastic throughput.\n\nDeployment type: Global Standard\nVersion upgrade policy: Opt out of automatic model version upgrades"},{"user":"robert_ico","date":"2026-08-14","up":1,"text":"I would go with B) Global Standard (clues: scalable, high-throughput; Standard: specific Azure Region, capaicity associated to that region; Global Provisioned: reserves provisioned capacity) and B) Opt out... why? the model version used by Agent1 MUST remain CONSISTENT to ensure STABLE responses (so no automatic upgrades required)"},{"user":"batmanx","date":"2026-07-19","up":1,"text":"Standard\nDeployment type Standard\nVersion update policy Opt out of automatic model version upgrades"}]},{"n":2,"id":1000630,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You need to configure Agent1 to meet the security and compliance requirements.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you use?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"self-harm content filtering"},{"k":"B","html":"prompt shields"},{"k":"C","html":"Personally identifiable information (PII) Detection"},{"k":"D","html":"violence content filtering"}],"answer":"B","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"B","p":54,"n":15},{"a":"BC","p":4,"n":1},{"a":"C","p":43,"n":12}],"page":1,"case":"d421f5cb15","thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/808a2bddb42d0873a172a321c9c909aa1000630/","comments":[{"user":"seesee1","date":"2026-08-04","up":4,"text":"The requirement in question is: \"The product sheets might contain images that include embedded text. Agent1 must be protected from malicious instructions potentially hidden within the images.\"\n\nThis describes an indirect prompt injection attack - malicious instructions embedded in content (in this case, text hidden inside images) that could hijack the agent's behavior when it processes that document. Microsoft Foundry's Prompt Shields (part of Azure AI Content Safety) is purpose-built to detect and block both direct and indirect prompt injection attempts, including those embedded in documents/images ingested by an agent, before they reach the model.","pick":"B"},{"user":"CharlieMike","date":"2026-07-04","up":4,"text":"I think it is C due to the security/compliance requirement","pick":"C","replies":[{"user":"profitchannel","date":"2026-06-12","up":2,"text":"customer information ist not nescessarily PII. that's why i think it is B."}]},{"user":"RPC112","date":"2026-07-16","up":3,"text":"Personally Identifiable Information (PII) Detection\n\nThe requirement\"must never reveal customer information\" is a hard compliance requirement.\nPrompt Shields solve the hidden-instructions problem, but they do not directly prevent disclosure of customer data. [learn.microsoft.com], [learn.microsoft.com]\nThe latest AI‑103 discussion sites and explanations for this exact case study also mark PII Detection as the correct answer","pick":"C"},{"user":"Vasent","date":"2026-06-02","up":3,"text":"Since the case-study question mentions the requirement of NOT including any Customer information, so Agent1 must have the configuration setting of any \"Personally identifiable Information\" to be identified.","pick":"C"},{"user":"a5f05ea","date":"2026-10-06","up":2,"text":"It should be B & C both, because for malicious text embedded in images prompt shields are used.\nFor loss of user data PII detection.\nSo this should be a multi answer question.","pick":"BC"},{"user":"Srikantha","date":"2026-08-30","up":2,"text":"Prompt Shields detect both direct prompt injection (jailbreaks) and indirect prompt injection attacks. Indirect prompt injection occurs when external sources (such as product documents or OCR-extracted text from embedded images) contain hidden adversarial instructions intended to hijack or manipulate the model's behavior.","pick":"B"},{"user":"AdrienBnhm","date":"2026-08-27","up":2,"text":"it a question of malicious instruction set injection. The best answer here is B : \"Prompt shield\".\n\nSee the documentation here : https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/foundry/openai/concepts/content-filter-prompt-shields\n\n\"Agent1 must never reveal customer information, even if a document that contains customer data is added erroneously to the product sheet repository in storage1.\nThe product sheets might contain images that include embedded text. Agent1 must be protected from malicious instructions potentially hidden within the images.\"","pick":"B"},{"user":"momo53","date":"2026-08-06","up":2,"text":"Answer C. From what I understand, the requirements here mention protection against text in images, which is not addressed by Prompt Shields (which protects only from user prompts & document prompt). To protect from text in images, it must uses Azure Content Safety image moderation module.\n\nSources:\n- \"Securing Azure AI Applications: Against Prompt Injection | Part - 2\" in Tech Community\n- \"Azure AI Content Safety documentation\" in MS Learn (Quickstarts part)","pick":"C"},{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-09","up":2,"text":"The requirement is that the agent must never reveal customer information even if a document with customer data is mistakenly added to the repository. PII detection is the control that identifies and redacts personal data in content. Prompt shields (B) defend against injection, not data leakage; self-harm (A) and violence (D) filtering address harmful content categories, not customer-data exposure.","pick":"B"},{"user":"cayenne06","date":"2026-06-06","up":2,"text":"I think it's B due to :\"The product sheets might contain images that include embedded text. Agent1 must be protected from malicious instructions potentially hidden within the images.\"","pick":"B","replies":[{"user":"cloudera","date":"2026-06-10","up":2,"text":"It's C. The technical requirement directly links to PII: Agent1 must never reveal customer information, even if it is added to storage1 by mistake.\n\nProtection of PII is not optional; it is non-negotiable for every organisation — except perhaps a dodgy one."}]},{"user":"cayenne06","date":"2026-06-06","up":2,"text":"I think it's C due to :\"The product sheets might contain images that include embedded text. Agent1 must be protected from malicious instructions potentially hidden within the images.\"","pick":"B","replies":[{"user":"cloudera","date":"2026-06-10","up":1,"text":"It's C. The technical requirement directly links to PII: Agent1 must never reveal customer information, even if it is added to storage1 by mistake.\n\nProtection of PII is not optional; it is non-negotiable for every organisation — except perhaps a dodgy one.\nThanks me :)","replies":[{"user":"profitchannel","date":"2026-06-12","up":2,"text":"customer information ist not nescessarily PII. that's why i think it is B."}]}]},{"user":"batmanx","date":"2026-07-19","up":1,"text":"Feature PII Detection Prompt Shields\nDetects personal data ✔ Yes ✔ Yes (indirectly)\nPrevents data leakage ❌ No ✔ Yes\nBlocks prompt injection ❌ No ✔ Yes\nProtects against malicious image text ❌ No ✔ Yes\nMeets Contoso’s compliance requirements ❌ No ✔ Yes","pick":"B"}]},{"n":3,"id":1000631,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You are planning a Microsoft Foundry project named Project1 that will contain multiple agents. Each agent will access the same Azure AI Search resource.</p><p>You need to recommend a solution to centrally manage the Azure AI Search credentials within Project1. The solution must be implemented across all the agents.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you recommend?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Enable role-based access control (RBAC) for the Azure AI Search resource."},{"k":"B","html":"Disable key-based access control on the Azure AI Search resource."},{"k":"C","html":"Add a connection to the Azure AI Search resource."},{"k":"D","html":"Create a managed private endpoint that connects to the Azure AI Search resource."}],"answer":"C","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"C","p":100,"n":2}],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/7b287c7adbc6a8b60e53e949de9abb921000631/","comments":[{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-09","up":3,"text":"A project connection centralizes the credential/endpoint once and is reused by every agent in the project, which is exactly 'centrally manage ... across all agents.' RBAC (A) and disabling key auth (B) are good security practices but do not centralize the credential reference, and a managed private endpoint (D) addresses network isolation, not credential management.","pick":"C"}]},{"n":4,"id":1000632,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>Your company is piloting a customer support agent in a Microsoft Foundry project name Project1. Project1 is connected to an existing Application Insights resource, and the company’s support team reviews runs in the Traces tab.</p><p>The Foundry Agent Service is configured to perform the following actions:</p><ul><li>Retrieve the Application Insights connection string by calling project_client.telemetry.get_application_insights_connection_string().</li><li>Call configure_azure_monitor(connection_string=...) to enable telemetry.</li></ul><p>A separate LangChain service is configured to use OpenTelemetry and has the following configurations:</p><ul><li>Uses AzureAIOpenTelemetryTracer(connection_string=..., enable_content_recording=False)</li><li>Passes the tracer by using config={“callbacks”:[azure_tracer]}</li></ul><p>Company policy has the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Telemetry from LangChain and OpenTelemetry must be distinguishable within the same Application Insights resource.</li><li>Secrets and credentials must NOT be stored in prompts, tool arguments, or span attributes.</li></ul><p class=\"ask\">For each of the following statements, select Yes if the statement is true. Otherwise, select No.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image3.png\" alt=\"image3\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image4.png\" alt=\"image4\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/d3f451d63d1dc1a217538046282887f91000632/","comments":[{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":2,"text":"A project connection centralizes the credential/endpoint once and is reused by every agent in the project, which is exactly 'centrally manage ... across all agents.' RBAC (A) and disabling key auth (B) are good security practices but do not centralize the credential reference, and a managed private endpoint (D) addresses network isolation, not credential management."},{"user":"robert_ico","date":"2026-08-14","up":1,"text":"1) The configuration of Azure Monitor Telemetry does not magically instrument an independent LangChain service (or similar)\n2) OTEL_SERVICE_NAME = OpenTelemetry Service Name, and is the service name used in Application Insights (we would then query by cloud_RoleName; e.g., if OTEL_SERVICE_NAME = \"LangChain\" and \"Agent\", query with kql : ... | where cloud_RoleName=\"LangChain\")\n3) enable_content_recodring=False redacts message content and tool call arguments from traces (almost a direct definition)"}]},{"n":5,"id":1000633,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that processes procurement documents submitted by suppliers.</p><p>You need to implement two pipelines by using Azure Content Understanding in Foundry Tools. The solution must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Include a pipeline named Pipeline1 that supports cost-effective, high-volume processing of standalone PDF invoices.</li><li>Include a pipeline named Pipeline2 that supports cross-document validation by using multi-step reasoning and reference data.</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>How should you configure each pipeline?</strong> To answer, drag the appropriate configurations to the correct pipelines. Each configuration may be used once, more than once, of not at all. You may need to drag the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image5.png\" alt=\"image5\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image6.png\" alt=\"image6\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/94c5bb340bd2735429ef5beac9054ab41000633/","comments":[{"user":"robert_ico","date":"2026-08-14","up":3,"text":"Pipeline 1: D - Single-file, standard\nClues: standalone files (one document at a time), high volume, cost-effective. These are basically the definition for standard mode (individual documents without complex reasoning)\nPipeline 2: A- Multi in pro\nClues: Cross-document (\"multi-file\"), multi-step reasongin, reference data (pro mode: multi-step, complex reasoning)"},{"user":"AIBoss","date":"2026-08-05","up":3,"text":"Content Understanding offers two modes for different scenarios:\n\nStandard mode\n- Ideal for processing single files with straightforward field extraction. Use standard mode when you need to extract structured data from individual documents, images, audio, or video files without cross-file analysis or complex reasoning requirements.\n\nPro mode\n- Designed for advanced scenarios requiring multi-step reasoning and cross-file analysis.\n\nUses of pro mode:\n\nProcess multiple input files in a single request\nApply reasoning across different documents to validate, enrich, or aggregate data\nUse reference data (knowledge base) to guide extraction and validation\nPerform complex multi-step analysis that goes beyond simple field extraction"},{"user":"examtopics53932","date":"2026-08-11","up":1,"text":"pipeline1: Singlefile standard\npipeline2: Multifile pro\n\nNote that pro-mode is only available in the 2025-05-01-preview API version.\ncurrent API (2025-11-01) and latest preview (2026-06-01-preview) has replaced pro-mode with agentic mode."}]},{"n":6,"id":1000634,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Python application named App1 that integrates with a Microsoft Foundry project named Project1.</p><p>You need to ensure that App1 meets the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Authenticates by using a Microsoft Entra managed identity</li><li>Sends prompts to a deployed model by using the Azure OpenAI Responses API</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>How should you complete the Python code?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image7.png\" alt=\"image7\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image8.png\" alt=\"image8\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/0aec1e6e5a4c5ea872dedbd9120225221000634/","comments":[{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":6,"text":"A managed identity is consumed through DefaultAzureCredential (not AzureKeyCredential, which is key-based, nor ClientSecretCredential, which needs a secret). The Responses API call to send a prompt is responses.create(); retrieve/compact are not the send operation."},{"user":"robert_ico","date":"2026-08-14","up":1,"text":"AzureKeyCredential needs an PI ley; ClientSecretCredential uses a service principal (not managed; requires client id and client secret), DefaultAzureCredential: can use the application's managed identity (as a matter of fact, this method is used as standard in dev (e.g., in VSCODE, to detect your az login) and in Foundry (after deployed) or the final app like teams or copilot (when published))."}]},{"n":7,"id":1000635,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains a workflow for a customer support triage process.</p><p>You have an Ask a question node that stores user responses in a local variable named Var01.</p><p>You need to create the following Power Fx expressions:</p><ul><li>An if/else condition expression that ensures that Var01 contains a value</li><li>A Send message expression that returns the stored user response in uppercase</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>How should you configure the expressions?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image9.png\" alt=\"image9\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image10.png\" alt=\"image10\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/44bfce193dee337919ceb9b54c95b6471000635/","comments":[{"user":"robert_ico","date":"2026-08-14","up":2,"text":"IsEmpty(): used to determine if a table/collection has no records; IsBlank is for checking blank, null values in variables; Upper() converts to uppercase; Local.Var01 is the correct way to address Var01.\nANSWER: Not(IsBlank(Local.Var01)) and {Upper(Local.Var01)}"},{"user":"Sridhar_AI_Engineer","date":"2026-07-09","up":1,"text":"Why Upper ? required\nA Send message expression that returns the stored user response\n\nWhy not Local.Var01 ?","replies":[{"user":"AIBoss","date":"2026-08-11","up":2,"text":"Because it mentioned in the question.\n\"...... that returns the stored user response in uppercase\""}]}]},{"n":8,"id":1000636,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains a customer support agent built by using the Foundry Agent Service.</p><p>The agent uploads user-provided screenshots to Azure Storage through a ticketing tool and receives a blob URL for additional reasoning.</p><p>You need to use image moderation during agent runs and prevent harmful content from being returned during runs. Azure AI Content Safety must access the images by using the blob URL. The solution must follow the principle of least privilege.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you configure for Content Safety?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image11.png\" alt=\"image11\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image12.png\" alt=\"image12\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/591b4291a87d666448103701f606d2d91000636/","comments":[{"user":"3f9a492","date":"2026-08-09","up":4,"text":"For the first question, select **Block** for all four intervention points: User input, Tool call, Tool response, and Output. For the second, select **system-assigned managed identity + Storage Blob Data Contributor**—Microsoft states that Content Safety access through `blobUrl` requires Contributor or Owner, so Reader is not supported.","replies":[{"user":"Alvarogc","date":"2026-08-21","up":1,"text":"The state that you mention is about Content Safety Custom Categories, which is a different situation. For this question, following the principle of least privilege, Storage Blob Data Reader is the correct answer."}]},{"user":"OnlineCH","date":"2026-09-30","up":2,"text":"Storage access: on https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/ai-services/content-safety/quickstart-image?pivots=programming-language-rest&tabs=visual-studio%2Cwindows#prepare-a-sample-image it is mentioned \"Only Storage Blob Data Contributor or Storage Blob Data Owner are valid roles to proceed.\" so \"Storage Blob Data Contributor\" instead of \".. Reader\" might be correct."},{"user":"robert_ico","date":"2026-08-14","up":2,"text":"1) For guardrails: two key parts; one says \"prevent\" so it's block, not just annotate (which would label, identify, but no prevent), and the complete configuration should include user input, oputput, tool response and tool call (option 1 is only the tool call, but doing so would not prevent harmfull content in what the user inputs, or what the tool outputs, or the ultimate output given by the agent).\n2) For Storage access: Content Safety needs to access the screenshots using their blob URLs; therefore, it needs READ permission (least priviledge); Contributor assigns unnecessary write/delete permissions."}]},{"n":9,"id":1000637,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains three agents as shown in the following table.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image13.png\" alt=\"image13\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>You need to orchestrate the agents to ensure that the customer requests meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Support a deterministic, step-based process that uses conditional branching and shared state across the agents.</li><li>Optionally trigger a ticket action based on the triage result.</li><li>The solution must minimize development effort.</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you include in the solution?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"a workflow"},{"k":"B","html":"threads and runs without a workflow"},{"k":"C","html":"a multi-agent group chat session"},{"k":"D","html":"separate agent runs coordinated in the application code"}],"answer":"A","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"A","p":100,"n":2}],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/c979b4e63e65d560f07ba01ce69c1f961000637/","comments":[{"user":"robert_ico","date":"2026-08-14","up":1,"text":"Deterministic, step-based process, conditional branching, shared state, optional ticket action, minimize development effort; those features describe what a workflow does. On the other hand, the others: B) lack deterministic orchestration + branching, C) agents collaborate dynamically, but lacks determinism and a step-based process as well, D) you should write the orchestration logic, which does not reduce development effort\nANSWER: A) Worklfow","pick":"A"},{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":1,"text":": The requirements - deterministic, step-based, conditional branching, shared state, optional triggered action, minimal dev effort - describe a Foundry workflow. Threads/runs (B) and app-code coordination (D) require custom orchestration (more effort), and a group-chat session (C) is non-deterministic conversational collaboration, not a deterministic branching process.","pick":"A"}]},{"n":10,"id":1000638,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains an agent. The agent uses Azure Speech in Foundry Tools.</p><p>You fine-tune a baseline speech to text model for the en-us locale and publish the model.</p><p>The agent calls the Speech to text REST API and returns an error message indicating that the project ID is invalid.</p><p>You need to set the project property to the correct ID.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>To what should you set the project property?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"the project URL"},{"k":"B","html":"the custom speech project ID"},{"k":"C","html":"the project ID"},{"k":"D","html":"the custom speech endpoint URL"}],"answer":"B","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"B","p":100,"n":4}],"page":1,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/13cf3868ec7b5729eb4553cca38220f81000638/","comments":[{"user":"cloudera","date":"2026-06-09","up":2,"text":"I am pretty sure the answer should be B. the custom speech project ID.","pick":"B"},{"user":"robert_ico","date":"2026-08-14","up":1,"text":"Microsoft documents that when using a custom speech model through the Speech-to-Text REST API, the request can specify the custom speech project ID using the project query parameter. The key thing here is that there are 2 \"projects\": the foundry project, and the custom project. According to this reference, we need to specify the custom project id: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/ai-services/speech-service/rest-speech-to-text","pick":"B"},{"user":"maxng52","date":"2026-07-27","up":1,"text":"The error is an invalid project ID for a fine-tuned Custom Speech model, so the `project` property must be set to the GUID of the **Custom Speech project** that owns the model — not a URL (A/D, which aren't IDs) and not the generic Foundry project ID (C)."},{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":1,"text":"The error is an invalid project ID for a custom speech model, so the project property must be set to the custom speech project ID (a GUID identifying the Custom Speech project). A URL or endpoint URL is not a project ID, and 'the project ID' (C) is the generic Foundry project, not the Custom Speech project that owns the fine-tuned model.","pick":"B"}]},{"n":11,"id":1000639,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains an agent named PaymentAgent.</p><p>PaymentAgent includes a function tool that issues customer refunds by using an external API.</p><p>You are creating a workflow in YAML.</p><p>You need to ensure that the workflow pauses for human approval and continues with the refund step only after approval is granted.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>How should you complete the workflow definition?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image14.png\" alt=\"image14\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image15.png\" alt=\"image15\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/9710d470478e862e090e93b388e76a741000639/","comments":[{"user":"TuanJin","date":"2026-08-28","up":1,"text":"Box 1: ask_question To create a human-in-the-loop approval step in a Microsoft Foundry workflow, you should fill in the missing type with ask_question.\nIn Microsoft Foundry, the ask_question step is specifically designed to pause a workflow, prompt a user for input (such as an approval or rejection), and store the response in a variable that can be evaluated by subsequent logic.\nBox 2: approval == \"approved\" Execute Condition: Use a condition such as steps.approval.output == 'approved' (or a similar logical check based on your choice variable) to ensure the refund only executes when authorized."}]},{"n":12,"id":1000640,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have an Azure Speech in Foundry Tools resource that hosts a custom speech to text model deployed to a custom endpoint. An agent uses the endpoint to perform real-time speech recognition.</p><p>You are approaching the expiration date of the custom speech to text model.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What is the expected behavior when the model expires?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Speech recognition requests will return a 4xx error until a new custom model is deployed."},{"k":"B","html":"Speech recognition requests will continue to use the expired custom model until the model is removed manually."},{"k":"C","html":"Speech recognition requests will fall back to the most recent base model for the same locale."},{"k":"D","html":"The custom model will be deleted automatically when the model expires."}],"answer":"C","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"A","p":11,"n":1},{"a":"C","p":89,"n":8}],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/09773ba6b0c18e59332a65f31065c3901000640/","comments":[{"user":"cloudera","date":"2026-06-10","up":6,"text":"C is correct.\n\nAccording to the Microsoft lifecycle policy for Custom Speech, when a custom model deployed to a custom endpoint expires, the endpoint does not suddenly shut down or throw errors. Instead, Azure Speech ensures service continuity by automatically falling back to the most recent available base model for that specific locale.\n\nFor more visit - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/ai-services/speech-service/how-to-custom-speech-model-and-endpoint-lifecycle?utm_source=chatgpt.com&pivots=ai-foundry-portal","pick":"C"},{"user":"7b5220c","date":"2026-07-07","up":3,"text":"Answer C is the correct choice.\n\nWhen a custom Speech-to-Text model in Azure reaches its expiration date, the endpoint does not experience an immediate outage. To prevent a hard disruption of service, Azure utilizes a fallback mechanism:\n\nSpeech recognition requests will automatically fall back to the most recent base model for the same locale.\n\nIn practice, this means:\n\nThe service continues to run: The agent will not receive 4xx errors (which makes Answer A incorrect).\n\nAccuracy may decrease: Since the system now uses the general base model instead of the specially trained custom model, the specific adaptations to your vocabulary or acoustic environment are lost until a new custom model is trained and deployed.","pick":"C"},{"user":"Srini7","date":"2026-07-08","up":1,"text":"Transcription route : Question is about Custom endpoint, So it fall back to the most recent base model for the same locale.\nIf the question is a batch transcription: then 'A\" it will be fail with a 4xx error.","pick":"C"},{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":1,"text":"When a Custom Speech model passes its expiration, the deployed endpoint stops serving it and requests fail rather than silently using the expired model (B) or auto-deleting (D)","pick":"A"}]},{"n":13,"id":1000641,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains a model deployment.</p><p>You have an application that calls the deployment by using the Azure OpenAI v1 API and DefaultAzureCredential.</p><p>The developers at your company receive HTTP 403 errors when they send inference requests, even after running az login.</p><p>You need to ensure that the developers can perform model inference. The solution must follow the principle of least privilege.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which role-based access control (RBAC) role should you assign to the developers?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Cognitive Services User"},{"k":"B","html":"Cognitive Services OpenAI User"},{"k":"C","html":"Contributor"},{"k":"D","html":"Cognitive Services Data Reader"}],"answer":"B","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"B","p":100,"n":3}],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/118d3e6ae4f1a69fa63b49882d9c3db41000641/","comments":[{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":3,"text":"DefaultAzureCredential authenticates but a 403 means missing data-plane authorization. The least-privilege role that grants inference (data actions) is Cognitive Services OpenAI User. Cognitive Services User (A) covers non-OpenAI services, Contributor (C) is over-privileged control-plane, and Data Reader (D) does not grant inference.","pick":"B"}]},{"n":14,"id":1000642,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains an agent. The agent has a Model Context Protocol (MCP) tool that queries a knowledge base stored in Azure AI Search.</p><p>Some agent runs return answers from the base model without invoking the knowledge base, which results in responses without grounded citations.</p><p>You are provided with the following code snippet that runs the agent.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image16.png\" alt=\"image16\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>You need to add the correct tool _choice parameter to the code to deterministically force the agent to invoke the MCP tool on each run.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you add?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"tool_choice={“required”}"},{"k":"B","html":"tool_choice={“auto”}"},{"k":"C","html":"tool_choice={“type”:“knowledge_base”}"},{"k":"D","html":"tool_choice ={“type”:“mcp”}"}],"answer":"A","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"A","p":57,"n":12},{"a":"D","p":43,"n":9}],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/21aaa74739d68467d61316ed25b325dc1000642/","comments":[{"user":"Mattt","date":"2026-07-22","up":6,"text":"D is more precise. required only forces the use of some tool, while {\"type\":\"mcp\"} explicitly forces the MCP tool. Also, option A uses incorrect Python syntax.","pick":"D"},{"user":"3f9a492","date":"2026-08-10","up":3,"text":"Must use a tool every run → required\nThe option displays tool_choice={\"required\"}, but proper Python SDK syntax is normally tool_choice=\"required\"","pick":"A"},{"user":"cloudera","date":"2026-06-12","up":3,"text":"Syntax error but I will still go with A: tool_choice=\"required\"\n\nThe issue is that the agent sometimes answers from the base model without calling the knowledge base tool. tool_choice=\"required\" forces the agent to call a tool on each run, which prevents it from skipping retrieval and helps ensure grounded citations.\n\nD is tempting because MCP is the tool type, but the question is about forcing tool use at runtime, not defining the MCP tool itself.\n\nFor more - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/search/agentic-retrieval-how-to-create-pipeline","pick":"A"},{"user":"shank23","date":"2026-10-13","up":2,"text":"\"required\" explicitly forces the model to select and execute at least one tool before returning a text response. This overrides the base model's default behavior, ensuring it cannot answer directly using only its pre-trained internal weights","pick":"A"},{"user":"Sky_Akash","date":"2026-10-03","up":2,"text":"Why not A ({\"required\"})?\n{\"required\"} only ensures some tool is used, not specifically the MCP tool.\n\nIf multiple tools exist, the agent could pick another one.\n\nThe question explicitly says “deterministically force the agent to invoke the MCP tool”, so you must specify its type.\n\nSo even though A is “most voted,” D is the technically correct and exam-accurate choice.","pick":"D"},{"user":"RPC112","date":"2026-07-21","up":2,"text":"Its not D. Its A.\nThe question says:\"force the agent to invoke the MCP tool on each run\"\nThe documented behavior of tool_choice=\"required\" is:\nForce the model to call a tool instead of answering directly.\nThat directly addresses the problem statement:\nSome runs return answers from the base model without invoking the knowledge base.\n\nD. tool_choice={\"type\":\"mcp\"}\nMCP is the tool protocol, not the standard tool_choice value used to force invocation.\nSimply specifying \"mcp\" does not represent the documented way to require tool use.","pick":"A"},{"user":"ChrisJ99","date":"2026-10-14","up":1,"text":"Option A (\"required\") forces the agent to call a tool. But, it does not specify which tool. If the agent has more than one tool, it can select a different tool. Thus, this option is not deterministic for the MCP tool. Also, the syntax {\"required\"} is not correct. The correct form is a string: tool_choice=\"required\".","pick":"D"},{"user":"a5f05ea","date":"2026-10-06","up":1,"text":"For those answering D, understand question, it says deterministically force the agent to invoke the MCP tool. Now with option D it just tell agent you've a tool but it doesn't force the agent to use that tool. But option A forces agent to use the tool, which is the ask.","pick":"A"},{"user":"Srikantha","date":"2026-09-17","up":1,"text":"Why Option D is Incorrect\nOption D (tool_choice={\"type\":\"mcp\"}) is incorrect because it violates the expected schema for the Azure OpenAI API, which powers Microsoft Foundry agents.","pick":"A"},{"user":"rqFamily","date":"2026-08-09","up":1,"text":"Force-by-type works only when the type uniquely identifies one tool, so you do tool_choice={\"type\":\"file_search\"}, otherwise you do {\"type\":\"mcp\",\"name\":\"mcptoolname\"}, so our only option is A","pick":"A"},{"user":"CharlieMike","date":"2026-07-09","up":1,"text":"tool_choice(\"required\") forces the agent to invoke a tool every time. Since the MCP tool is the only applicable tool, the agent will use it on every run, ensuring grounded responses with citations instead of answering from the base model.","pick":"A"},{"user":"Srini7","date":"2026-07-08","up":1,"text":"Its D. Question Clearly state \" add the correct tool _choice parameter to the code to deterministically force the agent to invoke the MCP tool on each run\" in that case, we can't say \"required\" , becuase if you have more than one tool , its not valid. So answer is D","pick":"D"},{"user":"Danielly","date":"2026-07-03","up":1,"text":"Its D because tool_choice=\"required\" only forces it to use a tool its not speficifed if the agent has other tools . Then you have to force that SPECIFIC tool","pick":"D"},{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":1,"text":"To deterministically force a SPECIFIC tool, tool_choice must name the tool by type, so {\"type\":\"mcp\"} (D) is the intent. 'auto' (B) lets the model decide (the current bug), and {\"required\"} (A) is malformed set syntax; 'required' as a value forces some tool but not specifically the MCP one. The exact accepted schema for MCP tool_choice should be confirmed against the current Agents SDK","pick":"D"}],"variants":[119]},{"n":15,"id":1000643,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains a customer support agent grounded in internal documentation.</p><p>After a recent update, users report the following issues:</p><ul><li>Some answers are unsupported by retrieved documents.</li><li>A small number of responses are flagged for policy violations.</li></ul><p>You need to evaluate each issue.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which observability signals should you use for each issue?</strong> To answer, drag the appropriate observability signals to the correct issues. Each observability signal may be used once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to drag the spit bar between panes or scroll to view content.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image17.png\" alt=\"image17\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image18.png\" alt=\"image18\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/249855c723c1fe7bb69aa38eda0a93961000643/","comments":[{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":2,"text":"Answers unsupported by retrieved documents are a groundedness problem, measured by groundedness evaluation metrics. Responses flagged for policy violations map to the risk and safety evaluators"}]},{"n":16,"id":1000644,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project named Project1 that contains an agent. The agent uses an OpenAPI 3.0 specification to call an external weather service.</p><p>The weather service requires a key to be passed in an HTTP header. The key value is stored as a connection in Project1.</p><p>You need to ensure that the key value from the connection is included automatically whenever the OpenAPI tool is invoked.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you configure in the OpenAPI specification?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"a header parameter defined for each operation"},{"k":"B","html":"an Azure Key Vault connection"},{"k":"C","html":"an API key security scheme"},{"k":"D","html":"a Bearer token security scheme"}],"answer":"C","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"C","p":100,"n":2}],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/a022fb079879222d1c5ebd3a6efc6ddc1000644/","comments":[{"user":"Srikantha","date":"2026-09-17","up":1,"text":"components:\nsecuritySchemes:\nApiKeyAuth:\ntype: apiKey\nin: header\nname: X-Weather-API-Key # The header name expected by the service","pick":"C"},{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":1,"text":"The OpenAPI tool injects a connection-stored key automatically when the spec declares an API key security scheme (apiKey in header). A per-operation header parameter (A) would require passing the value manually, a Key Vault connection (B) is not an OpenAPI construct, and a Bearer scheme (D) is for OAuth/JWT tokens, not a static header key.","pick":"C"}]},{"n":17,"id":1000645,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that serves a high-volume chat app.</p><p>Most requests are simple FAQs, but some require advanced reasoning.</p><p>You need to reduce costs and latency for common queries, without degrading the quality of the responses to complex questions.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you do?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Route all the requests to a smaller model."},{"k":"B","html":"Use a model cascade that routes the requests to different models."},{"k":"C","html":"Increase the value of the max_tokens parameter for all the requests."},{"k":"D","html":"Route all the requests to the most capable model."}],"answer":"B","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"B","p":100,"n":2}],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/b0b2c844f80f0498e3279c4729ed7b3d1000645/","comments":[{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":2,"text":"A model cascade sends simple FAQs to a small/cheap model and escalates complex queries to a capable model, reducing cost/latency without degrading hard-question quality. Routing everything to a small model (A) hurts complex answers; routing all to the largest model (D) keeps costs high; raising max_tokens (C) does not reduce cost or latency.","pick":"B"},{"user":"shank23","date":"2026-10-13","up":1,"text":"A Model Cascade (also known as LLM Cascading) is an optimization and reliability pattern where an AI system chains multiple language models together sequentially. Instead of sending every single user query to a highly intelligent, expensive model, the system leverages a fast and cheap model first","pick":"B"}]},{"n":18,"id":1000646,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains an internal Q&amp;A agent.</p><p>Users report the following issues when they ask the agent questions:</p><ul class=\"kv\"><li><b>An increase in the following response:</b> “No relevant information found”</li><li>Periodic HTTP 429 rate limit exceeded errors during peak hours</li></ul><p>You need to identify whether each issue is caused by model unavailability, resource limits, or inference failures.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you do?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image19.png\" alt=\"image19\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image20.png\" alt=\"image20\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/e92ba1490d595271fb3eccae2e7880421000646/","comments":[{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-11","up":4,"text":"Select Model Availability Rate and Provisioned Utilization because they help identify model availability issues and resource limits causing HTTP 429 errors. Select RequestResponse logs to investigate inference failures and understand why the agent returns “No relevant information found.”"},{"user":"Retinol2","date":"2026-10-12","up":3,"text":"I think the correct answer for diagnostic log is 'trace'. The question contains 'identify whether each issue is caused by model unavailability, resource limits or inference failures. That is a diagnostic/root-cause question hence 'trace'"}]},{"n":19,"id":1000647,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains a high-traffic agent.</p><p>After a recent update, operational costs increase significantly.</p><p>Monitoring confirms that the volume of user traffic to the agent remains unchanged.</p><p>You suspect that changes to the request or response characteristics are causing the increase. You need to identify whether the additional costs are driven by the model input size, the model output size, or expanded tool usage.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which observability capability should you use?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"latency"},{"k":"B","html":"evaluation metrics"},{"k":"C","html":"run success rate"},{"k":"D","html":"token usage"}],"answer":"D","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"D","p":100,"n":1}],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/7e77622641b386af6ef224e11153ca431000647/","comments":[{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":1,"text":": Cost is driven by tokens, so token-usage observability reveals whether input size, output size, or expanded tool calls increased consumption. Latency (A), evaluation metrics (B), and run success rate (C) do not attribute cost to input/output/tool token volume.","pick":"D"}]},{"n":20,"id":1000648,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains an agent.</p><p>The agent uses tools to retrieve internal content and call external APIs. The agent is configured to let the model decide when to call the tools.</p><p>You need to publish the agent for a compliance workflow. The solution must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Each workflow run must include a retrieval step before generating a response.</li><li>Tool calls must authenticate by using the published agent’s own identity.</li><li>Tool access must use an identity isolated from other project resources.</li><li>Tool access must use support audit tracing.</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you do?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image21.png\" alt=\"image21\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image22.png\" alt=\"image22\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":2,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/c96a0b40aee0fa45a09fa39d8fe15fb91000648/","comments":[{"user":"8ac3742","date":"2026-09-30","up":1,"text":"The problem statement notes that the agent is currently configured to \"let the model decide when to call the tools\" (which is what tool_choice: \"auto\" does). However, the compliance requirement mandates:\n​\"Each workflow run must include a retrieval step before generating a response.\"\nIf left as auto, the model might choose to answer directly from parametric memory without executing a tool call. Setting tool_choice: \"required\" forces the model to call one of its available tools before generating an answer."},{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":1,"text":"Forcing a retrieval step every run requires tool_choice=required (auto lets the model skip tools; none disables them). For an isolated, auditable identity that is the published agent's own, a distinct agent identity bound to the client app is correct; storing keys in prompts violates security and a shared project identity is not isolated."}]},{"n":21,"id":1000649,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project named Project1 that contains the following:</p><ul><li>An OpenAPI tool that calls an external API</li><li>A project connection named Connection1 that stores the API key of the external API</li></ul><p>When an agent calls the OpenAPI tool, the API returns a 401 unauthorized error, and traces show that the API key header is NOT being sent.</p><p>You need to ensure that the OpenAPI tool automatically includes the API key from Connection1 on all requests.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you do?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Enable identity passthrough so that the tool uses the Microsoft Entra token of the caller."},{"k":"B","html":"Add the API key header manually to the OpenAPI specification."},{"k":"C","html":"Configure the tool to use the default connection of Project1."},{"k":"D","html":"Connect the tool to Connection1."}],"answer":"D","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"D","p":100,"n":6}],"page":3,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/9f3ad306cd7fc80ffeab13533fb4762c1000649/","comments":[{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":3,"text":"The 401 with a missing key header means the tool is not bound to the connection holding the key. Connecting the tool to Connection1 makes Foundry inject the stored key automatically. Identity passthrough (A) sends the caller's Entra token, not the API key; manually adding the header (B) hardcodes secrets; the default project connection (C) is not necessarily Connection1.","pick":"D"},{"user":"8ac3742","date":"2026-09-30","up":2,"text":"​Bind to the Connection:\n​In the tool configuration blade, scroll to the Authentication section.\n​Switch the authentication method/source to Project Connection (or Saved Connection).\n​From the dropdown list of available connections, select Connection1.\n​Verify that the security scheme defined in the OpenAPI specification (e.g., apiKey in header) matches the key/secret stored in Connection1.","pick":"D"},{"user":"cloudera","date":"2026-06-09","up":2,"text":"D. Connect the tool to Connection1.\n\nB is incomplete answer and can expose secrets if done wrong.","pick":"D"}]},{"n":22,"id":1000650,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains a customer support agent. The agent calls an internal knowledge API tool before generating responses.</p><p>Users report the following issues:</p><ul><li>Some requests take more than 15 seconds to complete.</li><li>Some responses are incorrect, even when the knowledge API returns the expected data.</li></ul><p>You need to inspect individual agent runs to view the ordered sequence of large language model (LLM) calls, tool invocations, and timing information.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which observability capability should you use?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"token usage"},{"k":"B","html":"monitoring"},{"k":"C","html":"safety metrics"},{"k":"D","html":"tracing"}],"answer":"D","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"D","p":100,"n":1}],"page":3,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/027d8da6055db81e1e623d1c7ecc37ab1000650/","comments":[{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":1,"text":"Tracing shows the ordered span sequence of LLM calls, tool invocations, and timing within a single run, which is exactly what is needed to diagnose latency and incorrect-despite-correct-data behavior. Token usage (A), monitoring (B), and safety metrics (C) are aggregate signals, not per-run ordered traces.","pick":"D"}]},{"n":23,"id":1000651,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a multimodal AI generative model that accepts image uploads and uses extracted image text to generate responses.</p><p>You discover that users can upload unsafe images and embed hidden instructions into images to manipulate the model.</p><p>You need to implement controls to mitigate the risk.</p><div class=\"solution\"><span>Proposed solution</span>You configure a prompt shield for user prompts.</div><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Does this meet the goal?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Yes"},{"k":"B","html":"No"}],"answer":"B","type":"yesno","votes":[{"a":"A","p":14,"n":1},{"a":"B","p":86,"n":6}],"page":3,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/91bd89a7dda63eb254d4cc2b97e0651d1000651/","comments":[{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":4,"text":"The threat is hidden instructions embedded in uploaded IMAGES (indirect/document attack) plus unsafe image content. A prompt shield for USER PROMPTS addresses direct jailbreak text from the user, not injected content extracted from images, so it does not meet the goal.","pick":"B"},{"user":"a5f05ea","date":"2026-09-29","up":1,"text":"B. No\n\nA Prompt Shield for user prompts protects against prompt injection attacks coming directly from user-entered text. It does not protect against malicious instructions embedded inside uploaded documents or images.","pick":"B"},{"user":"Dinesh_87","date":"2026-08-08","up":1,"text":"Requires - Content Safety image/multimodal harm filters + Spotlighting, to mark extracted/image-derived text as untrusted so the model treats it as data, not instructions","pick":"B"},{"user":"profitchannel","date":"2026-06-18","up":1,"text":"but since one of the 4 questions should have a right answer, this is more likely the one with the right answer?","pick":"A"},{"user":"cloudera","date":"2026-06-09","up":1,"text":"I don't think user prompts only does not fully meet the goal. It need Insafe Images and document/indirect prompt injection risk. Azure AI Content Safety Prompt Shields can detect both User Prompt Attacks and Document Attacks.","pick":"B"}],"series":true},{"n":24,"id":1000652,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a multimodal AI generative model that accepts image uploads and uses extracted image text to generate responses.</p><p>You discover that users can upload unsafe images and embed hidden instructions into images to manipulate the model.</p><p>You need to implement controls to mitigate the risk.</p><div class=\"solution\"><span>Proposed solution</span>You configure image moderation to block unsafe content before processing the images.</div><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Does this meet the goal?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Yes"},{"k":"B","html":"No"}],"answer":"B","type":"yesno","votes":[{"a":"B","p":100,"n":7}],"page":3,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/2c8f6d4c0875ecdcda0e7f0cd6ff549c1000652/","comments":[{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":3,"text":": Image moderation blocks unsafe visual content, which handles the 'unsafe images' half, but it does NOT neutralize hidden text instructions embedded in images (the prompt-injection half). Because the stated goal includes mitigating embedded instructions, image moderation alone does not fully meet the goal","pick":"B"},{"user":"cloudera","date":"2026-06-09","up":3,"text":"Correct answer is B (No) again.\nThere is two issues here 1)unsafe image 2) hidden instructions.\n\nImage moderation address unsafe image, but doesn't help with the #2 above. The 2nd part required prompt injection protection which is missing in the configuration.","pick":"B"},{"user":"RPC112","date":"2026-07-18","up":1,"text":"Hidden instructions in images/documents → Prompt Shields for documents\nUnsafe visual content (violence, nudity, illegal imagery, etc.) → Image content moderation / Analyze Image API\n\nThe scenario in questions 23–26 describes both risks together, which is why none of the four individual solutions on their own \"meets the goal\" as stated — each one only solves half the problem.\n\nWould be A if Unsafe images were isolated and not combined with embedded hidden instructions.","pick":"B"}],"series":true},{"n":25,"id":1000653,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a multimodal AI generative model that accepts image uploads and uses extracted image text to generate responses.</p><p>You discover that users can upload unsafe images and embed hidden instructions into images to manipulate the model.</p><p>You need to implement controls to mitigate the risk.</p><div class=\"solution\"><span>Proposed solution</span>You configure a prompt shield for documents.</div><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Does this meet the goal?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Yes"},{"k":"B","html":"No"}],"answer":"B","type":"yesno","votes":[{"a":"A","p":44,"n":8},{"a":"B","p":56,"n":10}],"page":3,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/9ecc652bd5a2ca38a7d86bcee75d90541000653/","comments":[{"user":"Srikantha","date":"2026-09-17","up":3,"text":"Correct Solution:\nTo mitigate both risks, you must use:\nAzure AI Content Safety Image Moderation to scan uploaded images for unsafe visual content (Adult, Violence, Hate, Self-harm).\nPrompt Shields for User Input / Images (or running OCR text through Prompt Shields) to detect embedded prompt injection instructions hidden inside the image text.","pick":"B"},{"user":"Mattt","date":"2026-07-23","up":3,"text":"A is correct.\nHere, “unsafe images” refers to images containing hidden malicious instructions. Prompt Shields for Documents can analyze the extracted text and detect these indirect prompt-injection attacks.","pick":"A"},{"user":"a5f05ea","date":"2026-10-03","up":2,"text":"For unsafe images it should be Image moderation and for embed text prompt shield, since prompt shield aloe cannot solve both the issue.","pick":"B"},{"user":"VimalChauhan","date":"2026-09-23","up":2,"text":"The threat described is:\n\nUsers upload images.\nThe model extracts text from those images (OCR or multimodal processing).\nHidden instructions in the extracted text attempt to manipulate the model.\n\nIn Azure AI Foundry, Prompt Shields for Documents are designed to protect against indirect prompt injection attacks originating from external content, including:\n\nDocuments\nWeb pages\nFiles\nImages containing embedded text\n\nWhen the model processes text extracted from an image, Prompt Shields for Documents can detect and mitigate malicious instructions embedded in that content before it influences the model's behavior.","pick":"A"},{"user":"JoaoCA","date":"2026-08-25","up":2,"text":"B. No - Prompt Shields for documents catches the hidden-instruction (indirect injection) half, but doesn't block unsafe image content. Still only half the goal, so it doesn't fully meet it.","pick":"B"},{"user":"Dinesh_87","date":"2026-08-08","up":2,"text":"Prompt Shields for Documents, applied to the OCR/extracted text before it reaches the LLM","pick":"A"},{"user":"cloudera","date":"2026-06-11","up":2,"text":"Two problem that need solving:\n1) Upload Unsafe Image Content (eg. visually inappropriate, illegal, or violent imagery).\n2) Indirect hidden prompt instructions.\n\nPrompt Shield for documents can address the second part (hidden text). For the Upload unsafe image (#1 above) content, you will need Image moderation / Analyze image API.\n\nSo the answer is B.","pick":"B"},{"user":"AzureGeek79","date":"2026-10-10","up":1,"text":"There is not a single answer to this question. It should be:\na) You configure a prompt shield for documents.\nb) You configure image moderation to block unsafe content before processing the images.","pick":"A"},{"user":"Jedi","date":"2026-08-23","up":1,"text":"I'm going with A, See prompt shields for documents: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/foundry/openai/concepts/content-filter-prompt-shields","pick":"A"},{"user":"7e4a230","date":"2026-07-13","up":1,"text":"Prompt Shields for Documents detect hidden or malicious instructions embedded in uploaded content. Because the model extracts the image’s text before processing it, the shield can analyze that extracted text for indirect prompt-injection attacks.","pick":"A"},{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":1,"text":"Same as the 23 question. The threat is hidden instructions embedded in uploaded IMAGES (indirect/document attack) plus unsafe image content. A prompt shield for USER PROMPTS addresses direct jailbreak text from the user, not injected content extracted from images, so it does not meet the goal.","pick":"B","replies":[{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":2,"text":"Apologies, this should be A.\nPrompt Shields for Documents detects malicious instructions embedded in third-party content such as text extracted from images, which directly mitigates the hidden-instruction (indirect injection) risk."}]},{"user":"cloudera","date":"2026-06-09","up":1,"text":"B No.\n\nPrompt shield for documents helps with the hidden instruction problem. But doesn't handle unsafe image content.","pick":"B"}],"series":true},{"n":26,"id":1000654,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a multimodal AI generative model that accepts image uploads and uses extracted image text to generate responses.</p><p>You discover that users can upload unsafe images and embed hidden instructions into images to manipulate the model.</p><p>You need to implement controls to mitigate the risk.</p><div class=\"solution\"><span>Proposed solution</span>You configure protected material detection.</div><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Does this meet the goal?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Yes"},{"k":"B","html":"No"}],"answer":"B","type":"yesno","votes":[{"a":"B","p":100,"n":4}],"page":3,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/44381e123706cd74a7ce1338e0f06eeb1000654/","comments":[{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":2,"text":"Protected material detection identifies copyrighted/owned content in output. It has nothing to do with unsafe images or embedded malicious instructions, so it does not meet the goal.","pick":"B"},{"user":"Munish_20","date":"2026-09-20","up":1,"text":"protected material detection is for copy right related prevention, not for required protection","pick":"B"},{"user":"Dinesh_87","date":"2026-08-08","up":1,"text":"Protected material detection serves a completely different purpose — it's designed to identify copyrighted or owned content, specifically pinpointing copyrighted content and providing sources for preexisting text and code. It checks whether the model's output matches known copyrighted text or code (song lyrics, articles, licensed code snippets, etc.)\n\nTo actually meet the goal, you'd need:\n\nContent Safety image/multimodal harm filters → for unsafe images\nPrompt Shields for Documents → for hidden instructions in extracted image text","pick":"B"}],"series":true},{"n":27,"id":1000655,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You need to recommend a solution to assess the responses generated by Agent1 when the agent uses the product information stored in storage1. The solution must meet the technical requirements.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you include in the recommendation?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"a Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) evaluator"},{"k":"B","html":"a custom guardrail"},{"k":"C","html":"model fine-tuning"},{"k":"D","html":"a groundedness evaluator"}],"answer":"D","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"A","p":30,"n":3},{"a":"D","p":70,"n":7}],"page":3,"case":"d421f5cb15","thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/5541d98b93c0cbb1883160522a71d74b1000655/","comments":[{"user":"Darkren4eveR","date":"2026-07-09","up":5,"text":"Requirements says relevant, complete and Accurate\nSo should be D","pick":"D"},{"user":"8ac3742","date":"2026-10-04","up":2,"text":"Groundedness Evaluator (Option D) measures only one dimension: whether the response is strictly derived from the context without fabricating informatio\n\nRetrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) Evaluator (Option A) evaluates the end-to-end RAG architecture across all three required metrics:\n\nRelevance (Retrieval & Question-Answer Relevance)\nCompleteness (Context / Answer Completeness)\nAccuracy / Faithfulness (Groundedness)","pick":"A"},{"user":"_QzL","date":"2026-09-04","up":2,"text":"Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) evaluator because : \"Responses generated by using the product sheet information must be relevant, complete, and accurate\"","pick":"A","replies":[{"user":"AIBoss","date":"2026-09-06","up":2,"text":"The question says \"to assess the responses\".\nGroundedness evaluator is a subset of RAG evaluators. RAG evaluators has other evaluators also which is not relevent here.\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/foundry/concepts/evaluation-evaluators/rag-evaluators"}]},{"user":"Sakthi Indra","date":"2026-10-16","up":1,"text":"The question states that Agent1 must generate responses using product information stored in Azure Blob Storage (storage1).\nThe technical requirements specify that the responses must be:\n- Relevant — Address the customer's question.\n- Complete — Include all necessary product information.\n- Accurate — Provide correct information based on the retrieved documents.\nA RAG evaluation approach assesses retrieval quality and generated-response quality, including relevance, completeness, and groundedness.","pick":"A"},{"user":"shank23","date":"2026-10-13","up":1,"text":"In Azure, you explicitly load GroundednessEvaluator to measure this specific risk, whereas \"RAG\" refers to the entire multi-metric pipeline (which includes other elements like search indexing performance that you don't need to measure for this specific compliance constraint)","pick":"D"},{"user":"Christie0223","date":"2026-10-11","up":1,"text":"Requirements says relevant, complete and Accurate, which should be RAG Evaluator. Groundedness evaluator only checks faithfulness.","pick":"A"},{"user":"_Lucifer_","date":"2026-09-27","up":1,"text":"D-a groundedness evaluator\ngroundedness work is to check whether the answer matched the context or not and in the question we have to do the same","pick":"D"},{"user":"a5f05ea","date":"2026-09-26","up":1,"text":"Groundedness measures whether Agent1's generated answers are actually supported by the retrieved product information in storage1 — i.e., it detects hallucinated or unsupported claims against the source context. That's precisely \"assess the responses when the agent uses the product information stored in storage1.\"","pick":"D"}]},{"n":28,"id":1000656,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You need to configure Agent1 to answer customer questions about only the Contoso products. The solution must meet the business requirements.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you do?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Modify the system message instructions."},{"k":"B","html":"Add few-shot examples."},{"k":"C","html":"Apply top-p sampling."},{"k":"D","html":"Increase the value of the temperature parameter."}],"answer":"A","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"A","p":100,"n":3}],"page":3,"case":"d421f5cb15","thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/3945335a80909895ebd327c7717be88d1000656/","comments":[{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":4,"text":"Constraining the agent to answer only about Contoso products is a scope/grounding instruction best enforced through the system message. Few-shot examples (B) shape style but do not reliably bound scope; top-p (C) and temperature (D) tune randomness, not topic restriction.","pick":"A"},{"user":"Srikantha","date":"2026-09-17","up":2,"text":"he correct answer is A. Modify the system message instructions.\nReasoning:\nThe system message (system prompt) defines the agent's persona, operational boundaries, tone, and guardrails. Updating the system instructions with explicit domain-scoping rules (for example, \"You are a support assistant for Contoso. You must answer questions ONLY about Contoso products and politely decline out-of-scope inquiries.\") is the standard and most effective method to restrict the model's behavior and scope.","pick":"A"}]},{"n":29,"id":1000657,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project.</p><p>You plan to build a customer support solution that contains an agent. The solution must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Provide accurate, context-aware responses grounded in internal product documentation stored in Azure AI Search.</li><li>Require deep, multi-step reasoning across long contexts.</li><li>Generate detailed natural language responses.</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which type of model should you use to power the agent?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"a multimodal model"},{"k":"B","html":"a small language model (SLM)"},{"k":"C","html":"a key phrase extraction model"},{"k":"D","html":"a large language model (LLM)"}],"answer":"D","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"D","p":100,"n":4}],"page":3,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/c3b75da0dc8f42f53573aed01b686b811000657/","comments":[{"user":"_Lucifer_","date":"2026-09-27","up":2,"text":"Multimodal is usefull when in question they have asked image + text ,image + audio\nLLM fits in this case when u want multireasoning and other requirements\nso answer is D-LLM","pick":"D"},{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":2,"text":"Deep multi-step reasoning over long contexts with detailed natural-language generation is the strength of an LLM. An SLM (B) trades reasoning depth for cost/latency; a multimodal model (A) adds image/audio not required here; key phrase extraction (C) is a narrow NLP task, not a generative reasoner.","pick":"D"},{"user":"Shaharaz","date":"2026-10-03","up":1,"text":"An LLM is best suited because the agent must:\n\nPerform deep, multi-step reasoning\nProcess long contexts\nGenerate detailed natural-language responses\nUse retrieval-augmented generation, or RAG, to ground answers in internal product documentation retrieved from Azure AI Search\n\nRAG combines search with an LLM by retrieving relevant internal content, adding it to the model’s context, and generating an answer grounded in that content","pick":"D"}]},{"n":30,"id":1000658,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains a deployed ticket-triage agent.</p><p>You discover that sometimes the agent responds without calling any tools, even when a tool is required.</p><p>You need to ensure that the agent calls a tool during execution.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>How should you complete the Python code?</strong> To answer, drag the appropriate values to the correct targets. Each value may be used once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to drag the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image23.png\" alt=\"image23\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image24.png\" alt=\"image24\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":3,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/89b650e888f9e936d42f6714566de0ab1000658/","comments":[{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":4,"text":"To guarantee a tool is invoked, set the tool_choice key to the value 'required'. The highlighted drag values place \"tool_choice\" as the key and \"required\" as the value, which forces tool usage on every run."}]},{"n":31,"id":1000659,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You are building a web app named App1 that generates responses by using a model deployed to a Microsoft Foundry project named Project1.</p><p>Before sending the prompts to the model, App1 must retrieve documents by using Azure AI Search.</p><p>You need to integrate Project1 and App1. The solution must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Multiple client applications must use the same search configuration.</li><li>A security policy must prevent key-based authentication.</li><li>Administrative effort must be minimized.</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you do?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Create a custom HTTP connection in Foundry and manually configure Azure AI Search endpoints per application."},{"k":"B","html":"Configure an Azure AI Search connection in Project1 and reference the connection in each application."},{"k":"C","html":"Call Azure AI Search directly from each application by using Microsoft Entra authentication."},{"k":"D","html":"Enable a managed identity for each application and call Azure AI Search directly."}],"answer":"B","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"B","p":100,"n":3}],"page":4,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/d361202481d5efcd6407e01de55bf3bb1000659/","comments":[{"user":"8ac3742","date":"2026-10-04","up":1,"text":"Microsoft Foundry project connections natively support Microsoft Entra ID / Managed Identity authentication without storing or exposing API keys.","pick":"B"},{"user":"e886835","date":"2026-07-06","up":1,"text":"Centralized Configuration: Configuring the Azure AI Search connection at the project level (Project1) satisfies the requirement that multiple client applications use the same search configuration, minimizing redundancy.\n\nSecurity & Compliance: Azure AI Foundry connections support Microsoft Entra ID (Azure RBAC) for authentication. This allows you to avoid API keys completely, ensuring compliance with the policy against key-based authentication.\n\nMinimized Administrative Effort: Instead of managing endpoints, credentials, or custom code across every single client application individually (as suggested in options A, C, and D), you manage a single, shared connection within the Foundry project that the applications can simply reference.","pick":"B"},{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":1,"text":"A single project connection gives all apps the same search configuration and uses Entra-based (keyless) auth with minimal admin effort. Custom per-app HTTP config (A) and calling Search directly from each app (C, D) duplicate configuration and increase administrative effort.","pick":"B"}]},{"n":32,"id":1000660,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains an agent used by the financial analysts at your company.</p><p>You need to optimize the agent workflow by providing additional data access and processing capabilities. The solution must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Ensure that the agent can perform calculations during conversations.</li><li>Ensure that the agent can access up-to-date information from public websites.</li><li>Ensure that the agent can retrieve information from documents uploaded directly to the agent.</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you use for each requirement?</strong> To answer, drag the appropriate tools to the correct requirements. Each tool may be used once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to drag the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image25.png\" alt=\"image25\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image26.png\" alt=\"image26\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":4,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/fb16ab6665836a5468ddf9e004f0781a1000660/","comments":[{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":2,"text":"Grounding with Bing Search supplies current public-web information; Code interpreter executes calculations during a conversation; File search retrieves from documents uploaded directly to the agent. Each highlighted pairing matches the canonical Foundry Agent Service tool."},{"user":"8ac3742","date":"2026-10-04","up":1,"text":"(1)Access up-to-date information from public websites: Grounding with Bing Search (2)Perform calculations during conversations: Code interpreter Retrieve information from (3)documents uploaded directly to the agent: File search\n\nCode interpreter: Runs code in an isolated sandbox environment to execute precise mathematical operations, process datasets, and generate analytical calculations without hallucination."}]},{"n":33,"id":1000661,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains a prompt agent used by a customer support web app.</p><p>The agent is invoked from a Python service that does NOT run in the Foundry portal.</p><p>You need to implement end-to-end tracing to capture latency breakdowns and exceptions across agent runs.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which two components can you use?</strong> Each correct answer presents a complete solution.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"a Log Analytics workspace"},{"k":"B","html":"Application Insights"},{"k":"C","html":"OpenTelemetry"},{"k":"D","html":"the Azure Monitor Agent"},{"k":"E","html":"Microsoft Sentinel"}],"answer":"BC","type":"multi","votes":[{"a":"BC","p":100,"n":3}],"page":4,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/328e700630be5f9163df3cd3749ab7651000661/","comments":[{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":2,"text":"For end-to-end tracing of agent runs from an external Python service, OpenTelemetry instruments the code and Application Insights stores/visualizes the traces - each is a complete tracing solution as worded. A Log Analytics workspace (A) backs App Insights but is not itself the tracing capability; Azure Monitor Agent (D) and Sentinel (E) are not used for agent run tracing","pick":"BC"},{"user":"8ac3742","date":"2026-10-04","up":1,"text":"Application Insights (Option B):Microsoft Foundry projects integrate natively with Azure Application Insights to provide end-to-end distributed tracing, latency breakdowns (span timelines for LLM calls, tool executions, and retrieval), and automatic exception tracking across external application calls. Connecting the Python service to the project’s linked Application Insights resource fulfills the entire requirement out of the box. OpenTelemetry (Option C):The Azure AI Foundry SDK (azure-ai-projects / prompt flow / agent framework) is instrumented directly on top of the OpenTelemetry (OTel) open standard. In a standalone Python service outside the portal, you can enable end-to-end tracing using the OpenTelemetry SDK (via azure-monitor-opentelemetry or an OTel tracer) to capture spans, measure component latency, and log exceptions to any compatible backend.","pick":"BC"}]},{"n":34,"id":1000662,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a customer support agent that uses the Microsoft Foundry Agent Service.</p><p>Sometimes, customers return to a session days later to continue the same support case, and the agent must resume with the full historical context. The agent must provide the following:</p><ul><li>Multi-turn continuity within the session</li><li>Cross-session continuity for the same case</li><li>Access to the full interaction history, including user messages, agent messages, tool calls, and tool outputs</li></ul><p>You need to ensure that the agent automatically reloads the complete history on each new turn.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you do?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Create and reuse a conversation by storing the conversation’s ID and supplying the ID on subsequent requests."},{"k":"B","html":"Persist only the final model response stored in the client application and prepend the response to future prompts."},{"k":"C","html":"Enable memory summarization on the agent definition to persist the context automatically."}],"answer":"A","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"A","p":100,"n":3}],"page":4,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/a001fb1968e5e9c21360e016e48f14931000662/","comments":[{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":4,"text":"Persisting and reusing the conversation/thread ID reloads the full server-side history (user/agent messages, tool calls, tool outputs) on each new turn and supports cross-session resumption. Storing only the final response (B) loses tool history; memory summarization (C) condenses rather than reloads the complete interaction history.","pick":"A"},{"user":"8ac3742","date":"2026-10-04","up":1,"text":"In the Microsoft Foundry Agent Service (and the underlying OpenAI Assistants/threads model), a conversation (thread) is a stateful entity managed server-side by Azure. It automatically appends and preserves:User inputs and assistant responses. Internal reasoning steps, tool calls, and tool response outputs","pick":"A"}]},{"n":35,"id":1000663,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains a deployed chat model.</p><p>You have a Python service that sends API requests to the model. The service is integrated with an automated validation system that compares generated outputs against approved response patterns.</p><p>Stakeholders report that small wording differences are causing validation mismatches.</p><p>You need to update the request parameters to improve output stability. The solution must maximize reasoning quality.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>How should you complete the Python code?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image27.png\" alt=\"image27\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image28.png\" alt=\"image28\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":4,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/f1ad48df493ec4dc53096e1131711d691000663/","comments":[{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":5,"text":"To maximize output stability/determinism, set temperature to 0 (lowest randomness). To maximize reasoning quality on a reasoning model, set the effort to high. The two highlighted selections satisfy 'improve output stability' and 'maximize reasoning quality' respectively."}]},{"n":36,"id":1000664,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a chat app in a Microsoft Foundry project and an Azure AI Search vectorized index.</p><p>You need to connect to the index to meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Complex questions must retrieve information from multiple chunks.</li><li>Multi-turn conversations must influence retrieval planning.</li><li>Retrievals must run in parallel to reduce latency.</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which retrieval approach should you use?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"iterative retrieval"},{"k":"B","html":"agentic Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG)"},{"k":"C","html":"chain of thought"},{"k":"D","html":"classic Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG)"}],"answer":"B","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"B","p":100,"n":3}],"page":4,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/d8261e019d60fd127359de181ea9ea9c1000664/","comments":[{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":4,"text":"Agentic RAG decomposes complex questions into subqueries spanning multiple chunks, uses conversation history to influence query planning, and runs subqueries in parallel to cut latency - matching all three requirements.\nClassic RAG (D) is single-shot; iterative retrieval (A) is sequential; chain of thought (C) is a prompting technique, not a retrieval method.","pick":"B"}]},{"n":37,"id":1000665,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You need to recommend a plan to create a customer support agent by using the Microsoft Foundry Agent Service. The agent must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Retain user preferences across multiple conversations.</li><li>Enable users to provide contextual grounding by directly uploading documents during a chat.</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which Foundry capability should you recommend for each requirement?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image29.png\" alt=\"image29\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image30.png\" alt=\"image30\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":4,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/22b71826331fbc8de28aab81913ba91b1000665/","comments":[{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":1,"text":"Retaining user preferences across conversations requires persistent agent memory (conversation history alone resets per session; orchestration session context is in-session). Letting users ground via documents uploaded during chat is the File search tool (Azure AI Search tool targets a pre-built index; code interpreter is for compute)."}]},{"n":38,"id":1000666,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains an agent. The agent generates summaries from retrieved policy documents.</p><p>You need to improve response completeness. The solution must be implemented in the logic of the application code before responses are returned.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you do?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Add a retry evaluation before the responses are returned."},{"k":"B","html":"Decrease the value of the max_tokens parameter."},{"k":"C","html":"Switch to Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG)."},{"k":"D","html":"Replace the model with a smaller deployment."}],"answer":"A","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"A","p":100,"n":3}],"page":4,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/f1b6fbfbc183a82fd819ae4d84b8499a1000666/","comments":[{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":3,"text":"Implementing the fix 'in the logic of the application code before responses are returned' points to an evaluation/retry pass that checks completeness and regenerates if needed. Decreasing max_tokens (B) and using a smaller model (D) reduce completeness; switching to RAG (C) changes retrieval, not the in-code post-check requested.","pick":"A"},{"user":"8ac3742","date":"2026-10-04","up":1,"text":"Read the prompt's first sentence carefully:\"The agent generates summaries from retrieved policy documents.\" Because the agent is already retrieving policy documents and generating summaries from them, it is already using Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG). Switching to RAG is redundant and doesn't solve the issue.","pick":"A"}],"variants":[100,153]},{"n":39,"id":1000667,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a customer support agent built by using the Microsoft Foundry Agent Service. The agent calls an Azure OpenAI model deployment.</p><p>During load testing, calls intermittently fail and return an HTTP 429 rate limit exceeded error.</p><p>You need to handle throttling to reduce call failures and improve reliability under load. The solution must remain within the service and model limits.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you do?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Create a new thread and retry the calls immediately."},{"k":"B","html":"Reduce the number of registered tools."},{"k":"C","html":"Implement a retry policy that uses exponential backoff and jitter."},{"k":"D","html":"Spit uploaded content into smaller files."}],"answer":"C","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"C","p":100,"n":2}],"page":4,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/16deed2e6387fdbad577b2f669648b431000667/","comments":[{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":2,"text":"The standard, within-limits way to handle HTTP 429 is exponential backoff with jitter to spread retries. Immediate retry on a new thread (A) worsens throttling; reducing tools (B) and splitting files (D) do not address rate limits.","pick":"C"}]},{"n":40,"id":1000668,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains an agent.</p><p>You use a GitHub Actions workflow for CI/CD.</p><p>You need to configure the workflow to automatically evaluate the agent when a pull request (PR) is created and prevent branches from merging if the evaluation results do NOT meet the defined thresholds.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>How should you configure the workflow?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image31.png\" alt=\"image31\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image32.png\" alt=\"image32\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":4,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/7cd97860a050b2fd72037faf815011c41000668/","comments":[{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":1,"text":"GitHub Actions should authenticate to Azure with the Azure Login action using OIDC (federated credentials), avoiding stored secrets/PATs and managed identity isn't used for GitHub-hosted runners this way. To block merges when evaluation thresholds are not met, the workflow step must Fail (which fails the check and prevents merge); 'send an alert' or 'lock the branch' do not gate the PR check."}]},{"n":41,"id":1000669,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains an agent. The agent generates summaries from retrieved policy documents.</p><p>Users report that some responses omit required regulatory clauses, even when the clauses are present in the retrieved content.</p><p>You need to improve response completeness.</p><div class=\"solution\"><span>Proposed solution</span>You increase the value of the max_tokens parameter.</div><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Does this meet the goal?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Yes"},{"k":"B","html":"No"}],"answer":"B","type":"yesno","votes":[{"a":"A","p":22,"n":2},{"a":"B","p":78,"n":7}],"page":5,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/17cea198a2f38baf17a2c2f5fd8b84be1000669/","comments":[{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":4,"text":"Clauses are present in the retrieved content but omitted from the summary, so the problem is selection/faithfulness, not output length truncation. Increasing max_tokens does not force inclusion of the missing clauses, so it does not meet the goal.","pick":"B"},{"user":"Mattt","date":"2026-07-23","up":3,"text":"B. No.\nIncreasing max_tokens only allows a longer response; it does not ensure that required clauses are included. The issue is response completeness, not output truncation.","pick":"B"},{"user":"8ac3742","date":"2026-10-04","up":1,"text":"To ensure completeness for regulatory clauses, you should update the agent's system instructions (prompt engineering), enforce a structured output schema, or add a pre-response evaluation/retry loop in the application logic","pick":"B"},{"user":"Vasent","date":"2026-07-15","up":1,"text":"As Richard already explained, Increasing max_tokens does not force inclusion of the missing clauses (which is already present), so it does not meet the goal.","pick":"A"},{"user":"cloudera","date":"2026-06-10","up":1,"text":"Increasing max_tokens can help improve response completeness because it gives the model more output budget to include all required regulatory clauses.","pick":"A","replies":[{"user":"fc2fb70","date":"2026-10-11","up":1,"text":"cloudera is Wrong...."},{"user":"AIBoss","date":"2026-09-06","up":1,"text":"It says increase max_token but how much to increase? Suppose, previous max_token was 1000 , then increased to 1500 token. If response is 2000 tokens, then result is still truncated."}]}],"series":true},{"n":42,"id":1000670,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains an agent. The agent generates summaries from retrieved policy documents.</p><p>Users report that some responses omit required regulatory clauses, even when the clauses are present in the retrieved content.</p><p>You need to improve response completeness.</p><div class=\"solution\"><span>Proposed solution</span>You add a reflection pass that regenerates the response if the required clauses are missing.</div><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Does this meet the goal?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Yes"},{"k":"B","html":"No"}],"answer":"A","type":"yesno","votes":[{"a":"A","p":100,"n":4}],"page":5,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/b4287a3a41f94e3987a6223cfb6ce5b31000670/","comments":[{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":2,"text":"A reflection pass that regenerates the response when required clauses are missing directly enforces completeness by re-checking and re-prompting until the clauses appear. This meets the goal.","pick":"A"},{"user":"8ac3742","date":"2026-10-04","up":1,"text":"reflection pass:\n1.Send the retrieved documents and the draft summary to a cheaper model with below prompt:\nYou are a compliance reviewer. Inspect the generated summary against the source text.\nCheck if any regulatory, compliance, or mandatory policy clauses present in the\nsource documents were omitted from the summary.\nReturn JSON:\n{\n\"is_complete\": true | false,\n\"missing_clauses\": [\"list of omitted clauses\"],\n\"critique\": \"guidance on what needs to be added\"\n}\n2.If is_complete is false, the application issues a second call to the generator model:\n\"Your previous draft omitted: {missing_clauses}. Please regenerate the summary to ensure these required regulatory clauses are included.\"","pick":"A"},{"user":"Shaharaz","date":"2026-10-03","up":1,"text":"A reflection pass reviews the initial response against defined requirements, such as whether all mandatory regulatory clauses from the retrieved context are included.","pick":"A"},{"user":"cloudera","date":"2026-06-11","up":1,"text":"A. Yes Reflection Pass is the correct.","pick":"A"}],"series":true},{"n":43,"id":1000671,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains an agent. The agent generates summaries from retrieved policy documents.</p><p>Users report that some responses omit required regulatory clauses, even when the clauses are present in the retrieved content.</p><p>You need to improve response completeness.</p><div class=\"solution\"><span>Proposed solution</span>You increase the value of the temperature parameter.</div><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Does this meet the goal?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Yes"},{"k":"B","html":"No"}],"answer":"B","type":"yesno","votes":[{"a":"B","p":100,"n":2}],"page":5,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/74961c78081a2b9d59905454e95301f41000671/","comments":[{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":2,"text":"Raising temperature increases randomness/creativity; it does not make the model reliably include required regulatory clauses and can make omissions worse. It does not meet the goal.","pick":"B"}],"series":true},{"n":44,"id":1000672,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains an agent. The agent generates summaries from retrieved policy documents.</p><p>Users report that some responses omit required regulatory clauses, even when the clauses are present in the retrieved content.</p><p>You need to improve response completeness.</p><div class=\"solution\"><span>Proposed solution</span>You run an evaluation flow that scores responses for completeness and blocks responses that fall below a defined threshold.</div><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Does this meet the goal?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Yes"},{"k":"B","html":"No"}],"answer":"B","type":"yesno","votes":[{"a":"A","p":23,"n":3},{"a":"B","p":77,"n":10}],"page":5,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/1f2d485a2d4caa8be8b71157e9ffa52a1000672/","comments":[{"user":"NVIT2026","date":"2026-07-27","up":4,"text":"Simply blocking incomplete responses prevents poor output from reaching the user, but it does not fix, improve, or regenerate the response to make it complete. It results in a failed request or error message rather than delivering a complete summary containing the required regulatory clauses.","pick":"B"},{"user":"cloudera","date":"2026-06-11","up":4,"text":"While implementing an evaluation flow to score responses is an excellent practice for monitoring, but it does not actually improve the completeness of the generated summaries.","pick":"B"},{"user":"Mattt","date":"2026-07-23","up":3,"text":"B. No. The evaluation flow only detects and blocks incomplete responses; it does not regenerate them or add the missing clauses.","pick":"B"},{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":2,"text":"Running an evaluation flow that scores completeness and blocks sub-threshold responses enforces the completeness requirement before delivery, so it meets the goal.","pick":"A"},{"user":"38df6fe","date":"2026-08-16","up":1,"text":"Running an evaluation flow that scores responses for completeness and blocks/gates those below a defined threshold directly addresses the problem: responses omitting required regulatory clauses even when present in the retrieved content.","pick":"A"}],"series":true},{"n":45,"id":1000673,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You are creating an image-editing workflow in a Microsoft Foundry project.</p><p>The workflow must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Ensure that background objects can be removed by applying a mask-based inpainting edit.</li><li>Preserve the original lighting and style of the edited images.</li><li>Use the built-in image editing controls, NOT a custom model.</li></ul><p>You need to ensure that image edits apply exclusively inside the masked area.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>How should you configure the workflow?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Set generation mode to image_variation and provide the original image as a reference."},{"k":"B","html":"Enable text_to_image mode and a prompt describing the desired background removal."},{"k":"C","html":"Enable image_to_image mode and a high-strength value to regenerate the full image based on the prompt."},{"k":"D","html":"Enable mask_inpainting and supply both the input image and a mask indicating which part of the image to modify."}],"answer":"D","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"D","p":100,"n":1}],"page":5,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/f33998743083d51da571e50d05470ece1000673/","comments":[{"user":"8ac3742","date":"2026-10-04","up":1,"text":"In Microsoft Foundry / Azure AI, \"image-edit\" is not an agent. It is a inference workflow mode provided by diffusion models such as Stable Diffusion / FLUX models deployed through Foundry Model Catalog).\nWhen you invoke image models in Foundry workflows, the model supports different task modes:\ntext_to_image (Option B): Generates a brand-new image completely from scratch based on a textual prompt. It cannot edit an existing image in place.\nimage_variation (Option A): Takes an existing image and generates diverse stylistic variants of the whole picture. It does not allow targeted object removal.\nimage_to_image (Option C): Modifies the whole image globally according to a prompt and a strength parameter. Even with high or low strength, it evaluates and alters pixels across the entire frame, failing the requirement that edits apply exclusively inside the target area.\nmask_inpainting (Option D): The dedicated editing mode where the API accepts image + mask + prompt. The model regenerates only the masked pixels and blends them seamlessly into the surrounding context.\nBelow is one sample image workflow\n# Requirement: Input image and mask must be square PNGs with alpha channel\n# The mask transparent area indicates where the model should edit.\ndef run_mask_inpainting(original_png_path: str, mask_png_path: str):\nprint(\"Performing mask-based inpainting...\")\nwith open(original_png_path, \"rb\") as image_file, open(mask_png_path, \"rb\") as mask_file:\nedit_response = client.images.edit(\nmodel=\"dall-e-2\", # Deployment supporting mask-based edits\nimage=image_file,\nmask=mask_file,\nprompt=\"Seamless natural meadow background, matching the original grass and lighting perfectly\",\nn=1,\nsize=\"1024x1024\",\n)\nedited_url = edit_response.data[0].url\nprint(f\"Edited Image URL: {edited_url}\")\nreturn edited_url","pick":"D"},{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":1,"text":"Editing only inside a masked region while preserving the rest is exactly mask-based inpainting, which needs the input image plus a mask. image_variation (A) and text_to_image (B) regenerate broadly; high-strength image_to_image (C) regenerates the whole image, not just the masked area.","pick":"D"}]},{"n":46,"id":1000674,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that generates product marketing images from text prompts.</p><p>After publishing several images, the legal team at your company identifies a competitor’s logo on a sign in the background of an image.</p><p>You need to remove only the logo, while preserving the rest of the image.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you do?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Apply a mask-based inpainting edit to the part of the image that contains the logo."},{"k":"B","html":"Increase the prompt guidance strength."},{"k":"C","html":"Modify the original prompt to exclude brand names."},{"k":"D","html":"Rerun the prompt by using a different random seed."}],"answer":"A","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"A","p":100,"n":2}],"page":5,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/4e4ebf5dca426fd0f7f3c3a75b9c9c631000674/","comments":[{"user":"Shaharaz","date":"2026-10-03","up":1,"text":"With mask-based inpainting, you create a mask covering only the competitor’s logo.","pick":"A"},{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":1,"text":"To remove only the logo while keeping the rest intact, mask the logo region and inpaint. Increasing guidance (B), editing the prompt (C), or changing the seed (D) regenerate or re-roll the whole image and do not surgically remove one element.","pick":"A"}]},{"n":47,"id":1000675,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains an agent.</p><p>The agent ingests scanned PDF vendor invoices that contain tables and embedded QR codes.</p><p>The agent must preserve the PDF layout in the extracted output to ensure that downstream processing can reference sections and tables.</p><p>You plan to call Azure Content Understanding in Foundry Tools.</p><p>You need to extract content and layout elements and detect QR codes without requiring a language model deployment.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which built-in analyzer should you use?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"prebuilt-documentFieldSchema"},{"k":"B","html":"prebuilt-read"},{"k":"C","html":"prebuilt-documentSearch"},{"k":"D","html":"prebuilt-layout"}],"answer":"D","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"D","p":100,"n":1}],"page":5,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/c8c9893a24416d934a20a0002b4fff5a1000675/","comments":[{"user":"8ac3742","date":"2026-10-04","up":1,"text":"A. prebuilt-documentFieldSchema: This analyzer is used to discover or propose structured field definitions for unknown document schemas; it does not perform raw layout preservation.\nB. prebuilt-read: Provides basic optical character recognition (OCR) and text lines, but it strips away complex document layout hierarchy and does not reconstruct structured tables.\nC. prebuilt-documentSearch: A RAG-optimized analyzer intended to generate markdown chunks and semantic embeddings/descriptions for downstream search, typically utilizing language model processing\nD. prebuilt-layout:\n(1)Preserve PDF Layout & Tables: extract structure, paragraphs, reading order, and complex tables.\n(2)QR Codes & Barcodes\n(3)No Language Model Required","pick":"D"},{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":1,"text":"prebuilt-layout extracts content and layout elements (tables, structure) and detects barcodes/QR codes without needing a model deployment. prebuilt-read (B) does OCR text only (no layout/tables); documentFieldSchema (A) and documentSearch (C) are not the layout/QR extractor.","pick":"D"}]},{"n":48,"id":1000676,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains an agent and an image generation model deployment.</p><p>The agent generates original images from user-supplied product photos.</p><p>You need to ensure that the generated images maintain the product identity and visual characteristics of the provided photo.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you do?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Set the input_fidelity parameter to high."},{"k":"B","html":"Apply a groundedness detection filter."},{"k":"C","html":"Include a prompt and input image in the request."},{"k":"D","html":"Decrease the value of the temperature parameter."}],"answer":"A","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"A","p":100,"n":1}],"page":5,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/cd74c66f76a98608d451f793d9d8530f1000676/","comments":[{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":1,"text":"Maintaining the product's identity and visual characteristics from a supplied photo is what high input_fidelity controls in image editing","pick":"A"}]},{"n":49,"id":1000677,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains an agent.</p><p>The agent accepts user-uploaded screenshots and uses a multimodal chat model.</p><p>Some screenshots contain potentially malicious embedded text.</p><p>You need to prevent a prompt injection attack and ensure that third-party content is treated as lower trust.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>How should you configure prompt shields for document attacks?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image33.png\" alt=\"image33\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image34.png\" alt=\"image34\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":5,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/489b31e58340f52269a3fb79fc34d5f01000677/","comments":[{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":3,"text":"To prevent prompt injection from document/image-embedded text, set the document-attack shield action to Block. Spotlighting is the Prompt Shields capability that marks third-party content as lower trust, directly satisfying 'treat third-party content as lower trust.' A custom blocklist or OCR pre-step do not provide the provenance/trust separation."}]},{"n":50,"id":1000678,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You are deploying a support agent that enables users to upload photos.</p><p>You need to automatically classify uploaded images for harmful content. The solution must block content based on severity levels.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you do?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Apply keyword scanning to optical character recognition (OCR) output by using Azure Vision in Foundry Tools."},{"k":"B","html":"Enable prompt shields."},{"k":"C","html":"Use blocklists."},{"k":"D","html":"Implement image moderation."}],"answer":"D","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"D","p":100,"n":6}],"page":5,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/fbdd149787af34e828fb1c948c359b311000678/","comments":[{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":5,"text":"Image moderation classifies images into harm categories with severity levels and can block above a threshold. OCR keyword scanning (A) only handles embedded text; prompt shields (B) target injection; blocklists (C) match terms, not visual harm severity.","pick":"D"},{"user":"cloudera","date":"2026-06-10","up":2,"text":"I thought we were supposed to leave the discussion section empty when the answer is already correct. Aren't to discuss only when the question requires correction or further clarification.\n\nIt’s frustrating to see someone commenting on every single answer just to restate what’s already been said. It adds noise rather than value. Please avoid doing that — it’s unnecessary and distracting.","pick":"D","replies":[{"user":"038c182","date":"2026-10-04","up":2,"text":"youre mad someone went through and explained / justified the answers? lol"},{"user":"profitchannel","date":"2026-06-12","up":11,"text":"the comments are really helpful and provide background, you see from the answer match already when the answer ist correct!","top":true}]}]},{"n":51,"id":1000679,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have an app named App1 that uses a Microsoft Foundry multimodal model deployment.</p><p>App1 runs optical character recognition (OCR) on uploaded images and appends the OCR output to the prompt as additional context.</p><p>Some uploaded images contain embedded text.</p><p>You need to prevent potentially malicious instructions from being processed by the model.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you use?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"image moderation"},{"k":"B","html":"prompt shields for documents"},{"k":"C","html":"protected material text"},{"k":"D","html":"prompt shields for user prompts"}],"answer":"B","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"B","p":100,"n":1}],"page":6,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/f7436950c77f89ab0a605fa2a5bc156e1000679/","comments":[{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":2,"text":"OCR text appended to the prompt is third-party/document content, so Prompt Shields for Documents is the control that detects embedded malicious instructions. Image moderation (A) checks visual harm not instructions; protected material (C) is copyright; prompt shields for user prompts (D) target direct user jailbreaks.","pick":"B"}]},{"n":52,"id":1000680,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains an agent.</p><p>You need to process mixed-format documents that contain scanned text, tables, and multicolumn layouts. The extracted content must preserve the document structure and be converted into the Markdown format for downstream reasoning.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you configure first?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"an Azure Language in Foundry Tools text analysis model deployment"},{"k":"B","html":"a generative chat completion request"},{"k":"C","html":"an Azure OpenAI Responses API call that uses a multimodal model"},{"k":"D","html":"an Azure Content Understanding in Foundry Tools analyzer"}],"answer":"D","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"D","p":100,"n":2}],"page":6,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/e0f97fc519afb8af75f2a5327979b9161000680/","comments":[{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":3,"text":"Content Understanding converts mixed-format documents (scanned text, tables, multicolumn) into structured Markdown for downstream reasoning, and Microsoft recommends it as the starting point for file processing. A Language text model (A), a chat completion (B), or a multimodal Responses call (C) do not provide structure-preserving Markdown extraction as a first step.","pick":"D"}]},{"n":53,"id":1000681,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have an application that processes scanned PDF invoices. The invoices have varied layouts and include multipage tables.</p><p>You have a pipeline that uses optical character recognition (OCR) and extracts totals and invoice numbers. The results are often incorrect because the document structure is ignored.</p><p>You need to implement a solution that provides OCR, layout analysis, and template-generalizing field extraction. The solution must NOT require training a custom model. The solution must minimize administrative effort.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you include in the solution?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Azure Language in Foundry Tools"},{"k":"B","html":"Azure Content Understanding in Foundry Tools"},{"k":"C","html":"an Azure Machine Learning model"}],"answer":"B","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"B","p":100,"n":4}],"page":6,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/68825075fb38a6ee30ffdd97dee118de1000681/","comments":[{"user":"2b61a0f","date":"2026-09-29","up":5,"text":"Some of us want to know also the details, not just the correct answer, I like that RICHARDALEX007 explains the answers."},{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":5,"text":"Content Understanding provides OCR, layout analysis, and template-generalizing field extraction without training a custom model and with minimal admin effort. Language (A) is text analytics, and an Azure ML model (C) requires building/training.","pick":"B","replies":[{"user":"cloudera","date":"2026-06-10","up":1,"text":"The answer is already correct. Why are you plastering your comments everywhere. Seriously, stop it — full stop.","replies":[{"user":"2b61a0f","date":"2026-09-29","up":5,"text":"Some of us want to know also the details, not just the correct answer, I like that RICHARDALEX007 explains the answers."}]}]}]},{"n":54,"id":1000682,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains an agent.</p><p>The agent uses a knowledge source built from documents stored in Azure Blob Storage. The documents include digitally scanned PDFs that contain multipage tables.</p><p>You have an ingestion job that extracts only plain text, causing loss of table structure, headings, and page-number metadata.</p><p>Users frequently ask questions that require the retrieval of specific table rows across the pages.</p><p>You need to configure an ingestion job for a Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) pipeline that performs optical character recognition (OCR) on scanned PDFs, preserves tables and headings as structure-aware chunks, and stores page-number metadata with each chunk.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>How should you configure the ingestion job?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Use advanced data parsing to reingest the documents."},{"k":"B","html":"Use OCR and page-level chunking."},{"k":"C","html":"Use page-level OCR extraction and store each page as a single chunk."},{"k":"D","html":"Use basic parsing and fixed-size chunking."}],"answer":"A","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"A","p":100,"n":6}],"page":6,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/67f274b84e4c3fbc1b357e12eb8f37491000682/","comments":[{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":4,"text":"Preserving tables/headings as structure-aware chunks with OCR and page-number metadata is what advanced/structure-aware data parsing provides; plain OCR with page-level chunking (B, C) stores whole pages and loses row-level table structure, and basic fixed-size chunking (D) ignores structure","pick":"A","replies":[{"user":"cloudera","date":"2026-06-10","up":1,"text":"Well done, you finally got it right.\nBTW, if I were you, I’d seriously mask my username. Just saying."}]},{"user":"8ac3742","date":"2026-10-04","up":2,"text":"In Foundry AI Search, you configure the parsing strategy:\nBasic parsing: Extracts only unstructured raw text from files and applies standard fixed-size chunking, discarding tables, formatting, headers, and visual layout.\nAdvanced data parsing (Option A): Automatically leverages the Azure AI Document Intelligence layout model during ingestion:\nRuns OCR on scanned images and PDFs.\nUnderstands layout hierarchy (headings, titles, sections).\nExtracts multipage tables into structured representations (Markdown/HTML).\nProduces structure-aware chunks while attaching page-number metadata to each chunk.","pick":"A"},{"user":"Srikantha","date":"2026-08-30","up":2,"text":"Advanced data parsing: In Microsoft Foundry (Azure AI Studio), the \"advanced\" data parsing option utilizes Azure AI Document Intelligence (specifically the Layout model). This capability is explicitly designed to perform Optical Character Recognition (OCR) while preserving complex document structures such as tables (even those spanning multiple pages), headings, and reading order. It outputs the data into structure-aware chunks (often formatted as Markdown) and automatically tags those chunks with metadata, including page numbers. This perfectly matches the requirement for accurate RAG retrieval of specific table rows","pick":"A"},{"user":"e886835","date":"2026-07-09","up":1,"text":"Not B because this handles the scanning part, blindly cutting chunks at strict page boundaries will slice multipage tables in half incorrectly, destroying row context that spans across page breaks","pick":"A"}]},{"n":55,"id":1000683,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains an agent.</p><p>The agent uses Azure AI Search as the retriever.</p><p>You plan to ingest PDF into an Azure AI Search index to ensure that the agent can ground responses in texts in both documents and embedded images.</p><p>Users require citations that link to the source files.</p><p>You need to ensure that during indexing, the images are extracted into a structure that can be used as input for the built-in optical character recognition (OCR) skill.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which indexing approach should you use?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"an indexer to extract image data into a normalized_images collection"},{"k":"B","html":"a Shaper skill to restructure the OCR input"},{"k":"C","html":"a skillset to run the OCR skill directly against the content field of the index"},{"k":"D","html":"the outputFieldMappings parameter to write image data to a searchable field"}],"answer":"A","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"A","p":100,"n":2}],"page":6,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/9320a1772d6b57c99eb2bca47d181ab91000683/","comments":[{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":2,"text":"To feed embedded images to the built-in OCR skill, the indexer must extract images into the normalized_images collection (the documented input for the OCR skill). A Shaper skill (B) restructures data, running OCR on the content field (C) is wrong because OCR needs image input, and outputFieldMappings (D) writes results, not image extraction.","pick":"A"}]},{"n":56,"id":1000684,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You need to recommend an invoice review solution that resolves the issue reported by the finance department.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you include in the recommendation?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"chat completions"},{"k":"B","html":"Azure Document Intelligence in Foundry Tools"},{"k":"C","html":"Azure Content Understanding in Foundry Tools"},{"k":"D","html":"Image Analysis"}],"answer":"C","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"C","p":100,"n":6}],"page":6,"case":"d421f5cb15","thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/896980394c95aa22c06112dd89bb1be91000684/","comments":[{"user":"cloudera","date":"2026-06-10","up":3,"text":"B attempting, but C is the correct answer. Why? The question is not only asking for invoice field extraction. The finance requirement is closer to “Understand invoice content and layout, then compare/validate it against contract terms.” This needs invoice processing plus contract/document reasoning or validation and for that Microsoft’s Content Understanding is the correct answer. For more visit https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/ai-services/document-intelligence/overview?view=doc-intel-4.0.0\n\nTo summarise:\nExtract fields from invoices is B - Azure Document Intelligence. To review invoices against contract layout, text and reasoning is C - Azure Content Understanding which is the answer for this question.","pick":"C"},{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":3,"text":"The finance requirement is to evaluate both visual layout and textual content of varied-layout invoices with tables and logos and verify against contract terms - Content Understanding handles multimodal layout+text and reasoning. Document Intelligence (B) extracts fields but the multimodal layout-plus-reasoning framing favors Content Understanding; chat completions (A) and Image Analysis (D) do not do document field/layout extraction","pick":"C"}]},{"n":57,"id":1000685,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains an agent.</p><p>The knowledge source for the agent is a set of scanned PDF troubleshooting guides stored in Azure Blob Storage. The guide pages contain two-column layouts and tables.</p><p>You use Azure Content Understanding in Foundry Tools to process the PDFs.</p><p>You plan to ingest the processed content into an index for Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) and store extracted fields for downstream automation.</p><p>Stakeholders must be able to verify where each extracted field value came from in the original PDF and route low-reliability extractions for manual review.</p><p>You need to ensure that the Content Understanding document analyzer output includes a per-field confidence score and source grounding to locations within the source document.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you do?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Set enableSegment to true."},{"k":"B","html":"Provide labeled samples."},{"k":"C","html":"Enable estimateFieldSourceAndConfidence."},{"k":"D","html":"Configure the analyzer to use generative extraction for all fields."}],"answer":"C","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"C","p":100,"n":3}],"page":6,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/2c8700285d772c602910d756db7d62ee1000685/","comments":[{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":4,"text":"estimateFieldSourceAndConfidence makes the Content Understanding analyzer return a per-field confidence score plus source grounding (page/bounding box) so values can be verified and low-confidence ones routed to review. enableSegment (A), labeled samples (B), and generative extraction (D) do not produce per-field confidence+grounding.","pick":"C"}]},{"n":58,"id":1000686,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You are building a speech processing solution in Microsoft Foundry for a customer support platform.</p><p>The platform will transcribe live phone calls, so that supervisors at your company can view call transcripts and detect issues while the calls are in progress. The call audio will arrive as a continuous stream from the telephony system.</p><p>You need to ensure that the call transcripts appear within only a few seconds of the audio stream.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you do?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Use text to speech by using a custom neural voice."},{"k":"B","html":"Use speech translation to generate the transcripts into multiple languages."},{"k":"C","html":"Run a batch transcription job on recorded audio files."},{"k":"D","html":"Use real-time speech to text to process streaming audio input."}],"answer":"D","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"D","p":100,"n":1}],"page":6,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/8fbe90e2ab3e8c6d9883db823910626a1000686/","comments":[{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":1,"text":"Transcripts within seconds of a continuous live stream require real-time speech to text. Batch transcription (C) is for recorded files (high latency); custom neural voice TTS (A) generates speech; speech translation (B) translates, neither giving low-latency live transcription.","pick":"D"}]},{"n":59,"id":1000687,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You are creating an agent workflow in a Microsoft Foundry project to support natural voice interactions.</p><p>The agent must receive continuous audio input, convert the input into text for reasoning, and then return spoken responses to a user. The workflow must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Support turn-taking dynamics, where the agent begins to generate the speech output before the user finishes speaking.</li><li>Operate with low latency to maintain conversational experience.</li></ul><p>You need to enable both speech to text and text to speech in a real-time agent interaction.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you do?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Use batch transcription to convert the audio input and return text responses from the agent."},{"k":"B","html":"Use real-time speech to text for incoming audio and text to speech for agent responses."},{"k":"C","html":"Use an embeddings model to encode the audio, and then decode the audio into text and speech."},{"k":"D","html":"Use speech translation to convert the audio into another language and return the translated text."}],"answer":"B","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"B","p":100,"n":1}],"page":6,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/f34aa6f507be8edfd36b5b6630a053fd1000687/","comments":[{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":2,"text":"A low-latency voice agent with turn-taking needs real-time STT on input and TTS on output. Batch transcription (A) is high-latency; embeddings (C) do not transcribe/synthesize; speech translation (D) changes language rather than enabling spoken responses.","pick":"B"}]},{"n":60,"id":1000688,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have an application named App1 that uses Azure Speech in Foundry Tools to transcribe live calls.</p><p>Transcript segments often contain both English and Spanish. App1 sends each segment to Azure Translator in Foundry Tools to translate to another language.</p><p>Sometimes, mixed-language segments result in incomplete or incorrect translations.</p><p>You need to reduce translation errors. The solution must ensure that the entire transcript is translated successfully.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you do before sending the segments to Translator?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Use document translation to translate the entire transcript as a single document."},{"k":"B","html":"Split the mixed-language segments into single-language segments and translate each segment separately."},{"k":"C","html":"Enable automatic language detection for the translation request."},{"k":"D","html":"Specify English as the source language in the translation request for all the segments."}],"answer":"B","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"B","p":100,"n":1}],"page":6,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/72109e527ab36cc07827ec2ebddb0e141000688/","comments":[{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":1,"text":"Translator works best per source language; splitting mixed English/Spanish segments into single-language pieces and translating each gives complete, correct results. Document translation (A) and auto-detect (C) still mis-handle a single mixed segment; forcing English as source (D) mistranslates the Spanish parts.","pick":"B"}]},{"n":61,"id":1000689,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You need to configure an indexing pipeline for Agent1 to retrieve the relevant product information in storage1. The solution must meet the technical requirement.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which two built-in skills should you use?</strong> Each correct answer presents part of the solution.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Azure OpenAI Embedding"},{"k":"B","html":"Entity Recognition"},{"k":"C","html":"Text Split"},{"k":"D","html":"Merge"},{"k":"E","html":"Language Detection"},{"k":"F","html":"key phrase extraction"}],"answer":"AC","type":"multi","votes":[{"a":"AC","p":100,"n":3}],"page":7,"case":"d421f5cb15","thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/75787095a2c68fe0f2afa2293789cc4d1000689/","comments":[{"user":"8ac3742","date":"2026-10-05","up":2,"text":"Let's look directly at the requirement in the case study:\"The product sheets must be processed by using an indexing pipeline that enables semantic and vector search, so that Agent1 can retrieve the relevant product information.\nIn Azure AI Search / Foundry indexing pipelines, generating vector embeddings from unstructured text documents (like the product sheets in storage1) requires two fundamental, coupled built-in skills:\n(1)Text Split (#Microsoft.Skills.Text.SplitSkill):Documents like product detail sheets in PDF format are typically multi-page and exceed model token limits.Before text can be vectorized, it must be chunked into semantically meaningful segments (pages, paragraphs, or fixed token lengths).\n(2)Azure OpenAI Embedding (#Microsoft.Skills.Text.AzureOpenAIEmbeddingSkill):Takes the individual text chunks output by the Text Split skill and generates the high-dimensional numerical vectors (embeddings) needed to populate the search index.This is what directly enables vector search.Together, Text Split then Azure OpenAI Embedding is the standard, foundational enrichment pipeline for vector search indexing in Azure.\nThe word \"embedding\" comes directly from mathematics (topology and geometry): discrete, symbolic human language is being embedded into a continuous, geometric vector space.\n{\"dog\"} = [1, 0, 0, 0}\n{\"cat\"} = [0, 1, 0, 0}\n{\"apple\"} = [0, 0, 1, 0}","pick":"AC"},{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":2,"text":"For an indexing pipeline enabling semantic/vector search over PDFs, Text Split chunks the documents and Azure OpenAI Embedding generates the vectors for vector search. Entity Recognition (B), Merge (D), Language Detection (E), and key phrase extraction (F) are not required to produce a vector index.","pick":"AC"}]},{"n":62,"id":1000690,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You need to recommend a solution to support the planned changes and technical requirements for Agent1 to use the product information stored in storage1.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you include in the recommendation?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Azure Translator in Foundry Tools"},{"k":"B","html":"Grounding with Bing Search"},{"k":"C","html":"Azure AI Search"},{"k":"D","html":"Azure Document intelligence in Foundry Tools"}],"answer":"C","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"C","p":100,"n":3}],"page":7,"case":"d421f5cb15","thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/bf12dc63c75244cdd209b5515d4af7bf1000690/","comments":[{"user":"8ac3742","date":"2026-10-05","up":2,"text":"Notice the exact wording of the question:\n\"You need to recommend a solution to support the planned changes and technical requirements for Agent1 to use the product information stored in storage1.\"\nThe Trap: You are thinking about the vendor invoices (which would use Document Intelligence / Content Understanding for layouts and tables).\nThe Actual Subject: The question is specifically asking about Agent1 retrieving the product information in storage1, not processing vendor invoices.\nThe core service that provides the indexing pipeline, vector search, and semantic search over documents stored in Azure Blob Storage to ground an agent via RAG is Azure AI Search.","pick":"C"},{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":2,"text":"The technical requirement is an indexing pipeline with semantic and vector search so the agent can retrieve product info - that is Azure AI Search. Translator (A) and Bing grounding (B) do not index private PDFs; Document Intelligence (D) extracts content but is not the retrieval/index layer.","pick":"C"}]},{"n":63,"id":1000691,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project named Project1.</p><p>Project1 contains an application that processes PDF vendor invoices.</p><p>You need to configure Azure Document Intelligence in Foundry Tools to generate a Markdown output that preserves the sections and table structure of the PDFs. The solution must minimize development effort.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you do?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Configure output=figures when you analyze the PDF."},{"k":"B","html":"Configure content=markdown when you analyze the document."},{"k":"C","html":"Increase the confidence threshold."},{"k":"D","html":"Set the output_content_format=ContentFormat.MARKDOWN value."}],"answer":"D","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"D","p":100,"n":2}],"page":7,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/a3c959c798c05173c46b0fbb4faeab751000691/","comments":[{"user":"Alvarogc","date":"2026-08-22","up":2,"text":"According to Microsoft Learn, the layout API can output the extracted text in Markdown format by using the outputContentFormat=markdown to specify the output format in Markdown. The Markdown content is then output as part of the content section.\n\nRefference: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/ai-services/document-intelligence/prebuilt/layout","pick":"D"}]},{"n":64,"id":1000692,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that ingests scanned PDF invoices stored in Azure Blob Storage. Each invoice contains printed fine items and has a table-based layout.</p><p>Extracted results are stored as structured JSON and used as grounding data for an agent in a Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) solution.</p><p>You need to create a single analyzer that meets the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Extracts the invoice number, invoice date, vendor name, and total amount across varying templates</li><li>Returns confidence scores so that results with confidence below 0.80 can be routed for supervisor review</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you use?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"a Foundry agent that has groundedness guardrails enabled to extract invoice fields and confidence scores"},{"k":"B","html":"a custom Azure Content Understanding in Foundry Tools analyzer that defines the required fields as the extracted fields and the returned confidence scores for routing"},{"k":"C","html":"the Azure Content Understanding in Foundry Tools prebuilt-layout analyzer"},{"k":"D","html":"the Azure Content Understanding in Foundry Tools prebuilt-documentSearch analyzer and search.score from the Azure AI Search results for routing"}],"answer":"B","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"B","p":100,"n":1}],"page":7,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/300408113207d9735589b936c7ca84721000692/","comments":[{"user":"RICHARDALEX007","date":"2026-06-10","up":1,"text":"Extracting specific fields across varying templates AND returning confidence scores for sub-0.80 routing is a custom Content Understanding analyzer with estimateFieldSourceAndConfidence. prebuilt-layout (C) lacks the custom fields; documentSearch + search.score (D) is search relevance, not extraction confidence; a groundedness-guardrail agent (A) does not produce structured field confidence.","pick":"B"}]},{"n":65,"id":1000693,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that uses Azure AI Search to ground an agent in internal documentation.</p><p>After a recent content update, users report that the agent’s answers have become less accurate.</p><p>You need to identify whether the retrieved content is negatively influencing the model’s generated responses.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which observability signal should you review?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"indexer status and failure history"},{"k":"B","html":"latency breakdown traces"},{"k":"C","html":"prediction drift metrics"},{"k":"D","html":"groundedness evaluation metrics"}],"answer":"D","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"D","p":100,"n":1}],"page":7,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/71ddfe8d70b84f6da1c4b1865c61a34b1000693/","comments":[{"user":"Alvarogc","date":"2026-08-22","up":1,"text":"As defined by Microsoft Learn, Groundedness measures how grounded the response is in the retrieved context. It returns a score from 1–5 using a model-based judgment. This way you can evaluate if retrieved documents are influencing the model's generated responses.\n\nRefference: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/foundry/concepts/built-in-evaluators","pick":"D"}]},{"n":66,"id":1009423,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You need to ensure that the marketing department can generate videos by using the model deployed to Project2.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>How should you complete the Python code?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image35.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image36.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":7,"case":"d421f5cb15","thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/a5626d82b502a9c83dda2e1bacced4bc1009423/","comments":[{"user":"8ac3742","date":"2026-10-05","up":1,"text":"create and retrieve\n\nGenerating video is a long-running, asynchronous operation.\nclient.videos.create(...) initiates the video generation job and immediately returns an initial job object containing an id and an initial status (e.g., \"queued\" or \"processing\").\nthen retrieve\nwhile video.status not in [\"completed\", \"failed\", \"cancelled\"]:\ntime.sleep(20)\nvideo = client.videos.retrieve(video.id)\nWhy not list? list() takes no ID and returns a paginated list of all video generation jobs."}]},{"n":67,"id":1009424,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You need to configure personalized user interactions for Agent1. The solution must meet the business requirements.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you include in the solution?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"knowledge"},{"k":"B","html":"memory"},{"k":"C","html":"guardrails"},{"k":"D","html":"tools"}],"answer":"B","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"B","p":100,"n":1}],"page":7,"case":"d421f5cb15","thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/0b45a022ad354877c3fd832223f90a431009424/","comments":[{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-10","up":1,"text":"Memory should be included to provide personalized interactions for Agent1.\n\nThe business requirement states that Agent1 must retain conversation context and recall relevant information from previous interactions. This is exactly what agent memory is designed to provide.\n\nA. Knowledge ❌ → Provides external information, such as product details from the product sheets.\nB. Memory ✅ → Retains relevant information and conversation context across interactions.\nC. Guardrails ❌ → Restrict or control the agent's behavior and content.\nD. Tools ❌ → Allow the agent to perform actions or interact with external services.\nFinal Answer: B. Memory","pick":"B"}],"variants":[146]},{"n":68,"id":1009425,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You need to ensure that Agent1Dev Team can access Agent1. The solution must meet the security and compliance requirements.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>How should you complete the Python code?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image37.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image38.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":7,"case":"d421f5cb15","thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/f5de0549ed77371241fa20b227e9cda41009425/","comments":[{"user":"8ac3742","date":"2026-10-05","up":1,"text":"(1) DefaultAzureCredential\nSecurity & Compliance Requirement:\n\"API keys must NOT be used to access Foundry-deployed models.\"\n\"The developers at Contoso must authenticate to Microsoft Foundry resources by using Microsoft Entra authentication.\"\nDefaultAzureCredential() integrates with Microsoft Entra ID and honors the RBAC assignments granted to the security group SC_Agent1_Dev.\n\n(2) get\nWhy not create_version?\ncreate_version requires specification of model deployments, instructions, and tools to construct a new revision. It is an authoring method, not a retrieval method."}]},{"n":69,"id":1009426,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains a Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) chat solution used by customer support agents.</p><p>You are adding an automated pre-production evaluation step to a CI/CD pipeline named Pipeline1. The evaluation will run against a labeled test dataset that contains support questions and the expected grounding context.</p><p>You need to ensure that Pipeline1 fails if unsupported content or a retrieval mismatch exceeds a defined threshold:</p><ul><li>responses include claims not supported by the retrieved source content</li><li>retrieved source content does not align with the labeled expected context</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which two built-in evaluators should you use in Pipeline1?</strong> Each correct answer presents pat of the solution.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Retrieval"},{"k":"B","html":"Fluency"},{"k":"C","html":"Coherence"},{"k":"D","html":"Groundedness"},{"k":"E","html":"Response Completeness"}],"answer":"AD","type":"multi","votes":[{"a":"A","p":50,"n":1},{"a":"AD","p":50,"n":1}],"page":7,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/e4e92875a882c04f861ece57cc34cffe1009426/","comments":[{"user":"8ac3742","date":"2026-10-05","up":1,"text":"Groundness and retrieval\nRequirement 1: \"responses include claims not supported by the retrieved source content\"\nEvaluated by D. Groundedness (GroundednessEvaluator)\nRequirement 2: \"retrieved source content does not align with the labeled expected context\"\nEvaluated by A. Retrieval : Compares the chunks/documents retrieved by the system against the ground-truth expected context in the labeled test dataset to ensure the search component fetches the correct grounding data.\n\nNotes tell about retrieval and coherence/fluence\nBelow is the examples of coherence/fluence\n(1)High Fluency, Low Coherence\n\"It was pouring rain outside. Therefore, she put on her favorite sunglasses and went swimming in the lake to stay dry.\"\nCoherence: Low (1/5) — It makes no logical sense. Rain does not lead to wearing sunglasses, and swimming in a lake will not keep you dry.\n(2)High Coherence, low Fluency\n\"Rain heavy fall sky. Girl take umbrella. Water no wet coat.\"","pick":"AD","replies":[{"user":"8ac3742","date":"2026-10-05","up":1,"text":"translate \"compares the chunks/documents retrieved by the system against the ground-truth expected context in the labeled test dataset\"\nfor example, in the test dataset for evaluation,\nfor question \" what is the counterparty of trade A\"?\nthe expected context: chunk = B, RBC\nIf retrieval returns : chuck = A, the settlement date = 2026-10-10\nThen the retrieval evaluation failed"}]},{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-10","up":1,"text":"For a RAG chat solution, the two requirements map directly to these evaluators:\n\nA. Retrieval ✅ → Checks whether the retrieved source content matches the expected/labeled context.\nD. Groundedness ✅ → Checks whether the response claims are supported by the retrieved source content.\nThe other options measure different aspects:\n\nB. Fluency → Measures how naturally and clearly the response is written.\nC. Coherence → Measures whether the response is logical and consistent.\nE. Response Completeness → Measures whether the response adequately addresses the question.\n👉 Final Answer: A. Retrieval + D. Groundedness","pick":"A"}]},{"n":70,"id":1009427,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains a support-ticket triage agent built by using the Foundry Agent Service.</p><p>The agent uses tool to classify the ticket type and sot the ticket priority.</p><p>Sometimes, the same support case continues across multiple sessions over several days.</p><p>You need to persist state by using a durable ID to ensure that the agent can automatically reuse the full interaction history. The solution must preserve previous user messages, tool calls and tool outputs across turns and sessions.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which runtime component should you use?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"output item"},{"k":"B","html":"agent"},{"k":"C","html":"conversation"},{"k":"D","html":"response"}],"answer":"C","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"C","p":100,"n":1}],"page":7,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/71c97415868540e5f0183fd3288becf11009427/","comments":[{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-10","up":1,"text":"A Conversation in Microsoft Foundry Agent Service provides a durable ID that allows the agent to persist and reuse interaction history across multiple turns and sessions.\n\nIt preserves:\n\nPrevious user messages\n\nTool calls\n\nTool outputs\n\nInteraction history across sessions\n\nA. Output item ❌ → Represents an individual piece of generated output.\n\nB. Agent ❌ → Defines the agent and its capabilities.\n\nC. Conversation ✅ → Maintains the persistent interaction state.\n\nD. Response ❌ → Represents a single response from the agent.\n\nFinal Answer: C. Conversation","pick":"C"}]},{"n":71,"id":1009428,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Founcy project that contains a Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) solution.</p><p>You need to run a pre-production evaluation by using labeled CSV dataset that contains the query, context, response and ground truth. The evaluation must measure the following:</p><ul><li>Whether responses address the user query</li><li>Whether responses are supported by the provided context</li><li>Whether responses contain sensitive or proprietary information</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which AI quality evaluation metrics should you use?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image39.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image40.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":8,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/3cafce112ca92d4801f17db284f03bdd1009428/","comments":[{"user":"8ac3742","date":"2026-10-05","up":1,"text":"(1)To measure whether the responses are supported by the provided context and address the user query:\nGroundedness and Relevance\n(2)To measure whether responses contain sensitive or proprietary information:\nProtected material"},{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-10","up":1,"text":"Correct Metrics\nWhether responses address the user query → Response Completeness\nWhether responses are supported by the provided context → Groundedness\nWhether responses contain sensitive or proprietary information → Content Safety\n👉 Final Answer:\nResponse Completeness + Groundedness + Content Safety"}]},{"n":72,"id":1009429,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You plan to configure an evaluation in Microsoft Foundry for a Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) chat app.</p><p>You need to provide scores for groundedness, relevance, and harmful content categories.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which two evaluation categories can you use?</strong> Each correct answer presents a complete solution.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"risk and safety metrics"},{"k":"B","html":"fluency evaluator"},{"k":"C","html":"similarity evaluators"},{"k":"D","html":"AI quality (NLP) metrics"},{"k":"E","html":"AI quality (AI assisted) metrics"}],"answer":"AE","type":"multi","votes":[{"a":"AD","p":38,"n":3},{"a":"AE","p":63,"n":5}],"page":8,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/08eacc637f30de712ba3ddac962cbf491009429/","comments":[{"user":"Srikantha","date":"2026-09-11","up":4,"text":"The two correct evaluation categories are A. risk and safety metrics and E. AI quality (AI assisted) metrics.\nExplanation:\nE. AI quality (AI assisted) metrics: This category uses a judge model (such as GPT-4) to measure quality aspects like groundedness and relevance.\nA. Risk and safety metrics: This category evaluates harmful content across various severity levels (such as self-harm, hate/unfairness, violence, and sexual content).","pick":"AE"},{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-10","up":3,"text":"Correct Answers: A. Risk and Safety Metrics and D. AI Quality (NLP) Metrics\nA. Risk and Safety Metrics ✅ → Used to evaluate harmful content categories and safety risks.\nD. AI Quality (NLP) Metrics ✅ → Used to measure groundedness and relevance of responses.\nWhy not the others?\n\nB. Fluency evaluator → Measures how naturally the response is written.\nC. Similarity evaluators → Focus on similarity between responses/reference content.\nE. AI Quality (AI-assisted) metrics → Uses AI-based evaluation for certain quality dimensions, but the question specifically maps groundedness/relevance and harmful content to the two categories above.\n👉 Final Answer: A and D.","pick":"AD"},{"user":"8ac3742","date":"2026-10-05","up":1,"text":"The two correct evaluation categories are:\nA. risk and safety metrics\nE. AI quality (AI assisted) metrics\n\nWhy \"AI assisted\" and NOT \"NLP\"?\nMicrosoft Foundry categorizes evaluation metrics into distinct buckets:\nAI quality (AI assisted) metrics:\nThese use an LLM (such as GPT-4o) as an automated judge to reason over unstructured inputs and context.\n(NLP) metrics are traditional, deterministic mathematical string-matching and overlap formulas.They cannot assess complex semantic concepts like groundedness or contextual relevance.","pick":"AE"}]},{"n":73,"id":1009430,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains an agent. The agent uses two tools to perform the following actions:</p><ul><li>Use Azure AI Search to retrieve answers from a private product documentation index.</li><li>Use the web search tool to retrieve public information on the internet.</li></ul><p>You need to ensure that for a specific run, the agent deterministically retrieves information only from the internet.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>To what should you set tool_choice?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"{“type”: “bing_grouding”}"},{"k":"B","html":"{“type”: “azure_ai-search”}"},{"k":"C","html":"“auto”"},{"k":"D","html":"“required”"}],"answer":"A","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"A","p":100,"n":1}],"page":8,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/181a1810bb14f6e612be35fdf72e514a1009430/","comments":[{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-10","up":1,"text":"Correct Answer: A. {“type”: “bing_grounding”}\nTo ensure the agent deterministically uses only the internet for a specific run, set tool_choice to the Bing grounding/web search tool.\n\nA. {\"type\": \"bing_grounding\"} ✅ → Forces the agent to use internet search.\nB. {\"type\": \"azure_ai-search\"} ❌ → Uses the private Azure AI Search index.\nC. \"auto\" ❌ → Allows the model to decide which tool to use.\nD. \"required\" ❌ → Requires a tool to be used but does not specify which tool.\nFinal Answer: A. {\"type\": \"bing_grounding\"}","pick":"A"}]},{"n":74,"id":1009431,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains a customer support agent built on a deployed chat model.</p><p>The agent responses are validated by using an automated testing system that compares generated answers to stored expected outputs. Identical prompts must return consistent response to prevent automated test failures.</p><p>You need to reduce response variability, without modifying the prompt or reducing factual accuracy.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you do for the model?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Increase the max_tokens parameter."},{"k":"B","html":"Remove stop sequences from the requests."},{"k":"C","html":"Decrease the temperature parameter."},{"k":"D","html":"Increase the temperature parameter."}],"answer":"C","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"C","p":100,"n":1}],"page":8,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/07486bbced89225fb1700183c41a3faf1009431/","comments":[{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-10","up":1,"text":"The temperature controls how much variability or randomness the model uses when generating responses. A lower temperature makes the model more deterministic and consistent.\n\nA. Increase max_tokens ❌ — Controls response length, not variability.\nB. Remove stop sequences ❌ — Does not directly reduce randomness.\nC. Decrease temperature ✅ — Produces more consistent responses.\nD. Increase temperature ❌ — Makes responses more varied and unpredictable.\n\n✅ Answer: C. Decrease the temperature parameter.","pick":"C"}]},{"n":75,"id":1009432,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You are developing prompts for a Micosoft Foundry project that classifies incoming support tickets by category.</p><p>You need to improve accuracy by showing the model how correct classifications look, without retaining the model or storing knowledge permanently.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which prompt engineering approach should you use?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG)"},{"k":"B","html":"zero-shot learning"},{"k":"C","html":"chain of thought"},{"k":"D","html":"few-shot learning"}],"answer":"D","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"D","p":100,"n":2}],"page":8,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/254a8689d314dba5c0e9db4624a453681009432/","comments":[{"user":"8ac3742","date":"2026-10-05","up":1,"text":"\"Showing the model how correct classifications look\" means providing input-output demonstration examples directly within the prompt.\n\"Without retraining the model or storing knowledge permanently\" describes in-context learning.\nThe examples live strictly within the prompt context window of that specific API call; the underlying model weights are not altered or fine-tuned, and no permanent state is kept.\nDo not choose zero-shot learning: Provides only instructions and the input data without any example demonstrations of the expected output format or classification","pick":"D"},{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-10","up":1,"text":"Option D: few-shot learning is correct.\n\nFew-shot learning provides concrete input-output examples inside the prompt to demonstrate classification patterns without needing model fine-tuning or permanent storage.","pick":"D"}]},{"n":76,"id":1009433,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains an agent for a customer support chat app. The agent uses a memory store and a memory search tool.</p><p>You need to ensure that the conversation history does NOT persist across separate sessions.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>To what should you set the scope of the memory tool?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"session"},{"k":"B","html":"{{$conversationId}}"},{"k":"C","html":"{{$userId}}"},{"k":"D","html":"global"}],"answer":"A","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"A","p":100,"n":2}],"page":8,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/2e43067f4c446cc4eacda6ab800ee13e1009433/","comments":[{"user":"8ac3742","date":"2026-10-05","up":1,"text":"tell about session and conversation(chat)\n\nYou open ChatGPT or your customer support chat portal (Session starts).\nYou have one chat\nYou click \"New Chat\" (Conversation 1 ends, Conversation 2 starts).\nBoth happened inside the exact same login Session.","pick":"A"},{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-10","up":1,"text":"The memory tool scope should be set to session when you want conversation history to remain available only during the current session and not persist across separate sessions.\n\nA. Session ✅ → Memory is limited to the current session.\nB. {{$conversationId}} ❌ → Ties memory to a specific conversation, but the requirement specifically calls for session-level isolation.\nC. {{$userId}} ❌ → Allows memory to persist for the same user across sessions.\nD. Global ❌ → Makes memory available broadly rather than limiting it to one session.\nFinal Answer: A. Session","pick":"A"}]},{"n":77,"id":1009434,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains an agent.</p><p>You need to enable long-term memory to ensure that the agent can recall user preferences across separate conversations. Stored memories must be isolated per authenticated user without the client application manually generating user IDs.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>How should you complete the Python code?</strong> To answer, drag the appropriate values to the correct targets. Each value may be used once, more than once, or not at all.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image41.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image42.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":8,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/9f0a32cb15a60cc1b6d911f3999ebf251009434/","comments":[{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-10","up":1,"text":"The correct values are:\n\nscope= → \"{{$userId}}\"\ntools= → [memory_tool]\nExplanation:\n{{$userId}} ensures that each authenticated user has a separate memory scope. This allows the agent to remember user preferences across different conversations without mixing one user's memories with another user's data."}]},{"n":78,"id":1009435,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a web app named App1 that processes user prompts by integrating with a Microsoft Foundry project named Project1. App1 performs the following actions:</p><ul><li>Sends prompts directly to a model by using the Azure OpenAI Responses API</li><li>Invokes the Azure AI Content Safety tool by using a Foundry connection within the same request</li></ul><p>You need to configure end-to-end visibility into each step of the request workflow.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you do?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Enable logging by using the client SDK for Content Safety."},{"k":"B","html":"Enable logging by using Foundry Local."},{"k":"C","html":"Enable application tracing in Project1."},{"k":"D","html":"Route requests through the Azure OpenAI endpoint."}],"answer":"C","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"C","p":100,"n":1}],"page":8,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/03e814afd0b9e553d4d957129b486eb11009435/","comments":[{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-10","up":1,"text":"Application tracing provides end-to-end visibility into the request, including model and tool calls.\n\nThis is especially useful for troubleshooting, monitoring, and understanding how requests move through the application.\n\nA. Content Safety logging ❌ — Focuses on Content Safety rather than the complete workflow.\nB. Foundry Local ❌ — Not used for end-to-end application tracing.\nC. Application tracing ✅ — Provides visibility across the request workflow.\nD. Azure OpenAI endpoint ❌ — The app already uses the API; routing alone doesn't provide full tracing.\n\nAnswer: C. Enable application tracing in Project1.","pick":"C"}]},{"n":79,"id":1009436,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains two agents named PolicyWriter and RskReviewer.</p><p>PolicyWriter generates daft updates for customer polices, and RiskReviewer reviews the drafts.</p><p>In the visual builder, you need to create a workflow that meets the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Finalizes low-risk updates without manual intervention</li><li>Ensures predictable execution across the agents</li><li>Requires user approval for highs updates</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you configure?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each comet selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image43.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image44.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":8,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/adb08c5b2bf295b5a0ade1628f3a3e601009436/","comments":[{"user":"Srikantha","date":"2026-09-12","up":4,"text":"nswer Key\nOrchestration pattern: The sequential template that passes outputs node by-node\nApproval checkpoints: Add a Condition statement."},{"user":"ExamProAzure","date":"2026-08-20","up":4,"text":"Orchestration pattern The sequential template that passes outputs node-by-node\nApproval checkpoints Add an Ask a question node"},{"user":"jwlnewsome","date":"2026-10-01","up":3,"text":"Orchestration pattern: The sequential template that passes outputs node by-node\nApproval checkpoints: Add a Condition statement.\nPredictable execution across the agents requires a Sequential orchestration pattern, where PolicyWriter → RiskReviewer execute in a fixed order and outputs are passed between nodes.\nFinalize low-risk updates without manual intervention and require user approval for high-risk updates requires evaluating the risk score/review outcome and branching accordingly. This is done with a Condition node:\nIf risk = Low → finalize automatically.\nIf risk = High → route to a human approval step."},{"user":"8ac3742","date":"2026-10-05","up":2,"text":"Orchestration pattern is the sequential template that passes outputs node-by-node\nKey requirement: \"Ensures predictable execution across the agents\" and \"PolicyWriter generates draft updates... and RiskReviewer reviews the drafts.\"\n\nA sequential template defines a strict, deterministic pipeline: PolicyWriter runs first to generate the draft, passing its output directly to RiskReviewer.\n\nWhy not \"group chat\"? The prompt specifically rules out dynamic routing: a group chat dynamically decides which agent speaks next using an LLM coordinator, which makes execution non-deterministic and unpredictable.\n\nWhy not \"human-in-the-loop template\"? The question asks for the overall orchestration pattern across the two agents. Low-risk updates must execute automatically without manual intervention, while human review is handled downstream via a branch checkpoint.\n\nWhy not \"human-in-the-loop template\"? The question asks for the overall orchestration pattern across the two agents. Low-risk updates must execute automatically without manual intervention, while human review is handled downstream via a branch checkpoint"}]},{"n":80,"id":1009437,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains an agent named Agent1.</p><p>Agent runs successful, but Foundry Control Plane does NOT display values for error rates, runs, and token usage, and the Traces tab is empty.</p><p>You need to ensure that Found Control Plane displays the appropriate values for Agent1.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you do?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Update Agent1 to a new version."},{"k":"B","html":"Restart Agent from Foundry Control Plan"},{"k":"C","html":"Assign to a Log Analytics workspace to Agent1."},{"k":"D","html":"Enable Application Insights for Agent1."}],"answer":"D","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"D","p":100,"n":1}],"page":8,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/247b2d65f403b74685c5a1257a42c4931009437/","comments":[{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-10","up":1,"text":"Correct Answer: D. Enable Application Insights for Agent1.\n\nEnable Application Insights to collect Agent1’s runs, errors, token usage, and traces.\nIt provides the telemetry needed to display monitoring information in the Foundry Control Plane.","pick":"D"}]},{"n":81,"id":1009438,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains an agent.</p><p>The agent uses Azure Content Understanding in Foundry Tools to process vendor onboarding packets. The packs include digital PDFs that contain tables and hyperlinks.</p><p>The extracted content is indexed for search and provided to a downstream agent in the Markdown format.</p><p>You need to generate a Markdown output that has a layout and a semantic structure optimized for Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) workflows.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which built-in analyzer should you use?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"prebuilt-documentFieldSchema"},{"k":"B","html":"prebuilt-documentSearch"},{"k":"C","html":"prebuilt-read"},{"k":"D","html":"prebuilt-layout"}],"answer":"B","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"B","p":71,"n":5},{"a":"D","p":29,"n":2}],"page":9,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/e47e69268f3d23b855f56b9d51146ef31009438/","comments":[{"user":"Srikantha","date":"2026-09-12","up":2,"text":". prebuilt-documentSearch\nExplanation:\nprebuilt-documentSearch: This is a dedicated RAG analyzer in Azure Content Understanding that extracts content from documents (such as PDFs with tables and links) while maintaining layout preservation, table detection, and structured Markdown output optimized specifically for downstream RAG and agent workflows.\nOther options: prebuilt-read provides basic OCR without layout analysis; prebuilt-layout focuses primarily on general document structure rather than being the specific prebuilt RAG search analyzer; prebuilt-documentFieldSchema is a utility analyzer used for proposing field schemas rather than extracting content for search.","pick":"B"},{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-10","up":2,"text":"Correct Answer: D. prebuilt-layout\nprebuilt-layout extracts document content while preserving layout and semantic structure, including tables and hyperlinks. This makes the Markdown output better suited for RAG workflows.","pick":"D"},{"user":"8ac3742","date":"2026-10-05","up":1,"text":"(1)prebuilt-documentSearch :Specifically engineered for RAG indexing pipelines.\nTransforms documents into enriched Markdown chunks with semantic hierarchy, section tags, table layout preservation, and document structure designed directly for search retrieval and LLM context windows.\n(2)prebuilt-layout:Focuses on raw visual layout analysis: reading order, checkboxes, barcode/QR code values, and basic table grids. It is not specifically targeted or pre-structured for RAG-optimized Markdown chunk generation.","pick":"B"},{"user":"jwlnewsome","date":"2026-10-02","up":1,"text":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/ai-services/content-understanding/concepts/prebuilt-analyzers#retrieval-augmented-generation-rag-analyzers","pick":"B"},{"user":"a5f05ea","date":"2026-09-26","up":1,"text":"Answer: B. prebuilt-documentSearch ✅\n\nprebuilt-documentSearch is specifically a RAG analyzer, optimized for retrieval-augmented generation scenarios. It performs semantic analysis and produces structured Markdown suitable for document ingestion, search applications, and knowledge bases.\n\nWhy not the others?\n\nA.prebuilt-documentFieldSchema: focused on schema/field extraction rather than RAG-ready document representation.\nC.prebuilt-read: primarily basic text/OCR extraction.\nD.prebuilt-layout: extracts layout elements such as words, paragraphs, figures, and tables, but isn't the analyzer specifically optimized for RAG.","pick":"B"}]},{"n":82,"id":1009439,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains an agent.</p><p>The agent uses Azure AI Search for Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG).</p><p>You plan to ingest and index PDF product manuals.</p><p>You need to build a solution that supports semantic similarity matching. The solution must ensure that the agent retrieves relevant data when user questions use different wording than the product manuals.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which indexing approach should you use?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"vector search"},{"k":"B","html":"semantic ranking"},{"k":"C","html":"suggesters"},{"k":"D","html":"analyzers"}],"answer":"A","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"A","p":100,"n":2}],"page":9,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/95aabb552b2bd5dca0ac6c481eb94e741009439/","comments":[{"user":"8ac3742","date":"2026-10-05","up":1,"text":"answer is vector search not semantic rank\n\n\"Which indexing approach should you use?\"\nSemantic ranking (Option B) is a query-time re-ranking feature (L2 ranker) applied to results after an initial search executes. It is not an indexing approach at all,its A query-side capability that evaluates the top 50 search results using cross-encoder models to reorder and produce semantic captions/answers.\nVector search (Option A) is the fundamental indexing approach that generates and indexes high-dimensional mathematical representations (embeddings) of text. It captures meaning and conceptual intent rather than exact keywords, ensuring match retrieval when users express questions in different wording than the manuals.","pick":"A"},{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-10","up":1,"text":"Correct answer: A. Vector search\n\nExplanation: Vector search converts text into numerical embeddings and finds content based on meaning and semantic similarity, not just exact keywords. This allows the agent to retrieve relevant information even when the user's question uses different wording from the PDF manuals.","pick":"A"}]},{"n":83,"id":1009440,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry agent that grounds responses from an Azure Search index that contains the following:</p><ul><li>Searchable text fields for product names and product codes</li><li>A vector field that stores embeddings for product descriptions</li></ul><p>You need to ensure that users can query the index by using the following:</p><ul><li>Exact product names or codes</li><li>Natural language descriptions of the products</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you configure?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"vector search only"},{"k":"B","html":"hybrid search"},{"k":"C","html":"keyword search only"},{"k":"D","html":"semantic search only"}],"answer":"B","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"B","p":100,"n":3}],"page":9,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/3090ff9344f8588b9d24969153ff96341009440/","comments":[{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-10","up":2,"text":"Hybrid search combines keyword search and vector search, allowing users to search with both exact terms and natural language.\n\nExact product names/codes → Keyword search\nNatural language descriptions → Vector search\n👉 Final Answer: B. Hybrid Search","pick":"B"},{"user":"8ac3742","date":"2026-10-05","up":1,"text":"hybrid of keyword search and vector search(embedding search)","pick":"B"}]},{"n":84,"id":1009441,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have an Azure AI Search indexer that ingests PDF policy manuals.</p><p>Client applications must display page-level citations that have bounding polygons for both text and images.</p><p>You need to add a single built-in multimodal content extraction skill to the Azure AI Search skillset. The solution must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Provide text and image location metadata.</li><li>Extract tables that span multiple pages.</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you add?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Document Extraction"},{"k":"B","html":"Azure Content Understanding in Foundry Tools"},{"k":"C","html":"GenAI Prompt"},{"k":"D","html":"Document Layout"}],"answer":"B","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"B","p":57,"n":4},{"a":"D","p":43,"n":3}],"page":9,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/40a2c4d612ead8e6cf2cc5e8902e0b571009441/","comments":[{"user":"Srikantha","date":"2026-09-12","up":3,"text":"B. Azure Content Understanding in Foundry Tools\nExplanation:\nAzure Content Understanding: This skill combines layout-aware extraction, image and text location metadata, and advanced structural support for extracting complex elements like cross-page tables as single semantic units.","pick":"B"},{"user":"a5f05ea","date":"2026-10-05","up":2,"text":"document layout skill to extract text, images, bounding polygons, and multi-page tables.\nAzure content understanding doesn't output individual bounding polygons.","pick":"D"},{"user":"8ac3742","date":"2026-10-05","up":2,"text":"Notes Azure AI Search does not have to call Azure Content Understanding to create or store an index. Calling Content Understanding (or Document Intelligence) is entirely optional.","pick":"D"},{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-10","up":2,"text":"The Document Layout skill can extract text, images, tables, and their location metadata, including bounding polygons. It also supports tables that span multiple pages, making it suitable for page-level citations in PDF documents.\n\nIn short: Text + images + bounding polygons + multi-page tables → Document Layout\n\n✅ Answer: D. Document Layout","pick":"D"},{"user":"a5f05ea","date":"2026-09-28","up":1,"text":"The deciding requirement is:\n\n“Extract tables that span multiple pages.”\nDocument Layout does satisfy much of the first requirement. It supports text/image extraction and provides location metadata for images.\n\nBut the question deliberately adds the cross-page table requirement. Microsoft's comparison specifically identifies recognition of a table spanning multiple pages as an advantage of Azure Content Understanding over Document Layout.","pick":"B"}],"variants":[116]},{"n":85,"id":1009442,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You are building an Azure AI Search indexing pipeline named Pipeline1 that ingests invoices stored in Azure Blob Storage. The invoices are stored as scanned images.</p><p>You need to enable users to search invoice data across the invoice fields.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which built-in skill should you add to the skillset of Pipeline1?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Text Split"},{"k":"B","html":"Text Translation"},{"k":"C","html":"optical character recognition (OCR)"},{"k":"D","html":"Image Analysis"}],"answer":"C","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"C","p":100,"n":2}],"page":9,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/520527ce471b75a0e4b46ab6cee4061c1009442/","comments":[{"user":"8ac3742","date":"2026-10-05","up":1,"text":"The invoices are stored as scanned images (e.g., TIFF, JPEG, or image-only files). In raw image files, there is no selectable text layer for Azure AI Search to read, so you have to choose OCR","pick":"C"},{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-10","up":1,"text":"Correct Answer: C. Optical Character Recognition (OCR)\nOCR extracts text from scanned invoice images, allowing the extracted invoice fields to become searchable in Azure AI Search.\n\nA. Text Split → Splits existing text into smaller sections.\nB. Text Translation → Translates text into another language.\nC. OCR ✅ → Extracts text from scanned images.\nD. Image Analysis → Analyzes visual content but isn't the best choice for extracting searchable invoice text.","pick":"C"}]},{"n":86,"id":1009443,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that uses Azure Content Understanding in Foundry Tools to analyze marketing videos.</p><p>Video segmentation is enabled.</p><p>You need to configure an analyzer to output a generated JSON field that describes the color scheme of each video segment.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>How should you configure the analyzer?</strong> To answer, drag the appropriate values to the correct targets. Each value may be used once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to drag the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image45.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image46.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":9,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/9116705d0b62e2cbe1256718822610f91009443/","comments":[{"user":"8ac3742","date":"2026-10-05","up":1,"text":"generate: Uses a generative AI model to synthesize, describe, summarize, or reason over content (ideal for visual descriptions like describing a scene's color scheme).\nclassify: Categorizes content into a fixed, predefined set of categories or enum options."},{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-11","up":1,"text":"Answer\nField value type: string\nField method: generate\nShort discussion:\nUse string because the generated JSON field contains a textual description of the color scheme. Use generate because the analyzer needs to create this description automatically for each video segment."}]},{"n":87,"id":1009444,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have an invoice-processing application named App1 that uses Azure Content Understanding in Foundry Tools.</p><p>You are building a new Content Understanding pipeline named Pipeline1 that must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Compare an invoice to its related purchase order</li><li>Validate the invoice against static vendor contact documents</li><li>Return a single structured output that includes discrepancy findings</li></ul><p>You need to configure Pipeline1 and expose the pipeline as a single analyzer endpoint.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you configure?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"a single-file task in standard mode that uses the vendor contract provided as an additional document during analysis."},{"k":"B","html":"a single-file task in standard mode that uses confidence scores enabled for the extracted fields."},{"k":"C","html":"a multiple-file task in pro mode that uses the vendor contract files as reference data"},{"k":"D","html":"a multi-file task in standard mode that uses the invoice and purchase order as input to the analyzer"}],"answer":"C","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"C","p":100,"n":2}],"page":9,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/0acaa06a0cd575afc9536df013bd8f5f1009444/","comments":[{"user":"8ac3742","date":"2026-10-05","up":1,"text":"In Content Understanding architecture, the invoice and the purchase order are the transaction-specific runtime inputs provided to the multiple-file task payload when calling the analyzer endpoint.\n\nThe static vendor contract documents represent the persistent reference data configured in the analyzer schema.\n\nOption C defines the task architecture: \"a multiple-file task in pro mode that uses the vendor contract files as reference data.\"","pick":"C"},{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-11","up":1,"text":"Correct answer: C. A multiple-file task in Pro mode that uses the vendor contract files as reference data.\n\nA multiple-file task is required because the pipeline must compare the invoice with its purchase order. Pro mode supports using reference data, allowing the analyzer to validate vendor information against static vendor documents and return the discrepancies in one structured output.","pick":"C"}]},{"n":88,"id":1009445,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that generates short promotional product videos.</p><p>After several clips are approved, reviewers notice a small watermark in the top-right corner of some videos.</p><p>You need to remove the watermark without regenerating the videos.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you do?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Modify the original prompt to exclude watermarks."},{"k":"B","html":"Crop the video by using the size parameter."},{"k":"C","html":"Increase the guidance scale."},{"k":"D","html":"Apply a mask-based inpainting edit to the affected part of the video."}],"answer":"D","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"D","p":100,"n":1}],"page":9,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/6f5eaeb5852e5f6c5b46b257c9d44ce91009445/","comments":[{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-11","up":1,"text":"inpainting edit to the affected part of the video.\nShort discussion:\nMask-based inpainting allows you to edit a specific area of an existing video. By masking the top-right watermark, you can remove it without regenerating the entire video.\n\nA ❌ modifies the prompt and requires regeneration.\nB ❌ cropping changes the video framing.\nC ❌ changes generation guidance, not an existing watermark.\nD ✅ directly edits the affected area.","pick":"D"}]},{"n":89,"id":1009446,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a web app named App1 that sends requests to a multimodal chat model deployment in a Microsoft Foundry project.</p><p>User messages can contain both text and images.</p><p>Currently, App1 includes image URL: as plain text inside the message content so the model cannot recognize them as images.</p><p>Traces show that the requests contain a single text message instead of a multimodal content array.</p><p>You need to send the message as a structured array that includes both the text portion and the image reference to ensure that the model can process the image correctly.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you do?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Set the user message content array to include items that have type: text and type: image_url."},{"k":"B","html":"Encode the image to base64 and include the encoded data inside the content string of the user message."},{"k":"C","html":"Add the image URL to the request metadata section, so the model can resolve the processing issue automatically."},{"k":"D","html":"Place the image URL inside the System Message and set type to image_url so the model loads the image at initialization."}],"answer":"A","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"A","p":100,"n":1}],"page":9,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/3a15af6e05191a52db9bcd8aa7c1b4631009446/","comments":[{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-11","up":1,"text":"Correct answer: A. Set the user message content array to include items that have type: text and type: image_url.\n\nMultimodal chat models require the user message to use a structured content array. The array should contain separate items for the text and image, such as type: \"text\" and type: \"image_url\".\n\nA ✅ Correct — enables the model to recognize and process both text and images.\nB ❌ Not necessary when using the image_url content type.\nC ❌ Metadata does not provide image content to the model.\nD ❌ Images should be included in the user content, not the system message.","pick":"A"}]},{"n":90,"id":1009447,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You are building a customer support web app named App1 in Microsoft Foundry that uses a GPT realtime model.</p><p>App1 must support:</p><ul><li>Live, low-latency voice conversations that use Azure OpenAI</li><li>Streaming audio input from users and playback audio responses</li></ul><p>You need to configure a connection method that supports real-time audio streaming in client application and targets approximately 100 ms latency.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which connection method should you use?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"RTMP"},{"k":"B","html":"WebRTC"},{"k":"C","html":"SIP"},{"k":"D","html":"WebSocket"}],"answer":"B","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"B","p":100,"n":6}],"page":9,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/50466c1628b1cc782c70cd66a2a99a8a1009447/","comments":[{"user":"MarceloManhaes","date":"2026-08-11","up":4,"text":"The correct response should be letter B. WebRTC has low latency than WebSocket. Source: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/foundry/openai/how-to/realtime-audio","pick":"B"},{"user":"8ac3742","date":"2026-10-05","up":1,"text":"Targeting sub-second ultra-low latency (~100 ms): The GPT Realtime API supports two transport mechanisms: WebSocket and WebRTC.\nWebRTC operates primarily over UDP (via SRTP)\nWebSockets run over TCP. Packet loss requires TCP retransmission, introducing jitter and latency spikes well above 100 ms for streaming raw interactive voice over consumer network connections.","pick":"B"},{"user":"Wella_","date":"2026-08-16","up":1,"text":"WebRTC - Correct answer\nWebSocket supports real-time bidirectional data, but WebRTC is the recommended method for browser-based real-time audio streaming with GPT Realtime.","pick":"B"}]},{"n":91,"id":1009448,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains an agent and uses a GitHub repository. The repository contains a YAM file named File1 that defines the evaluation settings of the agent.</p><p>You need to create a GitHub Actions workflow that runs the evaluation defined in File1 when a pull request (PR) is opened.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>How should you configure the workflow?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Set project-endpoint to the endpoint of the project."},{"k":"B","html":"Set evaluation-config to the path of the YAML file."},{"k":"C","html":"Set model-deployment-name to the deployed model."},{"k":"D","html":"Set tenant-id to the Microsoft Entra tenant ID"}],"answer":"B","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"B","p":100,"n":5}],"page":10,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/1b366766faecff8f355d843206bf0e2c1009448/","comments":[{"user":"VikashDubey","date":"2026-08-21","up":3,"text":"Evaluation is defined in a YAML file” → point the workflow to that YAML configuration.","pick":"B"},{"user":"ExamProAzure","date":"2026-08-20","up":2,"text":"The question says File1 is a YAML file that already defines the evaluation settings, and the GitHub Actions workflow needs to run that specific evaluation when the PR opens.","pick":"B"}]},{"n":92,"id":1009449,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains an agent.</p><p>The agent uses a stored access key to retrieve secrets from an Azure key vault, which violates a keyless-credentials requirement.</p><p>You need to ensure that the agent can retrieve the secrets. The solution must follow the principle of least privilege.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you configure?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image47.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image48.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":10,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/5204f51e3b873cec625423b1062b93e61009449/","comments":[{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-11","up":2,"text":"Correct selections\nManaged identity scope: ✅ Enable a system-assigned managed identity at the project level\nKey Vault authorization method: ✅ Assign the Key Vault Secrets User role to the managed identity\n\nUse a project-level managed identity so the agent can access Azure resources without storing credentials. Assign only the Key Vault Secrets User role, following the least-privilege principle."}]},{"n":93,"id":1009450,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains a customer support application.</p><p>You create an evaluation named Run1 that has the following configurations:</p><ul><li>Includes risk and safety metrics</li><li>Includes the protected material evaluation</li><li>Includes harmful content metrics that use a medium severity threshold</li></ul><p>You create an evaluation named Run2 that has the following configurations:</p><ul><li>Includes risk and safety metrics</li><li>Includes the protected material evaluation</li><li>Includes harmful content metrics that use a high severity threshold</li></ul><p>You run both evaluations against a dataset named DB1 and receive the following results:</p><ul><li><b>Content harm defect rate of Run1:</b> 12%</li><li><b>Content harm defect rate of Run2:</b> 4%</li><li><b>Protected material evaluation of Run1:</b> 6%</li><li><b>Protected material evaluation of Run1:</b> 6%</li></ul><p>You start a fine-tuning job by using DB1. The job fails during automatic RAI checks for multiple content harm types.</p><p>You discover that the content filtering configuration is set to high severity.</p><p class=\"ask\">For each of the following statements, select Yes if the statement is true. Otherwise, select No.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image49.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image50.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":10,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/1ed636d5720ae36c2b335c5d260d56731009450/","comments":[{"user":"8ac3742","date":"2026-10-05","up":1,"text":"correct answer\n\nHow Azure Content Safety thresholds work: The threshold sets the cutoff level where content is flagged or blocked.\n\nA High severity threshold is the least restrictive setting (it only flags/blocks High-severity harm).\n\nA Low severity threshold is the most restrictive setting (it flags/blocks Low, Medium, and High-severity harm).\n\nRun2 showed that 4% of DB1 contains High-severity content defects. Because the fine-tuning job already failed under the most permissive setting (High), tightening the filter to Low would block even more samples (at least 12% or more), causing more failures rather than resolving them. To fix the fine-tuning job, the dataset DB1 itself must be cleaned and remediated to remove the offending content."},{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-11","up":1,"text":"Correct Answers\n\nChanging the content filtering configuration to low severity will resolve the fine-tuning job issue: No (A low threshold makes filters stricter, triggering more RAI blocks).\n\nThe difference between the 12% and 4% content harm defect rate is consistent with the different severity thresholds used in Run1 and Run2: Yes (Medium threshold catches more items than a High threshold).\n\nThe identical 6% protected material evaluation values across Run1 and Run2 indicate that this metric is unaffected by the change in the severity threshold: Yes (Protected material detection is independent of content harm severity thresholds)."}]},{"n":94,"id":1009451,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains a multi-agent solution. The agents use tool calling to query internal systems.</p><p>You need to implement responsible AI auditing to meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Capture all the nested operations across the entire agent run.</li><li>Record tool invocation arguments and returned results as metadata.</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you use for each requirement?</strong> To answer, drag the appropriate options to the correct targets Each option may be used once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to drag the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image51.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image52.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":10,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/4a3f15e37ecca3672f6e0dabbd719ed91009451/","comments":[{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-11","up":1,"text":"Capture all the nested operations across the entire agent run: Hierarchical spans (Captures parent-child execution flow and nested sub-tasks in open telemetry/tracing).\n\nRecord tool invocation arguments and returned results as metadata: Tool call attributes (Attaches tool input arguments and output values as metadata attributes to individual telemetry spans)."}]},{"n":95,"id":1009452,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains an agent. The agent uses threads and file uploads and calls an Azure OpenAI model deployment.</p><p>During load testing, calls intermittently fall and return an HTTP 429 rate limit exceeded error. Some user uploads fail and generate an HTTP 400 file size exceeded error.</p><p>You need to mitigate the errors and reduce call failures. The solution must remain within the service and model limits.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you do to resolve each error?</strong> To answer, drag the appropriate actions to the correct errors. Each action may be used once, more than once or not at all. You may need to drag the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each comet selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image53.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image54.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":10,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/7f6e1483d10f3b22f16704952bb8bb1b1009452/","comments":[{"user":"8ac3742","date":"2026-10-05","up":1,"text":"correct answer\nWhy \"Implement exponential backoff and jitter\" instead of \"Increase tenant-wide quotas\"?Look closely at the constraint in the problem statement:\"The solution must remain within the service and model limits.\" HTTP 429 (Rate Limit Exceeded): In high-throughput or load-testing scenarios, temporary request bursts frequently cross TPM (tokens per minute) or RPM (requests per minute) thresholds. The standard architecture pattern to mitigate rate limiting while staying strictly within existing service and model limits is client-side retry handling using exponential backoff and jitter. Simply increasing tenant quotas does not build resiliency against bursting and violates the constraint to stay within the existing limits."},{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-11","up":1,"text":"Correct Answers\n\nHTTP 429: Implement exponential backoff and jitter in the retry logic. (Standard technique for handling rate limits/throttling without exceeding service quotas).\n\nHTTP 400: Split content into smaller files before uploading the files. (Directly resolves individual file size limits that trigger the HTTP 400 file size exceeded error)."}]},{"n":96,"id":1009453,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project.</p><p>You need to deploy a model from the model catalog to support a search solution for internal policy documents. The model must generate vector representations of the text in the documents and of user queries.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which type of model should you use?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"an embedding model"},{"k":"B","html":"an image generation model"},{"k":"C","html":"a large language model (LLM)"},{"k":"D","html":"a small language model (SLM)"}],"answer":"A","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"A","p":100,"n":1}],"page":10,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/27608a9999277fe30b4c433de3b4f2441009453/","comments":[{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-11","up":1,"text":"Correct answer: A. An embedding model\n\nAn embedding model converts documents and user queries into vector representations. These vectors can then be compared to find semantically similar content, making embedding models ideal for search and retrieval solutions.\n\nA ✅ Embedding model — creates text vectors for semantic search.\nB ❌ Image generation — creates images.\nC ❌ LLM — mainly generates and understands text.\nD ❌ SLM — smaller language model, but not specifically designed for embeddings.","pick":"A"}]},{"n":97,"id":1009454,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project.</p><p>You need to deploy a model from the model catalog to support real-time inference. The solution must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Use key-based authentication.</li><li>Support real-time REST API access.</li><li>NOT consume the vCPU quota of the virtual machines in the Azure subscription.</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which type of deployment should you use?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"serverless API"},{"k":"B","html":"batch"},{"k":"C","html":"self-hosted container"},{"k":"D","html":"standard"}],"answer":"A","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"A","p":100,"n":5}],"page":10,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/62ea273693bc3639526e1df5464e117b1009454/","comments":[{"user":"Alvarogc","date":"2026-08-23","up":5,"text":"The requirements here are the ones used on the definition of serverless API.\n\nRefference: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/foundry-classic/how-to/deploy-models-serverless","pick":"A"}]},{"n":98,"id":1009455,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You plan to create a Microsoft Foundry project named Project1 that will contain an agent and use an Azure key vault named KV1.</p><p>You need to configure a connection from Project1 to KV1.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>How should you complete the Bicep code?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area?</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image55.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image56.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":10,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/df8f58482e905026ed5fbd6220deba441009455/","comments":[{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-11","up":2,"text":"Correct Answers\n\ncategory: 'AzureKeyVault'\n\nExplanation: To connect an existing Key Vault instance to a Microsoft Foundry project, the connection category must be explicitly defined as 'AzureKeyVault'.\n\nauthType: 'AccountManagedIdentity'\n\nExplanation: Microsoft Foundry authenticates to Key Vault resources via Azure Managed Identity ('AccountManagedIdentity') using Azure RBAC roles such as Key Vault Secrets Officer."}]},{"n":99,"id":1009456,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project.</p><p>You need to create a customer support agent that meets the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Grounds responses only in company policy documents stored in curated repositories</li><li>Retains customer preferences across separate chat sessions</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>How should you configure the agent?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image57.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image58.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":10,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/edb502c09bd3e42cef6eda0c8b2571d41009456/","comments":[{"user":"8ac3742","date":"2026-10-05","up":1,"text":"correct answer\n\nRequirement: \"Grounds responses only in company policy documents stored in curated repositories\". The documents are maintained externally in curated repositories. Connecting to the curated repositories via retrieval from approved data sources ensures the agent searches live, managed enterprise stores (such as Azure AI Search or curated Blob containers) rather than copying static files directly into the agent. Why not \"Upload the policy documents direct to the agent\": Uploading files directly attaches static copies to the specific agent definition/Assistant tool, which decouples them from the central, curated policy repositories whenever policies get updated."},{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-11","up":1,"text":"Correct Answers\n\nKnowledge grounding: Configure retrieval from approved data sources. (Typoed as Configure revival... in the option; grounds responses dynamically using enterprise search/RAG over curated repositories rather than hardcoding static instructions or uploading raw files directly into the prompt).\n\nMemory: Enable agent memory that uses persistent storage. (Allows state and user preferences to persist across completely separate chat sessions)."}]},{"n":100,"id":1009457,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains an agent. The agent generates summaries from retrieved policy documents.</p><p>You need to improve response completeness. The solution must be implemented in the logic of the application code before responses are returned.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you do?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Add a retry evaluation before the responses are returned."},{"k":"B","html":"Decrease the value of the temperature parameter."},{"k":"C","html":"Increase the value of the presence_penalty parameter"},{"k":"D","html":"Replace the model with a smaller deployment."}],"answer":"A","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"A","p":100,"n":1}],"page":10,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/29be64707b7f60fc4638cf38e0cf552d1009457/","comments":[{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-11","up":1,"text":"Correct answer: A. Add a retry evaluation before the responses are returned.\n\nA retry evaluation can check whether the generated summary is complete and trigger another generation attempt when necessary. This directly improves response completeness through the application logic.\n\nA ✅ Retry evaluation — checks and improves incomplete responses.\nB ❌ Lower temperature mainly makes output more deterministic.\nC ❌ Presence penalty affects repetition/new-topic behavior, not completeness.\nD ❌ A smaller model generally won't improve completeness.","pick":"A"}],"variants":[38,153]},{"n":101,"id":1009458,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You develop a test method to verify the results retrieved from a call to the Azure Vision in Foundry Tools API. The call is used to analyze the existence of company logos in images. The call returns a collection of brands named brands.</p><p>You have the following code segment:</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image59.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p class=\"ask\">For each of the following statements, select Yes if the statement is true. Otherwise, select No.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image60.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image61.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":11,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/f40889d92bb39b92c0a18765de75551e1009458/","comments":[{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-11","up":1,"text":"Correct Answers\n\nThe code will display the name of each detected brand with a confidence equal to or higher than 75 percent: Yes (The if brand.confidence >= 0.75: condition filters and displays only brands with a 75%+ confidence score).\n\nThe code will display coordinates for the top-left corner of the rectangle that contains the brand logo of the displayed brands: Yes (In Azure Vision, brand.rectangle.x and brand.rectangle.y represent the top-left corner coordinates of the bounding box)."}]},{"n":102,"id":1009459,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have an Azure subscription.</p><p>You plan to build an app that will use the Azure AI DALL-E model.</p><p>You need to deploy the model.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you use?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"the Azure SDK for Python and PowerShell cmdlets."},{"k":"B","html":"the Azure SDK for JavaScript and Azure Machine Learning Studio."},{"k":"C","html":"Microsoft Foundry and the Azure Command Line Interface (CLI)"},{"k":"D","html":"the Azure portal and Microsoft Graph API"}],"answer":"C","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"C","p":100,"n":1}],"page":11,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/4fa05263f10e755e62d1842e70781b621009459/","comments":[{"user":"Srikantha","date":"2026-09-03","up":1,"text":"To deploy an Azure AI model like DALL-E, you must use administrative tools designed for resource provisioning and management. Microsoft Foundry (the unified platform for Azure AI resources) and the Azure CLI handle the infrastructure layer required to create, configure, and manage model deployments within your subscription.\nWhile SDKs (like Python or JavaScript) are used to interact with the model after it is deployed within your application code, they are not the primary tools used for the initial deployment of the model resource itself. Additionally, the Microsoft Graph API is used for interacting with Microsoft 365 data, not Azure AI model deployment.","pick":"C"}]},{"n":103,"id":1009460,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have an Azure subscription.</p><p>You need to create a new resource that will generate fictional stores in response to user prompts. The solution must ensure that the resource uses a customer-managed key to protect data.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>How should you complete the script?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image62.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image63.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":11,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/dd49e55555d881b422b0bc2bf118108a1009460/","comments":[{"user":"Alvarogc","date":"2026-08-23","up":3,"text":"First one is OpenAI, is the only one that generates free text.\n\nSecond one is --encryption, is the property that can receive the JSON on this code; --assign-identity doesn't receive any JSON.\n\nRefference: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/cli/azure/cognitiveservices/account?view=azure-cli-latest","replies":[{"user":"AIBoss","date":"2026-09-02","up":1,"text":"Yes, Second one is --encryption.\n\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/cli/azure/cognitiveservices/account?view=azure-cli-latest#az-cognitiveservices-account-create:~:text=Create%20a%20Text%20Analytics%20Cognitive%20Services%20account%20in%20West%20Europe%20without%20confirmation%20required%20and%20user%20Customer%2Dmanaged%20encryption."}]},{"user":"AzureGeek79","date":"2026-10-11","up":1,"text":"Open AI and assign-identity are the correct answers."},{"user":"Srikantha","date":"2026-09-15","up":1,"text":"Why\nOpenAI is required because the resource must generate fictional stores from user prompts using Azure OpenAI.\n--api-properties is the parameter used to specify the encryption key source and Azure Key Vault properties.\n\"keySource\": \"Microsoft.KeyVault\" indicates a customer-managed key (CMK) rather than a Microsoft-managed key.\n✅ Answer: OpenAI + --api-properties"}]},{"n":104,"id":1009461,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Python application collects customer comments before posting them to a public forum.</p><p>You need to send a text comment to Azure AI Content Safety and return the self-harm severity from the response.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>How should you complete the code?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image64.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image65.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":11,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/8a586e81dbce39b74bb5377e750dcd3d1009461/","comments":[{"user":"jwlnewsome","date":"2026-10-02","up":1,"text":"request: AnalyzeTextOptions(text=comment)\nresponse: client.analyze_text(request)\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/ai-services/content-safety/quickstart-text?tabs=visual-studio%2Cwindows&pivots=programming-language-python"},{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-11","up":1,"text":"Correct Answers\n\nrequest: AnalyzeTextOptions(text=comment)\n\nresponse: client.analyze_text(request)\n\nExplanations\n\nrequest: The AnalyzeTextOptions class takes the input string using the text parameter (e.g., AnalyzeTextOptions(text=comment)). It does not take a list or a category object as the primary argument.\n\nresponse: To perform text moderation using the ContentSafetyClient in the Azure AI Content Safety Python SDK, call the method client.analyze_text(request)."}]},{"n":105,"id":1009462,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a custom named entity recognition (NER) project in Azure Language in Foundry Tools for support tickets. The schema for the project contains an entity type named ContactInfo.</p><p>In tagged training files, ContactInfo is used for phone numbers, email addresses, and social media handles.</p><p>Model evaluation shows low precision for ContactInfo, including false positives in which nearby text is extracted as ContactInfo.</p><p>You need to improve the precision of the project.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you do before retraining the model?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Lower the confidence threshold for ContactInfo."},{"k":"B","html":"Trigger an auto-labeling job."},{"k":"C","html":"Add more support tickets as training data and label more ContactInfo entities."},{"k":"D","html":"Replace ContactInfo by using Phone, Email, and SocialMedia entities. Relabel every matching span."}],"answer":"D","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"D","p":100,"n":1}],"page":11,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/bc7f6ea0c1070ac6f0d64bc0324ec9c51009462/","comments":[{"user":"Srikantha","date":"2026-09-03","up":1,"text":"The Solution: Azure Custom NER best practices dictate that entities should maintain structural similarity. By breaking the broad entity down into three distinct, highly specific types (Phone, Email, and SocialMedia), you give the model clear, distinct patterns to recognize.","pick":"D"}]},{"n":106,"id":1009463,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You are building a text-to-speech solution that uses Azure Speech in Foundry Tools to read instructions from the script in a text file.</p><p>You discover that the solution often pronounces technical terms incorrectly.</p><p>You need to prevent the incorrect pronunciations. The solution must minimize development effort.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you do?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"From Speech Studio, train a custom neural voice"},{"k":"B","html":"Use Speech Synthesis Markup Language (SSML) to specify phonemes."},{"k":"C","html":"Use Speech Synthesis Markup Language (SSML) to apply say as rules."},{"k":"D","html":"Use Speech Synthesis Markup Language (SSML) to adjust the prosody of the voice."},{"k":"E","html":"From Azure OpenAI use the Whisper model."}],"answer":"B","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"B","p":100,"n":1}],"page":11,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/bcebda5f9beb3c2f0a477debe9e017b81009463/","comments":[{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-11","up":1,"text":"Correct answer: B. Use Speech Synthesis Markup Language (SSML) to specify phonemes.\n\nSSML phonemes let you explicitly control how specific technical terms are pronounced. This is the simplest and most targeted solution and avoids training a custom voice.\n\nA ❌ Custom voice is unnecessary and requires more development effort.\nB ✅ SSML phonemes directly correct pronunciation.\nC ❌ Say-as controls how text is interpreted, not exact phonetic pronunciation.\nD ❌ Prosody changes pitch, rate, and volume—not pronunciation.\nE ❌ Whisper is for speech-to-text, not text-to-speech.","pick":"B"}]},{"n":107,"id":1009464,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Python application that redacts sensitive information before sending prompt text to a language model. The application has the following code:</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image66.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p class=\"ask\">For each of the following statements, select Yes if the statement is true. Otherwise, select No.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image67.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image68.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":11,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/265095c7b167ecdad438602531b00ed51009464/","comments":[]},{"n":108,"id":1009465,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You are developing an application that will detect faulty components produced on a factory production line. The components are specific to your business.</p><p>You need to use the Azure Custom Vision API to help detect common faults.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which three actions should you perform in sequence?</strong> To answer, move the appropriate actions from the list of actions to the answer area and arrange them in the correct order.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image69.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image70.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":11,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/68a4de0b2e226be986530e716ed154031009465/","comments":[{"user":"Az301301X","date":"2026-09-07","up":5,"text":"Put Train the classifier model as number 3.\n\nThe correct full sequence is:\n\n1. Create a project\n2. Upload and tag images\n3. Train the classifier model\n\nHere you’re classifying components (faulty vs non‑faulty), not locating multiple objects in an image, so classifier—not object detection—is the right choice."}]},{"n":109,"id":1009466,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You are developing a new sales system that will process user-generated video and text from a public-facing website.</p><p>You plan to notify users that their data has been processed by the sales system.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which responsible AI principle does this help meet?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"fairness"},{"k":"B","html":"transparency"},{"k":"C","html":"inclusiveness"},{"k":"D","html":"reliability and safety"}],"answer":"B","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"B","p":100,"n":1}],"page":11,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/5315cfb13724e262a50319630681b4451009466/","comments":[{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-11","up":1,"text":"Notifying users that their data has been processed helps them understand how and when AI systems use their data, which is part of the transparency principle.\n\nA ❌ Fairness — focuses on avoiding unfair bias.\nB ✅ Transparency — provides users with information about AI/data processing.\nC ❌ Inclusiveness — ensures AI works for diverse users.\nD ❌ Reliability and safety — focuses on consistent and safe system behavior.\n\nCorrect answer: B. Transparency ✅","pick":"B"}]},{"n":110,"id":1009467,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You are designing a content management system.</p><p>You need to ensure that the reading experience is optimized for users who have reduced comprehension and learning differences, such as dyslexia. The solution must minimize development effort.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which Azure service should you include in the solution?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Azure Document Intelligence in Foundry Tools"},{"k":"B","html":"Azure Language in Foundry Tools"},{"k":"C","html":"Azure AI Immersive Reader"},{"k":"D","html":"Azure Translator in Foundry Tools"}],"answer":"C","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"C","p":100,"n":1}],"page":11,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/7fb937d8443540aef835b534c53f97dc1009467/","comments":[{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-11","up":1,"text":"Correct answer: C. Azure AI Immersive Reader\n\nAzure AI Immersive Reader is designed to improve reading comprehension and accessibility for users with learning differences such as dyslexia. It provides features like text spacing, line focus, and read-aloud, with minimal development effort.\n\nA ❌ Document Intelligence — extracts information from documents.\nB ❌ Azure Language — analyzes and processes text.\nC ✅ Immersive Reader — optimizes reading and accessibility.\nD ❌ Translator — translates text between languages.","pick":"C"}]},{"n":111,"id":1009468,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have an Azure subscription that contains an Azure App Service app named App1.</p><p>You provision a Microsoft Foundry Service resource named CSAccount1.</p><p>You need to configure App1 to access CSAccount1. The solution must minimize administrative effort.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you use to configure App1?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"the endpoint URI and subscription key"},{"k":"B","html":"the endpoint URI and an OAuth token"},{"k":"C","html":"the endpoint URI and a shared access signature (SAS) token"},{"k":"D","html":"a system assigned managed identity and an X.509 certificate"}],"answer":"A","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"A","p":100,"n":1}],"page":12,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/a5c96156210db2c0631cdca4e44541481009468/","comments":[{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-11","up":1,"text":"Using the endpoint URI and subscription key is the simplest configuration and requires the least administrative effort.\n\nA ✅ Simple and straightforward authentication.\nB ❌ OAuth requires additional token management.\nC ❌ SAS tokens aren't the standard choice here.\nD ❌ Managed identity and X.509 certificates require more configuration.\nAnswer: A","pick":"A"}]},{"n":112,"id":1009469,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a web app that uses Azure AI Search.</p><p>When reviewing activity you see greater than expected search query volumes. You suspect that the query key is compromised.</p><p>You need to prevent unauthorized access to the search endpoint and ensure that users only have read only access to the documents collection. The solution must minimize app downtime.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which three actions should you perform in sequence?</strong> To answer, move the appropriate actions from the list of actions to the answer area and arrange them in the correct order.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image71.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image72.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":12,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/8941f1355ee80bb39904a98b3bc865c81009469/","comments":[{"user":"Alvarogc","date":"2026-08-23","up":10,"text":"The order shown could cause service disruption. To minimize downtime, the correct sequence should be:\n\n1. Add a new query key\n2. Change the app to use the new query key\n3. Delete the compromised key","top":true}]},{"n":113,"id":1009470,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You need to create a new resource that will be used to perform sentiment analysis and optical character recognition (OCR). The solution must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Use a single key and endpoint to access multiple services.</li><li>Consolidate billing for future services that you might use.</li><li>Support the use of Azure Vision in Foundry Tools in the future.</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>How should you complete the HTTP request to create the new resource?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image73.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image74.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":12,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/7652e5174e2009fa92a22f3e148efb791009470/","comments":[{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-11","up":1,"text":"Correct Answers\n\nHTTP Method: PUT\n\nkind: \"CognitiveServices\"\n\nExplanations\n\nHTTP Method (PUT): In Azure Resource Manager (ARM) REST APIs, resource creation or full replacement at a specific URI uses the PUT verb.\n\nkind (\"CognitiveServices\"): The multi-service Azure AI services resource type is denoted by the \"CognitiveServices\" kind. Single-service kinds (like \"ComputerVision\" or \"TextAnalytics\") only provide access to individual APIs and cannot satisfy the requirement for consolidated billing, multi-service key/endpoint access, or future Vision integration."}]},{"n":114,"id":1009471,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You are building a model to detect objects in images.</p><p>The performance of the model based on training data is shown in the following exhibit.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image75.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>Use the drop-down menus to select the answer choice that completes each statement based on the information presented in the graphic.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image76.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image77.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":12,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/3f7b1c6d668e8aadc3d54b9ff669487e1009471/","comments":[{"user":"Srikantha","date":"2026-09-19","up":1,"text":"Step-by-Step Analysis\nThe percentage of false positives:\nPrecision Formula:\nPrecision=\nTrue Positives (TP)+False Positives (FP)\nTrue Positives (TP)\n​\n\nWith a Precision of 100.0% (1.0), there are no false positive predictions made by the model (FP=0).\nTherefore, the percentage of false positives is 0.\nThe value for the number of true positives divided by the total number of true positives and false negatives:\nRecall Formula:\nRecall=\nTrue Positives (TP)+False Negatives (FN)\nTrue Positives (TP)\n​\n\nThe definition in the prompt describes the formula for Recall.\nLooking at the performance metrics exhibit, Recall is 25.0%, which corresponds to 25."}]},{"n":115,"id":1009472,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You are developing an application that will use Azure AI Search for internal documents.</p><p>You need to implement document-level filtering for Azure AI Search.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which three actions should you include in the solution?</strong> Each correct answer presents part of the solution.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Add allowed groups to each index entry"},{"k":"B","html":"Create one index per group."},{"k":"C","html":"Send access tokens from Microsoft Entra ID, with the search request."},{"k":"D","html":"Retrieve all the groups."},{"k":"E","html":"Retrieve the group memberships of the user"},{"k":"F","html":"Supply the groups as a filter for the search requests"}],"answer":"AEF","type":"multi","votes":[{"a":"AEF","p":100,"n":1}],"page":12,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/fe26fef99380e1a615c4e01303171cf91009472/","comments":[{"user":"Srikantha","date":"2026-09-06","up":1,"text":"Add allowed groups to each index entry: Tag documents or index chunks with a security field specifying which groups have access rights.\nRetrieve the group memberships of the user: Identify the active security groups or permissions belonging to the user executing the search query.\nSupply the groups as a filter for the search requests: Apply an OData filter (such as using search.in or collection operators) containing the user's groups to restrict the search results to only authorized content.","pick":"AEF"}]},{"n":116,"id":1009473,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have an Azure AI Search indexer that ingest PDF policy manuals.</p><p>Client applications must display page-level citations that have bounding polygons for both text and images.</p><p>You need to add a single built-in multimodal content extraction skill to the Azure AI Search skillset. The solution must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Provide text and image location metadata.</li><li>Extract tables that span multiple pages.</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you add?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Document Layout"},{"k":"B","html":"Document Extraction"},{"k":"C","html":"Azure Content Understanding"},{"k":"D","html":"GenAI Prompt"}],"answer":"C","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"A","p":44,"n":4},{"a":"C","p":56,"n":5}],"page":12,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/94f545aaf31dbaa3b5a18b80f966c9eb1009473/","comments":[{"user":"Srikantha","date":"2026-09-18","up":3,"text":"A. Document Layout\nMicrosoft Documentation Explanation\nAccording to Microsoft Learn documentation on Azure AI Search multimodal skillsets:\nLocation Metadata & Bounding Polygons: The built-in Document Layout skill uses Azure AI Document Intelligence under the hood to extract text, figures, and embedded images along with spatial location metadata—specifically page numbers (pageNumber) and bounding coordinates (boundingPolygons / locationMetadata) for both text and image elements.\nMulti-Page Table Extraction: The layout extraction capability natively parses complex document structures, retaining tables and tabular data that span across multi-page boundaries as cohesive structured objects rather than disconnected text fragments.","pick":"A"},{"user":"554b579","date":"2026-09-14","up":3,"text":"C. Azure Content Understanding — TRUE per the key. The multimodal skill covering text and images in one pass, returning location metadata for both and handling tables spanning pages. The word “multimodal” in the stem is the hook\n\nA. Document Layout — FALSE per the key, and the community’s unanimous choice. It genuinely returns bounding polygons, structural elements, and multipage tables, which makes it a strong answer. The argument against it is that it is text-oriented, while the stem requires location metadata for images as well.","pick":"C"},{"user":"jwlnewsome","date":"2026-10-02","up":1,"text":"Document Extraction/Layout does not preserve cross-page tables.","pick":"C"},{"user":"a5f05ea","date":"2026-09-26","up":1,"text":"Document Layout → preserve/understand document structure\n\nAzure Content Understanding → richer multimodal understanding + semantic chunking + improved complex table extraction","pick":"C"},{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-11","up":1,"text":"Correct answer: A. Document Layout ✅\nShort discussion:\nThe Document Layout skill can extract both text and images with their location/bounding polygon metadata and supports tables that span multiple pages. This makes it suitable for generating page-level citations.\n\nA ✅ Document Layout — provides text/image positions and multi-page table extraction.\nB ❌ Document Extraction — focuses on extracting document content, not the required layout metadata.\nC ❌ Content Understanding — not the required built-in Search skill for this scenario.\nD ❌ GenAI Prompt — used for generative processing, not direct layout extraction.","pick":"A"}],"variants":[84]},{"n":117,"id":1009474,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You are creating an enrichment pipeline that will use Azure AI Search. The knowledge store contains unstructured JSON data and the text from scanned PDF documents.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which projection type should you use for each data type?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image78.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image79.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":12,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/0bf51e8f6c2d2701aa211832862fdd781009474/","comments":[{"user":"Alvarogc","date":"2026-08-24","up":3,"text":"1. Object projection\n2. Object projection\n\nIt should be Object projection for both answers. There's no specified relational structure on the question, so second one may not be Table projection; but File projection is only for normalized, binary image files.\n\nReference: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/search/knowledge-store-projection-overview"}]},{"n":118,"id":1012319,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You are building a custom vision model that will be deployed as part of an iOS app.</p><p>You have images of cats and dogs. Each image contains either a cat or a dog.</p><p>You need to use the Azure Custom Vision service to detect whether the image is of a cat or a dog.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>How should you configure the project in the Azure Custom Vision portal?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image80.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image81.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":12,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/063b628b5535fc7b7fb7257fb44bbdce1012319/","comments":[{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-11","up":1,"text":"Correct Answers\n\nProject Types: Classification\n\nClassification Types: Multiclass (Single tag per image)\n\nDomains: General (compact)\n\nExplanations\n\nProject Types: Classification is selected because the goal is to categorize the overall image rather than locate bounding boxes around objects.\n\nClassification Types: Multiclass (Single tag per image) is selected because each image contains either a cat or a dog, so only one label applies per image.\n\nDomains: General (compact) is required because the model will be deployed as part of an iOS app (on-device edge export like CoreML requires a compact domain)."}]},{"n":119,"id":1012320,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains an agent. The agent has a Model Context Protocol (MCP) tool named kbsearch that queries a knowledge base stored in Azure AI Search.</p><p>Some agent runs return answers from the base model without invoking the knowledge base, which results in responses without grounded citations.</p><p>You are provided with the following code snippet that runs the agent.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image82.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>You need to deterministically force the agent to invoke kbsearch on each run.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you do?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Add the response_format parameter to the create_and_process() method call."},{"k":"B","html":"Replace create_and_process() method with the create_thread_and_process_run() method."},{"k":"C","html":"Add the toolset parameter to the create_and_process() method call."},{"k":"D","html":"Add the tool_choice parameter to the create_and_process() method call."}],"answer":"D","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"D","p":100,"n":1}],"page":12,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/8749d7f28a197c44ad44cdac69785b001012320/","comments":[{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-11","up":1,"text":"Correct answer: D. Add the tool_choice parameter to the create_and_process() method call. ✅\n\nThe tool_choice parameter lets you explicitly force the agent to use a specific tool. Set it to kbsearch so the knowledge base is invoked on every run, ensuring responses are grounded and include citations.\n\nA ❌ response_format controls the output format.\nB ❌ Changing the processing method doesn't force tool usage.\nC ❌ toolset makes tools available but doesn't force their invocation.\nD ✅ tool_choice deterministically selects the required tool.","pick":"D"}],"variants":[14]},{"n":120,"id":1012321,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You are developing a text processing solution.</p><p>You have the following function.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image83.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>You call the function and use the following string as the second argument.</p><p>Our tour of London included a visit to Buckingham Palace</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What will be the output of the function?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"London and Buckingham Palace only"},{"k":"B","html":"Tour and visit only"},{"k":"C","html":"Our tour of London included a visit to Buckingham Palace"},{"k":"D","html":"London and Tour only"}],"answer":"A","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"A","p":100,"n":1}],"page":12,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/82c1b1ee88c335b622aa614add65a0e41012321/","comments":[{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-11","up":1,"text":"The function is extracting named entities (proper nouns) from the text. In the sentence:\n\n“Our tour of London included a visit to Buckingham Palace.”\n\nThe recognized entities are London and Buckingham Palace.\n\nAnswer: A","pick":"A"}]},{"n":121,"id":1012322,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You are building a solution that students will use to find references for essays.</p><p>You use the following code to start building the solution.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image84.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p class=\"ask\">For each of the following statements, select Yes is the statement is true. Otherwise, select No.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image85.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image86.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":13,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/f5e02ba673de28c6b3d9d1065b1b1acf1012322/","comments":[{"user":"Alvarogc","date":"2026-08-23","up":3,"text":"Second one should be \"no\", as the URL is not always from Bing. In fact, there's another parameter for Bing searchs called \"bing_entity_search_api_id\".\n\nFinal correct answer:\n\n1. No\n2. No\n3. Yes\n\nReference: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/python/api/azure-ai-textanalytics/azure.ai.textanalytics.linkedentity?view=azure-python"},{"user":"Codia","date":"2026-08-23","up":2,"text":"The correct answer for Statement 2 is No. While Bing's Knowledge Graph is used internally behind the scenes to perform entity resolution, and the SDK exposes a separate bing_entity_search_api_id attribute for API integration, the url field itself links to the underlying data source page (primarily Wikipedia), not a Bing search result URL."}]},{"n":122,"id":1012323,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project for a support ticket triage app that reads ticket text from a database.</p><p>You need to ensure that the app meets the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Compares candidate models by quality, cost, and throughput</li><li>Prevents hosting model weights in the Azure subscription</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you configure?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image87.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image88.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":13,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/98cb1e565388c6b6e6de5a0f47070b561012323/","comments":[{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-11","up":1,"text":"Correct Answers\n\nModel evaluation: Use model catalog leaderboards and model cards.\n\nDeployment option: Use a serverless deployment.\n\nExplanations\n\nModel evaluation: Model catalog leaderboards and model cards allow you to evaluate and compare models across benchmarks for quality, cost, latency, and throughput metrics prior to deployment.\n\nDeployment option: Serverless API deployments (Models-as-a-Service) host model weights in Microsoft-managed infrastructure, charging on a pay-as-you-go per-token basis and avoiding hosting/managing model weights or dedicated compute inside your own Azure subscription."}]},{"n":123,"id":1012324,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have an Azure subscription.</p><p>You need to build an app that will compare documents for semantic similarity. The solution must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Return numeric vectors that represent the tokens of each document.</li><li>Minimize development effort.</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which Azure OpenAI model should you use?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"GPT-3.5"},{"k":"B","html":"embeddings"},{"k":"C","html":"GPT-4"},{"k":"D","html":"DALL-E"}],"answer":"B","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"B","p":100,"n":1}],"page":13,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/37a9c74fcb7614c3da76337c1b94f9761012324/","comments":[{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-11","up":1,"text":"An embeddings model converts text into numeric vectors that capture semantic meaning. These vectors can then be compared to determine how semantically similar two documents are.\n\nA ❌ GPT-3.5 — primarily for text generation.\nB ✅ Embeddings — specifically designed to generate vector representations.\nC ❌ GPT-4 — primarily for understanding and generating content.\nD ❌ DALL-E — generates images.\nAnswer: B","pick":"B"}]},{"n":124,"id":1012325,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You are building an app that will provide users with definitions of common AI terms.</p><p>You create the following Python code.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image89.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p class=\"ask\">For each of the following statements, select Yes if the statement is true. Otherwise, select No.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image90.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image91.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":13,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/227be7d96e59cd3196a7a55fc73cbae21012325/","comments":[{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-11","up":1,"text":"Correct Answers\n\nThe response will contain an explanation of large language models (LLMs) that has a high degree of certainty: No (The abbreviation \"LLM\" is ambiguous and can mean Master of Laws in a legal context; without context steering, the model may return legal definition results instead of AI definitions).\n\nChanging \"What is an LLM?\" to \"What is an LLM in the context of AI models?\" will produce the intended response: Yes (Disambiguating the user prompt directly ensures the model targets the correct domain)."}]},{"n":125,"id":1012326,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have an Azure OpenAI model named AI1.</p><p>You are building a web app named App1 by using the Azure OpenAI SDK.</p><p>You need to configure App1 to connect to AI1.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What information must you provide?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"the deployment name, key, and model name"},{"k":"B","html":"the endpoint, key, and model type"},{"k":"C","html":"the deployment name, endpoint, and key"},{"k":"D","html":"the endpoint, key, and model name"}],"answer":"C","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"C","p":100,"n":1}],"page":13,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/e2f85c33e0fd7cc35161bc127a18fc051012326/","comments":[{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-11","up":1,"text":"When using the Azure OpenAI SDK, you need the endpoint, API key, and the deployment name to connect to the deployed model.\n\nA ❌ Model name isn't required; the deployment name identifies the deployed model.\nB ❌ Model type isn't required.\nC ✅ Deployment name + endpoint + key.\nD ❌ Model name is not required.\nAnswer: C","pick":"C"}]},{"n":126,"id":1012327,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You are building a solution in Azure that will use Azure Language in Foundry Tools service to process sensitive customer data.</p><p>You need to ensure that only specific Azure processes can access the Language service. The solution must minimize administrative effort.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you include in the solution?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Azure Application Gateway"},{"k":"B","html":"a virtual network gateway"},{"k":"C","html":"IPsec rules"},{"k":"D","html":"virtual network rules"}],"answer":"D","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"C","p":25,"n":1},{"a":"D","p":75,"n":3}],"page":13,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/c6102f36fd1c34ac641d0da30d52c44a1012327/","comments":[{"user":"Srikantha","date":"2026-09-18","up":2,"text":"Why this is correct:\nVirtual network rules (VNet firewalls) on the Azure AI Language resource allow you to restrict incoming traffic so that only applications or workloads running within designated Azure Virtual Network subnets can access the endpoint.\nThis natively secures sensitive customer data by isolating PaaS access to authorized Azure processes with minimal administrative effort, eliminating the need to deploy or manage additional networking infrastructure.","pick":"D"},{"user":"a5f05ea","date":"2026-09-27","up":1,"text":"Restrict an Azure service to selected VNets/subnets → Virtual network rules\n\nConnect/encrypt traffic between networks → VPN/IPsec\n\n✅ Therefore, D is correct, not C.","pick":"D"},{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-11","up":1,"text":"Virtual network rules allow you to restrict access to the Azure Language service to specific virtual networks and subnets, helping protect sensitive customer data with minimal administration.\n\nA ❌ Application Gateway — manages web traffic, not direct service access control.\nB ❌ Virtual network gateway — connects networks but doesn't provide this access restriction.\nC ❌ IPsec rules — not the appropriate Azure Language access-control mechanism.\nD ✅ Virtual network rules — restrict access to trusted Azure network resources.\nAnswer: D","pick":"C"}]},{"n":127,"id":1012328,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have an Azure subscription that contains a Microsoft Foundry Service resource named CSAccount1 and a virtual network named VNet1. CSAaccount1 is connected to VNet1.</p><p>You need to ensure that only specific resources can access CSAccount1. The solution must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Prevent external access to CSAccount1.</li><li>Minimize administrative effort.</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which two actions should you perform?</strong> Each correct answer presents part of the solution.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct answer is worth one point.</p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"In CSAccount1, modify the virtual network settings."},{"k":"B","html":"In VNet1, create a virtual subnet."},{"k":"C","html":"In VNet1, enable a service endpoint for CSAccount1."},{"k":"D","html":"In CSAccount1, configure the Access control (IAM) settings."},{"k":"E","html":"In VNet1, modify the virtual network settings."}],"answer":"AC","type":"multi","votes":[{"a":"AC","p":60,"n":3},{"a":"AE","p":40,"n":2}],"page":13,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/31d30e17451d36467a6e5f090de4780a1012328/","comments":[{"user":"Srikantha","date":"2026-09-07","up":2,"text":"ignore the previous\nEnable a service endpoint for CSAccount1 in VNet1 (Action A): This securely connects your virtual network to the Azure AI service resource over the Azure backbone network, routing traffic away from the public internet and helping satisfy the requirement to prevent external access.\nModify the virtual network settings in CSAccount1 (Action E): This allows you to restrict network access directly on the resource by setting access rules that block public traffic and permit only designated virtual networks and subnets, keeping administrative overhead minimal compared to configuring complex firewalls or routing mechanisms.","pick":"AE"},{"user":"Srikantha","date":"2026-09-07","up":2,"text":"Enable a service endpoint for CSAccount1 in VNet1 (Action A): This securely connects your virtual network to the Azure AI service resource over the Azure backbone network, routing traffic away from the public internet and helping satisfy the requirement to prevent external access.\nModify the virtual network settings in CSAccount1 (Action E): This allows you to restrict network access directly on the resource by setting access rules that block public traffic and permit only designated virtual networks and subnets, keeping administrative overhead minimal compared to configuring complex firewalls or routing mechanisms.","pick":"AC"},{"user":"a5f05ea","date":"2026-09-27","up":1,"text":"Correct answers: A and C\n\nA. In CSAccount1, modify the virtual network settings\nC. In VNet1, enable a service endpoint for CSAccount1","pick":"AC"}]},{"n":128,"id":1012329,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a collection of press releases stored as PDF files.</p><p>You need to extract text from the files and perform sentiment analysis.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which service should you use for each task?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image92.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image93.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":13,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/feea30542686abbc4d017692b750638e1012329/","comments":[{"user":"rokoskycloud","date":"2026-09-21","up":1,"text":"Extract text: Azure Vision in Foundry Tools\nThe Read API is the OCR operation built for extracting text from images and PDFs. Press releases are unstructured prose, so plain text extraction is exactly what's needed.\nPerform sentiment analysis: Azure Language in Foundry Tools\nSentiment analysis is a Language service feature, returning document-level and sentence-level sentiment with positive, neutral, and negative confidence scores"}]},{"n":129,"id":1012330,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You are designing an Azure AI solution to identify defective products on a production line.</p><p>You have a real-time video feed and an image library of sample products that are approved or rejected manually.</p><p>You need to recommend a service that meets the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Monitors the video feed and identifies the defective products.</li><li>Can train a new model by using the image library.</li><li>Minimizes development effort.</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you recommend?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Azure Vision in Foundry Tools"},{"k":"B","html":"Azure AI Video Indexer"},{"k":"C","html":"Azure AI Custom Vision"},{"k":"D","html":"Azure Machine Learning"}],"answer":"C","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"C","p":100,"n":1}],"page":13,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/07a40377f1a1288463231ec31999b6ed1012330/","comments":[{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-11","up":1,"text":"Custom Vision is designed to train custom image classification/object detection models using your own labeled image library. It can identify defective products from the video feed while requiring relatively little development effort.\n\nA ❌ Azure Vision — provides prebuilt vision capabilities but isn't the best fit for training this custom defect model.\nB ❌ Video Indexer — focuses on analyzing and indexing video content.\nC ✅ Custom Vision — supports custom training with approved/rejected product images.\nD ❌ Azure Machine Learning — more flexible but requires significantly more development and management.\n\nCorrect answer: C. Azure AI Custom Vision ✅","pick":"C"}]},{"n":130,"id":1012331,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You run the following command.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image94.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p class=\"ask\">For each of the following statements, select Yes if the statement is true. Otherwise, select No.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image95.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image96.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":13,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/3a6c0231289f69c07c2bec6fdf53c3471012331/","comments":[{"user":"Alvarogc","date":"2026-08-23","up":3,"text":"First one is a No, as you can see in the Microsoft Learn documentation: \" this URL verifies if the api-key used to start the container is valid WITHOUT causing an endpoint query\".\nSecond one is a No too, as it's not configured, and third one is a trivial Yes per definition.\n\n1. No\n2. No\n3. Yes\n\nReference: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/ai-services/language-service/sentiment-opinion-mining/how-to/use-containers"},{"user":"Srikantha","date":"2026-09-07","up":1,"text":"Going to http://localhost:5000/status will query the Azure endpoint to verify whether the API key used to start the container is valid: No (The /status endpoint verifies if the API key is valid locally without causing an endpoint query).\nThe container logging provider will write log data: Yes (Docker containers automatically log output to the configured container logging provider).\nGoing to http://localhost:5000/swagger will provide the details to access the documentation for the available endpoints: Yes (The Swagger UI provides the detailed description and documentation for the container's APIs)."},{"user":"ExamProAzure","date":"2026-08-21","up":1,"text":"Yes, No, Yes\nThe docker run command in the question includes only Eula, Billing, and ApiKey — no Logging: settings and no --mount for an output directory. Since none of the logging providers are explicitly configured or given a destination (like a mounted output folder), no log data will be written by the logging provider in this scenario."}]},{"n":131,"id":1012332,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You are developing an app that will use the Speech and Language APIs.</p><p>You need to provision resources for the app. The solution must ensure that each service is accessed by using a single endpoint and credential.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which type of resource should you create?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Azure Language in Foundry Tools"},{"k":"B","html":"Microsoft Foundry service"},{"k":"C","html":"Azure Speech in Foundry Tools"},{"k":"D","html":"Content Safety in Foundry Control Plane"}],"answer":"B","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"B","p":100,"n":1}],"page":14,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/c834a9b27d12daea61aec61063a716751012332/","comments":[{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-11","up":1,"text":"A Microsoft Foundry service resource can provide access to multiple AI capabilities, such as Speech and Language, through a single endpoint and credential. This minimizes resource and credential management.\n\nAnswer: B — Microsoft Foundry service","pick":"B"}]},{"n":132,"id":1012333,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You are building an app that will include one million scanned magazine articles. Each article will be stored as an image file.</p><p>You need to configure the app to extract text from the images. The solution must minimize development effort.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you include in the solution?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Azure Document Intelligence in Foundry Tools"},{"k":"B","html":"the Read API in Azure Vision in Foundry Tools"},{"k":"C","html":"Azure Vision in Foundry Tools Image Analysis"},{"k":"D","html":"Azure Language in Foundry Tools"}],"answer":"A","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"A","p":60,"n":3},{"a":"B","p":40,"n":2}],"page":14,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/54b987641f39f092edcda80398d49b581012333/","comments":[{"user":"ABHISHEK","date":"2026-09-19","up":5,"text":"The Read API is Azure's OCR engine for extracting printed and handwritten text from image files. It's a prebuilt, ready-to-call service, so you don't need to train a model or build a custom pipeline, which meets the \"minimize development effort\" requirement. It's also built to handle large volumes asynchronously, which suits one million images.","pick":"B"},{"user":"Alvarogc","date":"2026-08-23","up":2,"text":"Microsoft Learn recommends to use Azure Vision for labels, street signs or posters; while using Document Intelligence for books, articles and reports. In this case, we are talking about a million magazine ARTICLES, so A is the correct answer.\n\nReference: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/ai-services/computer-vision/how-to/call-read-api","pick":"A"},{"user":"Srikantha","date":"2026-09-18","up":1,"text":"Based on the official Microsoft Learn documentation, the recommended answer is A. Azure Document Intelligence in Foundry Tools.","pick":"A"}]},{"n":133,"id":1012334,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You are building an app that will scan confidential documents and use the Azure Language in Foundry Tools service to analyze the contents.</p><p>You provision a Microsoft Foundry Service resource.</p><p>You need to ensure that the app can make requests to the Azure Language in Foundry Tools service endpoint. The solution must ensure that confidential documents remain on-premises.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which three actions should you perform in sequence?</strong> To answer, move the appropriate actions from the list of actions to the answer area and arrange them in the correct order.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image97.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image98.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":14,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/db5e55342798a7073e40ce2c685019cd1012334/","comments":[{"user":"MarceloManhaes","date":"2026-08-16","up":5,"text":"Correct sequence:\n- Provision an on-premises Kubernetes cluster that has internet connectivity.\nThe container needs to have internet connectivity for billing/usage purposes\n- Pull an image from the Microsoft Container Registry (MCR).\nAzure AI Language containers are distributed through MCR, not Docker Hub.\n- Run the container and specify an API key and the Endpoint URL of the Azure AI resource.\nLanguage containers require:\n\nApiKey\nBilling (endpoint URI)\nEula=accept\nwhen started."}]},{"n":134,"id":1012335,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You are developing an app that will use the Azure Vision in Foundry Tools API to analyze an image.</p><p>You need configure the request that will be used by the app to identify whether an image is clipart or a line drawing.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>How should you complete the request?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image99.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image100.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":14,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/c591ec96a49a3907e0ed0c5d94f398fb1012335/","comments":[{"user":"Amelia233","date":"2026-09-11","up":1,"text":"Correct Answers\n\nHTTP Method: POST\n\nvisualFeatures: imageType\n\nHTTP Method (POST): The analyze endpoint in Azure Computer Vision requires sending image data (binary or URL) in the payload via a POST request.\n\nvisualFeatures (imageType): The ImageType feature specifically analyzes an image to determine whether it is clip art or a line drawing, returning scores for both types in the response."}]},{"n":135,"id":1012336,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You use the Azure Custom Vision service to build a classifier.</p><p>After training is complete, you need to evaluate the classifier.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which two metrics are available for review?</strong> Each correct answer presents a complete solution.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"F-score"},{"k":"B","html":"area under the curve (AUC)"},{"k":"C","html":"precision"},{"k":"D","html":"weighted accuracy"},{"k":"E","html":"recall"}],"answer":"CE","type":"multi","votes":[{"a":"CE","p":100,"n":1}],"page":14,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/c88765f463c56473ee49f2ed2aca5c261012336/","comments":[{"user":"AIBoss","date":"2026-09-05","up":1,"text":"Precision and recall are two different measurements of the effectiveness of a classifier:\n\nPrecision indicates the fraction of identified classifications that were correct. For example, if the model identified 100 images as dogs, and 99 of them were actually of dogs, then the precision would be 99%.\nRecall indicates the fraction of actual classifications that were correctly identified. For example, if there were actually 100 images of apples, and the model identified 80 as apples, the recall would be 80%.","pick":"CE"}]},{"n":136,"id":1018720,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have an Azure subscription that contains an Azure Language in Foundry Tools service resource named ta1 and a virtual network named vnet1.</p><p>You need to ensure that only resources in vnet1 can access ta1.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you configure?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"a network security group (NSG) for vnet1"},{"k":"B","html":"an Azure Language in Foundry Tools service container for ta1"},{"k":"C","html":"Azure Firewall for vnet1"},{"k":"D","html":"the virtual network settings for ta1"}],"answer":"D","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"D","p":100,"n":1}],"page":14,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/77358fe88162e488144d3476cd3a7faa1018720/","comments":[{"user":"Srikantha","date":"2026-09-18","up":1,"text":"D. the virtual network settings for ta1\nWhy this is correct:\nTo restrict access to an Azure AI / Language service resource (ta1) so that it only accepts traffic from a specific virtual network (vnet1), you must configure the Networking / Virtual network settings on ta1 itself. This is done by enabling access from \"Selected Networks and Private Endpoints\" and linking vnet1 (via Service Endpoints or Private Endpoints).","pick":"D"}]},{"n":137,"id":1018721,"topic":1,"series":true,"stem":"<p>You have an Azure subscription that contains a Microsoft Foundry resource named AI1 and a Content Safety in Foundry Control Plane resource named CS1.</p><p>You build an agent that uses AI1 to provide generative answers to specific questions and CS1 to check input and output for objectionable content.</p><p>You need to optimize the content filter configurations by running tests on sample questions.</p><div class=\"solution\"><span>Proposed solution</span>From Content Safety Studio, you use the Moderate text content feature to run the tests.</div><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Does this meet the requirement?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Yes"},{"k":"B","html":"No"}],"answer":"A","type":"yesno","votes":[],"page":14,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/7f8ce9c32415ea5300fb7c69b444382d1018721/","comments":[]},{"n":138,"id":1018722,"topic":1,"series":true,"stem":"<p>You have an Azure subscription that contains a Microsoft Foundry resource named AI1 and a Content Safety in Foundry Control Plane resource named CS1.</p><p>You build an agent that uses AI1 to provide generative answers to specific questions and CS1 to check input and output for objectionable content.</p><p>You need to optimize the content filter configurations by running tests on sample questions.</p><div class=\"solution\"><span>Proposed solution</span>From Content Safety Studio, you use the Safety metaprompt feature to run the tests.</div><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Does this meet the requirement?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Yes"},{"k":"B","html":"No"}],"answer":"B","type":"yesno","votes":[{"a":"B","p":100,"n":1}],"page":14,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/a8f9d3cdc3c149e9b13a1c772c6ad85d1018722/","comments":[{"user":"Srikantha","date":"2026-09-18","up":1,"text":"B. No\nWhy this does not meet the requirement:\nThe Safety metaprompt feature provides guidelines and template instructions to embed into an LLM's system prompt to encourage safer generation behaviors. It is not an interactive test harness used to run batch sample questions or adjust content filter thresholds.\nCorrect Solution:\nTo test sample questions and optimize sensitivity thresholds or blocklists for content filtering, you should use the Moderate text content feature within Azure AI Content Safety Studio.","pick":"B"}]},{"n":139,"id":1018723,"topic":1,"series":true,"stem":"<p>You have an Azure subscription that contains a Microsoft Foundry resource named AI1 and a Content Safety in Foundry Control Plane resource named CS1.</p><p>You build an agent that uses AI1 to provide generative answers to specific questions and CS1 to check input and output for objectionable content.</p><p>You need to optimize the content filter configurations by running tests on sample questions.</p><div class=\"solution\"><span>Proposed solution</span>From Content Safety Studio, you use the Protected material detection feature to run the tests.</div><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Does this meet the requirement?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Yes"},{"k":"B","html":"No"}],"answer":"B","type":"yesno","votes":[{"a":"B","p":100,"n":1}],"page":14,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/eef908aeb628b5e610a963a7ca99ce1e1018723/","comments":[{"user":"Srikantha","date":"2026-09-18","up":1,"text":"B. No\nWhy this does not meet the requirement:\nMonitor online activity is used to track and analyze real-time usage, trends, latency, and request metrics for already deployed moderation APIs. It is not designed for testing sample questions or tuning filter sensitivity levels prior to deployment.\nCorrect Solution:\nTo test sample questions and adjust/optimize sensitivity thresholds and blocklists for content filtering, you should use the Moderate text content feature in Azure AI Content Safety Studio.","pick":"B"}]},{"n":140,"id":1018724,"topic":1,"series":true,"stem":"<p>You have an Azure subscription that contains a Microsoft Foundry resource named AI1 and a Content Safety in Foundry Control Plane resource named CS1.</p><p>You build an agent that uses AI1 to provide generative answers to specific questions and CS1 to check input and output for objectionable content.</p><p>You need to optimize the content filter configurations by running tests on sample questions.</p><div class=\"solution\"><span>Proposed solution</span>From Content Safety Studio, you use the Monitor online activity feature to run the tests.</div><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Does this meet the requirement?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Yes"},{"k":"B","html":"No"}],"answer":"B","type":"yesno","votes":[{"a":"B","p":100,"n":1}],"page":14,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/19826d54ea541b80a40a1eddfd081bbc1018724/","comments":[{"user":"Srikantha","date":"2026-09-18","up":1,"text":"B. No\nWhy this does not meet the requirement:\nMonitor online activity is used to track and analyze real-time usage, trends, latency, and request metrics for already deployed moderation APIs. It is not designed for testing sample questions or tuning filter sensitivity levels prior to deployment.\nCorrect Solution:\nTo test sample questions and adjust/optimize sensitivity thresholds and blocklists for content filtering, you should use the Moderate text content feature in Azure AI Content Safety Studio.","pick":"B"}]},{"n":141,"id":1018725,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You are building an AI solution that will use Sentiment Analysis results from surveys to calculate bonuses for customer service staff.</p><p>You need to ensure that the solution meets the Microsoft responsible AI principles.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you do?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Add a human review and approval step before making decisions that affect the staff’s financial situation."},{"k":"B","html":"Include the Sentiment Analysis results when surveys return a low confidence score."},{"k":"C","html":"Use all the surveys, including surveys by customers who requested that their account be deleted and their data be removed."},{"k":"D","html":"Publish the raw survey data to a central location and provide the staff with access to the location."}],"answer":"A","type":"single","votes":[],"page":15,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/126d05a9031eb1c6350b6bc18d9d00301018725/","comments":[]},{"n":142,"id":1018726,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have an Azure DevOps pipeline named Pipeline1 that is used to deploy an app. Pipeline1 includes a step that will create an Azure AI services account.</p><p>You need to add a step to Pipeline1 that will identify the created Azure AI services account. The solution must minimize development effort.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which Azure Command-Line Interface (CLI) command should you run?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"az cognitiveservices account network-rule"},{"k":"B","html":"az cognitiveservices account show"},{"k":"C","html":"az account list"},{"k":"D","html":"az resource link"}],"answer":"B","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"B","p":100,"n":1}],"page":15,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/4b0f671de23639d2a0f4d74cc7fbc14a1018726/","comments":[{"user":"Srikantha","date":"2026-09-18","up":1,"text":"B. az cognitiveservices account show\nThis command retrieves the properties and details of a specific Azure Cognitive Services / Azure AI services account (by name and resource group). After the pipeline creates the account, you can call it to identify and confirm the resource with minimal extra code.\n\nA manages network access rules for the account and does not retrieve its identity/details.\nC (az account list) lists Azure subscriptions, not the AI services resource itself.\nD works with resource links and is unrelated to identifying a Cognitive Services account.","pick":"B"}]},{"n":143,"id":1018727,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You are building an internet-based training solution. The solution requires that a user’s camera and microphone remain enabled.</p><p>You need to monitor a video stream of the user and verify that the user is alone and is not collaborating with another user. The solution must minimize development effort.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you include in the solution?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"content moderation in Azure AI Azure Video Indexer"},{"k":"B","html":"speech-to-text in the Azure Speech in Foundry Tools"},{"k":"C","html":"object detection in Azure AI Custom Vision"},{"k":"D","html":"Spatial Analysis in Azure Vision in Foundry Tools"}],"answer":"D","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"D","p":100,"n":1}],"page":15,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/64e07773f576041d7d9a463d9f9f1c9e1018727/","comments":[{"user":"Srikantha","date":"2026-09-18","up":1,"text":"D. Spatial Analysis in Azure Vision in Foundry Tools\nWhy this is correct:\nSpatial Analysis is a pre-built capability in Azure AI Vision specifically designed to analyze real-time streaming video. It can detect the presence and movements of people in a video frame, making it the ideal solution to continuously count the number of people in the camera's view and verify that only one person (the user) is present. Because it is pre-built for this exact scenario, it minimizes development effort.","pick":"D"}]},{"n":144,"id":1018728,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You are developing a method that uses the Azure Vision in Foundry Tools client library. The method will perform optical character recognition (OCR) in images. The method has the following code.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image101.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>During testing, you discover that the call to the get_read_result method occurs before the read operation is complete.</p><p>You need to prevent the get_read_result method from proceeding until the read operation is complete.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which two actions should you perform?</strong> Each correct answer presents part of the solution.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Add code to verify the read_result.status value."},{"k":"B","html":"Add code to verify the status of the read_operation_location value."},{"k":"C","html":"Remove the operation_id parameter."},{"k":"D","html":"Wrap the call to get_read_result within a loop that contains a delay."}],"answer":"AD","type":"multi","votes":[],"page":15,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/b7e55c96617c8706552c8b25a9b78ba01018728/","comments":[]},{"n":145,"id":1018729,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You need to configure Agent1 to meet the security and compliance requirements.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you include in the solution?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"prompt shields"},{"k":"B","html":"protected material detection"},{"k":"C","html":"violence content filtering"},{"k":"D","html":"self-harm content filtering"}],"answer":"B","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"A","p":100,"n":2}],"page":15,"case":"d421f5cb15","thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/652040212b17cd65c8b55173aac60e2d1018729/","comments":[{"user":"a5f05ea","date":"2026-09-29","up":2,"text":"A. Prompt shields\n\nPrompt Shields in Microsoft Foundry/Azure AI Content Safety are designed to detect and block adversarial prompt attacks, including attacks embedded in external documents or content. This directly addresses the requirement that Agent1 be protected from malicious instructions hidden within product-sheet content.","pick":"A"},{"user":"Srikantha","date":"2026-09-18","up":1,"text":"A. prompt shields\nWhy this is correct:\nPrompt shields are a key security feature within Azure AI Content Safety designed to defend applications from direct (jailbreak) and indirect prompt injection attacks. Based on the Contoso case study's security and compliance requirements, Agent1 must be protected from malicious instructions that might be hidden within uploaded documents or embedded as text inside images (indirect prompt injections). Prompt shields specifically detect and block these types of hidden instructions before they can hijack the model.","pick":"A"}]},{"n":146,"id":1018730,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You need to configure personalized user interactions for Agent1 based on the business requirements.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you include in the solution?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"instructions"},{"k":"B","html":"memory"},{"k":"C","html":"tools"},{"k":"D","html":"guardrails"}],"answer":"B","type":"single","votes":[],"page":15,"case":"d421f5cb15","thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/23c19e0c82aaee8544fe65b201a78f981018730/","comments":[],"variants":[67]},{"n":147,"id":1018731,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have an agent named Agent1 that uses Model Context Protocol (MCP) calls to retrieve external data.</p><p>You need to implement guardrails to ensure that Agent1 cannot send any content tagged as Violence to the MCP server.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which intervention point should you use?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"tool call"},{"k":"B","html":"user input"},{"k":"C","html":"tool response"},{"k":"D","html":"output"}],"answer":"A","type":"single","votes":[],"page":15,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/0839e47f3f7a4b12d98b4c37883a01591018731/","comments":[]},{"n":148,"id":1018732,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a configurable guardrail in a Microsoft Foundry project.</p><p>You have a Python application. A text blocklist named ConfidentialTerms already contains terms that must be detected in user messages. The application stores each incoming user message in a variable named input_text.</p><p>You plan to moderate input_text before the text is sent to a language model.</p><p>You need to analyze input_text by using the existing blocklist.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>How should you complete the code?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image102.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image103.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":15,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/52dc0bb1504e9e5970dfb206207ab5d01018732/","comments":[]},{"n":149,"id":1018733,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have an Azure subscription that contains Microsoft Foundry resource.</p><p>You need to build an app that will suggest product names from a given product description.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which Foundry model should you use?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Whisper"},{"k":"B","html":"DALL-E"},{"k":"C","html":"embeddings"},{"k":"D","html":"GPT-4"}],"answer":"D","type":"single","votes":[],"page":15,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/85af1de3ec64996b9f4695915da29c431018733/","comments":[]},{"n":150,"id":1018734,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a factory that produces cardboard packaging for food products. The factory has intermittent internet connectivity.</p><p>The packages are required to include four samples of each product.</p><p>You need to build an Azure Custom Vision model that will identify defects in packaging and provide the location of the defects to an operator. The model must ensure that each package contains the four products.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which project type and domain should you use?</strong> To answer, move the appropriate options to the correct targets. You may use each option once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to move the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image104.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image105.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":15,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/0a168d5fbe4603c4fbeb394fde3c9ed51018734/","comments":[{"user":"Srikantha","date":"2026-09-18","up":1,"text":"Project type: Object detection\nDomain: General (compact)\nKey Reasons\nObject detection: The model must identify specific items (verifying that exactly four products are inside each package) and provide the location (bounding box coordinates) of defects to an operator. Image classification can only categorize an entire image as a whole and cannot return spatial locations or count individual items.\nGeneral (compact): The factory has intermittent internet connectivity, meaning the model must be exported to run locally on an edge device or container offline. In Azure Custom Vision, only domains designated as (compact) support model export (ONNX, TensorFlow, Docker, etc.)."}]},{"n":151,"id":1018735,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>In Microsoft Foundry, you use the Chat playground with the GPT-35 Turbo model.</p><p>You have a prompt that contains the following code.</p><p>function F(n)</p><p>{</p><p>var f = [0, 1];</p><p>for (var i = 2; i &lt; n; i++) f[i] = f[i-1] + f[i-2];</p><p>return f;</p><p>}</p><p>You need the model to create an explanation of the code. The solution must minimize costs.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you do?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Add // what does function F do? to the prompt."},{"k":"B","html":"Set the temperature parameter to 1."},{"k":"C","html":"Change the model to GPT-4-32k."},{"k":"D","html":"Add function F(explanation) to the prompt."}],"answer":"A","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"A","p":100,"n":1}],"page":16,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/d65f8fe3a38ea4db026a086a15f4b8601018735/","comments":[{"user":"Srikantha","date":"2026-09-18","up":1,"text":"The correct choice is A. Add // what does function F do? to the prompt.\nKey Reasons\nDirect Prompting via Code Comments: Appending // what does function F do? clearly instructs the model to explain the functionality of the JavaScript code (which generates a Fibonacci sequence) directly within the code context.\nMinimizes Token Costs: Adding a short comment requires very few input tokens and keeps the workload on GPT-35-Turbo, which is significantly less expensive per token than larger models like GPT-4.","pick":"A"}]},{"n":152,"id":1018736,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have an app that uses Azure AI Custom Vision and a custom trained classifier to identify products in images.</p><p>You need to add new products to the classifier. The solution must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Minimize how long it takes to add the products.</li><li>Minimize development effort.</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which five actions should you perform in sequence?</strong> To answer, move the appropriate actions from the list of actions to the answer area and arrange them in the correct order.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image106.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image107.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":16,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/29da4d95068372a81ff315d680047ade1018736/","comments":[{"user":"Srikantha","date":"2026-09-18","up":4,"text":"1: From the Custom Vision portal, open the project.\n2: Upload sample images of the new products.\n3: Label the sample images.\n4: Retrain the model.\n5: Publish the model."}]},{"n":153,"id":1018737,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry project that contains an agent. The agent generates summaries from retrieved policy documents.</p><p>You need to improve response completeness. The solution must be implemented in the logic of the application code before responses are returned.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you do?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Add a reflection pass before the responses are returned."},{"k":"B","html":"Enable response streaming."},{"k":"C","html":"Increase the value of the presence_penalty parameter."},{"k":"D","html":"Decrease the value of the max_tokens parameter."}],"answer":"A","type":"single","votes":[],"page":16,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/0b7c38fce40091a3d1d729319e13a08b1018737/","comments":[],"variants":[38,100]},{"n":154,"id":1018738,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Microsoft Foundry resource named AI1 that hosts three deployments of the GPT 3.5 model. Each deployment is optimized for a unique workload.</p><p>You plan to deploy three apps. Each app will access AI1 by using the REST API and will use the deployment that was optimized for the app’s intended workload.</p><p>You need to provide each app with access to AI1 and the appropriate deployment. The solution must ensure that only the apps can access AI1.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you use to provide access to AI1, and what should each app use to connect to its appropriate deployment?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image108.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image109.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":16,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/712a0828843604b51f745237a360681b1018738/","comments":[{"user":"Az301301X","date":"2026-09-21","up":3,"text":"Provide access to AI1 by using: An API key\nConnect to the deployment by using: A deployment name"},{"user":"AngusSzarpidrut","date":"2026-10-10","up":1,"text":"Correct Answer: A — Add a reflection pass before the responses are returned.\nWhy (from Microsoft Learn):\n• A reflection pass means having the application ask the model to re-check its own draft answer against the retrieved source material for gaps or missing points before the final response is sent back to the user — this is exactly an application-code-level check that can catch and fix incomplete summaries, matching \"implemented in the logic of the application code.\"\n• Response streaming (B) only changes how the text is delivered to the client (in chunks vs. all at once); it doesn't make the content itself more complete.\n• Increasing presence_penalty (C) discourages the model from repeating the same tokens/topics, which can actually reduce coverage of a topic rather than improve completeness.\n• Decreasing max_tokens (D) directly caps how much the model is allowed to write, which would make responses shorter and less complete, the opposite of what's needed here."},{"user":"rokoskycloud","date":"2026-09-19","up":1,"text":"Provide access to AI1 by using: An API key | It says three apps call a REST API.\nConnect to the deployment by using: A deployment name | The deployment name is a path segment in the request URL. That's what routes each app to its own tuned deployment of the same underlying model."}]},{"n":155,"id":1018739,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have an Azure subscription that contains an Azure Language in Foundry Tools service resource.</p><p>You need to identify the URL of the REST interface for the Language service.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which blade should you use in the Azure portal?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Networking"},{"k":"B","html":"Identity"},{"k":"C","html":"Properties"},{"k":"D","html":"Keys and Endpoint"}],"answer":"D","type":"single","votes":[],"page":16,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/fe85a872c133cfb7631c9dbb90fccd4b1018739/","comments":[]},{"n":156,"id":1018740,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have an Azure AI Search resource named Search1 that is used by multiple apps hosted in Azure.</p><p>You need to secure Search1. The solution must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Prevent access to Search1 from the internet.</li><li>Limit the access of each app to query specific indexes.</li></ul><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you do?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct answer is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image110.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image111.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":16,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/b9dd3941576dc1c8b327e6536d7d506d1018740/","comments":[{"user":"AngusSzarpidrut","date":"2026-10-10","up":2,"text":"• To prevent access from the internet: create a private endpoint.\n• To limit access to query specific indexes: use Azure roles.\nWhy (from Microsoft Learn):\n• An IP firewall only allows or blocks specific public IP ranges — the service is still technically reachable over the internet, just filtered — while a private endpoint gives Search1 a private IP inside your virtual network and removes public internet exposure entirely, which is what \"prevent access from the internet\" actually requires.\n• For scoping each app to only specific indexes, Azure roles (Azure RBAC data-plane roles for AI Search) let you assign fine-grained, per-resource permissions to each app's identity, whereas the older key-based authentication uses admin/query keys that grant blanket access across the whole search service with no per-index scoping — so only the RBAC/roles approach can satisfy the \"specific indexes\" requirement."},{"user":"Srikantha","date":"2026-09-18","up":2,"text":"To prevent access from the internet: Create a private endpoint.\nTo limit access to query specific indexes: Use Azure roles.\nKey Reasons\nPrevent Public Internet Access: Creating a private endpoint routes traffic over a private IP within your Azure Virtual Network (VNet) using Azure Private Link, blocking direct public internet access to Search1.\nIndex-Level Granular Control: Azure RBAC data-plane roles (such as Search Index Data Reader) can be assigned to individual app managed identities at the scope of a specific index (/indexes/index-name). In contrast, Azure AI Search query keys operate strictly at the service level, granting query access across all indexes in the service."}]},{"n":157,"id":1018741,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You plan to build an app that will generate a list of tags for uploaded images. The app must meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>Generate tags in a user’s preferred language.</li><li>Support English, French, and Spanish.</li><li>Minimize development effort.</li></ul><p>You need to build a function that will generate the tags for the app.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which Azure service endpoint should you use?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Azure Vision in Foundry Tools Image Analysis"},{"k":"B","html":"Azure Custom Vision image classification"},{"k":"C","html":"Content Safety in Foundry Control Plane"},{"k":"D","html":"Custom Translator"}],"answer":"A","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"A","p":100,"n":1}],"page":16,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/d035d7927fa73648730bc61a7b70e59d1018741/","comments":[{"user":"Srikantha","date":"2026-09-18","up":2,"text":"The correct choice is A. Azure Vision in Foundry Tools Image Analysis.\nKey Reasons\nNative Multi-Language Tagging: Azure Vision Image Analysis includes pre-built tagging capabilities that natively support localized tag output (including English, French, Spanish, and other languages) by simply passing the target language query parameter in the API request.\nMinimal Development Effort: It provides a ready-to-use pre-trained AI model out of the box, completely eliminating the need to collect training images, label datasets, or train custom models.","pick":"A"}]},{"n":158,"id":1018742,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have a Docker host named Host1 that contains a container base image.</p><p>You have an Azure subscription that contains a custom speech-to-text model named model1.</p><p>You need to run model1 on Host1.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which three actions should you perform in sequence?</strong> To answer, move the appropriate actions from the list of actions to the answer area and arrange them in the correct order.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image112.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image113.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"dragdrop","votes":[],"page":16,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/5235a73aaee9ce0262edeb247544a7851018742/","comments":[{"user":"Srikantha","date":"2026-09-18","up":4,"text":"To run the custom speech-to-text model on Host1, perform the following actions in sequence:\nRequest approval to run the container.\nExport model1 to Host1.\nRun the container.\nExplanation of Steps:\nStep 1: Azure AI Speech containers are gated services that require submitting an access request form to receive approval from Microsoft before deploying the container image.\nStep 2: The custom speech model (model1) must be exported/downloaded from Speech Studio and copied locally to the host directory so it can be mounted into the container.\nStep 3: Execute the docker run command on Host1 with the necessary billing parameters, API key, and local volume mount path to start the container instance."},{"user":"Kalut","date":"2026-09-17","up":1,"text":"Export model\nRun Container\nConfigure disk logging"}]},{"n":159,"id":1018743,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You are designing a solution that will answer questions about human resources (HR) policies stored in the PDF format.</p><p>You need to ensure that the identical answer to a specific question is returned every time. The solution must minimize development effort.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>Which service should you include in the solution?</strong></p>","choices":[{"k":"A","html":"Azure OpenAI"},{"k":"B","html":"Azure Language in Foundry Tools"},{"k":"C","html":"Azure Machine Learning"},{"k":"D","html":"Azure Document Intelligence in Foundry Tools"}],"answer":"B","type":"single","votes":[{"a":"B","p":100,"n":3}],"page":16,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/fef4e745b147ed7ffec7a95263d559061018743/","comments":[{"user":"Srikantha","date":"2026-09-18","up":2,"text":"The correct choice is B. Azure Language in Foundry Tools.\nKey Reasons\nDeterministic Responses: Azure Language includes the Question Answering feature (formerly QnA Maker). This service allows you to ingest documents like HR policy PDFs to create a knowledge base. Because it relies on matching user queries to static, predefined answers (or specific extracted passages) in the knowledge base, it guarantees that the exact identical answer is returned every time for a specific matched question.\nMinimal Development Effort: The Question Answering feature has built-in capabilities to automatically parse and extract question-answer pairs and hierarchical structures directly from PDFs, requiring almost no custom code compared to building a custom RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) pipeline.","pick":"B"},{"user":"Az301301X","date":"2026-09-23","up":1,"text":"Correct answer: B. Azure Language in Foundry Tools\nThe key phrase is “the identical answer to a specific question is returned every time.” That points to Exact Question Answering, not generative AI.","pick":"B"}]},{"n":160,"id":1018744,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You have 100,000 images.</p><p>You need to build an app that will perform the following actions:</p><ul><li>Identify road signs in the images and extract the text on the signs.</li><li>Analyze the text to identify well-known locations.</li></ul><p>The solution must minimize development effort.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>What should you use for each action?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image114.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image115.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":16,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/cd1617a84eabaa9725226aa7199390ff1018744/","comments":[{"user":"Srikantha","date":"2026-09-18","up":1,"text":"Extract the text: Azure Vision in Foundry Tools\nIdentify well-known locations: Azure Language in Foundry Tools\nKey Reasons\nExtract the text: Azure Vision includes powerful Optical Character Recognition (OCR) capabilities designed to detect and extract text from natural scene images (often called \"text in the wild\"), which is exactly what is needed for identifying text on road signs in photographs. Azure Document Intelligence is geared more toward structured documents and forms, not scene images.\nIdentify well-known locations: Azure Language provides pre-built Named Entity Recognition (NER) capabilities. By feeding the extracted text into Azure Language, it can automatically identify and categorize entities such as cities, landmarks, and other well-known locations with minimal development effort, eliminating the need to train a custom model."}]},{"n":161,"id":1018745,"topic":1,"stem":"<p>You plan to deploy a containerized version of an Azure AI Language service that will be used for sentiment analysis.</p><p>You configure https://contoso.cognitiveservices.azure.com as the endpoint URI for the service.</p><p>You need to run the container on an Azure virtual machine by using Docker.</p><p class=\"ask\"><strong>How should you complete the command?</strong> To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.</p><p class=\"note\">NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p><p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image116.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","choices":[],"answer":"","answerHtml":"<p><img src=\"data/img/ai-103/image117.png\" alt=\"exhibit\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>","type":"hotspot","votes":[],"page":17,"thread":"https://www.examtopics.com/comments/78840c2f501377d42915cec31b69cea11018745/","comments":[]}]}]};
